  'Q1. Which of the following is equivalent to the logic expression below?

(x + y) ∙ (x + z)

Here, the letters are logic variables; x + y, x ∙ y, and x̅ are OR, AND, and NOT operations on the corresponding variables, respectively.',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q1. Which of the following is equivalent to the logic expression below?\n\n(x + y) ∙ (x + z)\n\nHere, the letters are logic variables; x + y, x ∙ y, and x̅ are OR, AND, and NOT operations on the corresponding variables, respectively."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"x ∙ (y + z)"},{"label":"b","text":"x + y ∙ z"},{"label":"c","text":"x ∙ y + y ∙ z"},{"label":"d","text":"(x̅ + y) ∙ z"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is x + y ∙ z. By the distributive law of OR over AND, (x + y) ∙ (x + z) = x + y ∙ z. You can verify it by expanding: x∙x + x∙z + y∙x + y∙z = x + x∙z + x∙y + y∙z, and the absorption law reduces x + x∙z + x∙y to x, leaving x + y∙z.',
