  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is 0.5. A decimal fraction has a finite octal representation only if it can be written as a fraction whose denominator is a power of 2, and 0.5 = 1/2 = 4/8, which is 0.4 in octal. The others are 3/10, 2/5 and 4/5, whose denominators contain the factor 5, so their octal expansions repeat forever.',
