  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  12,
  'Q12. Which of the following is the performance of a CPU in MIPS when the instruction mix of the CPU is as listed in the table below? Here, the CPU does not use a pipeline architecture.

Instruction type | Instruction execution time in μs | Appearance ratio
Register to register operation | 0.1 | 40%
Register from memory operation | 0.3 | 50%
Unconditional branch operation | 0.6 | 10%',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q12. Which of the following is the performance of a CPU in MIPS when the instruction mix of the CPU is as listed in the table below? Here, the CPU does not use a pipeline architecture.\n\nInstruction type | Instruction execution time in μs | Appearance ratio\nRegister to register operation | 0.1 | 40%\nRegister from memory operation | 0.3 | 50%\nUnconditional branch operation | 0.6 | 10%"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0.04"},{"label":"b","text":"0.25"},{"label":"c","text":"4"},{"label":"d","text":"25"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is 4 MIPS. The average instruction time is 0.1 × 0.4 + 0.3 × 0.5 + 0.6 × 0.1 = 0.04 + 0.15 + 0.06 = 0.25 μs, so the CPU executes 1 ÷ 0.25 μs = 4 million instructions per second. Choice 0.25 is the average time itself, not the MIPS value.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
