  '["2021-april-a-q17-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A: Restoration of the running state, B: Selection of the process, C: Saving of the running state"},{"label":"b","text":"A: Saving of the running state, B: Restoration of the running state, C: Selection of the process"},{"label":"c","text":"A: Saving of the running state, B: Selection of the process, C: Restoration of the running state"},{"label":"d","text":"A: Selection of the process, B: Restoration of the running state, C: Saving of the running state"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is A = saving of the running state, B = selection of the process, C = restoration of the running state. After the interrupt, the OS first saves the context (registers, PC) of process A, then the dispatcher selects the next process to run from the ready queue, and finally restores the saved context of process B so that it can resume running.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
