  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2021-april-a-q22-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2021-april-a-q22-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2021-april-a-q22-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2021-april-a-q22-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is circuit c, two NAND gates feeding a NOR gate, which does not implement F. Its output is NOT(NOT(A•B) + NOT(C•D)) = A•B•C•D by De Morgan''s law, which differs from A•B + C•D. Circuit a is the direct AND-OR form, circuit b is NAND-NAND, and circuit d feeds NAND outputs into an OR with inverted inputs; b and d both equal A•B + C•D.',
