(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. Which of the following is the response time when a client and server at different locations communicate under the conditions below? Here, the response time is in seconds and starts from the moment the client sends a message until a response is received from the server. 1 MB is 10⁶ bytes. The propagation delay between the client and server can be ignored.

[Conditions]
Line speed between client and server | 8 Mbit/s
Transmission efficiency | 60%
Message size | 1 MB for upstreaming and 2 MB for downstreaming
Processing time at client side | Total of 0.4 s for sending and receiving
Processing time at server side | Total of 0.4 s for sending and receiving',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q30. Which of the following is the response time when a client and server at different locations communicate under the conditions below? Here, the response time is in seconds and starts from the moment the client sends a message until a response is received from the server. 1 MB is 10⁶ bytes. The propagation delay between the client and server can be ignored.\n\n[Conditions]\nLine speed between client and server | 8 Mbit/s\nTransmission efficiency | 60%\nMessage size | 1 MB for upstreaming and 2 MB for downstreaming\nProcessing time at client side | Total of 0.4 s for sending and receiving\nProcessing time at server side | Total of 0.4 s for sending and receiving"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1.4"},{"label":"b","text":"3.8"},{"label":"c","text":"5.0"},{"label":"d","text":"5.8"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is 5.8 seconds. The effective line speed is 8 Mbit/s × 0.6 = 4.8 Mbit/s, so sending 1 MB (8 Mbit) takes about 1.67 s and receiving 2 MB (16 Mbit) takes about 3.33 s, giving 5.0 s of transmission. Adding 0.4 s of client processing and 0.4 s of server processing gives 5.8 s.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
