  '[{"label":"a","text":"Attacking systems with scripts"},{"label":"b","text":"Containment"},{"label":"c","text":"Social engineering activities"},{"label":"d","text":"Stealing user credentials"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is containment. An incident response plan typically covers preparation, detection and analysis, containment, eradication, recovery and lessons learned, and containment limits the spread and damage of an incident. Script attacks, social engineering and credential theft are attacker activities, not response steps.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
