(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  64,
  'Q64. Which of the following is a technique that performs the optimum resource allocation for
 computerization investment in each category classified by the similarities of risks and
 investment value?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.16,81.19],"text":"Q64. Which of the following is a technique that performs the optimum resource allocation for"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[85.74,85.85,533.15,117.13],"text":"computerization investment in each category classified by the similarities of risks and\ninvestment value?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,407.12,190.21],"text":"a) 3C analysis\nb) Benchmarking\nc) Enterprise architecture\nd) IT portfolio"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"3C analysis"},{"label":"b","text":"Benchmarking"},{"label":"c","text":"Enterprise architecture"},{"label":"d","text":"IT portfolio"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the IT portfolio. IT portfolio management classifies IT investments into categories with similar risk and value characteristics and allocates resources to each category optimally, much like a financial investment portfolio. Enterprise architecture models the business and systems as a whole, and benchmarking compares practices with leading companies.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
