 investment value?

 a) 3C analysis b) Benchmarking
 c) Enterprise architecture d) IT portfolio',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  65,
  'Q65. In the verification of stakeholder requirements, which of the following indicates the ability
 to keep track of the process until the implementation of a change request?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,193.74,533.18,225.19],"text":"Q65. In the verification of stakeholder requirements, which of the following indicates the ability"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[85.2,229.85,445.56,260.89],"text":"to keep track of the process until the implementation of a change request?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,502.16,280.21],"text":"a) Interoperability\nb) Maintainability\nc) Traceability\nd) Usability"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Interoperability"},{"label":"b","text":"Maintainability"},{"label":"c","text":"Traceability"},{"label":"d","text":"Usability"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is traceability, the ability to follow a requirement or change request forward through design and implementation and back to its origin. It lets you verify that every stakeholder requirement has been implemented and tested. Interoperability, maintainability and usability are quality characteristics of the product, not of requirements tracking.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q65)',
