  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q72. The figure below shows the transaction model of an escrow service that is used in an Internet auction site or other similar transactions. Which of the following is the action that corresponds to (5) in this figure? Here, (1) through (6) indicate the sequence of transactions, and each of the numbers from (3) to (6) corresponds to an action in a) through d)."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2021-april-a-q72-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Notice of payment deposit"},{"label":"b","text":"Notice of product receipt"},{"label":"c","text":"Shipment of product"},{"label":"d","text":"Transfer of payment"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is notice of product receipt. After the buyer pays the escrow company (2), the escrow company notifies the seller of the payment deposit (3), the seller ships the product to the buyer (4), the buyer notifies the escrow company that the product was received (5), and only then is the payment transferred to the seller (6). Holding the payment until receipt is confirmed is what protects both parties.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q72)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q72. The figure below shows the transaction model of an escrow service that is used in an
 Internet auction site or other similar transactions. Which of the following is the action that
 corresponds to (5) in this figure? Here, (1) through (6) indicate the sequence of transactions,
 and each of the numbers from (3) to (6) corresponds to an action in a) through d).

 Escrow service company

 (3) (2) Payment
 for purchase
 (6) (5)
 (4)
 Seller Buyer
 (1) Agreement of sale

 a) Notice of payment deposit b) Notice of product receipt
 c) Shipment of product d) Transfer of payment',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  73,
  'Q73. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of HEMS?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,419.5,81.19],"text":"Q73.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of HEMS?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,527.06,118.21],"text":"a) It is a system that connects multiple home appliances through a network to visualize the"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,521.77,154.21],"text":"power and perform optimum control of power consumption.\nb) It is a system that converts the electricity produced by a solar power generation system"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,506.34,190.21],"text":"and a residential-use fuel cell for the electricity to be useable in households, etc.\nc) It is a system that recycles the useful parts of home appliances discarded by general"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,515.03,244.21],"text":"households and offices to reduce the amount of waste materials and promote the\neffective use of resources.\nd) It is an electric hot water supply system that generates a considerable quantity of heat"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,408.35,262.21],"text":"with a relatively small amount of energy by using a heat pump."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a system that connects multiple home appliances through a network to visualize the\n power and perform optimum control of power consumption."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a system that converts the electricity produced by a solar power generation system\n and a residential-use fuel cell for the electricity to be useable in households, etc."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a system that recycles the useful parts of home appliances discarded by general\n households and offices to reduce the amount of waste materials and promote the\n effective use of resources."},{"label":"d","text":"It is an electric hot water supply system that generates a considerable quantity of heat\n with a relatively small amount of energy by using a heat pump."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is a system that networks home appliances to visualize power use and optimally control power consumption. HEMS stands for Home Energy Management System. Choice b describes a power conditioner, choice c describes appliance recycling, and choice d describes a heat-pump water heater.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q73)',
  ARRAY[26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q73. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of HEMS?

 a) It is a system that connects multiple home appliances through a network to visualize the
 power and perform optimum control of power consumption.
 b) It is a system that converts the electricity produced by a solar power generation system
 and a residential-use fuel cell for the electricity to be useable in households, etc.
 c) It is a system that recycles the useful parts of home appliances discarded by general
 households and offices to reduce the amount of waste materials and promote the
 effective use of resources.
 d) It is an electric hot water supply system that generates a considerable quantity of heat
 with a relatively small amount of energy by using a heat pump.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[26]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  74,
  'Q74. When real-time systems are classified into hard real-time and soft real-time systems, which
 of the following is in the category of a hard real-time system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,301.74,533.14,315.19],"text":"Q74. When real-time systems are classified into hard real-time and soft real-time systems, which"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[85.74,319.85,387.9,333.13],"text":"of the following is in the category of a hard real-time system?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,358.91,431.87,408.19],"text":"a) Airbag control system\nb) Bank ATM system\nc) Seat reservation system\nd) Web delivery system"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Airbag control system"},{"label":"b","text":"Bank ATM system"},{"label":"c","text":"Seat reservation system"},{"label":"d","text":"Web delivery system"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the airbag control system. A hard real-time system must always meet its deadline because a late response causes a critical failure, and an airbag that deploys too late is useless. ATMs, seat reservations and web delivery are soft real-time: a delay reduces service quality but is not catastrophic.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q74)',
  ARRAY[26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q74. When real-time systems are classified into hard real-time and soft real-time systems, which
 of the following is in the category of a hard real-time system?

 a) Airbag control system b) Bank ATM system
 c) Seat reservation system d) Web delivery system',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[26]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  75,
  'Q75. Which of the following is an organizational structure of a corporation that is temporarily
 structured by specialists from each department to reach a specific goal over a limited period
 and operates independently from all other standing organizations?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,411.72,533.19,443.17],"text":"Q75. Which of the following is an organizational structure of a corporation that is temporarily"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,447.83,533.15,496.2],"text":"structured by specialists from each department to reach a specific goal over a limited period\nand operates independently from all other standing organizations?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,479.74,534.19],"text":"a) Company system organization\nb) Divisional system organization\nc) Functional organization\nd) Project organization"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Company system organization"},{"label":"b","text":"Divisional system organization"},{"label":"c","text":"Functional organization"},{"label":"d","text":"Project organization"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the project organization. It is assembled temporarily from specialists of various departments to achieve a specific goal within a limited period, and it is dissolved when the goal is reached. Functional, divisional and company-system organizations are permanent structures.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q75)',
  ARRAY[26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q75. Which of the following is an organizational structure of a corporation that is temporarily
 structured by specialists from each department to reach a specific goal over a limited period
 and operates independently from all other standing organizations?

 a) Company system organization b) Divisional system organization
 c) Functional organization d) Project organization',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[26]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  76,
  'Q76. There are several quality control tools that have been used primarily for manufacturing
 and inspection departments. Which of the following is a combined graph containing a bar
 graph that shows the numeric values of individual items in descending order, and a line graph
 that shows the cumulative total of the composition ratios of these numeric values?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,573.72,533.15,587.17],"text":"Q76. There are several quality control tools that have been used primarily for manufacturing"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[85.74,591.83,533.13,641.11],"text":"and inspection departments. Which of the following is a combined graph containing a bar\ngraph that shows the numeric values of individual items in descending order, and a line graph\nthat shows the cumulative total of the composition ratios of these numeric values?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,664.91,406.09,731.11],"text":"a) Control chart\nb) Histogram\nc) Pareto chart\nd) Scatter diagram"},{"type":"code","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 26 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Control chart"},{"label":"b","text":"Histogram"},{"label":"c","text":"Pareto chart"},{"label":"d","text":"Scatter diagram"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the Pareto chart. It combines bars sorted in descending order with a line showing the cumulative percentage, which highlights the few items causing most of the problems. A histogram shows a frequency distribution, a control chart tracks a process against control limits over time, and a scatter diagram shows the correlation between two variables.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q76)',
  ARRAY[26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q76. There are several quality control tools that have been used primarily for manufacturing
 and inspection departments. Which of the following is a combined graph containing a bar
 graph that shows the numeric values of individual items in descending order, and a line graph
 that shows the cumulative total of the composition ratios of these numeric values?

 a) Control chart b) Histogram
 c) Pareto chart d) Scatter diagram',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[26]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
