  'Q77. In a sampling inspection, which of the following can be used to ascertain the probability
 of acceptance of a lot with a certain defective ratio?

 a) Bathtub curve b) Gompertz curve
 c) Logistic curve d) OC curve',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[27]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-april',
  'A',
  78,
  'Q78. Which of following is an expression for calculating the cost of goods sold (or cost of sales)
 of a manufacturing company?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[70.5,178.91,533.14,209.17],"text":"Q78. Which of following is an expression for calculating the cost of goods sold (or cost of sales)"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,213.83,231.59,245.11],"text":"of a manufacturing company?"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,250.74,500.47,264.19],"text":"a) Material cost in current period + Labor cost in current period + Expense in current"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,268.91,529.1,300.19],"text":"period\nb) Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,304.91,529.11,336.19],"text":"− Product inventory at end of period\nc) Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,340.91,499.96,372.19],"text":"− Work in process inventory at end of period\nd) Work in process inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,376.91,389.13,407.11],"text":"current period − work in process inventory at end of period"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Material cost in current period + Labor cost in current period + Expense in current\n period"},{"label":"b","text":"Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period\n − Product inventory at end of period"},{"label":"c","text":"Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period\n − Work in process inventory at end of period"},{"label":"d","text":"Work in process inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in\n current period − work in process inventory at end of period"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is opening product inventory + product manufacturing cost for the period − closing product inventory. Cost of goods sold is the cost of finished products actually sold, so you add the products made this period to the finished goods already on hand and subtract those still unsold at the end. Choices c and d wrongly mix in work-in-process inventory, which belongs to the calculation of manufacturing cost.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021S, FE, Subject-A, Q78)',
  ARRAY[27]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q78. Which of following is an expression for calculating the cost of goods sold (or cost of sales)
 of a manufacturing company?

 a) Material cost in current period + Labor cost in current period + Expense in current
 period
 b) Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period
 − Product inventory at end of period
 c) Product inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in current period
 − Work in process inventory at end of period
 d) Work in process inventory at beginning of period + Product manufacturing cost in
 current period − work in process inventory at end of period',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[27]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
