  'Q79. The break-even point (BEP) is a level where total cost and total revenue are equal. The table below lists the fixed cost, variable cost per unit, price per unit, and BEP in units. Which of the following is a value of the price per unit?

Fixed cost ($) | 100,000
Variable cost per unit ($) | 2
Price per unit ($) |
BEP in units | 10,000',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q79. The break-even point (BEP) is a level where total cost and total revenue are equal. The table below lists the fixed cost, variable cost per unit, price per unit, and BEP in units. Which of the following is a value of the price per unit?\n\nFixed cost ($) | 100,000\nVariable cost per unit ($) | 2\nPrice per unit ($) |\nBEP in units | 10,000"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"4"},{"label":"b","text":"8"},{"label":"c","text":"12"},{"label":"d","text":"16"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is a price of 12 dollars. Break-even units = fixed cost ÷ (price − variable cost per unit), so 10,000 = 100,000 ÷ (price − 2), giving price − 2 = 10 and price = 12.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
