  'Blank A is 3: business transaction data must not be down 4 hours or more per year, so the 24-hour and 5-hour levels are ruled out and the smallest applicable availability value is "1 hour/year" = 3. Blanks B and C come from Table 6, which pairs spoofing with inadequate password management (B) and unauthorized access with inadequate access control (C). Blank D is 8: general supplier data can only be disclosed internally (confidentiality 2), and spoofing (2) × inadequate password management (2) gives 2 × 2 × 2 = 8. In Subquestion 2, server X''s integrity value is 2 (errors have only a slight impact), so the three risks are 2×3×3 = 18, 2×3×2 = 12 and 2×2×2 = 8; only 18 exceeds the acceptable integrity level of 15. That 18 comes from virus infection with no anti-virus software, so the right measure is installing antivirus software, which lowers the vulnerability value and brings the risk under 15.',
