  'Blank A is waiting 16, response 16, turnaround 24: under SJF, P2 is the longest job, so it waits until time 16 and finishes at 24 (16 + 8). With preemptive SJF (blank B), P5 runs 0-1, P6 preempts it and runs 1-5, then P8 (burst 5) beats the rest of P5 (7 left) and runs 5-10, and P5 finishes 10-17. So for P8 (blank C) waiting = response = 5 - 3 = 2 and turnaround = 10 - 3 = 7. With non-preemptive SJF (blank D), P5 runs to completion 0-8, then the shortest waiting jobs follow: P6 8-12, then P8 12-17. For P8 (blank E), waiting = response = 12 - 3 = 9 and turnaround = 17 - 3 = 14, which shows how non-preemption makes short jobs that arrive late wait longer.',
