  'Blank A is "directly connected" because CR''s own interface e0 (172.16.100.1/30) sits on 172.16.100.0/30. Blank B is 172.16.100.6: R1 reaches the Sales LAN 172.16.100.128/25 through its e0 link, whose neighbour on 172.16.100.4/30 is R2''s e1 address. Blank C is any/any: R2 needs a default route pointing to CR (172.16.100.1) so its hosts can reach the Internet. In Subquestion 2, the loopback ping works but the link light for PC3 is off on both the NIC and the switch, while the switch port works with other PCs, so the network cable is the most likely fault. In Subquestion 3, R2''s rule 1 allows the product department (10.1.1.128/25) to reach FS2 over SMB, which breaks the requirement that FS2 is for the sales department only. The fix is to remove that rule on R2 so the final deny-all rule blocks the traffic, while rule 2 still lets the administrator connect with SSH.',
