  'Blank A is In_use_ID: each Seat and each Ticket belongs to one bus trip, which is identified by an In_use record, so In_use_ID is the foreign key in both. Blank B is Driver_ID (nullable) and Route_ID: an In_use record links a trip to its route and later to its driver, and Driver_ID can be NULL until a driver accepts. In Figure 3, Driver assignment (blank C) reads the Driver store plus Bus, Bus_type and Route to choose a bus and route, and Driver confirmation (blank D) writes the accepted driver into In_use. During reservation, the Seat table is searched by In_use_ID (blank E) to find a vacant seat on the chosen trip. When a seat is free (blank F), the system inserts a new Ticket row and writes that Ticket_number into the Seat row, marking the seat as taken. No new Seat row is inserted, because all seats were registered as vacant two months before departure.',
