  '[{"label":"a","text":"Balanced tree"},{"label":"b","text":"Binary search tree"},{"label":"c","text":"Max heap"},{"label":"d","text":"Min heap"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The tree is a binary search tree. For every node, all keys in its left subtree are smaller and all keys in its right subtree are larger (for example 3 < 5 < 7, 8 < 9 < 10), so an in-order traversal yields 1 to 10 in sorted order. It is not a heap, because in a max heap the root would be the largest key and in a min heap the smallest, but the root here is 5.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
