  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q25. When the relationships between continent and country, and between country and city are shown in the class diagram below, which of the following is an appropriate combination of multiplicities that are to be inserted into blank A through blank D? Here, there are no cross continental countries. Each continent has at least one country, and each country has at least one city."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2021-october-a-q25-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A: 1..1, B: 1..*, C: 1..*, D: 1..1"},{"label":"b","text":"A: 1..1, B: 1..*, C: 1..1, D: 1..*"},{"label":"c","text":"A: 1..1, B: 0..*, C: 0..*, D: 1..1"},{"label":"d","text":"A: 1..1, B: 0..*, C: 1..1, D: 0..*"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct multiplicities are A = 1..1, B = 1..*, C = 1..1 and D = 1..*. Each country belongs to exactly one continent (A = 1..1) and each continent has at least one country (B = 1..*); likewise each city belongs to exactly one country (C = 1..1) and each country has at least one city (D = 1..*). Choices with 0..* would allow a continent or country with no countries or cities, which the conditions rule out.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
