(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. Which of the following is the most appropriate point to be checked in the audit of a
 system test?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.16,172.21],"text":"Q59.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate point to be checked in the audit of a\nsystem test?\n\na) The test cases were created comprehensively.\nb) The test plan was approved only by the responsible person on the user’s side.\nc) The test was performed in an environment where the actual business operations are"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,446.98,208.21],"text":"performed.\nd) The test was performed only by the person in charge on the user’s side."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The test cases were created comprehensively."},{"label":"b","text":"The test plan was approved only by the responsible person on the user’s side."},{"label":"c","text":"The test was performed in an environment where the actual business operations are\n performed."},{"label":"d","text":"The test was performed only by the person in charge on the user’s side."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'An auditor of a system test should check that the test cases were created comprehensively, so that requirements are adequately covered. Approval only by the user side, testing only by the user side, or testing in the live business environment are inappropriate, since system testing should involve the development side and be done in a separate test environment so as not to disrupt operations.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. Which of the following is the most appropriate point to be checked in the audit of a
 system test?

 a) The test cases were created comprehensively.
 b) The test plan was approved only by the responsible person on the user’s side.
 c) The test was performed in an environment where the actual business operations are
 performed.
 d) The test was performed only by the person in charge on the user’s side.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  60,
  'Q60. The director requested a system auditor to audit the operating status of an accounting system that was developed by the information systems department and is operated by the accounting department. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the system auditor for this audit?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q60. The director requested a system auditor to audit the operating status of an accounting system that was developed by the information systems department and is operated by the accounting department. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the system auditor for this audit?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The system auditor must be a certified public accountant because the accounting system must conform to the various standards of business accounting."},{"label":"b","text":"The system auditor must be a person who belongs to neither the information systems department nor the accounting department to guarantee independence."},{"label":"c","text":"The system auditor must report directly to the accounting department manager because the accounting system handles highly confidential information."},{"label":"d","text":"The system auditor must report directly to the information systems department manager to perform system audits efficiently."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The system auditor must belong to neither the information systems department nor the accounting department, to guarantee independence from the subject being audited. A system auditor does not need to be a certified public accountant, and audit results are reported to the requester (here the director), not to the managers of the audited departments.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q60)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q60. The director requested a system auditor to audit the operating status of an accounting
 system that was developed by the information systems department and is operated by the
 accounting department. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning
 the system auditor for this audit?

 a) The system auditor must be a certified public accountant because the accounting system
 must conform to the various standards of business accounting.
 b) The system auditor must be a person who belongs to neither the information systems
 department nor the accounting department to guarantee independence.
 c) The system auditor must report directly to the accounting department manager because
 the accounting system handles highly confidential information.
 d) The system auditor must report directly to the information systems department manager
 to perform system audits efficiently.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  61,
  'Q61. Which of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether
 the lifetime benefits of the proposed information system is greater than its lifetime costs?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,517.74,533.1,549.13],"text":"Q61.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether\nthe lifetime benefits of the proposed information system is greater than its lifetime costs?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,572.9,438.19,640.15],"text":"a) Economic feasibility\nb) Operational feasibility\nc) Scheduling feasibility\nd) Technical feasibility"},{"type":"code","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 23 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Economic feasibility"},{"label":"b","text":"Operational feasibility"},{"label":"c","text":"Scheduling feasibility"},{"label":"d","text":"Technical feasibility"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'This is economic feasibility, which asks whether the benefits of the system over its life exceed its lifetime costs, typically using cost-benefit analysis. Operational feasibility asks whether the system will be used and fit the organization, technical feasibility whether it can be built with available technology, and scheduling feasibility whether it can be done in time.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q61)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q61. Which of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether
