  66,
  'Q66. Which of the following is a technique that is used to identify and evaluate the internal
 and external factors that are helpful or harmful to the objectives of business organizations or
 projects?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,265.74,533.14,315.13],"text":"Q66.\nWhich of the following is a technique that is used to identify and evaluate the internal\nand external factors that are helpful or harmful to the objectives of business organizations or\nprojects?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,429.84,370.21],"text":"a) Five forces analysis\nb) PPM analysis\nc) SWOT analysis\nd) Value chain analysis"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Five forces analysis"},{"label":"b","text":"PPM analysis"},{"label":"c","text":"SWOT analysis"},{"label":"d","text":"Value chain analysis"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The technique is SWOT analysis, which identifies internal strengths and weaknesses and external opportunities and threats that help or harm an organization''s objectives. Five forces analysis looks only at industry competitive pressures, PPM classifies products by market growth and share, and value chain analysis examines the activities that create value.',
