  'A',
  69,
  'Q69. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation for product innovation in the
 management of technology?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,622.43,516.47,671.71],"text":"Q69.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate explanation for product innovation in the\nmanagement of technology?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,676.43,521.03,761.71],"text":"a) Acquiring business profits through achievements of the development of technology\nb) Developing new products or products that enable differentiation from other companies\nc) Making innovative reforms in business processes\nd) Strategically managing business with technology as the core"},{"type":"code","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 26 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Acquiring business profits through achievements of the development of technology"},{"label":"b","text":"Developing new products or products that enable differentiation from other companies"},{"label":"c","text":"Making innovative reforms in business processes"},{"label":"d","text":"Strategically managing business with technology as the core"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Product innovation means developing new products, or products that can be differentiated from those of other companies. Making innovative reforms in business processes is process innovation, and managing the business with technology as its core is the broader idea of management of technology itself.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q69)',
