),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  71,
  'Q71. Which of the following is a product that can take advantage of the cell production
 system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,158.93,533.18,207.13],"text":"Q71.\nWhich of the following is a product that can take advantage of the cell production\nsystem?"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,531.45,262.21],"text":"a) A product that needs to be produced in large quantities to improve productivity\nb) A product that requires a division of labor on the basis of standardization, simplification,"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,454.4,316.21],"text":"and specialization\nc) A product that requires a variety of types and needs flexible production\nd) A product whose specifications do not change over a long period of time"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A product that needs to be produced in large quantities to improve productivity"},{"label":"b","text":"A product that requires a division of labor on the basis of standardization, simplification,\n and specialization"},{"label":"c","text":"A product that requires a variety of types and needs flexible production"},{"label":"d","text":"A product whose specifications do not change over a long period of time"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Cell production suits products that come in many varieties and require flexible production. In a cell, one worker or a small team assembles a whole product, so it is easy to switch models in high-mix, low-volume production. Mass production with division of labor and long-unchanged specifications suits a line production system instead.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q71)',
  ARRAY[27]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q71. Which of the following is a product that can take advantage of the cell production
 system?

 a) A product that needs to be produced in large quantities to improve productivity
 b) A product that requires a division of labor on the basis of standardization, simplification,
 and specialization
 c) A product that requires a variety of types and needs flexible production
 d) A product whose specifications do not change over a long period of time',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[27]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  72,
  'Q72. Which of the following performs its processing according to steps (1) through (3)?

 (1) Based on the types, quantities, and the parts list of the product planned to be
 manufactured during a fixed period of time in the future, the required quantity of
 components is calculated.
 (2) The net order quantity of each component is calculated from the amount of inventory
 that can be allocated.
 (3) The ordering time of the components is determined while considering the
 manufacturing and procurement lead time.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,338.76,506.74,369.19],"text":"Q72.\nWhich of the following performs its processing according to steps (1) through (3)?"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[102.36,392.93,533.11,406.21],"text":"(1) Based on the types, quantities, and the parts list of the product planned to be"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[102.36,410.93,533.15,460.21],"text":"manufactured during a fixed period of time in the future, the required quantity of\ncomponents is calculated.\n(2) The net order quantity of each component is calculated from the amount of inventory"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[102.36,464.93,533.17,496.21],"text":"that can be allocated.\n(3) The ordering time of the components is determined while considering the"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,522.85,586.21],"text":"manufacturing and procurement lead time.\n\na) CAD (Computer Aided Design)\nb) CRP (Capacity Requirements Planning)\nc) JIT (Just In Time)\nd) MRP (Material Requirements Planning)"},{"type":"code","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 27 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"CAD (Computer Aided Design)"},{"label":"b","text":"CRP (Capacity Requirements Planning)"},{"label":"c","text":"JIT (Just In Time)"},{"label":"d","text":"MRP (Material Requirements Planning)"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The process is MRP (Material Requirements Planning). MRP explodes the production plan through the bill of materials to get gross requirements, subtracts allocatable inventory to get net requirements, and then offsets by lead time to determine when to order each component. CRP plans required machine and labour capacity, and JIT produces only what is needed when it is needed.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q72)',
  ARRAY[27]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q72. Which of the following performs its processing according to steps (1) through (3)?

 (1) Based on the types, quantities, and the parts list of the product planned to be
 manufactured during a fixed period of time in the future, the required quantity of
 components is calculated.
 (2) The net order quantity of each component is calculated from the amount of inventory
 that can be allocated.
 (3) The ordering time of the components is determined while considering the
 manufacturing and procurement lead time.

 a) CAD (Computer Aided Design) b) CRP (Capacity Requirements Planning)
 c) JIT (Just In Time) d) MRP (Material Requirements Planning)',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[27]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  73,
  'Q73. Which of the following is an appropriate description of Initial Coin Offering (ICO)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,514.12,99.13],"text":"Q73.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of Initial Coin Offering (ICO)?"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,529.35,118.21],"text":"a) A crowd-funding method in which backers contribute money toward an idea or a startup"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,522.7,154.21],"text":"and get rewards like physical products\nb) A fundraising method that is mainly used by a financially stable company which wants"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,503.49,190.21],"text":"to expand and develop to the public\nc) A popular fundraising method that is used primarily by a startup, normally through"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,491.35,226.21],"text":"utilizing cryptocurrency\nd) A process of offering shares of a private corporation to the public in a new stock"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,230.93,145.8,262.21],"text":"issuance"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A crowd-funding method in which backers contribute money toward an idea or a startup\n and get rewards like physical products"},{"label":"b","text":"A fundraising method that is mainly used by a financially stable company which wants\n to expand and develop to the public"},{"label":"c","text":"A popular fundraising method that is used primarily by a startup, normally through\n utilizing cryptocurrency"},{"label":"d","text":"A process of offering shares of a private corporation to the public in a new stock\n issuance"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'An ICO is a fundraising method used mainly by startups in which the company issues its own digital tokens and sells them to investors, typically in exchange for cryptocurrency. Rewards-based crowdfunding is choice a, and offering shares of a private company to the public in a new stock issuance is an IPO, the source of the name ICO.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q73)',
  ARRAY[28]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q73. Which of the following is an appropriate description of Initial Coin Offering (ICO)?

 a) A crowd-funding method in which backers contribute money toward an idea or a startup
 and get rewards like physical products
 b) A fundraising method that is mainly used by a financially stable company which wants
 to expand and develop to the public
 c) A popular fundraising method that is used primarily by a startup, normally through
 utilizing cryptocurrency
 d) A process of offering shares of a private corporation to the public in a new stock
 issuance',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[28]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  74,
  'Q74. Which of the following is an appropriate example of utilizing machine learning at a
 production site?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,533.12,315.13],"text":"Q74.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate example of utilizing machine learning at a\nproduction site?"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,526.42,352.21],"text":"a) Instead of programming the working method for the production robot in the factory, the"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,522.51,388.21],"text":"robot itself learns, thus improving the efficiency of work.\nb) The causes for the occurrence of defects in a factory are decomposed and arranged in a"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,526.28,424.21],"text":"tree shape so that analysts can statistically look for the cause and solution.\nc) The production equipment in a factory is connected through high-speed communication"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,490.79,460.21],"text":"so that the host computer can be controlled in real time.\nd) The productivity of employees in the factory improves each time the cumulative"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,464.93,466.65,496.21],"text":"production volume doubles, and the unit cost reduces at a fixed percentage."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Instead of programming the working method for the production robot in the factory, the\n robot itself learns, thus improving the efficiency of work."},{"label":"b","text":"The causes for the occurrence of defects in a factory are decomposed and arranged in a\n tree shape so that analysts can statistically look for the cause and solution."},{"label":"c","text":"The production equipment in a factory is connected through high-speed communication\n so that the host computer can be controlled in real time."},{"label":"d","text":"The productivity of employees in the factory improves each time the cumulative\n production volume doubles, and the unit cost reduces at a fixed percentage."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The example of machine learning is a production robot that learns its working method by itself instead of being explicitly programmed, improving its efficiency. Decomposing defect causes into a tree is a logic tree or fault tree analysis, real-time control over high-speed links is just networking, and falling unit cost as cumulative volume doubles is the experience (learning) curve, not machine learning.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q74)',
  ARRAY[28]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q74. Which of the following is an appropriate example of utilizing machine learning at a
 production site?

 a) Instead of programming the working method for the production robot in the factory, the
 robot itself learns, thus improving the efficiency of work.
 b) The causes for the occurrence of defects in a factory are decomposed and arranged in a
 tree shape so that analysts can statistically look for the cause and solution.
 c) The production equipment in a factory is connected through high-speed communication
 so that the host computer can be controlled in real time.
 d) The productivity of employees in the factory improves each time the cumulative
 production volume doubles, and the unit cost reduces at a fixed percentage.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[28]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  75,
  'Q75. Which of the following is a management organization that creates a cross-functional team
 between project and functional organizations to flexibly respond to changes in the business
 environment?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,518.76,533.16,586.21],"text":"Q75.\nWhich of the following is a management organization that creates a cross-functional team\nbetween project and functional organizations to flexibly respond to changes in the business\nenvironment?"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,466.12,622.21],"text":"a) Divisional organization\nb) Line and staff organization\nc) Matrix organization\nd) Project organization"},{"type":"code","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 28 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Divisional organization"},{"label":"b","text":"Line and staff organization"},{"label":"c","text":"Matrix organization"},{"label":"d","text":"Project organization"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is the matrix organization, in which members belong to a functional department and to a project team at the same time, creating cross-functional teams that can respond flexibly to change. Its drawback is that members report to two managers. A project organization is a temporary team separate from functional departments, and a divisional organization is split by product or region.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q75)',
  ARRAY[28]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q75. Which of the following is a management organization that creates a cross-functional team
 between project and functional organizations to flexibly respond to changes in the business
 environment?

 a) Divisional organization b) Line and staff organization
 c) Matrix organization d) Project organization',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[28]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  76,
  'Q76. Which of the following is an example of Green IT?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,356.51,81.19],"text":"Q76.\nWhich of the following is an example of Green IT?"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,340.85,118.21],"text":"a)\nDevelopment of a powerful in-house data center"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,324.17,136.21],"text":"b)\nDevelopment of efficient in-house software"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,346.48,154.21],"text":"c)\nUsing a desktop PC instead of a thin client laptop"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,384.04,190.21],"text":"d)\nUsing web conferencing instead of travelling to meetings"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Development of a powerful in-house data center"},{"label":"b","text":"Development of efficient in-house software"},{"label":"c","text":"Using a desktop PC instead of a thin client laptop"},{"label":"d","text":"Using web conferencing instead of travelling to meetings"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Using web conferencing instead of travelling to meetings is an example of Green IT, because it uses IT to reduce energy consumption and CO₂ emissions from transport. Green IT covers both making IT itself energy-efficient and using IT to reduce environmental impact elsewhere; building a powerful data center or using a desktop instead of a thin client would increase energy use.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q76)',
  ARRAY[29]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q76. Which of the following is an example of Green IT?

 a) Development of a powerful in-house data center
 b) Development of efficient in-house software
 c) Using a desktop PC instead of a thin client laptop
 d) Using web conferencing instead of travelling to meetings',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[29]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  77,
  'Q77. Which of the following is a description of a CIO?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[65.22,194.76,348.4,225.19],"text":"Q77.\nWhich of the following is a description of a CIO?"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,250.91,521.63,264.19],"text":"a) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies in the area of"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,268.91,504.62,300.19],"text":"finances, such as fund-raising or financial reporting\nb) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies regarding"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,304.91,523.23,336.19],"text":"information management and information systems\nc) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of technological strategies"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,340.91,530.01,372.19],"text":"and R&D plans of the company\nd) The chief executive that governs the planning of business strategies and the execution of"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,376.91,145.75,408.19],"text":"business"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies in the area of\n finances, such as fund-raising or financial reporting"},{"label":"b","text":"The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies regarding\n information management and information systems"},{"label":"c","text":"The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of technological strategies\n and R&D plans of the company"},{"label":"d","text":"The chief executive that governs the planning of business strategies and the execution of\n business"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A CIO (Chief Information Officer) governs the planning and execution of strategies for information management and information systems. The finance executive is the CFO, the executive for technology strategy and R&D is the CTO, and the one responsible for business strategy and execution is the CEO or COO.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q77)',
  ARRAY[29]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q77. Which of the following is a description of a CIO?

 a) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies in the area of
 finances, such as fund-raising or financial reporting
 b) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of strategies regarding
 information management and information systems
 c) The chief executive that governs the planning and execution of technological strategies
 and R&D plans of the company
 d) The chief executive that governs the planning of business strategies and the execution of
 business',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[29]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  78,
  'Q78. Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning creation and operation
 of a Business Continuity Plan (BCP)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[65.22,411.72,533.12,461.11],"text":"Q78.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate description concerning creation and operation\nof a Business Continuity Plan (BCP)?"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,466.91,499.71,498.19],"text":"a) In addition to natural disasters, device failure in information systems and malware"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,488.05,534.19],"text":"infections are also included in the scope of examination.\nb) The planning contents are important matters related to the business strategy and"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[84.12,538.91,529.0,588.19],"text":"therefore, only senior managers are notified.\nc) The planning contents are restricted to those activities performed by the company.\nd) The recovery of business processes dependent on IT is prioritized according to technical"},{"type":"text","page":29,"bbox":[102.12,592.91,205.45,606.19],"text":"easiness of recovery."},{"type":"code","page":29,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,808.39],"text":"– 29 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"In addition to natural disasters, device failure in information systems and malware\n infections are also included in the scope of examination."},{"label":"b","text":"The planning contents are important matters related to the business strategy and\n therefore, only senior managers are notified."},{"label":"c","text":"The planning contents are restricted to those activities performed by the company."},{"label":"d","text":"The recovery of business processes dependent on IT is prioritized according to technical\n easiness of recovery."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct statement is that a BCP should cover not only natural disasters but also failures of information system devices and malware infections, since any of these can halt business. A BCP must be shared with the staff who will carry it out, should consider business partners and suppliers as well as the company itself, and should prioritize recovery by business importance rather than technical ease.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q78)',
  ARRAY[29]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q78. Which of the following is the appropriate description concerning creation and operation
 of a Business Continuity Plan (BCP)?

 a) In addition to natural disasters, device failure in information systems and malware
 infections are also included in the scope of examination.
 b) The planning contents are important matters related to the business strategy and
 therefore, only senior managers are notified.
 c) The planning contents are restricted to those activities performed by the company.
 d) The recovery of business processes dependent on IT is prioritized according to technical
 easiness of recovery.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[29]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2021-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2021-october',
  'A',
  79,
  'Q79. Company A has two media plans. One plan is for a series of 30-second radio advertisements (ads) and the other is for 60-second TV ads. Exposure is rated in points. The company is considering an exposure of at least 60 points in the city and at most 40 points outside the city. The table below shows the cost and exposure of both TV and radio ads. Which of the following is the set of expressions that can determine the number of media ads to minimize the total cost?

 | Cost | In the city exposure (points) | Outside the city exposure (points)
TV ads | 2000 | 8 | 6
Radio ads | 800 | 10 | 3',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q79. Company A has two media plans. One plan is for a series of 30-second radio advertisements (ads) and the other is for 60-second TV ads. Exposure is rated in points. The company is considering an exposure of at least 60 points in the city and at most 40 points outside the city. The table below shows the cost and exposure of both TV and radio ads. Which of the following is the set of expressions that can determine the number of media ads to minimize the total cost?\n\n | Cost | In the city exposure (points) | Outside the city exposure (points)\nTV ads | 2000 | 8 | 6\nRadio ads | 800 | 10 | 3"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Conditions 8x + 6y ≤ 60, 10x + 3y ≤ 40, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0\nObjective function 2000x + 800y → minimize"},{"label":"b","text":"Conditions 8x + 6y ≥ 60, 10x + 3y ≤ 40, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0\nObjective function 2000x + 800y → minimize"},{"label":"c","text":"Conditions 8x + 10y ≤ 60, 6x + 3y ≤ 40, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0\nObjective function 2000x + 800y → minimize"},{"label":"d","text":"Conditions 8x + 10y ≥ 60, 6x + 3y ≤ 40, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0\nObjective function 2000x + 800y → minimize"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct formulation is 8x + 10y ≥ 60, 6x + 3y ≤ 40, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0, minimizing 2000x + 800y, where x is the number of TV ads and y the number of radio ads. In the city TV gives 8 points and radio 10, and at least 60 points are required; outside the city TV gives 6 and radio 3, with at most 40 points allowed. Choices a and b wrongly pair the TV coefficients 8 and 6 in the same constraint.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2021A, FE, Subject-A, Q79)',
  ARRAY[30]::int[],
  'manual_review',
