  'Placing an order always requires the customer to state when they will collect the food, so Place order includes Set pickup time (A). Confirming the order is a mandatory part of both Place order and Cancel order, so both connect to Confirm order with an include arrow pointing from the base use case to Confirm order (B); extend would mean optional behaviour. When cooking starts the restaurant sends a "Cannot cancel order" message, so the use case linking Cancel order and Manage kitchen is No cancellation (C). The Place order input must identify each chosen item, so it needs the Food ID (D) alongside the menu ID. In the basic flow the customer enters the number of dishes for each food item, which the application checks (E), and at submission the customer fills in the pickup time, which is checked against the rules such as same-day pickup (F).',
