  '[{"label":"a","text":"A̅ ∙ (A + B̅)"},{"label":"b","text":"A̅ ∙ (A̅ + B̅)"},{"label":"c","text":"B ∙ (A + B̅)"},{"label":"d","text":"B̅ ∙ (A̅ + B̅)"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is NOT A AND (A OR NOT B). NOR is NOT(A + B), which by De Morgan''s law equals NOT A AND NOT B. Expanding choice a gives (NOT A AND A) + (NOT A AND NOT B); the first term is always 0, so the expression reduces to NOT A AND NOT B, exactly NOR. The other choices simplify to different functions, for example choice b reduces to just NOT A.',
