  'The correct choice is a continuous, bell-shaped distribution that is symmetric about its mean, which is the definition of the normal (Gaussian) distribution. The bathtub curve describes failure rates over a product''s life, the distribution counting events in a fixed interval is the Poisson distribution, and equal probability for all outcomes is the discrete uniform distribution.',
