  'The correct answer is 9 exchanges. Each bubble sort swap fixes exactly one inverted pair, so the number of swaps equals the number of pairs that are out of order. Counting them: 9 is greater than 2, 3, 0 (3 pairs); 2 is greater than 0 (1); 13 is greater than 3, 0 (2); 21 is greater than 3, 0 (2); and 3 is greater than 0 (1), for a total of 9.',
