  '[{"label":"a","text":"DHCP"},{"label":"b","text":"NAPT (IP masquerade)"},{"label":"c","text":"Packet filtering"},{"label":"d","text":"PPPoE"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is NAPT (IP masquerade). NAPT translates both the private IP address and the port number of each PC to the single global IP address with a distinct port, so many PCs can share one global address at the same time. DHCP only hands out addresses on the LAN, and PPPoE is the protocol used to establish the connection to the provider.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
