  '[{"label":"a","text":"192.168.128.63"},{"label":"b","text":"192.168.128.127"},{"label":"c","text":"192.168.128.252"},{"label":"d","text":"192.168.128.255"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct answer is 192.168.128.63. A /26 prefix leaves 6 host bits, so each network has 2^6 = 64 addresses, and this one covers 192.168.128.0 to 192.168.128.63. The broadcast address has all host bits set to 1, which is the last address, .63.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
