  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Botnet"},{"label":"b","text":"DMZ"},{"label":"c","text":"Honey pot"},{"label":"d","text":"SIEM"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is a honeypot, a decoy system or network deliberately left vulnerable to attract attackers or malware so their behavior can be observed and analyzed. A botnet is a network of infected computers, a DMZ is a buffer network segment, and SIEM collects and correlates security logs.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
