  50,
  'Q50. Which of the following is a software development model that repeats the development processes from requirements analysis to implementation?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q50. Which of the following is a software development model that repeats the development processes from requirements analysis to implementation?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Prototyping model"},{"label":"b","text":"Relational model"},{"label":"c","text":"Spiral model"},{"label":"d","text":"Waterfall model"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the spiral model, which develops the system by repeating cycles of requirements analysis, design, implementation and evaluation, expanding the system and managing risk in each round. The waterfall model goes through the phases only once in sequence, and the relational model is a database model, not a development model.',
