(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  61,
  'Q61. Which of the following is an explanation of enterprise architecture (EA)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,462.04,297.19],"text":"Q61.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of enterprise architecture (EA)?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,495.73,334.21],"text":"a) It is a technique to abstract and express business processes with the four (4) basic"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,524.71,370.21],"text":"elements of data flow, process, file, and data sources and absorption.\nb) It is a technique to analyze each business operation and information system through the"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,517.14,424.21],"text":"four (4) systems of business, data, application, and technology, and reexamine it from\nthe viewpoint of total optimization.\nc) It is a technique to analyze or design a system by using schematic diagrams such as a"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,527.98,478.21],"text":"class diagram, and it is developed by integrating and standardizing various methods that\nsupport an object-oriented design.\nd) It is a technique to clarify the data structure and the relationship between data items by"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[74.46,482.93,434.74,514.21],"text":"expressing the conceptual data model with entities and relationships."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a technique to abstract and express business processes with the four (4) basic\n elements of data flow, process, file, and data sources and absorption."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a technique to analyze each business operation and information system through the\n four (4) systems of business, data, application, and technology, and reexamine it from\n the viewpoint of total optimization."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a technique to analyze or design a system by using schematic diagrams such as a\n class diagram, and it is developed by integrating and standardizing various methods that\n support an object-oriented design."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a technique to clarify the data structure and the relationship between data items by\n expressing the conceptual data model with entities and relationships."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is analyzing business operations and information systems through four architectures, business, data, application and technology, and reexamining them for total optimization of the organization. The other choices describe DFDs (data flow diagrams), UML, and E-R diagrams.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q61)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q61. Which of the following is an explanation of enterprise architecture (EA)?

 a) It is a technique to abstract and express business processes with the four (4) basic
 elements of data flow, process, file, and data sources and absorption.
 b) It is a technique to analyze each business operation and information system through the
 four (4) systems of business, data, application, and technology, and reexamine it from
 the viewpoint of total optimization.
 c) It is a technique to analyze or design a system by using schematic diagrams such as a
 class diagram, and it is developed by integrating and standardizing various methods that
 support an object-oriented design.
 d) It is a technique to clarify the data structure and the relationship between data items by
 expressing the conceptual data model with entities and relationships.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  62,
  'Q62. When a workflow system is used for business improvement, which of the following is
 an appropriate effect that can be expected?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,518.76,523.56,604.21],"text":"Q62.\nWhen a workflow system is used for business improvement, which of the following is\nan appropriate effect that can be expected?\n\na) Improved processing speed for office procedures, from document submission to"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,526.24,640.21],"text":"approval\nb) The provision of a standard protocol used for data exchange between a company and its"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,522.3,676.21],"text":"customers\nc) The provision of services such as a discount according to the amount of the customer’s"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,680.93,432.43,747.13],"text":"purchase\nd) Warehouse automation of shipping and receipt of stocked products"},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Improved processing speed for office procedures, from document submission to\n approval"},{"label":"b","text":"The provision of a standard protocol used for data exchange between a company and its\n customers"},{"label":"c","text":"The provision of services such as a discount according to the amount of the customer’s\n purchase"},{"label":"d","text":"Warehouse automation of shipping and receipt of stocked products"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is improved processing speed for office procedures from document submission to approval. A workflow system routes electronic documents automatically along a defined approval path, which reduces delays and lets people track progress. Standard data exchange protocols are EDI, purchase-based discounts are a loyalty program, and warehouse automation is a logistics system.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q62)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q62. When a workflow system is used for business improvement, which of the following is
 an appropriate effect that can be expected?

 a) Improved processing speed for office procedures, from document submission to
 approval
 b) The provision of a standard protocol used for data exchange between a company and its
 customers
 c) The provision of services such as a discount according to the amount of the customer’s
 purchase
 d) Warehouse automation of shipping and receipt of stocked products',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  63,
  'Q63. In computerization investment planning, which of the following is an explanation of
 ROI as an evaluation index for investment value?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,525.38,136.21],"text":"Q63.\nIn computerization investment planning, which of the following is an explanation of\nROI as an evaluation index for investment value?\n\na) ROI is a measure that indicates market competitiveness in the event that a project is not"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,527.73,172.21],"text":"implemented.\nb) ROI is a measure that is calculated by dividing the profit generated through factors such"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,530.69,208.21],"text":"as sales increase and cost reduction by the investment amount.\nc) ROI is a measure that is calculated by subtracting the current value of cash outflow from"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,515.09,244.21],"text":"the current value of cash inflow.\nd) ROI is a measure that is obtained by comparing some parameters, such as the sales to"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,485.32,280.21],"text":"investment ratio and the amount of investment per employee, with that of other\ncompanies."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"ROI is a measure that indicates market competitiveness in the event that a project is not\n implemented."},{"label":"b","text":"ROI is a measure that is calculated by dividing the profit generated through factors such\n as sales increase and cost reduction by the investment amount."},{"label":"c","text":"ROI is a measure that is calculated by subtracting the current value of cash outflow from\n the current value of cash inflow."},{"label":"d","text":"ROI is a measure that is obtained by comparing some parameters, such as the sales to\n investment ratio and the amount of investment per employee, with that of other\n companies."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is that ROI is the profit generated by the investment, for example from increased sales or reduced costs, divided by the investment amount. A higher ROI means more return per unit of money invested. Subtracting the present value of outflows from the present value of inflows is NPV (net present value).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q63)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q63. In computerization investment planning, which of the following is an explanation of
 ROI as an evaluation index for investment value?

 a) ROI is a measure that indicates market competitiveness in the event that a project is not
 implemented.
 b) ROI is a measure that is calculated by dividing the profit generated through factors such
 as sales increase and cost reduction by the investment amount.
 c) ROI is a measure that is calculated by subtracting the current value of cash outflow from
 the current value of cash inflow.
 d) ROI is a measure that is obtained by comparing some parameters, such as the sales to
 investment ratio and the amount of investment per employee, with that of other
 companies.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  64,
  'Q64. Which of the following is a description that corresponds to CSR procurement?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,487.12,333.19],"text":"Q64.\nWhich of the following is a description that corresponds to CSR procurement?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,523.02,388.21],"text":"a) Choosing the product with the lowest price to minimize costs\nb) Having multiple suppliers to avoid situations in which procurement is impossible, such"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,526.95,424.21],"text":"as after a disaster\nc) Indicating procurement standards that consider the environment, human rights, etc., and"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,428.93,505.68,478.21],"text":"requesting that suppliers comply with these\nd) Using EDI to purchase goods in order to perform prompt and accurate procurement"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Choosing the product with the lowest price to minimize costs"},{"label":"b","text":"Having multiple suppliers to avoid situations in which procurement is impossible, such\n as after a disaster"},{"label":"c","text":"Indicating procurement standards that consider the environment, human rights, etc., and\n requesting that suppliers comply with these"},{"label":"d","text":"Using EDI to purchase goods in order to perform prompt and accurate procurement"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is setting procurement standards that consider the environment, human rights and similar issues, and asking suppliers to comply with them. CSR procurement extends corporate social responsibility to the whole supply chain rather than judging suppliers only on price and delivery. Multiple suppliers for disasters relates to business continuity, and EDI is about efficiency.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q64)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q64. Which of the following is a description that corresponds to CSR procurement?

 a) Choosing the product with the lowest price to minimize costs
 b) Having multiple suppliers to avoid situations in which procurement is impossible, such
 as after a disaster
 c) Indicating procurement standards that consider the environment, human rights, etc., and
 requesting that suppliers comply with these
 d) Using EDI to purchase goods in order to perform prompt and accurate procurement',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  65,
  'Q65. Which of the following is an explanation of the core competence?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,482.76,426.78,513.19],"text":"Q65.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the core competence?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,536.76,510.7,550.21],"text":"a) Corporate activities that comply with laws, various regulations, and social norms for"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,491.32,586.21],"text":"managing business\nb) The business domain decided from the viewpoint of the market, technology, and"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,506.12,622.21],"text":"products (or services)\nc) The overall business and system optimization methods for achieving the purpose of"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,626.93,510.83,658.21],"text":"organizational activities\nd) The predominant abilities in the company’s business area, which competitors cannot"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[102.12,662.93,138.4,676.21],"text":"imitate"},{"type":"code","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 23 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Corporate activities that comply with laws, various regulations, and social norms for\n managing business"},{"label":"b","text":"The business domain decided from the viewpoint of the market, technology, and\n products (or services)"},{"label":"c","text":"The overall business and system optimization methods for achieving the purpose of\n organizational activities"},{"label":"d","text":"The predominant abilities in the company’s business area, which competitors cannot\n imitate"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the company''s predominant abilities in its business area that competitors cannot imitate. Core competence is the unique set of skills or technologies that gives a company its competitive advantage and can be leveraged across products. Complying with laws is compliance, and defining a business domain by market, technology and product is domain definition.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q65)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q65. Which of the following is an explanation of the core competence?

 a) Corporate activities that comply with laws, various regulations, and social norms for
 managing business
 b) The business domain decided from the viewpoint of the market, technology, and
 products (or services)
 c) The overall business and system optimization methods for achieving the purpose of
 organizational activities
 d) The predominant abilities in the company’s business area, which competitors cannot
 imitate',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  66,
  'Q66. Companies are classified on the basis of their competitive position in the market.
 There are typically four types: leader, challenger, follower, and nicher. Which of the
 following is the most appropriate characteristic of a leader’s strategy?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,504.45,136.21],"text":"Q66.\nCompanies are classified on the basis of their competitive position in the market.\nThere are typically four types: leader, challenger, follower, and nicher. Which of the\nfollowing is the most appropriate characteristic of a leader’s strategy?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,140.76,527.64,154.21],"text":"a) Applying a differentiation strategy to all aspects of products, services, advertising, price"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,530.72,208.21],"text":"and distribution channels or indirectly attacking the competitor’s weaknesses or the gaps\nin the competitor’s market coverage\nb) Capturing a specific market that high-ranking companies do not target and concentrating"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,524.01,244.21],"text":"management resources in order to secure and maintain predominance in the market\nc) Determining the challenger company’s real ability in the market and prioritize securing"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,532.71,280.21],"text":"stable profits over expanding the market share by doing as the leader company does\nd) Proposing a new product and its usage method to consumers in order to increase the total"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,381.41,316.21],"text":"demand while maintaining or expanding the market share"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Applying a differentiation strategy to all aspects of products, services, advertising, price\n and distribution channels or indirectly attacking the competitor’s weaknesses or the gaps\n in the competitor’s market coverage"},{"label":"b","text":"Capturing a specific market that high-ranking companies do not target and concentrating\n management resources in order to secure and maintain predominance in the market"},{"label":"c","text":"Determining the challenger company’s real ability in the market and prioritize securing\n stable profits over expanding the market share by doing as the leader company does"},{"label":"d","text":"Proposing a new product and its usage method to consumers in order to increase the total\n demand while maintaining or expanding the market share"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is proposing new products and uses to grow total market demand while maintaining or expanding market share. As the largest player, a leader benefits most when the whole market grows, so it pursues full-line, market-expanding strategies. Differentiation and attacking the leader''s weak points fit a challenger, focusing on a niche fits a nicher, and imitating the leader fits a follower.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q66)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q66. Companies are classified on the basis of their competitive position in the market.
 There are typically four types: leader, challenger, follower, and nicher. Which of the
 following is the most appropriate characteristic of a leader’s strategy?

 a) Applying a differentiation strategy to all aspects of products, services, advertising, price
 and distribution channels or indirectly attacking the competitor’s weaknesses or the gaps
 in the competitor’s market coverage
 b) Capturing a specific market that high-ranking companies do not target and concentrating
 management resources in order to secure and maintain predominance in the market
 c) Determining the challenger company’s real ability in the market and prioritize securing
 stable profits over expanding the market share by doing as the leader company does
 d) Proposing a new product and its usage method to consumers in order to increase the total
 demand while maintaining or expanding the market share',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  67,
  'Q67. Which of the following is an explanation of the introduction stage of the product life
 cycle?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,320.93,516.02,388.21],"text":"Q67.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the introduction stage of the product life\ncycle?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,503.67,406.21],"text":"a) It is the stage at which companies sell products to early adopters. Companies adopt"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,528.45,442.21],"text":"strategies to enhance product recognition.\nb) It is the stage at which growth in demand slows. Companies try to maintain their market"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,504.05,478.21],"text":"share and secure profits through various means, such as improving product quality.\nc) It is the stage at which sales and profit gradually decline. Companies refrain from"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,476.46,514.21],"text":"making additional investments and consider withdrawing from the market.\nd) It is the stage at which sales increase rapidly. The market becomes active and"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,518.93,389.93,532.21],"text":"competition intensifies because of new market participants."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is the stage at which companies sell products to early adopters. Companies adopt\n strategies to enhance product recognition."},{"label":"b","text":"It is the stage at which growth in demand slows. Companies try to maintain their market\n share and secure profits through various means, such as improving product quality."},{"label":"c","text":"It is the stage at which sales and profit gradually decline. Companies refrain from\n making additional investments and consider withdrawing from the market."},{"label":"d","text":"It is the stage at which sales increase rapidly. The market becomes active and\n competition intensifies because of new market participants."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is the stage where products are sold to early adopters and companies work to raise product recognition. In the introduction stage the market is small, so promotion focuses on awareness. Rapid sales growth with new competitors describes the growth stage, slowing demand describes maturity, and declining sales describe the decline stage.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q67)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q67. Which of the following is an explanation of the introduction stage of the product life
 cycle?

 a) It is the stage at which companies sell products to early adopters. Companies adopt
 strategies to enhance product recognition.
 b) It is the stage at which growth in demand slows. Companies try to maintain their market
 share and secure profits through various means, such as improving product quality.
 c) It is the stage at which sales and profit gradually decline. Companies refrain from
 making additional investments and consider withdrawing from the market.
 d) It is the stage at which sales increase rapidly. The market becomes active and
 competition intensifies because of new market participants.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  68,
  'Q68. Which of the following is the purpose of CRM?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,340.19,604.21],"text":"Q68.\nWhich of the following is the purpose of CRM?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,478.08,658.21],"text":"a) Acquisition of customer loyalty and maximization of customer lifetime value\nb) Ascertainment of the sales information for each product at the time of sales\nc) Determination of the order quantity and order timing of material requirred for"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,662.93,419.52,730.21],"text":"manufacturing\nd) Reduction in loss of sales opportunities due to inventory shortage"},{"type":"code","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 24 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Acquisition of customer loyalty and maximization of customer lifetime value"},{"label":"b","text":"Ascertainment of the sales information for each product at the time of sales"},{"label":"c","text":"Determination of the order quantity and order timing of material requirred for\n manufacturing"},{"label":"d","text":"Reduction in loss of sales opportunities due to inventory shortage"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is acquiring customer loyalty and maximizing customer lifetime value. CRM manages long-term relationships with customers by sharing customer information across the company. Capturing sales data at the time of sale is POS, determining material order quantities is MRP, and preventing stock-outs is inventory management or SCM.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q68)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q68. Which of the following is the purpose of CRM?

 a) Acquisition of customer loyalty and maximization of customer lifetime value
 b) Ascertainment of the sales information for each product at the time of sales
 c) Determination of the order quantity and order timing of material requirred for
 manufacturing
 d) Reduction in loss of sales opportunities due to inventory shortage',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-april',
  'A',
  69,
  'Q69. Which of the following is the appropriate description of process innovation?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q69. Which of the following is the appropriate description of process innovation?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Development of an innovative new product on the basis of an original and high technology"},{"label":"b","text":"Development of innovative manufacturing procedures that improve the quality of a product"},{"label":"c","text":"Outsourcing manufacturing to another company that has a semiconductor manufacturing process"},{"label":"d","text":"Wide adoption after passing the competition, resulting in the establishment of a de facto standard"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is developing innovative manufacturing procedures that improve product quality. Process innovation changes how products are made or delivered, for example the production method. Developing an innovative new product itself is product innovation, and outsourcing or becoming a de facto standard are not process innovation.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022S, FE, Subject-A, Q69)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q69. Which of the following is the appropriate description of process innovation?

 a) Development of an innovative new product on the basis of an original and high
 technology
 b) Development of innovative manufacturing procedures that improve the quality of a
 product
 c) Outsourcing manufacturing to another company that has a semiconductor manufacturing
 process
 b) Wide adoption after passing the competition, resulting in the establishment of a de facto
 standard',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
