  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q77. Products A, B, C, and D are to be introduced to the market. The table below shows the expected profit for each product with three (3) sales forecasts (High, Medium, and Low) that are estimated to occur in accordance with the probability in the table. Which of the following is the product that is expected to make the highest profit according to the expected value principle?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2022-april-a-q77-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A"},{"label":"b","text":"B"},{"label":"c","text":"C"},{"label":"d","text":"D"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is product B. Expected value is the sum of profit × probability: A = 75,000 + 4,000 − 2,000 = 77,000; B = 78,000 + 9,000 − 2,000 = 85,000; C = 75,000 + 12,000 − 4,000 = 83,000; D = 70,000 + 2,000 − 5,000 = 67,000. B has the highest expected profit.',
