  'Risk value = asset value × threat × vulnerability. Blank A (R5, integrity) = I 2 × threat T5 2 × vulnerability V5 2 = 8, and blank B (R6, availability) = A 1 × T6 1 × V6 1 = 1. For Subquestion 2, reason (ii) is about information leaking out of the company, which is confidentiality (C), and reason (iii) is about inconsistent program versions, which is integrity (I). For Subquestion 3, a risk needs extra measures when any C, I or A value exceeds 12; only R1 (C = 3×3×2 = 18) and R4 (C = 3×3×2 = 18) do, so 2 threats need additional measures, while R5''s C value of 12 is still accepted. Subquestion 4 has no answer in the key used here.',
