  'Blank A: every registered customer has at least one account, so the Account end of the Customer relationship is many and mandatory (one or more). In SQL1 the Employee table is self-joined, so blank B is Employee (alias S for the superior) and blank C is S.EmpID = E.SuperiorEmpID, matching each employee''s SuperiorEmpID to the superior''s EmpID; the LEFT OUTER JOIN keeps Bob, whose superior is NULL, and ISNULL shows (none). Blank D: as written, EXISTS selects accounts opened before 2020 that DO have a 2020-2021 transaction, so it outputs 50001 and 50003. Blank E: changing EXISTS to NOT EXISTS returns the unused pre-2020 accounts 50002 and 50004; EXISTS returns each account at most once, so the duplicate-row choices are wrong.',
