  'Blank A: the smaller of the two advertised MSS values is used, so the segment size is 1240 bytes (RWIN values are buffer sizes, not segment sizes). Blank B: the server''s 22-byte data started at SeqNo 11, so its next sequence number, used by the FIN, is 11 + 22 = 33. Blank C: the client first acknowledges the FIN with an ACK whose AckNo is 33 + 1 = 34, and blank D: it then sends its own FIN. Blank E: the client''s sequence number is still 21 because after the SYN (20) it sent no data and pure ACKs consume no sequence number; the server''s final ACK of 22 confirms this. For Subquestion 2, SYN flooding fills the queue of half-open connections, so it blocks new clients from connecting rather than dropping already established connections.',
