  'Blank A: all tested bits are 1 exactly when (Data & Mask) = Mask, and blank B: all tested bits are 0 when (Data & Mask) = ''00000000''B. With only one mask bit, the tested bits cannot be mixed, so BitTest never returns 1 (C); when Data equals Mask, Data & Mask = Mask, so it always returns 2 (D). Blank E: for an all-zero Mask both conditions are true, so only change proposal (2), which tests condition B first and returns 0, works; proposals (1) and (3) would return 2. For the rightmost-bit test, (Work | ''00000001''B) = Work (F) and (Work & ''11111110''B) ≠ Work (G) both hold only when bit 0 is 1. Blank H: with Data = 0 the WHILE body never runs, so the minimum time is 1 + 1 + 2 + 2 = 6. Blank I: 01100110 − 1 = 01100101, and ANDing gives 01100100, clearing the lowest 1 bit.',
