(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  1,
  'Q1. For an 8-bit binary integer, which of the following sets the least significant bit to 1 while
 leaving the other bits unchanged?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,533.17,81.25],"text":"Q1.  For an 8-bit binary integer, which of the following sets the least significant bit to 1 while"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[85.74,85.85,249.76,99.13],"text":"leaving the other bits unchanged?"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,104.93,346.41,208.21],"text":"a) Perform bitwise AND operation with 00000001.\nb) Perform bitwise NAND operation with 11111110.\nc) Perform bitwise OR operation with 00000001.\nd) Perform bitwise XOR operation with 00000001."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Perform bitwise AND operation with 00000001."},{"label":"b","text":"Perform bitwise NAND operation with 11111110."},{"label":"c","text":"Perform bitwise OR operation with 00000001."},{"label":"d","text":"Perform bitwise XOR operation with 00000001."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is a bitwise OR with 00000001. OR with 0 leaves a bit unchanged and OR with 1 always gives 1, so only the least significant bit is forced to 1. AND with 00000001 would clear the other seven bits, and XOR with 00000001 would flip the last bit (turning an existing 1 into 0) rather than set it.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q1)',
  ARRAY[3]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q1. For an 8-bit binary integer, which of the following sets the least significant bit to 1 while
 leaving the other bits unchanged?

 a) Perform bitwise AND operation with 00000001.
 b) Perform bitwise NAND operation with 11111110.
 c) Perform bitwise OR operation with 00000001.
 d) Perform bitwise XOR operation with 00000001.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[3]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  2,
  'Q2. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the loss of significance?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,480.62,261.13],"text":"Q2. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the loss of significance?"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[83.22,265.68,519.44,279.13],"text":"a) It occurs when the result of an operation exceeds the maximum handle limit and raises"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[83.22,283.85,533.11,315.13],"text":"an exception.\nb) It occurs when two nearly equal floating-point numbers are subtracted to produce a result"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[83.22,319.85,517.11,351.13],"text":"of unacceptably reduced significant digits.\nc) It refers to a rounding error that occurs when the part smaller than the least significant"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[83.22,355.85,521.75,387.13],"text":"digit of the result is rounded off, up, or down in floating-point operations.\nd) It refers to the case when two floating-point numbers are added, but the less significant"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,391.85,308.31,423.13],"text":"digits of either one do not affect the result."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It occurs when the result of an operation exceeds the maximum handle limit and raises\n an exception."},{"label":"b","text":"It occurs when two nearly equal floating-point numbers are subtracted to produce a result\n of unacceptably reduced significant digits."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to a rounding error that occurs when the part smaller than the least significant\n digit of the result is rounded off, up, or down in floating-point operations."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the case when two floating-point numbers are added, but the less significant\n digits of either one do not affect the result."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Loss of significance (cancellation) happens when two nearly equal floating-point numbers are subtracted: the matching leading digits cancel out and the result keeps only a few meaningful significant digits. Choice a describes overflow, c describes rounding error, and d describes information loss (absorption) when adding numbers of very different magnitudes.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q2)',
  ARRAY[3]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q2. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the loss of significance?

 a) It occurs when the result of an operation exceeds the maximum handle limit and raises
 an exception.
 b) It occurs when two nearly equal floating-point numbers are subtracted to produce a result
 of unacceptably reduced significant digits.
 c) It refers to a rounding error that occurs when the part smaller than the least significant
 digit of the result is rounded off, up, or down in floating-point operations.
