(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  7,
  'Q7. Five (5) characters, A, C, K, S, and T, are input in this order. When using stacks, what is
 the minimum number of stacks required to rearrange the characters and output S, T, A, C, and
 K, in this order? Here, when a pop operation is performed for any stack, the popped character
 always becomes an output. Also, characters cannot be moved between stacks.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,533.11,279.25],"text":"Q7.  Five (5) characters, A, C, K, S, and T, are input in this order. When using stacks, what is"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[85.74,283.85,533.12,333.13],"text":"the minimum number of stacks required to rearrange the characters and output S, T, A, C, and\nK, in this order? Here, when a pop operation is performed for any stack, the popped character\nalways becomes an output. Also, characters cannot be moved between stacks."},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[86.22,356.93,435.72,370.21],"text":"a)\n1\nb) 2\nc) 3\nd) 4"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1"},{"label":"b","text":"2"},{"label":"c","text":"3"},{"label":"d","text":"4"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Three stacks are needed. A, C and K arrive before S, so they must all be held, but they must leave in the order A, C, K; since a stack is last-in first-out, none of them can be stacked on top of another that must leave earlier, so each needs its own stack. S and T can then be pushed and popped immediately, followed by popping A, C and K in turn.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
