(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  11,
  'Q11. There is a 32-bit microprocessor with 32-bit external data bus, driven by 64 MHz input
 clock, and the processor takes 8 input clock cycles to complete 1 bus cycle. What is the
 theoretical maximum data transfer rate in megabytes per second (MB/s) for the external data
 bus of the processor?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":5,"bbox":[65.22,176.93,533.13,280.15],"text":"Q11.\nThere is a 32-bit microprocessor with 32-bit external data bus, driven by 64 MHz input\nclock, and the processor takes 8 input clock cycles to complete 1 bus cycle. What is the\ntheoretical maximum data transfer rate in megabytes per second (MB/s) for the external data\nbus of the processor?"},{"type":"text","page":5,"bbox":[65.22,284.93,476.1,316.21],"text":"a) 3\nb) 32\nc) 256\nd) 320"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"3"},{"label":"b","text":"32"},{"label":"c","text":"256"},{"label":"d","text":"320"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum rate is 32 MB/s. Since one bus cycle takes 8 clock cycles, the bus completes 64 MHz ÷ 8 = 8 million bus cycles per second. Each bus cycle transfers 32 bits = 4 bytes, so the rate is 8 million × 4 bytes = 32 MB/s.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
