  '2022-october',
  'A',
  17,
  'Q17. On a computer with virtual memory, the number of blocks in real memory is three (3). One of the two (2) algorithms of FIFO and LFU (least frequently used) is used for selecting the page to be removed from real memory. When five (5) pages are referenced in the page-reference sequence shown below as a string, which of the following is an appropriate combination of the number of page fault operations for each algorithm? Here, the three (3) blocks in the real memory are initially empty.

[Page reference string]
1, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5, 2, 3, 4, 5',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q17. On a computer with virtual memory, the number of blocks in real memory is three (3). One of the two (2) algorithms of FIFO and LFU (least frequently used) is used for selecting the page to be removed from real memory. When five (5) pages are referenced in the page-reference sequence shown below as a string, which of the following is an appropriate combination of the number of page fault operations for each algorithm? Here, the three (3) blocks in the real memory are initially empty.\n\n[Page reference string]\n1, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5, 2, 3, 4, 5"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"FIFO: 3, LFU: 2"},{"label":"b","text":"FIFO: 4, LFU: 6"},{"label":"c","text":"FIFO: 5, LFU: 3"},{"label":"d","text":"FIFO: 6, LFU: 9"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'FIFO causes 6 page faults and LFU causes 9. With FIFO, the faults are on 1, 3, 2, 4 (removes 1), 5 (removes 3) and 3 (removes 2), while 1, 2, 4 and 5 later hit, giving 6. With LFU, page 1 is referenced twice early on and stays in memory, so the other two blocks keep evicting pages that each have a count of 1. Every reference after the fourth one therefore faults: 3 initial faults + 6 = 9.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q17)',
