  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2022-october-a-q20-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2022-october-a-q20-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2022-october-a-q20-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2022-october-a-q20-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct diagram is the one where A and B feed an XOR gate for S and an AND gate for C. The sum column (0,1,1,0) is the XOR truth table, because it is 1 only when the inputs differ. The carry column (0,0,0,1) is the AND truth table, because it is 1 only when both inputs are 1. The other diagrams use NOR or AND for the sum or put the gates on the wrong outputs.',
