  '2022-october',
  'A',
  23,
  'Q23. For a given decimal data, the check digit is calculated with the method below and is
 appended to the original data. When the given data is 7394, what is the result? Here, the
 weight is 1234 and the base number is 11.

 (1) For each digit of the data, calculate the product with the digit at the same radix of the
 weight and calculate the sum of these products.
 (2) Calculate the remainder after the division of the sum by the base number.
 (3) Subtract the remainder from the base number and let the last digit of the result be the
 check digit.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,140.76,533.13,207.13],"text":"Q23.\nFor a given decimal data, the check digit is calculated with the method below and is\nappended to the original data. When the given data is 7394, what is the result? Here, the\nweight is 1234 and the base number is 11."},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[87.6,229.85,516.17,243.13],"text":"(1) For each digit of the data, calculate the product with the digit at the same radix of the"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[87.6,247.85,514.87,297.13],"text":"weight and calculate the sum of these products.\n(2) Calculate the remainder after the division of the sum by the base number.\n(3) Subtract the remainder from the base number and let the last digit of the result be the"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[105.6,301.85,164.59,315.13],"text":"check digit."},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,320.93,488.1,369.13],"text":"a) 73940\nb) 73941\nc) 73944\nd) 73947"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"73940"},{"label":"b","text":"73941"},{"label":"c","text":"73944"},{"label":"d","text":"73947"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The result is 73940. The weighted sum is 7×1 + 3×2 + 9×3 + 4×4 = 7 + 6 + 27 + 16 = 56, and 56 mod 11 = 1. Then 11 − 1 = 10, whose last digit 0 becomes the check digit, so the data becomes 73940.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q23)',
  ARRAY[9]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q23. For a given decimal data, the check digit is calculated with the method below and is
 appended to the original data. When the given data is 7394, what is the result? Here, the
 weight is 1234 and the base number is 11.

 (1) For each digit of the data, calculate the product with the digit at the same radix of the
