),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  24,
  'Q24. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of augmented reality (AR)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,391.8,529.78,405.25],"text":"Q24.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate explanation of augmented reality (AR)?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,518.01,442.21],"text":"a) By appealing to the five senses through equipment, such as a head-mounted display, a"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,511.7,478.21],"text":"person can experience locations or worlds that do not exist as if they were real.\nb) By constructing a 3D virtual space that is natural to humans and changing the virtual"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,529.26,532.21],"text":"space in accordance with a person’s movement, he or she can feel as if he or she were in\nthat place.\nc) By seamlessly interweaving computer-generated information with the physical world,"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,522.22,568.21],"text":"the viewer can perceive it as an immersive aspect of the real environment.\nd) By viewing a video recorded in the past, the viewer can feel as if he or she were in that"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,572.76,223.78,604.15],"text":"era and at that location."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"By appealing to the five senses through equipment, such as a head-mounted display, a\n person can experience locations or worlds that do not exist as if they were real."},{"label":"b","text":"By constructing a 3D virtual space that is natural to humans and changing the virtual\n space in accordance with a person’s movement, he or she can feel as if he or she were in\n that place."},{"label":"c","text":"By seamlessly interweaving computer-generated information with the physical world,\n the viewer can perceive it as an immersive aspect of the real environment."},{"label":"d","text":"By viewing a video recorded in the past, the viewer can feel as if he or she were in that\n era and at that location."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Augmented reality overlays computer-generated information, such as images, text or 3D objects, on the real physical world so that the user sees them as part of the actual environment. Choices a and b describe virtual reality, which replaces the real world with a simulated one, and d describes simply watching recorded video.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q24)',
  ARRAY[9]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q24. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of augmented reality (AR)?

 a) By appealing to the five senses through equipment, such as a head-mounted display, a
 person can experience locations or worlds that do not exist as if they were real.
 b) By constructing a 3D virtual space that is natural to humans and changing the virtual
 space in accordance with a person’s movement, he or she can feel as if he or she were in
 that place.
 c) By seamlessly interweaving computer-generated information with the physical world,
 the viewer can perceive it as an immersive aspect of the real environment.
 d) By viewing a video recorded in the past, the viewer can feel as if he or she were in that
 era and at that location.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[9]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
