),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  25,
  'Q25. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the mapping between a relational
 model and relational database as its implementation?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,608.76,533.16,657.13],"text":"Q25.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of the mapping between a relational\nmodel and relational database as its implementation?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,662.93,427.41,748.21],"text":"a) A domain is mapped to a character type or a character string type.\nb) A relation is mapped to a table.\nc) Attributes and columns are ordered from left to right.\nd) Neither tuples nor rows have duplicates."},{"type":"code","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,312.66,807.79],"text":"– 9 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A domain is mapped to a character type or a character string type."},{"label":"b","text":"A relation is mapped to a table."},{"label":"c","text":"Attributes and columns are ordered from left to right."},{"label":"d","text":"Neither tuples nor rows have duplicates."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'In the implementation, a relation of the relational model is represented as a table, a tuple as a row and an attribute as a column. A domain is not restricted to character types, attributes have no left-to-right order in the theory, and SQL tables, unlike relations, can contain duplicate rows, so the other choices are wrong.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q25)',
  ARRAY[9]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q25. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the mapping between a relational
 model and relational database as its implementation?

 a) A domain is mapped to a character type or a character string type.
 b) A relation is mapped to a table.
 c) Attributes and columns are ordered from left to right.
 d) Neither tuples nor rows have duplicates.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[9]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  26,
  'Q26. In a relational database, which of the following is an appropriate purpose for defining a
 foreign key?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,533.15,99.13],"text":"Q26.\nIn a relational database, which of the following is an appropriate purpose for defining a\nforeign key?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,507.95,136.21],"text":"a) To prevent fragmentation in the record storage area due to the repeated deletion and"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,532.95,172.21],"text":"insertion of records\nb) To provide a constraint to maintain referential consistency between the records of related"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,522.3,208.21],"text":"tables\nc) To restore as many records as possible when they are damaged by failure, based on the"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,533.72,279.25],"text":"mutual relationship between tables\nd) To speed up the searching and updating of related tables by storing them closer together"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To prevent fragmentation in the record storage area due to the repeated deletion and\n insertion of records"},{"label":"b","text":"To provide a constraint to maintain referential consistency between the records of related\n tables"},{"label":"c","text":"To restore as many records as possible when they are damaged by failure, based on the\n mutual relationship between tables"},{"label":"d","text":"To speed up the searching and updating of related tables by storing them closer together"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A foreign key enforces referential integrity: each value in the referencing column must match an existing primary key value in the referenced table (or be NULL). This prevents orphan records, for example an order that points to a customer who does not exist. It is not a storage, recovery or performance mechanism.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q26)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q26. In a relational database, which of the following is an appropriate purpose for defining a
 foreign key?

 a) To prevent fragmentation in the record storage area due to the repeated deletion and
 insertion of records
 b) To provide a constraint to maintain referential consistency between the records of related
 tables
 c) To restore as many records as possible when they are damaged by failure, based on the
 mutual relationship between tables
 d) To speed up the searching and updating of related tables by storing them closer together',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[10]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  27,
  'Q27. In the process of table implementation, which of the following is an appropriate SQL
 statement that removes a column in an existing table?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,533.1,316.21],"text":"Q27.\nIn the process of table implementation, which of the following is an appropriate SQL\nstatement that removes a column in an existing table?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[86.52,337.68,258.21,351.83],"text":"a)\nALTER TABLE table_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[323.28,337.68,492.27,351.83],"text":"b)\nALTER TABLE table_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[86.52,359.33,515.08,405.83],"text":"DROP COLUMN column_name\n\nc)\nUPDATE TABLE table_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[103.5,359.33,292.97,387.25],"text":"DELETE COLUMN column_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[323.28,391.68,498.39,405.83],"text":"d)\nUPDATE TABLE table_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[103.5,413.33,292.97,441.25],"text":"DELETE COLUMN column_name"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[337.38,413.33,514.18,441.25],"text":"DROP COLUMN column_name"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"ALTER TABLE table_name\n  DELETE COLUMN column_name"},{"label":"b","text":"ALTER TABLE table_name\n  DROP COLUMN column_name"},{"label":"c","text":"UPDATE TABLE table_name\n  DELETE COLUMN column_name"},{"label":"d","text":"UPDATE TABLE table_name\n  DROP COLUMN column_name"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct statement is ALTER TABLE table_name DROP COLUMN column_name. ALTER TABLE changes the definition (structure) of an existing table, and DROP is the keyword for removing a column. UPDATE modifies data values in rows, not the table structure, and DELETE COLUMN is not valid SQL.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q27)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q27. In the process of table implementation, which of the following is an appropriate SQL
 statement that removes a column in an existing table?

 a) ALTER TABLE table_name b) ALTER TABLE table_name

 DELETE COLUMN column_name DROP COLUMN column_name

 c) UPDATE TABLE table_name d) UPDATE TABLE table_name

 DELETE COLUMN column_name DROP COLUMN column_name',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[10]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  28,
  'Q28 Which of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of
 a relational database?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,463.8,533.08,495.13],"text":"Q28\nWhich of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of\na relational database?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[91.98,518.93,533.12,532.21],"text":"a) To enable efficient access to the storage location of data so that the search speed can be"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[91.98,536.93,533.06,586.21],"text":"improved\nb) To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column\nc) To match the value of the column of the foreign key with the value of the primary key"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[91.98,590.93,527.38,622.21],"text":"of another table\nd) To save disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved on several disks"},{"type":"code","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 10 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To enable efficient access to the storage location of data so that the search speed can be\n improved"},{"label":"b","text":"To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column"},{"label":"c","text":"To match the value of the column of the foreign key with the value of the primary key\n of another table"},{"label":"d","text":"To save disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved on several disks"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'An index lets the DBMS locate the rows that match a search condition without scanning the whole table, which speeds up searches. Uniqueness is guaranteed by a UNIQUE or primary key constraint, matching a foreign key to a primary key is referential integrity, and spreading a table over several disks is partitioning.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q28)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q28 Which of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of
 a relational database?

 a) To enable efficient access to the storage location of data so that the search speed can be
 improved
 b) To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column
 c) To match the value of the column of the foreign key with the value of the primary key
 of another table
 d) To save disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved on several disks',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[10]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
