(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. In an IP network consisting of four (4) hosts, two (2) L2 switches, and a router shown below, a packet is transmitted from PC01 to PC03. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of the source and destination addresses of this packet when it leaves Switch1?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q30. In an IP network consisting of four (4) hosts, two (2) L2 switches, and a router shown below, a packet is transmitted from PC01 to PC03. Which of the following is an appropriate combination of the source and destination addresses of this packet when it leaves Switch1?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2022-october-a-q30-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Destination MAC: cc:cc:cc:cc:cc:cc, Source MAC: aa:aa:aa:aa:aa:aa, Destination IP: 192.168.1.11, Source IP: 192.168.1.31"},{"label":"b","text":"Destination MAC: cc:cc:cc:cc:cc:cc, Source MAC: aa:aa:aa:aa:aa:aa, Destination IP: 192.168.2.31, Source IP: 192.168.1.31"},{"label":"c","text":"Destination MAC: ee:ee:ee:ee:ee:ee, Source MAC: aa:aa:aa:aa:aa:aa, Destination IP: 192.168.1.11, Source IP: 192.168.1.31"},{"label":"d","text":"Destination MAC: ee:ee:ee:ee:ee:ee, Source MAC: aa:aa:aa:aa:aa:aa, Destination IP: 192.168.2.31, Source IP: 192.168.1.31"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'PC03 (192.168.2.31) is on another subnet, so PC01 sends the frame to its default gateway. When the packet leaves Switch1, the destination MAC is the router port 01 address cc:cc:cc:cc:cc:cc and the source MAC is PC01''s aa:aa:aa:aa:aa:aa. The IP addresses stay end to end: destination 192.168.2.31 and source 192.168.1.31. The router''s IP 192.168.1.11 is never the destination IP, and PC03''s MAC only appears after the router forwards the packet.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q30)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
