(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  33,
  'Q33. Which of the following protocol supports the congestion control feature?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,646.86,460.72,678.25],"text":"Q33.\nWhich of the following protocol supports the congestion control feature?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,701.93,474.93,715.21],"text":"a) ARP\nb) ICMP\nc) TCP\nd) UDP"},{"type":"code","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 12 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"ARP"},{"label":"b","text":"ICMP"},{"label":"c","text":"TCP"},{"label":"d","text":"UDP"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'TCP has congestion control. It adjusts its congestion window, for example with slow start and congestion avoidance, based on packet loss and acknowledgements, so it does not overload the network. UDP is connectionless and has no flow or congestion control, ICMP carries control messages, and ARP resolves addresses.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
