  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[13]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  36,
  'Q36. When a system with a database is being developed, a security requirement states that the
 data must be encrypted with a key before being saved to the database, and the same key is
 required for decryption when the data is being read. Which of the following is an appropriate
 algorithm that can be used to satisfy the security requirement?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,266.76,533.13,351.13],"text":"Q36.\nWhen a system with a database is being developed, a security requirement states that the\ndata must be encrypted with a key before being saved to the database, and the same key is\nrequired for decryption when the data is being read. Which of the following is an appropriate\nalgorithm that can be used to satisfy the security requirement?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,374.93,504.16,406.21],"text":"a) AES\nb) Diffie-Hellman\nc) RSA\nd) SHA-256"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"AES"},{"label":"b","text":"Diffie-Hellman"},{"label":"c","text":"RSA"},{"label":"d","text":"SHA-256"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The requirement describes symmetric (common-key) encryption, where the same key encrypts and decrypts, and AES is a symmetric block cipher. RSA is public-key encryption with different keys for encryption and decryption, Diffie-Hellman is a key-exchange method, and SHA-256 is a one-way hash that cannot be decrypted.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q36)',
