(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  41,
  'Q41. An attacker calls a corporate help desk, masquerading as an employee who has forgotten
 his password. The help desk staff resets the password to the company default “password1. ”
 The attacker then uses this password to access the company network and information on the
 server. What is this type of attack called?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,158.76,533.21,244.21],"text":"Q41.\nAn attacker calls a corporate help desk, masquerading as an employee who has forgotten\nhis password. The help desk staff resets the password to the company default “password1. ”\nThe attacker then uses this password to access the company network and information on the\nserver. What is this type of attack called?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,448.13,298.21],"text":"a) Buffer overflow attack\nb) Denial-of-Service attack\nc) Shoulder surfing\nd) Social engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Buffer overflow attack"},{"label":"b","text":"Denial-of-Service attack"},{"label":"c","text":"Shoulder surfing"},{"label":"d","text":"Social engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'This is social engineering: the attacker uses deception over the phone, pretending to be an employee, to manipulate help desk staff into resetting the password. No technical vulnerability is exploited. Shoulder surfing means watching someone enter a password, and buffer overflow and DoS are technical attacks.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q41)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q41. An attacker calls a corporate help desk, masquerading as an employee who has forgotten
 his password. The help desk staff resets the password to the company default “password1. ”
 The attacker then uses this password to access the company network and information on the
 server. What is this type of attack called?

 a) Buffer overflow attack b) Denial-of-Service attack
 c) Shoulder surfing d) Social engineering',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  42,
  'Q42. When a biometric authentication system is introduced, which of the following is the most
 appropriate point to be taken into account?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,337.8,533.11,369.13],"text":"Q42.\nWhen a biometric authentication system is introduced, which of the following is the most\nappropriate point to be taken into account?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,503.36,406.21],"text":"a) Adjusting the device by considering both the probability of incorrectly rejecting an"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,523.59,442.21],"text":"authorized user and that of incorrectly accepting an unauthorized user\nb) Preventing the decrease in the probability of incorrectly rejecting an authorized user by"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,502.48,478.21],"text":"using a product that frequently updates the malware definition file\nc) Requesting an entrusted third party to issue a digital certificate for the person to be"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,523.46,514.21],"text":"authenticated\nd) Setting the appropriate amount of knowledge for authentication to balance the amounts"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,530.29,568.21],"text":"of knowledge that cannot be easily guessed and that can be memorized by a person to be\nauthenticated"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Adjusting the device by considering both the probability of incorrectly rejecting an\n authorized user and that of incorrectly accepting an unauthorized user"},{"label":"b","text":"Preventing the decrease in the probability of incorrectly rejecting an authorized user by\n using a product that frequently updates the malware definition file"},{"label":"c","text":"Requesting an entrusted third party to issue a digital certificate for the person to be\n authenticated"},{"label":"d","text":"Setting the appropriate amount of knowledge for authentication to balance the amounts\n of knowledge that cannot be easily guessed and that can be memorized by a person to be\n authenticated"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Biometric systems must balance the false rejection rate (FRR, rejecting a genuine user) against the false acceptance rate (FAR, accepting an impostor). Tightening the threshold lowers FAR but raises FRR, so the device must be tuned with both in mind. Malware definition files, digital certificates and memorized knowledge are unrelated to biometrics.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'access-control'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q42)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q42. When a biometric authentication system is introduced, which of the following is the most
 appropriate point to be taken into account?

 a) Adjusting the device by considering both the probability of incorrectly rejecting an
 authorized user and that of incorrectly accepting an unauthorized user
 b) Preventing the decrease in the probability of incorrectly rejecting an authorized user by
 using a product that frequently updates the malware definition file
 c) Requesting an entrusted third party to issue a digital certificate for the person to be
 authenticated
 d) Setting the appropriate amount of knowledge for authentication to balance the amounts
 of knowledge that cannot be easily guessed and that can be memorized by a person to be
 authenticated',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  43,
  'Q43. Which of the following is the purpose of using a message authentication code?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,589.8,488.2,603.25],"text":"Q43.\nWhich of the following is the purpose of using a message authentication code?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,608.93,358.71,730.15],"text":"a) To check the encryption method of a message\nb) To check the overview of a message\nc) To confirm that there is no falsification of a message\nd) To secure the confidentiality of a message"},{"type":"code","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 14 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To check the encryption method of a message"},{"label":"b","text":"To check the overview of a message"},{"label":"c","text":"To confirm that there is no falsification of a message"},{"label":"d","text":"To secure the confidentiality of a message"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A MAC (message authentication code) is calculated from the message and a shared secret key. The receiver recomputes it, and a match shows that the message was not falsified (integrity) and came from a holder of the key. A MAC does not encrypt the message, so it does not provide confidentiality.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q43)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q43. Which of the following is the purpose of using a message authentication code?

 a) To check the encryption method of a message
 b) To check the overview of a message
 c) To confirm that there is no falsification of a message
 d) To secure the confidentiality of a message',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  44,
  'Q44. Which of the following is an explanation of WAF?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,353.27,81.25],"text":"Q44.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of WAF?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,513.81,118.21],"text":"a) It centrally stores and manages operation logs from various systems to quickly detect"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,530.4,154.21],"text":"and analyze an event that can be a security threat.\nb) It is a standard of encryption methods for wireless LAN, certified by the Wi-Fi Alliance,"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,513.82,190.21],"text":"and supports AES encryption.\nc) It is equipped with firewall functions and has antivirus, intrusion detection, and other"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,525.66,244.21],"text":"functions that work together to manage multiple security functions in an integrated\nmanner.\nd) It monitors the accesses to a website, and when it detects a pattern that is likely from an"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,265.05,280.15],"text":"attacker, it blocks those accesses."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It centrally stores and manages operation logs from various systems to quickly detect\n and analyze an event that can be a security threat."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a standard of encryption methods for wireless LAN, certified by the Wi-Fi Alliance,\n and supports AES encryption."},{"label":"c","text":"It is equipped with firewall functions and has antivirus, intrusion detection, and other\n functions that work together to manage multiple security functions in an integrated\n manner."},{"label":"d","text":"It monitors the accesses to a website, and when it detects a pattern that is likely from an\n attacker, it blocks those accesses."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A WAF (Web Application Firewall) inspects HTTP traffic to a web application and blocks requests that match attack patterns such as SQL injection or cross-site scripting. Choice a describes SIEM, b describes WPA2/WPA3, and c describes UTM (unified threat management).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q44)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q44. Which of the following is an explanation of WAF?

 a) It centrally stores and manages operation logs from various systems to quickly detect
 and analyze an event that can be a security threat.
 b) It is a standard of encryption methods for wireless LAN, certified by the Wi-Fi Alliance,
 and supports AES encryption.
 c) It is equipped with firewall functions and has antivirus, intrusion detection, and other
 functions that work together to manage multiple security functions in an integrated
 manner.
 d) It monitors the accesses to a website, and when it detects a pattern that is likely from an
 attacker, it blocks those accesses.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  45,
  'Q45. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a UML use case diagram?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,502.69,315.25],"text":"Q45.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of a UML use case diagram?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,532.68,406.21],"text":"a) It shows the behavior during the object’s life cycle using finite state transitions.\nb) It shows the exchange of messages among objects and objects’ lifelines in a time series.\nc) It shows the flow from one activity to another activity in a system or business process.\nd) It shows the scenarios for how actors, i.e., external users or machines, interact with a"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[102.12,410.93,141.51,424.21],"text":"system."}]'::jsonb,
