 for debugging a program?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.15,118.21],"text":"Q48.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate description of a stack trace that is used\nfor debugging a program?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,368.59,208.21],"text":"a) A trace of call stack methods/functions/subroutines\nb) Stacking/gathering the traces left by other programs\nc) The traces left in memory from a stack data structure\nd) Tracing stack data structure that is used in the program"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A trace of call stack methods/functions/subroutines"},{"label":"b","text":"Stacking/gathering the traces left by other programs"},{"label":"c","text":"The traces left in memory from a stack data structure"},{"label":"d","text":"Tracing stack data structure that is used in the program"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A stack trace lists the chain of active method, function or subroutine calls on the call stack at a given moment, typically when an exception occurs. It shows where the error happened and how execution reached that point. It has nothing to do with a stack data structure that the program itself uses.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
