  52,
  'Q52. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the Responsibility Assignment
 Matrix that is used for project human resource management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.1,100.21],"text":"Q52.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of the Responsibility Assignment\nMatrix that is used for project human resource management?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,451.05,190.21],"text":"a) Allocating work packages to those who are responsible for project work\nb) Defining the limits of the project sponsor’s responsibilities\nc) Defining the terms of reference of the project\nd) Monitoring the current engagement level of stakeholders"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Allocating work packages to those who are responsible for project work"},{"label":"b","text":"Defining the limits of the project sponsor’s responsibilities"},{"label":"c","text":"Defining the terms of reference of the project"},{"label":"d","text":"Monitoring the current engagement level of stakeholders"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A Responsibility Assignment Matrix, such as a RACI chart, maps work packages or activities from the WBS to the project team members and shows who is responsible, accountable, consulted or informed for each. It does not define the sponsor''s limits or the terms of reference, and it is not used to monitor stakeholder engagement.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
