(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  53,
  'Q53. Which of the following is an appropriate purpose for using a WBS (work breakdown
 structure) in a software development project?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,230.76,533.1,298.21],"text":"Q53.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate purpose for using a WBS (work breakdown\nstructure) in a software development project?\n\na) To clarify the time sequence of activities and understand the critical path that should be"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,513.66,334.21],"text":"intensively managed\nb) To decompose a development task into smaller sub-tasks with a manageable size and"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,521.04,370.21],"text":"organize them into a hierarchical structure\nc) To optimize the total cost when there is a trade-off relationship between the number of"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,527.66,406.21],"text":"days and the costs required for development\nd) To show the schedule of activities by using bars and clarify the start dates and end dates"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,384.05,442.21],"text":"of the activities as well as the progress at the current point"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To clarify the time sequence of activities and understand the critical path that should be\n intensively managed"},{"label":"b","text":"To decompose a development task into smaller sub-tasks with a manageable size and\n organize them into a hierarchical structure"},{"label":"c","text":"To optimize the total cost when there is a trade-off relationship between the number of\n days and the costs required for development"},{"label":"d","text":"To show the schedule of activities by using bars and clarify the start dates and end dates\n of the activities as well as the progress at the current point"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A WBS decomposes the project deliverables and work hierarchically into smaller, manageable units called work packages, which can be estimated, assigned and controlled. Critical path analysis is done with a network diagram, cost-time trade-offs with crashing, and bar schedules with a Gantt chart.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q53)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q53. Which of the following is an appropriate purpose for using a WBS (work breakdown
 structure) in a software development project?

 a) To clarify the time sequence of activities and understand the critical path that should be
 intensively managed
 b) To decompose a development task into smaller sub-tasks with a manageable size and
 organize them into a hierarchical structure
 c) To optimize the total cost when there is a trade-off relationship between the number of
 days and the costs required for development
 d) To show the schedule of activities by using bars and clarify the start dates and end dates
 of the activities as well as the progress at the current point',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  54,
  'Q54. Which of the following is an appropriate description for group decision-making
 techniques used in the estimation process of an activity duration?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,464.76,533.18,514.21],"text":"Q54.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description for group decision-making\ntechniques used in the estimation process of an activity duration?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,489.04,532.21],"text":"a) The estimates created using these techniques may include contingency reserves,"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,523.39,586.21],"text":"sometimes referred to as time reserves or buffers, in the project schedule to account for\nschedule uncertainty.\nb) These are team-based approaches, such as brainstorming, the Delphi, or nominal group"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,508.47,640.21],"text":"techniques, which are useful for engaged team members to improve their estimation\naccuracy and commit to the estimates.\nc) These techniques use statistical relationships between historical data and project"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,532.13,676.21],"text":"parameters to calculate an estimate for project cost, budget, or duration.\nd) Using these techniques, a group of experts, guided by historical information, can provide"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,680.93,522.8,748.21],"text":"duration estimate information or recommended maximum activity durations from prior\nsimilar projects."},{"type":"code","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 17 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The estimates created using these techniques may include contingency reserves,\n sometimes referred to as time reserves or buffers, in the project schedule to account for\n schedule uncertainty."},{"label":"b","text":"These are team-based approaches, such as brainstorming, the Delphi, or nominal group\n techniques, which are useful for engaged team members to improve their estimation\n accuracy and commit to the estimates."},{"label":"c","text":"These techniques use statistical relationships between historical data and project\n parameters to calculate an estimate for project cost, budget, or duration."},{"label":"d","text":"Using these techniques, a group of experts, guided by historical information, can provide\n duration estimate information or recommended maximum activity durations from prior\n similar projects."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Group decision-making techniques, such as brainstorming, Delphi and nominal group technique, involve the team members in producing the estimates, which improves estimation accuracy and commitment to the estimates. Choice a describes reserve analysis, c parametric estimating, and d expert judgment or analogous estimating.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q54)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q54. Which of the following is an appropriate description for group decision-making
 techniques used in the estimation process of an activity duration?

 a) The estimates created using these techniques may include contingency reserves,
 sometimes referred to as time reserves or buffers, in the project schedule to account for
 schedule uncertainty.
 b) These are team-based approaches, such as brainstorming, the Delphi, or nominal group
 techniques, which are useful for engaged team members to improve their estimation
 accuracy and commit to the estimates.
 c) These techniques use statistical relationships between historical data and project
 parameters to calculate an estimate for project cost, budget, or duration.
 d) Using these techniques, a group of experts, guided by historical information, can provide
 duration estimate information or recommended maximum activity durations from prior
 similar projects.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  55,
  'Q55. Which of the following is an appropriate meaning of a mission-critical system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,490.47,81.25],"text":"Q55.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate meaning of a mission-critical system?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,507.8,118.21],"text":"a) As with an operating system, it is an indispensable system necessary for operating a"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,510.13,154.21],"text":"business system.\nb) It is a system that has a significant impact on corporate activities and society when a"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,483.7,190.21],"text":"failure occurs.\nc) It is a system that is first installed on a trial basis, and if successful, a full-scale"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,427.35,226.21],"text":"installation is implemented.\nd) It is a system where the operating performance is close to the limit."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"As with an operating system, it is an indispensable system necessary for operating a\n business system."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a system that has a significant impact on corporate activities and society when a\n failure occurs."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a system that is first installed on a trial basis, and if successful, a full-scale\n installation is implemented."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a system where the operating performance is close to the limit."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A mission-critical system is one whose failure would seriously affect corporate activities or society, such as a banking, air traffic control or power grid system, so it requires very high reliability and availability. It is not defined by being basic infrastructure like an OS, by being a pilot installation, or by running close to its performance limit.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q55)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q55. Which of the following is an appropriate meaning of a mission-critical system?

 a) As with an operating system, it is an indispensable system necessary for operating a
 business system.
 b) It is a system that has a significant impact on corporate activities and society when a
 failure occurs.
 c) It is a system that is first installed on a trial basis, and if successful, a full-scale
 installation is implemented.
 d) It is a system where the operating performance is close to the limit.',
