  'Q56. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record
 of an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,266.76,533.16,334.21],"text":"Q56.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record\nof an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?\n\na) A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the record of the problem is included in"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,527.95,370.21],"text":"the record of the problem.\nb) If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,516.27,424.21],"text":"record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted.\nc) One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record.\nd) Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.12,428.93,151.45,442.21],"text":"incidents."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the record of the problem is included in\n the record of the problem."},{"label":"b","text":"If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the\n record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted."},{"label":"c","text":"One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record."},{"label":"d","text":"Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of\n incidents."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'In ITIL-style IT service management, a problem record investigates the root cause of one or more incidents, and it keeps a cross-reference to the incident or incidents that triggered it so the records can be traced. Incident records are not deleted when known errors are identified, one problem can relate to many incidents, and problems are normally classified with the same scheme as incidents.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q56)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q56. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record
 of an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?

 a) A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the record of the problem is included in
 the record of the problem.
 b) If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the
 record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted.
 c) One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record.
 d) Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of
 incidents.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  57,
  'Q57. A system is planned to be operational 22 hours per day. However, there are two (2)
 failures with downtimes of 0.5 hours and 1.5 hours in 100 days. Which of the following is the
 approximate MTBF of this system during the period in hours?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,481.8,533.12,531.13],"text":"Q57.\nA system is planned to be operational 22 hours per day. However, there are two (2)\nfailures with downtimes of 0.5 hours and 1.5 hours in 100 days. Which of the following is the\napproximate MTBF of this system during the period in hours?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,554.76,468.22,586.15],"text":"a) 0.00091\nb) 1.0\nc) 2.0\nd) 1100"},{"type":"code","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 18 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0.00091"},{"label":"b","text":"1.0"},{"label":"c","text":"2.0"},{"label":"d","text":"1100"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The MTBF is about 1100 hours. The planned operating time is 22 h × 100 days = 2200 h, and subtracting 2 h of downtime gives 2198 h of actual operation. Dividing by the 2 failures gives 2198 ÷ 2 ≈ 1099 h, or about 1100. MTTR would be 2 h ÷ 2 = 1.0 h, which is the tempting wrong choice.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q57)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q57. A system is planned to be operational 22 hours per day. However, there are two (2)
 failures with downtimes of 0.5 hours and 1.5 hours in 100 days. Which of the following is the
 approximate MTBF of this system during the period in hours?

 a) 0.00091 b) 1.0 c) 2.0 d) 1100',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  58,
  'Q58. When a business continuity plan (BCP) is developed given the possibility of a system
 failure, which of the following is the item that is implemented as part of business impact
 analysis?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.14,154.21],"text":"Q58.\nWhen a business continuity plan (BCP) is developed given the possibility of a system\nfailure, which of the following is the item that is implemented as part of business impact\nanalysis?\n\na) Collectively educating the concerned persons about the alternate procedures and"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,531.4,226.21],"text":"recovery procedures during an information system failure\nb) Determining the maximum allowable downtime for the information system\nc) Executing a test to verify the effectiveness of BCP\nd) Revising the contents of the BCP given changes in the internal and external environment"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[102.12,230.93,228.81,244.21],"text":"of the information system"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Collectively educating the concerned persons about the alternate procedures and\n recovery procedures during an information system failure"},{"label":"b","text":"Determining the maximum allowable downtime for the information system"},{"label":"c","text":"Executing a test to verify the effectiveness of BCP"},{"label":"d","text":"Revising the contents of the BCP given changes in the internal and external environment\n of the information system"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Business impact analysis (BIA) assesses how a disruption would affect the business and sets targets such as the maximum tolerable downtime and the recovery time objective for each system. Training staff, testing the BCP and revising it later are implementation and maintenance activities that come after the analysis.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q58)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q58. When a business continuity plan (BCP) is developed given the possibility of a system
 failure, which of the following is the item that is implemented as part of business impact
 analysis?

 a) Collectively educating the concerned persons about the alternate procedures and
 recovery procedures during an information system failure
 b) Determining the maximum allowable downtime for the information system
 c) Executing a test to verify the effectiveness of BCP
 d) Revising the contents of the BCP given changes in the internal and external environment
 of the information system',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. Which of the following is the most appropriate purpose for which a system auditor
 exchanges opinions with an audited department concerning the draft version of an audit
 report?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,533.19,370.21],"text":"Q59.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate purpose for which a system auditor\nexchanges opinions with an audited department concerning the draft version of an audit\nreport?\n\na) To confirm that there are no factual errors in the findings and recommendations to be"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,530.6,406.21],"text":"described in the audit report\nb) To issue the audit report to the audited department before the audit report is submitted to"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,524.34,442.21],"text":"the person who is requesting the audit\nc) To receive the approval of the responsible person of the audited department concerning"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,516.47,478.21],"text":"the recommendations described in the audit report\nd) To substitute with additional auditing activities concerning the part of the audit report"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[102.12,482.93,505.33,496.21],"text":"for which evidence is insufficient by orally confirming with the audited department"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To confirm that there are no factual errors in the findings and recommendations to be\n described in the audit report"},{"label":"b","text":"To issue the audit report to the audited department before the audit report is submitted to\n the person who is requesting the audit"},{"label":"c","text":"To receive the approval of the responsible person of the audited department concerning\n the recommendations described in the audit report"},{"label":"d","text":"To substitute with additional auditing activities concerning the part of the audit report\n for which evidence is insufficient by orally confirming with the audited department"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The auditor reviews the draft report with the audited department to confirm that the findings and recommendations contain no factual errors before the final report is issued. The report is addressed to the person who requested the audit, the auditee''s approval of the recommendations is not needed (the auditor stays independent), and oral confirmation cannot replace missing audit evidence.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. Which of the following is the most appropriate purpose for which a system auditor
 exchanges opinions with an audited department concerning the draft version of an audit
 report?

 a) To confirm that there are no factual errors in the findings and recommendations to be
 described in the audit report
 b) To issue the audit report to the audited department before the audit report is submitted to
 the person who is requesting the audit
 c) To receive the approval of the responsible person of the audited department concerning
 the recommendations described in the audit report
 d) To substitute with additional auditing activities concerning the part of the audit report
 for which evidence is insufficient by orally confirming with the audited department',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
