  60,
  'Q60. Which of the following is the appropriate activity performed by a system auditor who
 audits access control?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,533.27,567.13],"text":"Q60.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate activity performed by a system auditor who\naudits access control?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,408.79,658.21],"text":"a) Creating and storing the access control records for the software\nb) Establishing an access control policy for the network\nc) Implementing the access control procedures for hardware\nd) Viewing the access control rules for data"},{"type":"code","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 19 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Creating and storing the access control records for the software"},{"label":"b","text":"Establishing an access control policy for the network"},{"label":"c","text":"Implementing the access control procedures for hardware"},{"label":"d","text":"Viewing the access control rules for data"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A system auditor is independent and gathers evidence, for example by viewing and checking the access control rules that are set for data. Creating records, establishing policies and implementing procedures are responsibilities of the audited organization, and an auditor who did them would be auditing their own work.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
