(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  61,
  'Q61. Which of the following is a description of SOA?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,343.36,81.25],"text":"Q61.\nWhich of the following is a description of SOA?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,106.91,526.69,120.19],"text":"a) It consists of four (4) main concepts; the business scheme, data scheme, application and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,124.91,519.47,174.19],"text":"processing scheme, and technical scheme, and it aims to optimize the business and the\nsystem.\nb) It makes it easier to address a change in the business by constructing software from"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,178.91,517.77,210.19],"text":"components called services.\nc) It performs design at the component levels by using a combination of three (3) logical"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,214.91,517.1,246.19],"text":"structures; a sequence, selection, and iteration.\nd) It uses a data flow diagram and simultaneously creates a model regarding information"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[74.28,250.91,263.4,282.19],"text":"and a model regarding functions."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It consists of four (4) main concepts; the business scheme, data scheme, application and\n processing scheme, and technical scheme, and it aims to optimize the business and the\n system."},{"label":"b","text":"It makes it easier to address a change in the business by constructing software from\n components called services."},{"label":"c","text":"It performs design at the component levels by using a combination of three (3) logical\n structures; a sequence, selection, and iteration."},{"label":"d","text":"It uses a data flow diagram and simultaneously creates a model regarding information\n and a model regarding functions."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'SOA (Service-Oriented Architecture) builds systems by combining loosely coupled, reusable components called services that correspond to business functions, so the system can be adapted quickly when the business changes. Choice a describes Enterprise Architecture, c describes structured programming, and d describes structured analysis with DFDs.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q61)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q61. Which of the following is a description of SOA?

 a) It consists of four (4) main concepts; the business scheme, data scheme, application and
 processing scheme, and technical scheme, and it aims to optimize the business and the
 system.
 b) It makes it easier to address a change in the business by constructing software from
 components called services.
 c) It performs design at the component levels by using a combination of three (3) logical
 structures; a sequence, selection, and iteration.
 d) It uses a data flow diagram and simultaneously creates a model regarding information
 and a model regarding functions.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  62,
  'Q62. Which of the following is an appropriate description of BPR (Business Process
 Reengineering)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,285.84,533.12,335.11],"text":"Q62.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of BPR (Business Process\nReengineering)?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,340.91,531.89,372.19],"text":"a) BPR is a management practice used to provide the overall governance of an organization"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,376.91,511.4,408.19],"text":"in a business process environment to improve agility and operational performance.\nb) BPR is a management strategy used to automate key business processes that helps in"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,412.91,528.96,462.19],"text":"saving time, promoting efficiency, and ultimately reducing costs to enhance the value of\nan organization.\nc) BPR is a management system used in marketing and business to automate the sales"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,466.91,493.09,498.19],"text":"activities, such as contact management, order taking and fulfillment, information\nsharing, inventory monitoring, and sales forecast analysis."},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,488.38,516.19],"text":"d) BPR is a management technique used to redesign and restructure value-creating"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,520.91,511.75,587.11],"text":"processes in an organization to gain significant benefits in productivity, profitability,\nservice, and quality through maximizing the potential of individuals and teams."},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"BPR is a management practice used to provide the overall governance of an organization\n in a business process environment to improve agility and operational performance."},{"label":"b","text":"BPR is a management strategy used to automate key business processes that helps in\n saving time, promoting efficiency, and ultimately reducing costs to enhance the value of\n an organization."},{"label":"c","text":"BPR is a management system used in marketing and business to automate the sales\n activities, such as contact management, order taking and fulfillment, information\n sharing, inventory monitoring, and sales forecast analysis."},{"label":"d","text":"BPR is a management technique used to redesign and restructure value-creating\n processes in an organization to gain significant benefits in productivity, profitability,\n service, and quality through maximizing the potential of individuals and teams."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'BPR (Business Process Reengineering) fundamentally redesigns and restructures business processes, not just automating existing ones, to achieve dramatic improvements in productivity, cost, service and quality. Choice b describes business process automation and c describes sales force automation (SFA).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q62)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q62. Which of the following is an appropriate description of BPR (Business Process
 Reengineering)?

 a) BPR is a management practice used to provide the overall governance of an organization
 in a business process environment to improve agility and operational performance.
 b) BPR is a management strategy used to automate key business processes that helps in
 saving time, promoting efficiency, and ultimately reducing costs to enhance the value of
 an organization.
 c) BPR is a management system used in marketing and business to automate the sales
 activities, such as contact management, order taking and fulfillment, information
 sharing, inventory monitoring, and sales forecast analysis.
 d) BPR is a management technique used to redesign and restructure value-creating
 processes in an organization to gain significant benefits in productivity, profitability,
 service, and quality through maximizing the potential of individuals and teams.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  63,
  'Q63. Which of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for
 visualizing business processes?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,533.13,99.13],"text":"Q63.\nWhich of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for\nvisualizing business processes?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,510.45,136.21],"text":"a) Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,517.33,172.21],"text":"entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities.\nb) To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,501.5,208.21],"text":"data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow.\nc) To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,529.67,262.21],"text":"methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for\nobject modeling.\nd) To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[102.12,266.93,430.37,280.21],"text":"single request are described by using the conditional branch format."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as\n entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities."},{"label":"b","text":"To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and\n data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow."},{"label":"c","text":"To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling\n methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for\n object modeling."},{"label":"d","text":"To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a\n single request are described by using the conditional branch format."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'UML is a standardized object-modeling notation that offers several purpose-specific diagrams, such as activity, use case and sequence diagrams, so a business process can be modeled from multiple viewpoints. Choice a describes E-R diagrams, b describes data flow diagrams, and d describes a decision table or flowchart style representation.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q63)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q63. Which of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for
 visualizing business processes?

 a) Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as
 entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities.
 b) To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and
 data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow.
 c) To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling
 methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for
 object modeling.
 d) To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a
 single request are described by using the conditional branch format.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  64,
  'Q64. In computerization planning, which of the following is an activity that should be
 performed?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,320.76,533.13,352.21],"text":"Q64.\nIn computerization planning, which of the following is an activity that should be\nperformed?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,521.56,388.21],"text":"a) Clarifying what roles are assigned to the business and information-system departments"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,520.11,460.21],"text":"when the organizational structure of system development is planned and clarifying the\nbasis of cost calculation for the development, operation, and maintenance when\nconsidering the costs\nb) Determining interfaces, such as screens or forms, based on the requirements definition"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,497.71,496.21],"text":"document and describing them in the design document\nc) Performing maintenance and management of the system so that it conforms to the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,528.77,550.21],"text":"business and environment and analyzing details and clarifying the potential impacts of\nmodification requests\nd) Performing system startup and shutdown, monitoring, and file maintenance in a planned"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,422.1,604.15],"text":"manner and verifying that business is being carried out smoothly"},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Clarifying what roles are assigned to the business and information-system departments\n when the organizational structure of system development is planned and clarifying the\n basis of cost calculation for the development, operation, and maintenance when\n considering the costs"},{"label":"b","text":"Determining interfaces, such as screens or forms, based on the requirements definition\n document and describing them in the design document"},{"label":"c","text":"Performing maintenance and management of the system so that it conforms to the\n business and environment and analyzing details and clarifying the potential impacts of\n modification requests"},{"label":"d","text":"Performing system startup and shutdown, monitoring, and file maintenance in a planned\n manner and verifying that business is being carried out smoothly"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Computerization planning comes before development. It defines the overall plan, including how roles are divided between the business and IS departments for system development and how development, operation and maintenance costs will be calculated. Designing screens and forms belongs to design, handling modification requests to maintenance, and startup, shutdown and monitoring to operation.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q64)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q64. In computerization planning, which of the following is an activity that should be
 performed?

 a) Clarifying what roles are assigned to the business and information-system departments
 when the organizational structure of system development is planned and clarifying the
 basis of cost calculation for the development, operation, and maintenance when
 considering the costs
 b) Determining interfaces, such as screens or forms, based on the requirements definition
 document and describing them in the design document
 c) Performing maintenance and management of the system so that it conforms to the
 business and environment and analyzing details and clarifying the potential impacts of
 modification requests
 d) Performing system startup and shutdown, monitoring, and file maintenance in a planned
 manner and verifying that business is being carried out smoothly',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
