  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,519.78,539.18,587.11],"text":"Q67.\nPEST analysis is used to analyze the external environment in determining a business\nstrategy. Which of the following is an appropriate set of external environmental factors that\nPEST analysis analyzes?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,592.74,315.15,660.19],"text":"a) Politics, Economics, Society, Technology\nb) Politics, Enterprises, Society, Time\nc) Price, Economics, Satisfaction, Technology\nd) Price, Enterprises, Safety, Time"},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Politics, Economics, Society, Technology"},{"label":"b","text":"Politics, Enterprises, Society, Time"},{"label":"c","text":"Price, Economics, Satisfaction, Technology"},{"label":"d","text":"Price, Enterprises, Safety, Time"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'PEST stands for Political, Economic, Social and Technological factors, the four macro-environmental areas outside the company that can affect its strategy. The other choices replace these with terms such as price, enterprises and time, which are not part of the framework.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
