  70,
  'Q70. Which of the following is a characteristic of MRP?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,355.51,81.25],"text":"Q70.\nWhich of the following is a characteristic of MRP?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,509.01,118.21],"text":"a) The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,532.01,154.21],"text":"simultaneously in parallel.\nb) The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,158.93,499.84,225.25],"text":"plan of a product.\nc) The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received.\nd) Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed\n simultaneously in parallel."},{"label":"b","text":"The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production\n plan of a product."},{"label":"c","text":"The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received."},{"label":"d","text":"Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'MRP (Material Requirements Planning) starts from the master production plan for finished products and uses the bill of materials and inventory data to calculate how many of each component is needed and when. Choice a describes concurrent engineering, c describes build-to-order production, and d describes the use of production instruction sheets.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q70)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q70. Which of the following is a characteristic of MRP?

 a) The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed
 simultaneously in parallel.
 b) The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production
 plan of a product.
 c) The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received.
 d) Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  71,
  'Q71. Which of the following is an explanation of the Kanban (just-in-time) system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,248.76,486.4,262.21],"text":"Q71.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the Kanban (just-in-time) system?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[86.22,283.85,533.14,297.13],"text":"a) To improve work efficiency at each operation, parts and semi-finished products having"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,301.85,274.36,315.13],"text":"unified specifications are procured."},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,530.62,334.21],"text":"b) To minimize intermediate stock, parts required for the production line are procured from"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,512.7,388.21],"text":"the previous process on the basis of a production plan.\nc) To procure parts efficiently, they are procured from affiliated companies.\nd) To procure parts of higher quality, parts are procured via competitive bidding among"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,392.93,205.7,406.21],"text":"designated suppliers."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To improve work efficiency at each operation, parts and semi-finished products having\n unified specifications are procured."},{"label":"b","text":"To minimize intermediate stock, parts required for the production line are procured from\n the previous process on the basis of a production plan."},{"label":"c","text":"To procure parts efficiently, they are procured from affiliated companies."},{"label":"d","text":"To procure parts of higher quality, parts are procured via competitive bidding among\n designated suppliers."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'In the Kanban (just-in-time) system, each process withdraws only the parts it needs, when it needs them, from the preceding process, signalled by kanban cards, so intermediate inventory stays minimal. The other choices describe standardization, affiliate sourcing and competitive bidding, which are not the defining feature of just-in-time.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q71)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q71. Which of the following is an explanation of the Kanban (just-in-time) system?

 a) To improve work efficiency at each operation, parts and semi-finished products having
 unified specifications are procured.
 b) To minimize intermediate stock, parts required for the production line are procured from
 the previous process on the basis of a production plan.
 c) To procure parts efficiently, they are procured from affiliated companies.
 d) To procure parts of higher quality, parts are procured via competitive bidding among
 designated suppliers.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  72,
  'Q72. Which of the following is a description of Online-to-Offline in net business?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,445.8,477.82,459.25],"text":"Q72.\nWhich of the following is a description of Online-to-Offline in net business?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,484.91,524.02,498.19],"text":"a) It is a business model that provides a basic service or product for free and charges a fee"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,504.0,534.19],"text":"for advanced or special functions.\nb) It is a mechanism that can prevent trouble in electronic commerce, such as the case"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,538.91,525.99,588.19],"text":"where the price is paid but the product is not delivered or the case where the product is\nsent but the price is not paid.\nc) It is a mechanism that leads a customer that uses mobile devices to purchase by guiding"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,592.91,523.58,624.19],"text":"the customer from a virtual store to a real store or from a real store to a virtual store\nd) It is a scheme that starts production of the final product after receiving the order from a"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,628.91,492.05,659.23],"text":"customer, in order to realize customization according to customer specifications."},{"type":"code","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,794.45,315.66,807.79],"text":"– 24 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a business model that provides a basic service or product for free and charges a fee\n for advanced or special functions."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a mechanism that can prevent trouble in electronic commerce, such as the case\n where the price is paid but the product is not delivered or the case where the product is\n sent but the price is not paid."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a mechanism that leads a customer that uses mobile devices to purchase by guiding\n the customer from a virtual store to a real store or from a real store to a virtual store"},{"label":"d","text":"It is a scheme that starts production of the final product after receiving the order from a\n customer, in order to realize customization according to customer specifications."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Online-to-Offline (O2O) uses online channels, often on smartphones with coupons, apps or location services, to bring customers into physical stores, or links store visits back to online purchases. Choice a describes the freemium model, b describes an escrow service, and d describes build-to-order production.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q72)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q72. Which of the following is a description of Online-to-Offline in net business?

 a) It is a business model that provides a basic service or product for free and charges a fee
 for advanced or special functions.
 b) It is a mechanism that can prevent trouble in electronic commerce, such as the case
 where the price is paid but the product is not delivered or the case where the product is
 sent but the price is not paid.
 c) It is a mechanism that leads a customer that uses mobile devices to purchase by guiding
 the customer from a virtual store to a real store or from a real store to a virtual store
 d) It is a scheme that starts production of the final product after receiving the order from a
 customer, in order to realize customization according to customer specifications.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  73,
  'Q73. A smart meter is a highly functional electricity meter with a function for communications
 and a function for the management of other devices. Which of the following is not
 appropriate as the purpose of installing a smart meter?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,67.8,533.17,117.19],"text":"Q73.\nA smart meter is a highly functional electricity meter with a function for communications\nand a function for the management of other devices. Which of the following is not\nappropriate as the purpose of installing a smart meter?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,520.49,154.21],"text":"a) Continuing the power supply for a fixed amount of time by functioning as an auxiliary"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,509.1,208.21],"text":"power source at the time of a power failure\nb) Improving the efficiency of meter reading work through automatic meter reading\nc) Increasing awareness of power-saving through visualization of the amount of power"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,530.64,244.21],"text":"consumption\nd) Restraining peak power through control over power demand by using demand response"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Continuing the power supply for a fixed amount of time by functioning as an auxiliary\n power source at the time of a power failure"},{"label":"b","text":"Improving the efficiency of meter reading work through automatic meter reading"},{"label":"c","text":"Increasing awareness of power-saving through visualization of the amount of power\n consumption"},{"label":"d","text":"Restraining peak power through control over power demand by using demand response"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Acting as a backup power source during an outage is not a purpose of a smart meter. That is the role of a UPS or storage battery, and a smart meter only measures and communicates. Its real purposes include automatic remote meter reading, showing users their consumption to encourage energy saving, and controlling demand through demand response to reduce peak load.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q73)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q73. A smart meter is a highly functional electricity meter with a function for communications
 and a function for the management of other devices. Which of the following is not
 appropriate as the purpose of installing a smart meter?

 a) Continuing the power supply for a fixed amount of time by functioning as an auxiliary
 power source at the time of a power failure
 b) Improving the efficiency of meter reading work through automatic meter reading
 c) Increasing awareness of power-saving through visualization of the amount of power
 consumption
 d) Restraining peak power through control over power demand by using demand response',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2022-october',
  'A',
  74,
  'Q74. Which of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,418.8,298.21],"text":"Q74.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,516.59,334.21],"text":"a) It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,515.68,388.21],"text":"urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which leads to an improvement in the\nquality of people’s lives and helps achieve continuous economic growth.\nb) It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases as a result of"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,506.85,442.21],"text":"utilizing IT, and the demand-and-supply gap is eliminated via the progress of SCM,\nwhich leads to sustainable growth free from inflation.\nc) It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are combined in a"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,533.0,496.21],"text":"business transaction, and the strong points of both are utilized and linked to expanding\noverall sales.\nd) It is a mechanism mainly between individuals to share, lend, or borrow idle assets owned"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[102.12,500.93,433.81,514.21],"text":"by individuals by utilizing the community functions of social media."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and\n urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which leads to an improvement in the\n quality of people’s lives and helps achieve continuous economic growth."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases as a result of\n utilizing IT, and the demand-and-supply gap is eliminated via the progress of SCM,\n which leads to sustainable growth free from inflation."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are combined in a\n business transaction, and the strong points of both are utilized and linked to expanding\n overall sales."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a mechanism mainly between individuals to share, lend, or borrow idle assets owned\n by individuals by utilizing the community functions of social media."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A sharing economy lets individuals share, lend or rent idle assets they own, such as rooms, cars or skills, to other individuals, usually through online platforms with community features such as ratings and social media. Choice a describes the smart city concept, b the new economy idea, and c omni-channel or click-and-mortar retailing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2022A, FE, Subject-A, Q74)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q74. Which of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?

 a) It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and
 urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which leads to an improvement in the
 quality of people’s lives and helps achieve continuous economic growth.
 b) It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases as a result of
 utilizing IT, and the demand-and-supply gap is eliminated via the progress of SCM,
 which leads to sustainable growth free from inflation.
 c) It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are combined in a
 business transaction, and the strong points of both are utilized and linked to expanding
 overall sales.
 d) It is a mechanism mainly between individuals to share, lend, or borrow idle assets owned
 by individuals by utilizing the community functions of social media.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2022-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
