  '[{"label":"a","text":"Divisional organization"},{"label":"b","text":"Hierarchical organization"},{"label":"c","text":"Line and staff organization"},{"label":"d","text":"Matrix organization"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A matrix organization combines a functional structure with a project or product structure, so each member reports both to a functional manager and to a project manager. This lets resources be reassigned flexibly as the business environment changes. Its drawback is the confusion that can come from having two bosses.',
