  'The gradeBook maps student ID to grade, so blank A is String, Double (a generic type needs the wrapper class, not the primitive double). Blank B, putIfAbsent(sid, 0.0) == null, adds the student only if not already present and returns true only for a new entry; blank C, replace(sid, grade) != null, records a grade only for a student already in the map. Both faculty and student keep their courses keyed by course code, so blank D is String, Course. Blank E, course.getFaculty() == null, stops a course that already has a teacher from being assigned again, and blank F, course.addStudent(id), enforces the course capacity and duplicate check; blank G passes the Course object: faculties.get(fid).addCourse(courses.get(code)). Subquestion 2: student 16200 starts with 24 credit hours at 3.0 (72 grade points) and gains 3 × 3.0 + 3 × 2.0 = 15 points over 6 more hours, so CGPA = 87 / 30 = 2.90.',
