  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The result is 2AF3. ABCD in binary is 1010 1011 1100 1101; a logical right shift by two moves every bit two places right and fills the vacated high bits with 0, giving 0010 1010 1111 0011 = 2AF3. Filling with copies of the sign bit (giving EAF3) would be an arithmetic shift, and in a 32-bit register the upper bits of ABCD are 0 anyway.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
