  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The method is CRC (cyclic redundancy check). The sender divides the bit sequence by a generator polynomial and appends the remainder, and the receiver checks whether the received sequence is exactly divisible by the same polynomial. Hamming code adds parity bits that can also correct single-bit errors, and parity checks just count 1 bits rather than using polynomial division.',
