  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A divide-by-zero interrupt is an internal interrupt. Internal interrupts (exceptions or traps) are caused by the program currently executing, such as an illegal operation, overflow, or a supervisor call. Power failure, I/O completion, and memory parity errors come from hardware outside the running program and are external interrupts.',
