  15,
  'Q15. Which of the following is the RAID configuration for achieving the highest speed disk
 access at the cost of reliability?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,356.93,533.17,406.21],"text":"Q15.\nWhich of the following is the RAID configuration for achieving the highest speed disk\naccess at the cost of reliability?"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,496.46,460.21],"text":"a) RAID 0\nb) RAID 1\nc) RAID 5\nd) RAID 6"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"RAID 0"},{"label":"b","text":"RAID 1"},{"label":"c","text":"RAID 5"},{"label":"d","text":"RAID 6"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'RAID 0 gives the highest speed at the cost of reliability. It stripes data across disks so reads and writes proceed in parallel, but it has no redundancy, so failure of any one disk loses the data. RAID 1 mirrors and RAID 5 and 6 use parity, which add reliability.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q15)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q15. Which of the following is the RAID configuration for achieving the highest speed disk
 access at the cost of reliability?

 a) RAID 0 b) RAID 1 c) RAID 5 d) RAID 6',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  16,
  'Q16. When system availabilities of a cold standby system, a simplex system, and a dual system
 are compared, which of the following shows the order arranged from highest to lowest? Here
 a computer or computers that compose each system are all the same.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,464.93,533.17,532.21],"text":"Q16.\nWhen system availabilities of a cold standby system, a simplex system, and a dual system\nare compared, which of the following shows the order arranged from highest to lowest? Here\na computer or computers that compose each system are all the same."},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,354.49,622.21],"text":"a) Cold standby system, dual system, simplex system\nb) Cold standby system, simplex system, dual system\nc) Dual system, cold standby system, simplex system\nd) Simplex system, cold standby system, dual system"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Cold standby system, dual system, simplex system"},{"label":"b","text":"Cold standby system, simplex system, dual system"},{"label":"c","text":"Dual system, cold standby system, simplex system"},{"label":"d","text":"Simplex system, cold standby system, dual system"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The order is dual system, cold standby system, simplex system. A dual system runs two computers in parallel doing the same processing, so if one fails the other continues immediately. A cold standby system has a spare that must be started and loaded before taking over, so it is down for a while but still recovers faster than a simplex system, which has no backup at all.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q16)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q16. When system availabilities of a cold standby system, a simplex system, and a dual system
 are compared, which of the following shows the order arranged from highest to lowest? Here
 a computer or computers that compose each system are all the same.

 a) Cold standby system, dual system, simplex system
 b) Cold standby system, simplex system, dual system
 c) Dual system, cold standby system, simplex system
 d) Simplex system, cold standby system, dual system',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
