),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  17,
  'Q17. A printer prints 400 characters per second. The printer uses interrupt-driven I/O and each
 character printed requires an interrupt that takes 50 microseconds. What percentage of the
 printer''s CPU is available to do other work during printing? Here, other overhead time for the
 CPU can be ignored.',
  '[{"type":"table","page":7,"bbox":[80.28,659.22,530.1,731.22],"rows":[[null,"A printer prints 400 characters per second. The printer uses interrupt-driven I/O and each"],["character printed requires an interrupt that takes 50 microseconds. What percentage of the",null],["printer''s CPU is available to do other work during printing? Here, other overhead time for the",null],["CPU can be ignored.",null]]},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,662.76,533.24,748.21],"text":"Q17.\nA printer prints 400 characters per second. The printer uses interrupt-driven I/O and each\ncharacter printed requires an interrupt that takes 50 microseconds. What percentage of the\nprinter''s CPU is available to do other work during printing? Here, other overhead time for the\nCPU can be ignored."},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,752.76,464.44,766.21],"text":"a) 98\nb) 96\nc) 4\nd) 2"},{"type":"code","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 7 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"98"},{"label":"b","text":"96"},{"label":"c","text":"4"},{"label":"d","text":"2"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  '98% of the CPU is available. Each second the printer generates 400 interrupts of 50 microseconds each, so the CPU spends 400 × 50 microseconds = 20,000 microseconds = 20 ms per second on printing. That is 20 / 1,000 = 2% busy, leaving 98% for other work; the 2% choice is the busy time, not the available time.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q17)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q17. A printer prints 400 characters per second. The printer uses interrupt-driven I/O and each
 character printed requires an interrupt that takes 50 microseconds. What percentage of the
 printer''s CPU is available to do other work during printing? Here, other overhead time for the
 CPU can be ignored.

 a) 98 b) 96 c) 4 d) 2',
