(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  19,
  'Q19. Among the different types of backup methods, which of the following is incremental
 backup? Here, in the first backup, all files are backed up and the information that indicates a
 file update managed by the operating system is reset.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,356.26,533.15,423.19],"text":"Q19.\nAmong the different types of backup methods, which of the following is incremental\nbackup? Here, in the first backup, all files are backed up and the information that indicates a\nfile update managed by the operating system is reset."},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,427.91,492.45,459.19],"text":"a) All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,463.91,492.45,495.19],"text":"information indicating a file update is left unchanged.\nb) All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[102.12,499.91,314.67,513.19],"text":"information indicating a file update is reset."},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,517.91,520.35,531.19],"text":"c) Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,535.91,520.36,567.19],"text":"indicating a file update is left unchanged.\nd) Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,571.91,255.05,621.13],"text":"indicating a file update is reset."},{"type":"code","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 8 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the\n information indicating a file update is left unchanged."},{"label":"b","text":"All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the\n information indicating a file update is reset."},{"label":"c","text":"Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information\n indicating a file update is left unchanged."},{"label":"d","text":"Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information\n indicating a file update is reset."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'An incremental backup copies only files whose update flag is set and then resets that flag. Resetting means the next incremental backup contains only changes made since the most recent backup of any kind. Copying updated files but leaving the flag unchanged describes a differential backup, which keeps growing since the last full backup.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q19)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q19. Among the different types of backup methods, which of the following is incremental
 backup? Here, in the first backup, all files are backed up and the information that indicates a
 file update managed by the operating system is reset.

 a) All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the
 information indicating a file update is left unchanged.
 b) All files are backed up regardless of information indicating a file update, and the
 information indicating a file update is reset.
 c) Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information
 indicating a file update is left unchanged.
 d) Only files with information indicating a file update are backed up, and the information
 indicating a file update is reset.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
