 below?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,339.6,533.13,371.05],"text":"Q21.\nWhich of the following is the logic gate that is equivalent to the logic circuit shown\nbelow?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[86.64,495.89,98.94,509.17],"text":"a)"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[158.88,495.89,319.26,509.17],"text":"b)"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[86.64,531.89,98.94,545.17],"text":"c)"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[158.82,531.89,319.26,545.17],"text":"d)"},{"type":"code","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 9 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-april-a-q21-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2023-april-a-q21-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2023-april-a-q21-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2023-april-a-q21-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2023-april-a-q21-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The circuit is equivalent to an exclusive OR (XOR) gate. This is the classic four-NAND construction: the first NAND gives N = (AB)'', the middle NANDs give (AN)'' and (BN)'', and the final NAND gives AN + BN = (A + B)(AB)'', which is 1 exactly when A and B differ. The symbol with the extra curved line at the input is the XOR gate.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
