  22,
  'Q22. At the rising edge of the clock signal, the content of an 8-bit serial-in parallel-out shift register is shifted upward, while positive logic data is simultaneously read into the least significant bit. The value is fixed at the rising edge of a strobe. When the results of an observation of each signal’s waveform are as shown in the diagram below, which of the following is the value of the shift register after it is fixed? Here, numeric values are represented in hexadecimal.',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q22. At the rising edge of the clock signal, the content of an 8-bit serial-in parallel-out shift register is shifted upward, while positive logic data is simultaneously read into the least significant bit. The value is fixed at the rising edge of a strobe. When the results of an observation of each signal’s waveform are as shown in the diagram below, which of the following is the value of the shift register after it is fixed? Here, numeric values are represented in hexadecimal."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-april-a-q22-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"63"},{"label":"b","text":"8D"},{"label":"c","text":"B1"},{"label":"d","text":"C6"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The register holds 8D. On each clock rising edge the data line is shifted into the least significant bit, and reading the data level at the rising edges before the strobe gives 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1. An 8-bit register keeps only the last eight bits, 1000 1101, which is 8D in hexadecimal when the strobe fixes the value.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
