(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  23,
  'Q23. Which of the following is a case where outline fonts rather than bitmap fonts are suitable
 for use?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,338.93,533.17,388.21],"text":"Q23.\nWhich of the following is a case where outline fonts rather than bitmap fonts are suitable\nfor use?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,392.93,431.99,496.21],"text":"a) To display characters as quickly as possible\nb) To display characters in monospace\nc) To display single-byte and double-byte characters at the same time\nd) To enlarge characters by a given scale factor"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To display characters as quickly as possible"},{"label":"b","text":"To display characters in monospace"},{"label":"c","text":"To display single-byte and double-byte characters at the same time"},{"label":"d","text":"To enlarge characters by a given scale factor"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Outline fonts are suitable for enlarging characters by any scale factor. They store each character as outlines (curves and lines) that are recalculated at any size, so enlarged characters stay smooth, whereas enlarged bitmap fonts become jagged. Bitmap fonts are actually faster to display because no rendering calculation is needed.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q23)',
