  24,
  'Q24. What is the approximate minimum required bandwidth for delivering a 30-frames/second
 video in 800 x 600 pixel and 24-bit full color? Here, the data is not compressed during
 communication.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,500.93,533.14,568.21],"text":"Q24.\nWhat is the approximate minimum required bandwidth for delivering a 30-frames/second\nvideo in 800 x 600 pixel and 24-bit full color? Here, the data is not compressed during\ncommunication."},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,572.93,378.83,640.21],"text":"a) 350 kbps\nb) 3.5 Mbps\nc) 35 Mbps\nd) 350 Mbps"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"350 kbps"},{"label":"b","text":"3.5 Mbps"},{"label":"c","text":"35 Mbps"},{"label":"d","text":"350 Mbps"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'About 350 Mbps is needed. One frame is 800 × 600 pixels × 24 bits = 11,520,000 bits, and 30 frames per second gives 345,600,000 bits per second, roughly 350 Mbps. A common mistake is to calculate in bytes instead of bits, which gives a value eight times smaller.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
