),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. Which of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of
 a relational database by a user?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,361.56,533.13,429.01],"text":"Q30.\nWhich of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of\na relational database by a user?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,433.73,530.36,447.01],"text":"a) To enable economization of disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,451.73,521.97,483.01],"text":"on several disks.\nb) To enable efficient access to the storage location of data in order to improve the search"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,487.73,501.04,537.01],"text":"speed.\nc) To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column.\nd) To match the value of the foreign key column with the value of the primary key of"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,541.73,170.49,571.93],"text":"another table."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To enable economization of disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved\n on several disks."},{"label":"b","text":"To enable efficient access to the storage location of data in order to improve the search\n speed."},{"label":"c","text":"To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column."},{"label":"d","text":"To match the value of the foreign key column with the value of the primary key of\n another table."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'An index is set to give efficient access to where data is stored, which speeds up searches. It works like a book index, letting the DBMS locate rows without scanning the whole table. Preventing duplicates is the job of a unique or primary key constraint, and matching foreign key values is referential integrity.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q30)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q30. Which of the following is the purpose of setting an index in the columns of the table of
 a relational database by a user?

 a) To enable economization of disk space when a single large table is distributed and saved
 on several disks.
 b) To enable efficient access to the storage location of data in order to improve the search
 speed.
 c) To ensure that no value is duplicated in a column.
 d) To match the value of the foreign key column with the value of the primary key of
 another table.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[12]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following is a role of DNS in a TCP/IP network?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,576.54,410.2,607.99],"text":"Q31.\nWhich of the following is a role of DNS in a TCP/IP network?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,613.73,526.63,663.01],"text":"a) A private IP address is translated into a global IP address in order to access the Internet.\nb) A program in a server can be invoked only by its name without taking the server’s IP"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,667.73,528.4,717.01],"text":"address into consideration.\nc) Domain names, host names, and other such information are mapped to IP addresses.\nd) In response to an assignment request for an IP address from a PC or a printer, an unused"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[102.12,721.73,397.09,735.01],"text":"address is chosen from the addresses registered in the server."},{"type":"code","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 12 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A private IP address is translated into a global IP address in order to access the Internet."},{"label":"b","text":"A program in a server can be invoked only by its name without taking the server’s IP\n address into consideration."},{"label":"c","text":"Domain names, host names, and other such information are mapped to IP addresses."},{"label":"d","text":"In response to an assignment request for an IP address from a PC or a printer, an unused\n address is chosen from the addresses registered in the server."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'DNS maps domain names and host names to IP addresses (and the reverse), so users can use names instead of numbers. Translating private to global addresses is NAT, and assigning unused addresses to devices on request is DHCP.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following is a role of DNS in a TCP/IP network?

 a) A private IP address is translated into a global IP address in order to access the Internet.
 b) A program in a server can be invoked only by its name without taking the server’s IP
 address into consideration.
 c) Domain names, host names, and other such information are mapped to IP addresses.
 d) In response to an assignment request for an IP address from a PC or a printer, an unused
 address is chosen from the addresses registered in the server.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[12]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  32,
  'Q32. In the same subnet, which of the following is the devices that will receive the data when
 the destination address is set to 255.255.255.255?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.14,118.21],"text":"Q32.\nIn the same subnet, which of the following is the devices that will receive the data when\nthe destination address is set to 255.255.255.255?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,301.4,208.21],"text":"a) All devices in the same subnet\nb) All devices using the same DNS server\nc) Only the default gateway of the subnet\nd) Only the device sending the data to itself"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"All devices in the same subnet"},{"label":"b","text":"All devices using the same DNS server"},{"label":"c","text":"Only the default gateway of the subnet"},{"label":"d","text":"Only the device sending the data to itself"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'All devices in the same subnet receive the data. 255.255.255.255 is the limited broadcast address, so a packet sent to it is delivered to every host on the local network segment. Routers do not forward it, so it stays within the subnet.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
