  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'There are 62 host addresses. A /26 prefix leaves 32 − 26 = 6 host bits, giving 2⁶ = 64 addresses, and the network address and broadcast address cannot be assigned to hosts, so 64 − 2 = 62.',
