(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  36,
  'Q36. Which of the following is malware that is activated by attackers to launch attacks on
 other computers?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,536.76,533.17,586.21],"text":"Q36.\nWhich of the following is malware that is activated by attackers to launch attacks on\nother computers?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,590.93,494.78,622.21],"text":"a) Bot\nb) Rootkit\nc) Trojan Horse\nd) Worm"},{"type":"code","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 13 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Bot"},{"label":"b","text":"Rootkit"},{"label":"c","text":"Trojan Horse"},{"label":"d","text":"Worm"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is a bot. A bot infects a computer and waits for commands from the attacker''s command-and-control server, so the attacker can activate many infected computers (a botnet) to attack others, for example with DDoS. A rootkit hides the attacker''s presence, a Trojan horse disguises itself as useful software, and a worm spreads by copying itself.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q36)',
  ARRAY[13]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q36. Which of the following is malware that is activated by attackers to launch attacks on
 other computers?

 a) Bot b) Rootkit c) Trojan Horse d) Worm',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[13]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  37,
  'Q37. Which of the following is considered a violation of confidentiality?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,438.65,81.19],"text":"Q37.\nWhich of the following is considered a violation of confidentiality?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,509.31,118.21],"text":"a) Denial of services to a website handling confidential information by generating fake"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,527.45,154.21],"text":"heavy traffic in the network\nb) Destruction of server hardware storing personal information caused by high voltage due"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,486.73,208.21],"text":"to failure of voltage stabilizer\nc) Disturbing communication by destroying ciphertext of confidential information\nd) Tricking a user into providing personal information to a fake website"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Denial of services to a website handling confidential information by generating fake\n heavy traffic in the network"},{"label":"b","text":"Destruction of server hardware storing personal information caused by high voltage due\n to failure of voltage stabilizer"},{"label":"c","text":"Disturbing communication by destroying ciphertext of confidential information"},{"label":"d","text":"Tricking a user into providing personal information to a fake website"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Tricking a user into giving personal information to a fake website (phishing) violates confidentiality, because information is disclosed to someone not authorized to see it. A DoS attack and destroyed hardware harm availability, and destroying ciphertext harms availability or integrity, but none of these reveals the information.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q37)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q37. Which of the following is considered a violation of confidentiality?

 a) Denial of services to a website handling confidential information by generating fake
 heavy traffic in the network
 b) Destruction of server hardware storing personal information caused by high voltage due
 to failure of voltage stabilizer
 c) Disturbing communication by destroying ciphertext of confidential information
 d) Tricking a user into providing personal information to a fake website',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  38,
  'Q38. Which of the following is an appropriate description of “asymmetric encryption,” used
 for encrypting and decrypting messages for secure communication?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,231.28,533.15,280.21],"text":"Q38.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of “asymmetric encryption,” used\nfor encrypting and decrypting messages for secure communication?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,522.32,334.21],"text":"a) A ciphertext message is shorter than its original plaintext message.\nb) A message receiver’s public key is used to encrypt the message and his/her private key"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,525.72,370.21],"text":"is used to decrypt the message.\nc) A message sender’s private key is open to everyone and is used to encrypt the message,"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,374.93,484.36,424.15],"text":"and each message receiver’s public key is used to decrypt the message.\nd) A secret key needs to be shared among those who need to receive the message."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A ciphertext message is shorter than its original plaintext message."},{"label":"b","text":"A message receiver’s public key is used to encrypt the message and his/her private key\n is used to decrypt the message."},{"label":"c","text":"A message sender’s private key is open to everyone and is used to encrypt the message,\n and each message receiver’s public key is used to decrypt the message."},{"label":"d","text":"A secret key needs to be shared among those who need to receive the message."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'In asymmetric (public key) encryption the sender encrypts with the receiver''s public key and only the receiver''s private key can decrypt it. The private key is never published, and needing a shared secret key describes symmetric encryption.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q38)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q38. Which of the following is an appropriate description of “asymmetric encryption,” used
 for encrypting and decrypting messages for secure communication?

 a) A ciphertext message is shorter than its original plaintext message.
 b) A message receiver’s public key is used to encrypt the message and his/her private key
 is used to decrypt the message.
 c) A message sender’s private key is open to everyone and is used to encrypt the message,
 and each message receiver’s public key is used to decrypt the message.
 d) A secret key needs to be shared among those who need to receive the message.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  39,
  'Q39. Which of the following is a method of social engineering used in a targeted e-mail attack?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,446.76,533.17,514.21],"text":"Q39.\nWhich of the following is a method of social engineering used in a targeted e-mail attack?\n\na) “Unsolicited advertising” is shown in the subject.\nb) Content that appears to be related to the work of the recipient is shown in the subject or"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,499.1,550.21],"text":"body text.\nc) In order to make the recipients access a bogus website, the sender pretends to be a"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,509.01,586.21],"text":"financial institution and sends e-mails indiscriminately.\nd) In order to make the recipients transfer a fee that they do not need to pay, the sender"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,590.93,440.32,639.13],"text":"pretends to be a collection agency and sends e-mails indiscriminately."},{"type":"code","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 14 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"“Unsolicited advertising” is shown in the subject."},{"label":"b","text":"Content that appears to be related to the work of the recipient is shown in the subject or\n body text."},{"label":"c","text":"In order to make the recipients access a bogus website, the sender pretends to be a\n financial institution and sends e-mails indiscriminately."},{"label":"d","text":"In order to make the recipients transfer a fee that they do not need to pay, the sender\n pretends to be a collection agency and sends e-mails indiscriminately."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A targeted e-mail attack uses a subject or body that looks related to the recipient''s own work, so the recipient trusts it and opens the attachment or link. This social engineering is aimed at specific people or organizations. The choices describing e-mails sent indiscriminately are ordinary phishing or fraud, not targeted attacks.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q39)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q39. Which of the following is a method of social engineering used in a targeted e-mail attack?

 a) “Unsolicited advertising” is shown in the subject.
 b) Content that appears to be related to the work of the recipient is shown in the subject or
 body text.
 c) In order to make the recipients access a bogus website, the sender pretends to be a
 financial institution and sends e-mails indiscriminately.
 d) In order to make the recipients transfer a fee that they do not need to pay, the sender
 pretends to be a collection agency and sends e-mails indiscriminately.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  40,
  'Q40. In information security, which of the following is a back door?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,411.07,81.19],"text":"Q40.\nIn information security, which of the following is a back door?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,529.64,118.21],"text":"a) A LAN port that is incorporated into a switch in order to obtain network communication"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,504.77,154.21],"text":"packets and inspect details of the communication\nb) A tool that searches for an open TCP port on a server on the Internet, and identifies"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,515.98,190.21],"text":"running services\nc) A URL that enables access to a website without going through the official procedures"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,522.92,226.21],"text":"such as password authentication that are normally required for access\nd) An attack that causes a program to crash by entering a string with a length that exceeds"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,230.93,471.76,262.15],"text":"the size of an area of memory acquired by the program, causing an overflow"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A LAN port that is incorporated into a switch in order to obtain network communication\n packets and inspect details of the communication"},{"label":"b","text":"A tool that searches for an open TCP port on a server on the Internet, and identifies\n running services"},{"label":"c","text":"A URL that enables access to a website without going through the official procedures\n such as password authentication that are normally required for access"},{"label":"d","text":"An attack that causes a program to crash by entering a string with a length that exceeds\n the size of an area of memory acquired by the program, causing an overflow"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A back door is a hidden way into a system that bypasses normal procedures such as password authentication, here a URL giving access to a website without logging in. The other choices describe a mirror port for packet capture, a port scanner, and a buffer overflow attack.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q40)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q40. In information security, which of the following is a back door?

 a) A LAN port that is incorporated into a switch in order to obtain network communication
 packets and inspect details of the communication
 b) A tool that searches for an open TCP port on a server on the Internet, and identifies
 running services
 c) A URL that enables access to a website without going through the official procedures
 such as password authentication that are normally required for access
 d) An attack that causes a program to crash by entering a string with a length that exceeds
 the size of an area of memory acquired by the program, causing an overflow',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  41,
  'Q41. An asset valued at $200,000 has an exposure factor of 20% and an annual rate of
 occurrence of 0.5 for the risk of malware infection. How much (in dollars) is the annual loss
 expectancy of the asset due to malware infection?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,533.15,352.21],"text":"Q41.\nAn asset valued at $200,000 has an exposure factor of 20% and an annual rate of\noccurrence of 0.5 for the risk of malware infection. How much (in dollars) is the annual loss\nexpectancy of the asset due to malware infection?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,489.96,370.21],"text":"a) 20,000\nb) 40,000\nc) 80,000\nd) 100,000"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"20,000"},{"label":"b","text":"40,000"},{"label":"c","text":"80,000"},{"label":"d","text":"100,000"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The annual loss expectancy is $20,000. Single loss expectancy = asset value × exposure factor = 200,000 × 0.2 = $40,000, and ALE = SLE × annual rate of occurrence = 40,000 × 0.5 = $20,000. $40,000 is only the loss from a single occurrence.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q41)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
