  'A',
  44,
  'Q44. A packet filtering firewall is installed at the connection point of an internal network and the Internet. Which of the following is the appropriate combination of filtering rules that enables PCs on the internal network to access a web server on the Internet (port number 80)?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q44. A packet filtering firewall is installed at the connection point of an internal network and the Internet. Which of the following is the appropriate combination of filtering rules that enables PCs on the internal network to access a web server on the Internet (port number 80)?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Source: PC, Destination: Web server, Source port number: 80, Destination port number: 1024 or higher\nSource: Web server, Destination: PC, Source port number: 80, Destination port number: 1024 or higher"},{"label":"b","text":"Source: PC, Destination: Web server, Source port number: 80, Destination port number: 1024 or higher\nSource: Web server, Destination: PC, Source port number: 1024 or higher, Destination port number: 80"},{"label":"c","text":"Source: PC, Destination: Web server, Source port number: 1024 or higher, Destination port number: 80\nSource: Web server, Destination: PC, Source port number: 80, Destination port number: 1024 or higher"},{"label":"d","text":"Source: PC, Destination: Web server, Source port number: 1024 or higher, Destination port number: 80\nSource: Web server, Destination: PC, Source port number: 1024 or higher, Destination port number: 80"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct rules allow PC to web server from source port 1024 or higher to destination port 80, and web server to PC from source port 80 to destination port 1024 or higher. The client uses an ephemeral port (1024 or higher) and connects to the server''s well-known port 80, and the response comes back with the ports reversed. The other choices reverse the ports in one or both directions.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
