(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  45,
  'Q45. When a sender from domain A sends an e-mail to a recipient in domain B, which of the
 following is used by the mail server in domain A for authenticating the sender?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,519.12,533.06,568.57],"text":"Q45.\nWhen a sender from domain A sends an e-mail to a recipient in domain B, which of the\nfollowing is used by the mail server in domain A for authenticating the sender?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,573.29,526.65,604.57],"text":"a) APOP\nb) POP3S\nc) S/MIME\nd) SMTP-AUTH"},{"type":"code","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 16 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"APOP"},{"label":"b","text":"POP3S"},{"label":"c","text":"S/MIME"},{"label":"d","text":"SMTP-AUTH"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'SMTP-AUTH is used. It adds user authentication to SMTP so the sending mail server in domain A only accepts mail for sending from authorized users. APOP and POP3S authenticate users when they receive mail from their own mailbox, and S/MIME encrypts and signs message content.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
