(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  47,
  'Q47. Among the definitions of software quality characteristics, which of the following
 characteristics refers to the ease of modifying a program for a certain computer so that it can
 run on a different architecture?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,302.76,533.14,369.13],"text":"Q47.\nAmong the definitions of software quality characteristics, which of the following\ncharacteristics refers to the ease of modifying a program for a certain computer so that it can\nrun on a different architecture?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,405.17,406.21],"text":"a) Changeability\nb) Interoperability\nc) Portability\nd) Usability"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Changeability"},{"label":"b","text":"Interoperability"},{"label":"c","text":"Portability"},{"label":"d","text":"Usability"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The characteristic is portability, the ease of moving software from one hardware or software environment to another. Changeability concerns how easily software can be modified to meet changed requirements, and interoperability concerns exchanging information with other systems.',
