(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  48,
  'Q48. In the error embedding method, when the number of embedded errors is S, the number of discovered errors from the embedded errors is m, the number of latent errors before the start of testing not including embedded errors is T, and the total number of discovered errors is n, which of the following expresses the relationship of S, T, m, and n?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q48. In the error embedding method, when the number of embedded errors is S, the number of discovered errors from the embedded errors is m, the number of latent errors before the start of testing not including embedded errors is T, and the total number of discovered errors is n, which of the following expresses the relationship of S, T, m, and n?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"(m)/(S) = (n−m)/(T)"},{"label":"b","text":"(m)/(S) = (T)/(n−m)"},{"label":"c","text":"(m)/(S) = (n)/(T)"},{"label":"d","text":"(m)/(S) = (T)/(n)"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The relationship is m/S = (n − m)/T. The method assumes embedded and real errors are found at the same rate, so the fraction of embedded errors found (m out of S) equals the fraction of real errors found. Real errors found are the total found minus the embedded ones found, n − m, out of T, which lets T be estimated as S(n − m)/m.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q48)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
