  49,
  'Q49. Which of the following is an appropriate test case when a test is to be performed with decision condition coverage (branch coverage) on the section of a program shown in the figure below?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q49. Which of the following is an appropriate test case when a test is to be performed with decision condition coverage (branch coverage) on the section of a program shown in the figure below?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-april-a-q49-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A: False, B: True"},{"label":"b","text":"A: False, B: True; A: True, B: False"},{"label":"c","text":"A: False, B: False; A: True, B: True"},{"label":"d","text":"A: False, B: True; A: True, B: False; A: True, B: True"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The suitable test set is A False, B False and A True, B True. Branch coverage only requires the decision ''A OR B'' to take both the TRUE and FALSE outcomes; False/False makes it false and True/True makes it true. The other sets make the decision true every time, so the FALSE branch is never tested.',
