(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  55,
  'Q55. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the Function Point method for
 creating an estimate for software development?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.11,100.21],"text":"Q55.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of the Function Point method for\ncreating an estimate for software development?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,499.77,136.21],"text":"a) It is a method for estimating the overall workload, where the development work is"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,512.12,208.21],"text":"broken down into units of work items. The cumulative total of the workload for each\nitem is then calculated based on a predefined standard value for the workload that is\napplied to each individual work item.\nb) It is a method for estimating the person-hours and development duration, on the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,523.13,262.21],"text":"assumption that the development scale is known. It can be applied to all fields, not just\nto the business field.\nc) It is a method for estimating the scale and person-hours of development based on some"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,518.32,334.21],"text":"past experience of similar software, where similarities and differences of software are\nanalyzed while past data is used for the similarities and past experience for the\ndifferences.\nd) It is a method for estimating the scale of software, where the functions of the software"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,338.93,529.63,370.21],"text":"are quantitatively measured using elements such as the number of I/O data items and the\nnumber of files, and an adjustment is performed based on the complexity."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a method for estimating the overall workload, where the development work is\n broken down into units of work items. The cumulative total of the workload for each\n item is then calculated based on a predefined standard value for the workload that is\n applied to each individual work item."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a method for estimating the person-hours and development duration, on the\n assumption that the development scale is known. It can be applied to all fields, not just\n to the business field."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a method for estimating the scale and person-hours of development based on some\n past experience of similar software, where similarities and differences of software are\n analyzed while past data is used for the similarities and past experience for the\n differences."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a method for estimating the scale of software, where the functions of the software\n are quantitatively measured using elements such as the number of I/O data items and the\n number of files, and an adjustment is performed based on the complexity."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The function point method measures the size of software from its functions, counting elements such as inputs, outputs, inquiries, and files, and then adjusts the count for complexity. Breaking work into items with standard workloads is the standard task method, estimating effort from a known size describes COCOMO, and comparing with similar past projects is the analogy method.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q55)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q55. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the Function Point method for
 creating an estimate for software development?

 a) It is a method for estimating the overall workload, where the development work is
 broken down into units of work items. The cumulative total of the workload for each
 item is then calculated based on a predefined standard value for the workload that is
 applied to each individual work item.
 b) It is a method for estimating the person-hours and development duration, on the
 assumption that the development scale is known. It can be applied to all fields, not just
 to the business field.
 c) It is a method for estimating the scale and person-hours of development based on some
 past experience of similar software, where similarities and differences of software are
 analyzed while past data is used for the similarities and past experience for the
 differences.
 d) It is a method for estimating the scale of software, where the functions of the software
 are quantitatively measured using elements such as the number of I/O data items and the
 number of files, and an adjustment is performed based on the complexity.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
