  'A',
  57,
  'Q57. As for activities in capacity management to estimate a service’s capacity, capability, and
 performance, which of the following is trend analysis?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.17,100.21],"text":"Q57.\nAs for activities in capacity management to estimate a service’s capacity, capability, and\nperformance, which of the following is trend analysis?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,124.91,502.42,138.19],"text":"a) As the first phase of modeling, creating a model that accurately reflects the current"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,142.91,524.63,174.19],"text":"performance\nb) Generating simulated transactions and predicting the response time and throughput of a"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,178.91,500.45,210.19],"text":"service\nc) Understanding the chronological usage of a specific resource and predicting usage"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,214.91,515.14,246.19],"text":"changes in the future\nd) Using mathematical techniques, such as queueing theory, and predicting the response"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,250.91,260.66,282.13],"text":"time and throughput of a service"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"As the first phase of modeling, creating a model that accurately reflects the current\n performance"},{"label":"b","text":"Generating simulated transactions and predicting the response time and throughput of a\n service"},{"label":"c","text":"Understanding the chronological usage of a specific resource and predicting usage\n changes in the future"},{"label":"d","text":"Using mathematical techniques, such as queueing theory, and predicting the response\n time and throughput of a service"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Trend analysis examines how a specific resource has been used over time and predicts future changes in its usage. Building a model of current performance is baselining, generating simulated transactions is simulation modelling, and queueing theory calculations are analytical modelling.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q57)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q57. As for activities in capacity management to estimate a service’s capacity, capability, and
 performance, which of the following is trend analysis?

 a) As the first phase of modeling, creating a model that accurately reflects the current
 performance
 b) Generating simulated transactions and predicting the response time and throughput of a
 service
 c) Understanding the chronological usage of a specific resource and predicting usage
 changes in the future
 d) Using mathematical techniques, such as queueing theory, and predicting the response
 time and throughput of a service',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  58,
  'Q58. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning system operation?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,286.74,520.99,354.19],"text":"Q58.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description concerning system operation?\n\na) Disconnecting failed components to continue the system’s more important functions is"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,358.91,516.06,408.19],"text":"called fall back operation.\nb) Re-executing a program using data recorded at a checkpoint is called rebooting.\nc) Recording transactions for the purpose of restoring a database to its condition prior to"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,412.91,516.06,444.19],"text":"changes is called data logging.\nd) Regularly saving files to another recording media for the purpose of restoration in the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[102.12,448.91,269.66,462.19],"text":"event of failure is called restoring."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Disconnecting failed components to continue the system’s more important functions is\n called fall back operation."},{"label":"b","text":"Re-executing a program using data recorded at a checkpoint is called rebooting."},{"label":"c","text":"Recording transactions for the purpose of restoring a database to its condition prior to\n changes is called data logging."},{"label":"d","text":"Regularly saving files to another recording media for the purpose of restoration in the\n event of failure is called restoring."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Disconnecting failed components and continuing the more important functions is fallback (degraded) operation. Re-executing from a checkpoint is a restart rather than a reboot, recording transactions for restoring a database is journaling (logging for recovery), and regularly copying files to other media is backup, not restoring.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q58)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q58. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning system operation?

 a) Disconnecting failed components to continue the system’s more important functions is
 called fall back operation.
 b) Re-executing a program using data recorded at a checkpoint is called rebooting.
 c) Recording transactions for the purpose of restoring a database to its condition prior to
 changes is called data logging.
 d) Regularly saving files to another recording media for the purpose of restoration in the
 event of failure is called restoring.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. In the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk
 of user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,502.74,533.16,552.19],"text":"Q59.\nIn the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk\nof user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,556.91,517.58,570.19],"text":"a) Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,574.91,526.63,624.19],"text":"standards\nb) Whether the program specifications are created based on the system design documents\nc) Whether the test plan is created based on the system test requirements, and the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,628.91,524.36,660.19],"text":"manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained\nd) Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents"},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and\n standards"},{"label":"b","text":"Whether the program specifications are created based on the system design documents"},{"label":"c","text":"Whether the test plan is created based on the system test requirements, and the\n manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained"},{"label":"d","text":"Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The auditor should check whether the user department participates in reviewing the system design documents. User involvement in design reviews is the control that ensures user requirements are reflected in the design. The other choices concern programming standards, program specifications, and test planning, which control different risks.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. In the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk
 of user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?

 a) Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and
 standards
 b) Whether the program specifications are created based on the system design documents
 c) Whether the test plan is created based on the system test requirements, and the
 manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained
 d) Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  60,
  'Q60. When an information system department enters data sheets issued by a business
 operations department, which of the following is an appropriate task executed by the
 information system department?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.12,117.13],"text":"Q60.\nWhen an information system department enters data sheets issued by a business\noperations department, which of the following is an appropriate task executed by the\ninformation system department?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,524.38,154.21],"text":"a) The data sheets are retained in the information system department until the due date for"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,523.6,208.21],"text":"processing, and the number of sheets received is checked and confirmed just before the\ndue date.\nb) To enable the business operations department to check the processing results of each"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,503.72,244.21],"text":"data sheet, the processing results list is sent to that department.\nc) To prevent unauthorized use or leakage of confidential information, data sheets are"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,533.01,280.21],"text":"disposed of immediately after data entry is completed.\nd) When the data sheet contains an obvious error, the data sheet is corrected, and an entry is"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[102.12,284.93,390.26,298.21],"text":"made at the discretion of the person in charge of data entry."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The data sheets are retained in the information system department until the due date for\n processing, and the number of sheets received is checked and confirmed just before the\n due date."},{"label":"b","text":"To enable the business operations department to check the processing results of each\n data sheet, the processing results list is sent to that department."},{"label":"c","text":"To prevent unauthorized use or leakage of confidential information, data sheets are\n disposed of immediately after data entry is completed."},{"label":"d","text":"When the data sheet contains an obvious error, the data sheet is corrected, and an entry is\n made at the discretion of the person in charge of data entry."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The appropriate task is sending a list of processing results to the business operations department so it can check the result for each data sheet. This lets the originating department confirm that its data was entered completely and correctly. Correcting sheets at the data-entry person''s discretion, disposing of them immediately, or counting them only at the deadline weakens control.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q60)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q60. When an information system department enters data sheets issued by a business
 operations department, which of the following is an appropriate task executed by the
 information system department?

 a) The data sheets are retained in the information system department until the due date for
 processing, and the number of sheets received is checked and confirmed just before the
 due date.
 b) To enable the business operations department to check the processing results of each
 data sheet, the processing results list is sent to that department.
 c) To prevent unauthorized use or leakage of confidential information, data sheets are
 disposed of immediately after data entry is completed.
 d) When the data sheet contains an obvious error, the data sheet is corrected, and an entry is
 made at the discretion of the person in charge of data entry.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  61,
  'Q61. Which of the following is an example of RPA that is used to proceed with business
 innovation with the aim of resolving management issues, such as a shortage of staff members?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,338.76,533.12,370.21],"text":"Q61.\nWhich of the following is an example of RPA that is used to proceed with business\ninnovation with the aim of resolving management issues, such as a shortage of staff members?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,519.0,406.21],"text":"a) Deploying robots for assembly work instead of employees engaged in the assembly of"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,521.51,442.21],"text":"components on the manufacturing line.\nb) Processing standardized routine activities such as data input, and cross-checking of the"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,495.35,478.21],"text":"business system by software instead of the clerical staff members.\nc) Replacing manned stores with unmanned stores run by cameras and an electronic"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,517.03,514.21],"text":"payment system for analysis of IC tags and images.\nd) Replacing transfer of stored products through manual operations by using a forklift or"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,510.38,586.21],"text":"something similar with an automated warehouse system where computer control has\nrendered human labor obsolete."},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Deploying robots for assembly work instead of employees engaged in the assembly of\n components on the manufacturing line."},{"label":"b","text":"Processing standardized routine activities such as data input, and cross-checking of the\n business system by software instead of the clerical staff members."},{"label":"c","text":"Replacing manned stores with unmanned stores run by cameras and an electronic\n payment system for analysis of IC tags and images."},{"label":"d","text":"Replacing transfer of stored products through manual operations by using a forklift or\n something similar with an automated warehouse system where computer control has\n rendered human labor obsolete."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'RPA (robotic process automation) uses software robots to perform standardized routine clerical work such as data input and cross-checking in business systems in place of office staff. Assembly robots, unmanned stores, and automated warehouses are physical automation, not RPA.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q61)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q61. Which of the following is an example of RPA that is used to proceed with business
 innovation with the aim of resolving management issues, such as a shortage of staff members?

 a) Deploying robots for assembly work instead of employees engaged in the assembly of
 components on the manufacturing line.
 b) Processing standardized routine activities such as data input, and cross-checking of the
 business system by software instead of the clerical staff members.
 c) Replacing manned stores with unmanned stores run by cameras and an electronic
 payment system for analysis of IC tags and images.
 d) Replacing transfer of stored products through manual operations by using a forklift or
 something similar with an automated warehouse system where computer control has
 rendered human labor obsolete.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  62,
  'Q62. Which of the following is a system where the use of a state transition diagram is
 appropriate when the system is designed?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.18,117.13],"text":"Q62.\nWhich of the following is a system where the use of a state transition diagram is\nappropriate when the system is designed?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,508.03,136.21],"text":"a) Electricity charge calculation system that calculates charges based on the amount of"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,531.64,172.21],"text":"power usage from power meter readings.\nb) Greenhouse control system that keeps the environment in a greenhouse optimal based on"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,502.23,208.21],"text":"the data of an installed sensor.\nc) Inventory control system that performs the collection and aggregation of inventory"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,531.96,262.21],"text":"assets at the end of every month and at the time of settlement.\nd) System that measures the operational status of the system resources and creates a report."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Electricity charge calculation system that calculates charges based on the amount of\n power usage from power meter readings."},{"label":"b","text":"Greenhouse control system that keeps the environment in a greenhouse optimal based on\n the data of an installed sensor."},{"label":"c","text":"Inventory control system that performs the collection and aggregation of inventory\n assets at the end of every month and at the time of settlement."},{"label":"d","text":"System that measures the operational status of the system resources and creates a report."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A greenhouse control system is the best fit for a state transition diagram, because it reacts to sensor events and changes between states such as heating, cooling, and idle. The other systems are batch-style calculation or reporting processes with no meaningful state changes driven by events.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q62)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q62. Which of the following is a system where the use of a state transition diagram is
 appropriate when the system is designed?

 a) Electricity charge calculation system that calculates charges based on the amount of
 power usage from power meter readings.
 b) Greenhouse control system that keeps the environment in a greenhouse optimal based on
 the data of an installed sensor.
 c) Inventory control system that performs the collection and aggregation of inventory
 assets at the end of every month and at the time of settlement.
 d) System that measures the operational status of the system resources and creates a report.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
