(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  63,
  'Q63. Which of the following is an explanation of the digital divide?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,283.74,409.47,297.19],"text":"Q63.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the digital divide?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,501.32,334.21],"text":"a) It refers to an economic or social gap that occurs due to differences in abilities and"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,502.35,370.21],"text":"opportunities to use PCs and communications.\nb) It refers to communications and broadcast services that any citizen can access with"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,528.63,406.21],"text":"standard charges, without any differences between regions.\nc) It refers to the ability of citizens to participate directly in the policies of government and"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,531.99,442.21],"text":"autonomous bodies by using the Internet.\nd) It refers to the provision of all services in a single place for each event of the daily life of"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,308.03,478.21],"text":"citizens or each field of corporate activity."},{"type":"code","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 23 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to an economic or social gap that occurs due to differences in abilities and\n opportunities to use PCs and communications."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to communications and broadcast services that any citizen can access with\n standard charges, without any differences between regions."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to the ability of citizens to participate directly in the policies of government and\n autonomous bodies by using the Internet."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the provision of all services in a single place for each event of the daily life of\n citizens or each field of corporate activity."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The digital divide is the economic or social gap caused by differences in the ability and opportunity to use PCs, the Internet, and other information and communication technology. Uniform-price access to services is universal service, citizen participation via the Internet is e-democracy, and providing all services in one place is a one-stop service.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q63)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q63. Which of the following is an explanation of the digital divide?

 a) It refers to an economic or social gap that occurs due to differences in abilities and
 opportunities to use PCs and communications.
 b) It refers to communications and broadcast services that any citizen can access with
 standard charges, without any differences between regions.
 c) It refers to the ability of citizens to participate directly in the policies of government and
 autonomous bodies by using the Internet.
 d) It refers to the provision of all services in a single place for each event of the daily life of
 citizens or each field of corporate activity.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  64,
  'Q64. Procurement is performed by using the comprehensive evaluation bidding method under the conditions shown below. When the bidding prices and technology points of Companies A to D are as shown in the table below, which of the following is the successful bidder?

[Conditions]
(1) The bidder with the highest comprehensive evaluation points obtained by summing up the price points and the technology points is the successful bidder.
(2) The target price is 100,000 dollars. Any bids that exceed the target price are not evaluated.
(3) The price points are calculated by the formula shown below.
[1 − (Bidding price / Target price)] × 100

[Bidding price and technology points of Companies A to D]
 | Bidding price (1,000 dollars) | Technology points
Company A | 70 | 50
Company B | 80 | 65
Company C | 90 | 80
Company D | 110 | 100',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q64. Procurement is performed by using the comprehensive evaluation bidding method under the conditions shown below. When the bidding prices and technology points of Companies A to D are as shown in the table below, which of the following is the successful bidder?\n\n[Conditions]\n(1) The bidder with the highest comprehensive evaluation points obtained by summing up the price points and the technology points is the successful bidder.\n(2) The target price is 100,000 dollars. Any bids that exceed the target price are not evaluated.\n(3) The price points are calculated by the formula shown below.\n[1 − (Bidding price / Target price)] × 100\n\n[Bidding price and technology points of Companies A to D]\n | Bidding price (1,000 dollars) | Technology points\nCompany A | 70 | 50\nCompany B | 80 | 65\nCompany C | 90 | 80\nCompany D | 110 | 100"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Company A"},{"label":"b","text":"Company B"},{"label":"c","text":"Company C"},{"label":"d","text":"Company D"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Company C wins. Price points are (1 − price / 100) × 100: A = 30, B = 20, C = 10, giving totals A = 30 + 50 = 80, B = 20 + 65 = 85, C = 10 + 80 = 90. Company D has the most technology points but its 110,000 dollar bid exceeds the target price, so it is not evaluated.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
