  'A',
  65,
  'Q65. Which of the following is an explanation of green procurement (sustainable
 procurement)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,451.26,533.09,499.63],"text":"Q65.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of green procurement (sustainable\nprocurement)?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,505.43,528.38,536.71],"text":"a) It refers to a certificate that enables commercial trading of green power that is generated"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,541.43,507.81,572.71],"text":"from natural energy such as sunlight, biomass, wind power, and geothermal heat.\nb) It refers to a mass promotion of environmental protection activities and fund raising"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,577.43,473.4,608.71],"text":"from investors for the environmental protection\nc) It refers to a preferential purchase of products and services that exert a lower"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,613.43,530.05,644.71],"text":"environmental burden.\nd) It refers to international standards that employ labels to certify that a product contributes"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,649.43,241.5,662.71],"text":"to environmental protection."},{"type":"code","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 24 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a certificate that enables commercial trading of green power that is generated\n from natural energy such as sunlight, biomass, wind power, and geothermal heat."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to a mass promotion of environmental protection activities and fund raising\n from investors for the environmental protection"},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to a preferential purchase of products and services that exert a lower\n environmental burden."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to international standards that employ labels to certify that a product contributes\n to environmental protection."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Green procurement means preferentially buying products and services with a lower environmental burden. Tradable green power certificates, environmental fund raising, and eco-labels are related environmental schemes but not procurement policies.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
