(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  66,
  'Q66. Among the mechanisms that are utilized on the Internet, which of the following is an
 explanation of crowdfunding?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.11,100.21],"text":"Q66.\nAmong the mechanisms that are utilized on the Internet, which of the following is an\nexplanation of crowdfunding?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,513.93,136.21],"text":"a) It refers to a company placing an order with a person who is judged to be qualified to"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,492.76,190.21],"text":"outsource work to an unspecified number of people on the website through prior\nnotification of business operations.\nb) It refers to a web service for individuals that displays information on the account"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,523.42,244.21],"text":"transactions of multiple financial institutions at once by a single authentication through\nprior registration of multiple account information.\nc) It refers to payment from an advertiser to a website operator when a person who is"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,514.75,298.21],"text":"browsing the website purchases a product from the EC site by using the link from the\npublished advertisement.\nd) It refers to raising money from an unspecified number of individuals who support a"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[102.12,302.93,527.42,334.21],"text":"business project that is published on the website, and who expect to obtain products and\nrights in return."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a company placing an order with a person who is judged to be qualified to\n outsource work to an unspecified number of people on the website through prior\n notification of business operations."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to a web service for individuals that displays information on the account\n transactions of multiple financial institutions at once by a single authentication through\n prior registration of multiple account information."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to payment from an advertiser to a website operator when a person who is\n browsing the website purchases a product from the EC site by using the link from the\n published advertisement."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to raising money from an unspecified number of individuals who support a\n business project that is published on the website, and who expect to obtain products and\n rights in return."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Crowdfunding raises money from an unspecified number of individuals who support a project published on a website, often in return for products or rights. Outsourcing work to many people online is crowdsourcing, viewing multiple bank accounts at once is account aggregation, and paying a site when a link leads to a purchase is affiliate marketing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q66)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q66. Among the mechanisms that are utilized on the Internet, which of the following is an
 explanation of crowdfunding?

 a) It refers to a company placing an order with a person who is judged to be qualified to
 outsource work to an unspecified number of people on the website through prior
 notification of business operations.
 b) It refers to a web service for individuals that displays information on the account
 transactions of multiple financial institutions at once by a single authentication through
 prior registration of multiple account information.
 c) It refers to payment from an advertiser to a website operator when a person who is
 browsing the website purchases a product from the EC site by using the link from the
 published advertisement.
 d) It refers to raising money from an unspecified number of individuals who support a
 business project that is published on the website, and who expect to obtain products and
 rights in return.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  67,
  'Q67. Which of the following is a characteristic of the maturity stage in the product life cycle?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,358.69,533.08,387.19],"text":"Q67.\nWhich of the following is a characteristic of the maturity stage in the product life cycle?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,412.91,502.4,426.19],"text":"a) Demand decreases and some companies start withdrawing. A company determines"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,430.91,524.97,480.19],"text":"whether it can be a strong player in this stage and considers advancing into alternative\nmarkets.\nb) Demand grows, and the product differentiation and segmentation of the market become"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,484.91,516.88,534.19],"text":"evident. Competition intensifies, and it becomes important to add new models and\nreduce cost.\nc) Demand is partial, and cultivation of new demand is the key to success or failure. It is"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,538.91,515.76,570.19],"text":"necessary to persuade specific targets with conviction.\nd) The market begins to understand the value of a product. Both the product line and the"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[102.12,574.91,516.41,588.19],"text":"channel must be expanded. Sales increase, but investment is also needed in this stage."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Demand decreases and some companies start withdrawing. A company determines\n whether it can be a strong player in this stage and considers advancing into alternative\n markets."},{"label":"b","text":"Demand grows, and the product differentiation and segmentation of the market become\n evident. Competition intensifies, and it becomes important to add new models and\n reduce cost."},{"label":"c","text":"Demand is partial, and cultivation of new demand is the key to success or failure. It is\n necessary to persuade specific targets with conviction."},{"label":"d","text":"The market begins to understand the value of a product. Both the product line and the\n channel must be expanded. Sales increase, but investment is also needed in this stage."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The official answer describes growing demand, visible product differentiation and market segmentation, intensifying competition, and the need for new models and cost reduction. In the maturity stage the market fills up, so firms compete through differentiation, segmentation, and cost. The other choices describe decline (falling demand and withdrawal), introduction (creating new demand), and growth (expanding the line and channels with heavy investment).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q67)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q67. Which of the following is a characteristic of the maturity stage in the product life cycle?

 a) Demand decreases and some companies start withdrawing. A company determines
 whether it can be a strong player in this stage and considers advancing into alternative
 markets.
 b) Demand grows, and the product differentiation and segmentation of the market become
 evident. Competition intensifies, and it becomes important to add new models and
 reduce cost.
 c) Demand is partial, and cultivation of new demand is the key to success or failure. It is
 necessary to persuade specific targets with conviction.
 d) The market begins to understand the value of a product. Both the product line and the
 channel must be expanded. Sales increase, but investment is also needed in this stage.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  68,
  'Q68. Which of the following is mostly tacit knowledge?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,627.72,353.87,641.17],"text":"Q68.\nWhich of the following is mostly tacit knowledge?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,646.91,452.29,713.11],"text":"a) A list of countries and their capitals\nb) An inventory of assets\nc) Contents of a washing machine manual\nd) How to ride a bicycle"},{"type":"code","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 25 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A list of countries and their capitals"},{"label":"b","text":"An inventory of assets"},{"label":"c","text":"Contents of a washing machine manual"},{"label":"d","text":"How to ride a bicycle"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'How to ride a bicycle is tacit knowledge, which is gained by experience and is hard to put into words or documents. A list of capitals, an asset inventory, and a washing machine manual are explicit knowledge already written down.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q68)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q68. Which of the following is mostly tacit knowledge?

 a) A list of countries and their capitals b) An inventory of assets
 c) Contents of a washing machine manual d) How to ride a bicycle',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-april',
  'A',
  69,
  'Q69. Which of the following is an appropriate example of a core technology for the creation
 of competitive advantage?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.1,100.21],"text":"Q69.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate example of a core technology for the creation\nof competitive advantage?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,518.26,136.21],"text":"a) It is a development technology that combines general components with the purpose of"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,509.42,172.21],"text":"fast-track development and fast-track market introduction of products.\nb) It is a device technology that employs the same CPU core as that of competitors and"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,510.34,208.21],"text":"enhances the portability of software.\nc) It is an idle reduction technology of an automobile engine that cannot be imitated by"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,533.01,244.21],"text":"competitors.\nd) It is an interface technology whose purpose is to create standard interfaces by forming an"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,266.13,262.21],"text":"alliance and use them commonly."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a development technology that combines general components with the purpose of\n fast-track development and fast-track market introduction of products."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a device technology that employs the same CPU core as that of competitors and\n enhances the portability of software."},{"label":"c","text":"It is an idle reduction technology of an automobile engine that cannot be imitated by\n competitors."},{"label":"d","text":"It is an interface technology whose purpose is to create standard interfaces by forming an\n alliance and use them commonly."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A core technology for competitive advantage is unique and hard for rivals to imitate, like an engine idle reduction technology that competitors cannot copy. Using general components, the same CPU core as competitors, or jointly standardized interfaces does not set the company apart.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q69)',
  ARRAY[26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q69. Which of the following is an appropriate example of a core technology for the creation
 of competitive advantage?

 a) It is a development technology that combines general components with the purpose of
 fast-track development and fast-track market introduction of products.
 b) It is a device technology that employs the same CPU core as that of competitors and
 enhances the portability of software.
 c) It is an idle reduction technology of an automobile engine that cannot be imitated by
