  '[{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,617.22,539.11,648.67],"text":"Q71.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of cryptocurrency mining that is enabled by\nblock chain?"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,653.39,527.96,720.67],"text":"a) Making payments or settlements by using cryptocurrency in brick-and-mortar stores\nb) Obtaining capital gain by buying and selling cryptocurrency\nc) Obtaining cryptocurrency as a reward for participation in checking or record calculation"},{"type":"text","page":26,"bbox":[84.12,725.39,442.87,756.67],"text":"of cryptocurrency transactions\nd) Transferring money to an individual or organization in cryptocurrency"},{"type":"code","page":26,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 26 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Making payments or settlements by using cryptocurrency in brick-and-mortar stores"},{"label":"b","text":"Obtaining capital gain by buying and selling cryptocurrency"},{"label":"c","text":"Obtaining cryptocurrency as a reward for participation in checking or record calculation\n of cryptocurrency transactions"},{"label":"d","text":"Transferring money to an individual or organization in cryptocurrency"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Mining means taking part in verifying cryptocurrency transactions and doing the calculations to record them in the blockchain, and receiving cryptocurrency as a reward. Paying in shops, trading for capital gains, and sending money are uses of cryptocurrency, not mining.',
