  'A',
  74,
  'Q74. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the constituent elements of IoT?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,518.76,532.54,550.21],"text":"Q74.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of the constituent elements of IoT?"},{"type":"text","page":27,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,502.23,622.21],"text":"a) They cover all items that can connect to the Internet or a closed network.\nb) They cover all tangible objects except humans and living things.\nc) They cover digital type devices, and do not cover analog type devices.\nd) They cover only devices that autonomously collect data and perform data analysis."},{"type":"code","page":27,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 27 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"They cover all items that can connect to the Internet or a closed network."},{"label":"b","text":"They cover all tangible objects except humans and living things."},{"label":"c","text":"They cover digital type devices, and do not cover analog type devices."},{"label":"d","text":"They cover only devices that autonomously collect data and perform data analysis."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The constituent elements of IoT include everything that can connect to the Internet or a closed network. IoT is not limited to non-living objects, digital devices, or devices that analyse data themselves; analog sensors with a network interface, wearables on people, and simple data-sending devices all count.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023S, FE, Subject-A, Q74)',
  ARRAY[27]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q74. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the constituent elements of IoT?

 a) They cover all items that can connect to the Internet or a closed network.
 b) They cover all tangible objects except humans and living things.
 c) They cover digital type devices, and do not cover analog type devices.
 d) They cover only devices that autonomously collect data and perform data analysis.',
