  '[{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,402.81,459.13],"text":"Q77.\nWhich of the following is a description of the ABC analysis?"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,519.37,478.21],"text":"a) It analyzes a region in more detail on the basis of various data (population, purchasing"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,520.23,514.21],"text":"power, etc.) by dividing the region into a grid with multiple sections.\nb) It arranges products in order of high sales or high gross profit, divides them into levels"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,523.33,568.21],"text":"on the basis of the cumulative ratio, and then plans to increase the volume of product\nsales at high levels.\nc) It classifies and aggregates multiple parts of the survey data by factor, and analyzes the"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,511.7,604.21],"text":"sales capacity and status of purchasing the same products.\nd) It repeatedly surveys the same panelist (respondent) many times. This data is used to"},{"type":"text","page":28,"bbox":[102.12,608.93,374.4,622.21],"text":"understand regional trends or changes in the purchasers."},{"type":"code","page":28,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 28 –"}]'::jsonb,
