  'Blank A is South: with the strict test UnempRate > UnempRateHigh, South (15.0) replaces the high value first and West''s equal 15.0 does not replace it. Blank B is ????: when every rate is 0.0, the test 0.0 > 0.0 is never true, so CityHigh keeps its initial value. Blank C is West: after changing the operators to ≥ and ≤, every city with 100.0 satisfies 100.0 ≤ UnempRateLow (initially 100.0), so the last city read, West, ends up as CityLow. Blank D is North: rerunning test case 1 with ≤, North''s 10.0 ties East''s and overwrites it. Blanks E and F are −0.1 and 100.1: starting the high value below 0 and the low value above 100 guarantees the first city always updates both, while keeping the strict > and < comparisons so ties keep the first city.',
