  'Blank A is str[i] < ''0'' || str[i] > ''9'', which is true for any non-digit character (the && version can never be true). Blank B is i = len - 1, j = 0; i >= 0; i--, j++, copying characters from the last to the first so that j ends at len for the terminating NUL. Blank C is str[len - 1 - i], the character mirrored from position i. In add, blank D is digit % 10 (the digit to store) and blank E is digit / 10 (the carry into the next position). Blank F is −1, the value doLychrelProcess returns when no palindrome appears within the maximum attempts. In Subquestion 2, blank G is str - 1, because after skipping a string of only zeros str points at the NUL, so stepping back one gives the last ''0''; blank H is strNum, skipLeadingZeros(strNum), strlen(skipLeadingZeros(strNum)) + 1, which moves the digits after the leading zeros to the front of strNum, with + 1 so the NUL terminator is copied too.',
