  '2023-october',
  'A',
  1,
  'Q1. In a school class, 13 students play basketball and 19 play football. Among them, 8
 students play both. Further, 7 students play neither. How many students are there in the
 class?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,494.53,82.21],"text":"Q1.  In a school class, 13 students play basketball and 19 play football. Among them, 8"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,86.93,507.74,136.21],"text":"students play both. Further, 7 students play neither. How many students are there in the\nclass?"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,140.93,470.1,172.21],"text":"a) 17\nb) 31\nc) 33\nd) 47"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"17"},{"label":"b","text":"31"},{"label":"c","text":"33"},{"label":"d","text":"47"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is 31 students. By inclusion-exclusion, the students who play at least one sport number 13 + 19 − 8 = 24, because the 8 who play both were counted twice. Adding the 7 who play neither gives 24 + 7 = 31. Simply adding 13 + 19 + 7 = 39 or similar totals double-counts the overlap.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q1)',
  ARRAY[3]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
