),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  2,
  'Q2. n is a binary integer represented in two’s complement. Which of the following operations
 get the value 7 × n using only bit shifting and an addition or subtraction operation?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,176.93,528.78,208.21],"text":"Q2.  n is a binary integer represented in two’s complement. Which of the following operations"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,486.44,244.21],"text":"get the value 7 × n using only bit shifting and an addition or subtraction operation?"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,369.09,334.21],"text":"a) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then add n to the result.\nb) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result.\nc) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then add n to the result.\nd) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Shift n 2 bits to the left, then add n to the result."},{"label":"b","text":"Shift n 2 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."},{"label":"c","text":"Shift n 3 bits to the left, then add n to the result."},{"label":"d","text":"Shift n 3 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is to shift n 3 bits to the left and then subtract n. A 3-bit left shift multiplies by 2³ = 8, and 8n − n = 7n. Shifting 2 bits gives 4n, so adding or subtracting n would give only 5n or 3n, and 8n + n would be 9n.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q2)',
  ARRAY[3]::int[],
