  3,
  'Q3. A parking lot has 10 parking spaces in a row, and 7 cars are parked at random parking spaces. What is the probability that the three empty places are adjacent to each other?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q3. A parking lot has 10 parking spaces in a row, and 7 cars are parked at random parking spaces. What is the probability that the three empty places are adjacent to each other?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1/90"},{"label":"b","text":"1/72"},{"label":"c","text":"1/15"},{"label":"d","text":"1/12"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The probability is 1/15. Choosing which 3 of the 10 spaces stay empty gives C(10,3) = 120 equally likely outcomes. Three adjacent spaces in a row of 10 can start at positions 1 through 8, so there are 8 favourable outcomes, and 8/120 = 1/15.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
