(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  5,
  'Q5. Which of the following expressions in postfix notation is equivalent to the expression
 2+5×3+4 in infix notation? Here, the operator “×” has higher precedence than “+”.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,546.89,510.28,577.15],"text":"Q5.  Which of the following expressions in postfix notation is equivalent to the expression"},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,581.87,485.86,612.07],"text":"2+5×3+4 in infix notation? Here, the operator “×” has higher precedence than “+”."},{"type":"text","page":3,"bbox":[84.12,617.87,392.83,649.15],"text":"a) 2 5 3 4 × + +\nb) 2 5 + 3 4 × +\nc) 2 5 3 + × 4 +\nd) 2 5 3 × + 4 +"},{"type":"code","page":3,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 3 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"2 5 3 4 × + +"},{"label":"b","text":"2 5 + 3 4 × +"},{"label":"c","text":"2 5 3 + × 4 +"},{"label":"d","text":"2 5 3 × + 4 +"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct postfix form is 2 5 3 × + 4 +. Because × binds tighter, the expression is evaluated as (2 + (5 × 3)) + 4, so 5 3 × is formed first, then added to 2, and finally 4 is added. Option 2 5 + 3 4 × + would mean (2 + 5) + (3 × 4), which changes the meaning.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q5)',
  ARRAY[3]::int[],
