  '2023-october',
  'A',
  6,
  'Q6. There is communication data that consists of five characters “A”, “B”, “C”, “D”, and “E” that have different appearance frequencies, and in order to compress the data by using Huffman coding, the code table shown below is created. Which of the following is an appropriate code that should be inserted in the blank?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q6. There is communication data that consists of five characters “A”, “B”, “C”, “D”, and “E” that have different appearance frequencies, and in order to compress the data by using Huffman coding, the code table shown below is created. Which of the following is an appropriate code that should be inserted in the blank?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-october-a-q06-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"001"},{"label":"b","text":"010"},{"label":"c","text":"101"},{"label":"d","text":"110"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The code for D is 110. Huffman codes must be prefix-free, and the existing codes 00, 01, 10 and 111 leave only the branch 11x for D besides E''s 111, so D gets 110. This also matches the construction: the two least frequent symbols D (13%) and E (12%) are merged first and become siblings 110 and 111. Codes 001, 010 and 101 would start with A''s, B''s or C''s code and could not be decoded uniquely.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
