(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  7,
  'Q7. When the series of stack operations below is performed on an empty stack, which of the
 following is the data that is read out by the last READ operation? Here, “PUSH x” is the
 operation to put data x in the stack, “POP” is used to retrieve data from the stack, and
 “READ” is used to read data from the top of the stack without removing the original data.

 PUSH 2 → READ → PUSH 3 → PUSH 6 → POP → READ → PUSH 4
 →READ → PUSH 7 → PUSH 5→ POP → POP → READ',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,346.97,521.12,378.25],"text":"Q7.  When the series of stack operations below is performed on an empty stack, which of the"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[85.74,382.97,523.26,432.25],"text":"following is the data that is read out by the last READ operation?  Here, “PUSH x” is the\noperation to put data x in the stack, “POP” is used to retrieve data from the stack, and\n“READ” is used to read data from the top of the stack without removing the original data."},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,454.97,477.94,504.25],"text":"PUSH 2 → READ → PUSH 3 → PUSH 6 → POP → READ → PUSH 4\n→READ → PUSH 7 → PUSH 5→ POP → POP → READ"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[84.12,507.2,464.6,522.68],"text":"a) 2\nb) 3\nc) 4\nd) 6"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"2"},{"label":"b","text":"3"},{"label":"c","text":"4"},{"label":"d","text":"6"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The last READ returns 4. Tracing the stack (bottom to top): after PUSH 2, PUSH 3, PUSH 6 and POP it is [2, 3]; PUSH 4 gives [2, 3, 4]; PUSH 7 and PUSH 5 give [2, 3, 4, 7, 5]; the two POPs remove 5 and 7, leaving 4 on top. READ looks at the top without removing it, so 4 is read.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q7)',
