  8,
  'Q8. In the binary search tree below, when a new node of value 11 is inserted, where will this insertion be made?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q8. In the binary search tree below, when a new node of value 11 is inserted, where will this insertion be made?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-october-a-q08-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Left child of 16"},{"label":"b","text":"Left child of 23"},{"label":"c","text":"Right child of 3"},{"label":"d","text":"Right child of 10"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The new node becomes the right child of 10. Starting at the root, 11 < 14 goes left to 7, 11 > 7 goes right to 12, 11 < 12 goes left to 10, and 11 > 10 goes right, where the position is empty. In a binary search tree, insertion always follows these comparisons down to an empty child slot.',
