  10,
  'Q10. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning XML?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":5,"bbox":[65.22,353.51,453.14,383.77],"text":"Q10.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description concerning XML?"},{"type":"text","page":5,"bbox":[84.12,389.51,528.61,474.79],"text":"a) It is based on HTML and expands its functions.\nb) It requires a dedicated editor for writing XML documents.\nc) It integrates the logical structure and display style of documents.\nd) It enables users to define the attribute information and logical structure of documents by"},{"type":"text","page":5,"bbox":[102.12,479.51,229.49,492.79],"text":"using the user’s own tags."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is based on HTML and expands its functions."},{"label":"b","text":"It requires a dedicated editor for writing XML documents."},{"label":"c","text":"It integrates the logical structure and display style of documents."},{"label":"d","text":"It enables users to define the attribute information and logical structure of documents by\n using the user’s own tags."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'XML lets users define their own tags to describe the logical structure and attributes of a document. It is a markup meta-language derived from SGML, not an extension of HTML, and can be written in any text editor. XML describes structure and content, while the display style is kept separate, for example in stylesheets such as XSL or CSS.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
