(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  12,
  'Q12. Which of the following is an appropriate CPU operation associated with cache
 memory?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,487.19,100.21],"text":"Q12.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate CPU operation associated with cache\nmemory?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,458.98,190.21],"text":"a) When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from ROM.\nb) When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory.\nc) When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the cache memory.\nd) When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from ROM."},{"label":"b","text":"When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory."},{"label":"c","text":"When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the cache memory."},{"label":"d","text":"When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches the data from main memory, normally also copying it into the cache. A cache hit means the data is already in the cache, so it is read from the cache, not from main memory or ROM. Option c is contradictory, since a miss means the cache does not contain the data.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q12)',
  ARRAY[6]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q12. Which of the following is an appropriate CPU operation associated with cache
 memory?

 a) When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from ROM.
 b) When a cache hit occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory.
 c) When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the cache memory.
 d) When a cache miss occurs, the CPU fetches data from the main memory.',
