  13,
  'Q13. Which of the following is a computer architecture in which a processor executes the
 same instruction on multiple data?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,213.28,513.8,280.15],"text":"Q13.\nWhich of the following is a computer architecture in which a processor executes the\nsame instruction on multiple data?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,284.93,484.05,316.15],"text":"a) MIMD\nb) MISD\nc) SIMD\nd) SISD"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"MIMD"},{"label":"b","text":"MISD"},{"label":"c","text":"SIMD"},{"label":"d","text":"SISD"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'SIMD (Single Instruction, Multiple Data) applies one instruction to many data elements at once, as in vector processors and GPU or multimedia extensions. In Flynn''s classification, SISD is a conventional single processor, MIMD is independent processors running different instructions, and MISD applies many instructions to one data stream.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
