 same instruction on multiple data?

 a) MIMD b) MISD c) SIMD d) SISD',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[6]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  14,
  'Q14. ECC is used for error detection and correction in memory. When n+2 redundant bits are
 required for a data bus having a width of 2^n bits, what is the number of redundant bits that
 are required for a data bus having a width of 128 bits?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,320.76,532.53,388.21],"text":"Q14.\nECC is used for error detection and correction in memory. When n+2 redundant bits are\nrequired for a data bus having a width of 2^n bits, what is the number of redundant bits that\nare required for a data bus having a width of 128 bits?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,470.1,424.21],"text":"a) 3\nb) 8\nc) 9\nd) 10"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"3"},{"label":"b","text":"8"},{"label":"c","text":"9"},{"label":"d","text":"10"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Nine redundant bits are needed. A 128-bit bus means 2 to the power n = 128, so n = 7, and the rule n + 2 gives 7 + 2 = 9. A common trap is plugging 128 directly into the formula instead of first finding the exponent n.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q14)',
  ARRAY[6]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q14. ECC is used for error detection and correction in memory. When n+2 redundant bits are
 required for a data bus having a width of 2n bits, what is the number of redundant bits that
 are required for a data bus having a width of 128 bits?

 a) 3 b) 8 c) 9 d) 10',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[6]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  15,
  'Q15. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of grid computing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,489.14,477.19],"text":"Q15.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate explanation of grid computing?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,472.46,514.21],"text":"a) A computing task is distributed to several computers in the network to attain"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,503.95,550.21],"text":"computational capacity.\nb) Physical devices such as computers or network devices are emulated to circumvent"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,524.39,586.21],"text":"compatibility constraints and attain software portability and flexibility.\nc) Requirements are stated as constraints on response time and/or on the temporal validity"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,510.38,622.21],"text":"of sensory data.\nd) Sensing devices are connected to a network to provide feedback and control through"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[85.14,626.76,224.44,658.21],"text":"personal mobile devices."},{"type":"code","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 6 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A computing task is distributed to several computers in the network to attain\n computational capacity."},{"label":"b","text":"Physical devices such as computers or network devices are emulated to circumvent\n compatibility constraints and attain software portability and flexibility."},{"label":"c","text":"Requirements are stated as constraints on response time and/or on the temporal validity\n of sensory data."},{"label":"d","text":"Sensing devices are connected to a network to provide feedback and control through\n personal mobile devices."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Grid computing distributes a computing task across many computers connected by a network so that together they provide large computational capacity, like a single virtual high-performance machine. Emulating physical devices describes virtualization, timing constraints describe real-time systems, and networked sensors with mobile feedback describe IoT.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q15)',
  ARRAY[6]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q15. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of grid computing?

 a) A computing task is distributed to several computers in the network to attain
 computational capacity.
 b) Physical devices such as computers or network devices are emulated to circumvent
 compatibility constraints and attain software portability and flexibility.
 c) Requirements are stated as constraints on response time and/or on the temporal validity
 of sensory data.
 d) Sensing devices are connected to a network to provide feedback and control through
 personal mobile devices.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[6]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
