  16,
  'Q16. Which of the following is an RAID configuration that deploys two parity records to
 different disk drives enabling two simultaneous disk drive failures in the same RAID group
 to be recovered?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,527.59,118.21],"text":"Q16.\nWhich of the following is an RAID configuration that deploys two parity records to\ndifferent disk drives enabling two simultaneous disk drive failures in the same RAID group\nto be recovered?"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,493.43,154.21],"text":"a) RAID0\nb) RAID1\nc) RAID5\nd) RAID6"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"RAID0"},{"label":"b","text":"RAID1"},{"label":"c","text":"RAID5"},{"label":"d","text":"RAID6"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'RAID6 stores two independent parity blocks for each stripe on different disks, so data survives the simultaneous failure of two disks in the group. RAID5 has only one distributed parity block and tolerates just one failure, RAID1 is mirroring and RAID0 is striping with no redundancy.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
