  17,
  'Q17. Which of the following occurs when a program attempts to access a page that is
 mapped in the virtual address space but is not located in the main memory? Here, the OS
 supports paging.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,194.76,515.63,244.21],"text":"Q17.\nWhich of the following occurs when a program attempts to access a page that is\nmapped in the virtual address space but is not located in the main memory? Here, the OS\nsupports paging."},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,421.39,298.21],"text":"a) Fatal error\nb) Page fault\nc) Scheduling error\nd) Segmentation fault"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Fatal error"},{"label":"b","text":"Page fault"},{"label":"c","text":"Scheduling error"},{"label":"d","text":"Segmentation fault"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A page fault occurs when a program accesses a page that is valid in its virtual address space but is not currently loaded in main memory. The OS handles the interrupt by loading the page from secondary storage and resuming the program. A segmentation fault, by contrast, is an access to an address the process is not allowed to use.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q17)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
