  '3.0',
  'Q17. Which of the following occurs when a program attempts to access a page that is
 mapped in the virtual address space but is not located in the main memory? Here, the OS
 supports paging.

 a) Fatal error b) Page fault
 c) Scheduling error d) Segmentation fault',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  18,
  'Q18. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the round robin
 process scheduling method?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,320.76,496.72,370.21],"text":"Q18.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description concerning the round robin\nprocess scheduling method?"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,510.73,406.21],"text":"a) CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of priority specified in advance"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,528.36,442.21],"text":"when a particular event occurs.\nb) CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of processing time from shortest to"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,491.25,478.21],"text":"longest.\nc) CPU resources are allocated to the first executable process in the queue when an"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,517.38,514.21],"text":"interval-timer interrupt is generated.\nd) CPU resources are allocated to the process that needs to start immediately when some"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[102.12,518.93,247.46,532.21],"text":"kind of interrupt is generated."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of priority specified in advance\n when a particular event occurs."},{"label":"b","text":"CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of processing time from shortest to\n longest."},{"label":"c","text":"CPU resources are allocated to the first executable process in the queue when an\n interval-timer interrupt is generated."},{"label":"d","text":"CPU resources are allocated to the process that needs to start immediately when some\n kind of interrupt is generated."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'In round robin scheduling, each process runs for a fixed time slice; when the interval-timer interrupt fires, the running process goes to the back of the queue and the CPU is given to the first executable process in the queue. Allocating by priority describes priority scheduling, and shortest processing time first describes SPT (shortest job first).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q18)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q18. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the round robin
 process scheduling method?

 a) CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of priority specified in advance
 when a particular event occurs.
 b) CPU resources are allocated to each process in order of processing time from shortest to
 longest.
 c) CPU resources are allocated to the first executable process in the queue when an
 interval-timer interrupt is generated.
 d) CPU resources are allocated to the process that needs to start immediately when some
 kind of interrupt is generated.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
