  '[{"label":"a","text":"Adder circuit"},{"label":"b","text":"Capacitor"},{"label":"c","text":"Flip-flop"},{"label":"d","text":"NAND gate"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A flip-flop is a sequential circuit with two stable states, so it can store one bit and is used in registers and SRAM. An adder and a NAND gate are combinational circuits whose outputs depend only on current inputs, and a capacitor is an electronic component rather than a logic circuit.',
