  21,
  'Q21. Which of the following is equivalent to the logic circuit shown below?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,175.74,449.14,189.19],"text":"Q21.\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the logic circuit shown below?"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[94.02,285.23,112.32,298.51],"text":"a)"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[301.44,285.23,319.92,298.51],"text":"b)"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[94.02,339.23,106.32,352.51],"text":"c)"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[301.44,339.23,314.46,352.51],"text":"d)"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-october-a-q21-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2023-october-a-q21-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2023-october-a-q21-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2023-october-a-q21-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2023-october-a-q21-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The equivalent circuit is an AND gate with inputs NOT A, B and C. B and C enter a NAND gate giving NOT(B·C), and this goes into a NOR gate with A, so the output is NOT(A + NOT(B·C)). By De Morgan''s law this equals NOT A · B · C, which is exactly an inverter on A feeding a 3-input AND with B and C.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
