  22,
  'Q22. A power supply unit has a rated output power of 500 watts and an efficiency of 80%. In
 order to obtain an output power of 500 watts from this power supply unit, how many watts
 is the minimum input power?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,430.14,531.37,515.59],"text":"Q22.\nA power supply unit has a rated output power of 500 watts and an efficiency of 80%. In\norder to obtain an output power of 500 watts from this power supply unit, how many watts\nis the minimum input power?\n\na) 100\nb) 400\nc) 625\nd) 900"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"100"},{"label":"b","text":"400"},{"label":"c","text":"625"},{"label":"d","text":"900"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The minimum input power is 625 watts. Efficiency is output divided by input, so input = 500 ÷ 0.8 = 625 W; the extra 125 W is lost as heat. Answering 400 W comes from wrongly multiplying 500 by 0.8.',
