  'Q27. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the primary role
 of an SQL query optimizer?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,410.76,528.08,460.15],"text":"Q27.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate description concerning the primary role\nof an SQL query optimizer?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,436.73,532.21],"text":"a) It determines the most efficient way to execute a query.\nb) It minimizes the number of rows in a result set.\nc) It parses a query and improves it for efficient network transmission.\nd) It stores the results of frequently used queries in a cache."},{"type":"code","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 9 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It determines the most efficient way to execute a query."},{"label":"b","text":"It minimizes the number of rows in a result set."},{"label":"c","text":"It parses a query and improves it for efficient network transmission."},{"label":"d","text":"It stores the results of frequently used queries in a cache."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The query optimizer determines the most efficient way to execute a query by comparing possible execution plans, such as index use and join order, typically based on cost estimates. It does not change the result rows, does not handle network transmission, and caching results is a separate function.',
