  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A router forwards packets at the network layer, so it looks up the destination IP address in its routing table to choose the next hop. MAC addresses are layer 2 identifiers that only matter within a single link and are rewritten at each hop, and source addresses do not decide where a packet goes.',
