 c) Source IP address d) Source MAC address',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[10]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following is a feature of a switching hub (layer 2 switch) network device?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,645.72,530.8,659.17],"text":"Q31.\nWhich of the following is a feature of a switching hub (layer 2 switch) network device?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,664.91,493.94,732.19],"text":"a) It breaks a received packet into smaller pieces (fragments) in the network layer.\nb) It dynamically allocates an IP address for a terminal connected to its LAN port.\nc) It forwards a received packet only to its LAN port connected to a device with the"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,736.91,400.69,768.19],"text":"packet’s destination MAC address.\nd) It forwards a received packet to all its LAN ports (broadcast)."},{"type":"code","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 10 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It breaks a received packet into smaller pieces (fragments) in the network layer."},{"label":"b","text":"It dynamically allocates an IP address for a terminal connected to its LAN port."},{"label":"c","text":"It forwards a received packet only to its LAN port connected to a device with the\n packet’s destination MAC address."},{"label":"d","text":"It forwards a received packet to all its LAN ports (broadcast)."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A switching hub learns which MAC addresses are reachable on which port and forwards each frame only to the port leading to the destination MAC address. Forwarding to all ports is the behavior of a repeater hub, fragmentation happens at the network layer in routers, and dynamic IP assignment is done by DHCP.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following is a feature of a switching hub (layer 2 switch) network device?

 a) It breaks a received packet into smaller pieces (fragments) in the network layer.
 b) It dynamically allocates an IP address for a terminal connected to its LAN port.
 c) It forwards a received packet only to its LAN port connected to a device with the
 packet’s destination MAC address.
