  'Cross-site scripting (XSS) injects malicious JavaScript into content that a vulnerable website sends to the victim''s browser, where it runs with that site''s privileges, for example to steal cookies. Cross-site request forgery instead makes the victim''s browser send unwanted requests, and SQL injection targets the database rather than the browser.',
