 security properties that ensure that such information is from the signer and has not been
 altered or tampered with during transmission?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,516.69,190.21],"text":"Q38.\nWhen information, such as an e-mail or a document file, is sent and received with a\ndigital signature via the Internet, which of the following is an appropriate combination of\nsecurity properties that ensure that such information is from the signer and has not been\naltered or tampered with during transmission?\n\na) Atomicity and consistency\nb) Authenticity and integrity\nc) Availability and confidentiality\nd) Durability and isolation"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Atomicity and consistency"},{"label":"b","text":"Authenticity and integrity"},{"label":"c","text":"Availability and confidentiality"},{"label":"d","text":"Durability and isolation"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A digital signature provides authenticity and integrity. Verifying the signature with the signer''s public key confirms that the message came from the holder of the private key, and comparing hash values confirms it was not altered. Atomicity, consistency, isolation and durability are transaction (ACID) properties, and a signature alone does not provide confidentiality.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q38)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q38. When information, such as an e-mail or a document file, is sent and received with a
 digital signature via the Internet, which of the following is an appropriate combination of
 security properties that ensure that such information is from the signer and has not been
 altered or tampered with during transmission?

 a) Atomicity and consistency b) Authenticity and integrity
 c) Availability and confidentiality d) Durability and isolation',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[12]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  39,
  'Q39. Which of the following is an example of a behavior of a key logger?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,212.76,438.48,243.19],"text":"Q39.\nWhich of the following is an example of a behavior of a key logger?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,518.31,280.21],"text":"a) It interrupts the communication between two parties and then collects and falsifies the"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,504.79,334.21],"text":"information being exchanged.\nb) When Internet banking is used, it collects the password entered by the user.\nc) When the user browses movies on a web browser, it arbitrarily displays unintended"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,515.35,370.21],"text":"advertisements for the user.\nd) When the web browser is started, it arbitrarily displays a tool bar that the user has not"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[86.22,374.93,148.8,406.21],"text":"installed."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It interrupts the communication between two parties and then collects and falsifies the\n information being exchanged."},{"label":"b","text":"When Internet banking is used, it collects the password entered by the user."},{"label":"c","text":"When the user browses movies on a web browser, it arbitrarily displays unintended\n advertisements for the user."},{"label":"d","text":"When the web browser is started, it arbitrarily displays a tool bar that the user has not\n installed."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A key logger records the user''s keystrokes, so it can capture a password typed into an Internet banking site and send it to an attacker. Intercepting and falsifying communication is a man-in-the-middle attack, and unwanted advertisements or toolbars are typical of adware.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q39)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q39. Which of the following is an example of a behavior of a key logger?

 a) It interrupts the communication between two parties and then collects and falsifies the
 information being exchanged.
 b) When Internet banking is used, it collects the password entered by the user.
 c) When the user browses movies on a web browser, it arbitrarily displays unintended
 advertisements for the user.
 d) When the web browser is started, it arbitrarily displays a tool bar that the user has not
 installed.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[12]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  40,
  'Q40. Which of the following is a role of a PKI certification authority as a reliable third party?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,527.38,441.19],"text":"Q40. Which of the following is a role of a PKI certification authority as a reliable third party?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,464.93,516.65,567.13],"text":"a) Adding a digital signature to an e-mail body as requested by a user\nb) Enabling the synchronization of time by returning an accurate time to a user’s request\nc) Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the private key of a user or server\nd) Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the public key of a user or server"},{"type":"code","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 12 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Adding a digital signature to an e-mail body as requested by a user"},{"label":"b","text":"Enabling the synchronization of time by returning an accurate time to a user’s request"},{"label":"c","text":"Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the private key of a user or server"},{"label":"d","text":"Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the public key of a user or server"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A certification authority (CA) issues digital certificates that bind a public key to its owner, a user or server, and signs them with the CA''s own private key. It never certifies or handles the user''s private key, which must stay secret with its owner. Returning accurate time is the role of a time-stamping authority.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q40)',
  ARRAY[12]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q40. Which of the following is a role of a PKI certification authority as a reliable third party?

 a) Adding a digital signature to an e-mail body as requested by a user
 b) Enabling the synchronization of time by returning an accurate time to a user’s request
 c) Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the private key of a user or server
 d) Issuing a digital certificate that certifies the public key of a user or server',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[12]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  41,
  'Q41. As shown in the figure below, an application on a client accesses the data in the database on a server via database connection programs. Which of the following is a measure for preventing the leakage of the commands and execution results transmitted between the application and database?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q41. As shown in the figure below, an application on a client accesses the data in the database on a server via database connection programs. Which of the following is a measure for preventing the leakage of the commands and execution results transmitted between the application and database?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-october-a-q41-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Changing the port number from its initial value that the database connection programs\n use for communication in the database management system"},{"label":"b","text":"Encrypting the communication between the database connection programs"},{"label":"c","text":"Restricting the IP addresses of the clients that can access the database connection\n program on the server to only those that are required"},{"label":"d","text":"Setting a password for starting or stopping the database connection program on the\n server"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Encrypting the communication between the database connection programs prevents an eavesdropper who taps the line from reading the commands and results. Changing the port number, restricting client IP addresses or protecting start and stop with a password limit who can connect, but they do nothing about data that has already been intercepted in transit.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q41)',
