  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The encrypted private-key of the website"},{"label":"b","text":"The encrypted public-key of the website"},{"label":"c","text":"The unencrypted private-key of the website"},{"label":"d","text":"The unencrypted public-key of the website"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'An SSL/TLS certificate contains the website''s public key in unencrypted form, together with the owner''s identity and the CA''s signature. The public key is meant to be shared, so there is no need to encrypt it, and the private key is never placed in a certificate because it must stay secret on the server.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
