  'A decision table lists combinations of conditions and the actions to be taken for each combination, which makes complex logic complete and unambiguous. Rectangles connected by lines describe an E-R diagram, control-flow arrows describe a flowchart, and data flowing between external entities, processes and stores describes a DFD.',
