(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  49,
  'Q49. Which of the following is an appropriate description of an extreme programming (XP)
 practice?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,374.76,525.49,406.21],"text":"Q49.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of an extreme programming (XP)\npractice?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,503.01,442.21],"text":"a) After the code is created, and it is confirmed that it can be integrated, test cases are"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,440.69,532.21],"text":"created.\nb) Integration of the code and testing are continuously repeated.\nc) The code that passed the tests is not refactored until the next iteration.\nd) The customer is responsible for the specification of unit tests."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"After the code is created, and it is confirmed that it can be integrated, test cases are\n created."},{"label":"b","text":"Integration of the code and testing are continuously repeated."},{"label":"c","text":"The code that passed the tests is not refactored until the next iteration."},{"label":"d","text":"The customer is responsible for the specification of unit tests."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Extreme programming uses continuous integration, so code is integrated and tested repeatedly, many times a day. XP writes tests before or together with the code (test-driven development), refactors continuously rather than waiting, and has programmers write unit tests while customers specify acceptance tests.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'development-processes'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q49)',
