(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  56,
  'Q56. Which of the following is the most appropriate characteristic of the “big bang” or all-at-once migration method that is one of the system migration methods?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,529.74,172.21],"text":"Q56.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate characteristic of the “big bang” or all-at-\nonce migration method that is one of the system migration methods?\n\na) Additional operational costs are incurred because of parallel operations.\nb) An additional application is required for connecting the old and new systems.\nc) The old and new systems operate in parallel, and migration to the new system is"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,492.37,208.21],"text":"performed at a particular point of time.\nd) The problems that occur during migration to the new system have a big impact."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Additional operational costs are incurred because of parallel operations."},{"label":"b","text":"An additional application is required for connecting the old and new systems."},{"label":"c","text":"The old and new systems operate in parallel, and migration to the new system is\n performed at a particular point of time."},{"label":"d","text":"The problems that occur during migration to the new system have a big impact."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'In big bang migration, the whole old system is replaced by the new one at once, so any problem during migration affects all operations and has a big impact. Its advantage is that no parallel operation or bridging program is needed, which is why the options about parallel-operation costs and connecting software describe other migration methods.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q56)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q56. Which of the following is the most appropriate characteristic of the “big bang” or all-at-once migration method that is one of the system migration methods?

 a) Additional operational costs are incurred because of parallel operations.
 b) An additional application is required for connecting the old and new systems.
 c) The old and new systems operate in parallel, and migration to the new system is
 performed at a particular point of time.
 d) The problems that occur during migration to the new system have a big impact.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  57,
  'Q57. In IT service management, which of the following is a problem management activity that
 is performed proactively?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,229.74,531.35,261.19],"text":"Q57. In IT service management, which of the following is a problem management activity that"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,265.68,212.38,297.13],"text":"is performed proactively?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,508.68,316.21],"text":"a) Analyzing the occurrence trend of incidents and proposing measures that prevent an"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,508.97,352.21],"text":"incident from occurring in the future\nb) Classifying problems that have been detected and recorded, and setting the response"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,526.57,406.21],"text":"priority\nc) Evaluating the effectiveness of a resolution to a critical problem\nd) Monitoring whether an incident occurs again or not for a certain period of time after the"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,199.7,442.15],"text":"problem is resolved"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Analyzing the occurrence trend of incidents and proposing measures that prevent an\n incident from occurring in the future"},{"label":"b","text":"Classifying problems that have been detected and recorded, and setting the response\n priority"},{"label":"c","text":"Evaluating the effectiveness of a resolution to a critical problem"},{"label":"d","text":"Monitoring whether an incident occurs again or not for a certain period of time after the\n problem is resolved"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Proactive problem management analyzes incident trends to find underlying causes and proposes measures before incidents happen. Classifying and prioritizing problems already recorded, evaluating a resolution and monitoring for recurrence are reactive activities that respond to problems that have already occurred.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q57)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q57. In IT service management, which of the following is a problem management activity that
 is performed proactively?

 a) Analyzing the occurrence trend of incidents and proposing measures that prevent an
 incident from occurring in the future
 b) Classifying problems that have been detected and recorded, and setting the response
 priority
 c) Evaluating the effectiveness of a resolution to a critical problem
 d) Monitoring whether an incident occurs again or not for a certain period of time after the
 problem is resolved',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  58,
  'Q58. Which of the following is a method that restores the system to its initial state and restarts
 it when a system failure occurs, that does not accompany preprocessing of a copy before/after
 an update, and that is also called initial program load?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,446.76,533.12,514.21],"text":"Q58.\nWhich of the following is a method that restores the system to its initial state and restarts\nit when a system failure occurs, that does not accompany preprocessing of a copy before/after\nan update, and that is also called initial program load?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,384.15,568.21],"text":"a) Cold start\nb) Rollback\nc) Rollforward\nd) Warm start"},{"type":"code","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 18 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Cold start"},{"label":"b","text":"Rollback"},{"label":"c","text":"Rollforward"},{"label":"d","text":"Warm start"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A cold start, also called initial program load, reinitializes the system and restarts it from its initial state, discarding the state at the time of failure. Rollback and rollforward use before-images and after-images from the log to recover data, and a warm start restarts while keeping some of the processing state.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q58)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q58. Which of the following is a method that restores the system to its initial state and restarts
 it when a system failure occurs, that does not accompany preprocessing of a copy before/after
 an update, and that is also called initial program load?

 a) Cold start b) Rollback
 c) Rollforward d) Warm start',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. Which of the following is an explanation of an audit work paper?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,423.75,81.19],"text":"Q59.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of an audit work paper?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,501.2,118.21],"text":"a) A compilation of the information security promissory letter that is presented to the"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,521.41,154.21],"text":"audited department when the auditor implements an audit\nb) A compilation of the standards and guidelines used by the auditor for implementing an"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,522.17,190.21],"text":"audit\nc) A document that must be disclosed along with the audit report to prove that the auditor"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,532.63,226.21],"text":"has fulfilled his or her obligations with proper attention\nd) An execution record of the auditing procedure by an auditor, and it forms the basis of the"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[102.12,230.93,168.79,244.21],"text":"audit opinion"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A compilation of the information security promissory letter that is presented to the\n audited department when the auditor implements an audit"},{"label":"b","text":"A compilation of the standards and guidelines used by the auditor for implementing an\n audit"},{"label":"c","text":"A document that must be disclosed along with the audit report to prove that the auditor\n has fulfilled his or her obligations with proper attention"},{"label":"d","text":"An execution record of the auditing procedure by an auditor, and it forms the basis of the\n audit opinion"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Audit work papers are the auditor''s records of the audit procedures performed and the evidence obtained, and they form the basis for the audit opinion. They are kept by the auditor as support for the audit report rather than being disclosed with it, and they are not a collection of standards or pledges.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. Which of the following is an explanation of an audit work paper?

 a) A compilation of the information security promissory letter that is presented to the
 audited department when the auditor implements an audit
 b) A compilation of the standards and guidelines used by the auditor for implementing an
 audit
 c) A document that must be disclosed along with the audit report to prove that the auditor
 has fulfilled his or her obligations with proper attention
 d) An execution record of the auditing procedure by an auditor, and it forms the basis of the
 audit opinion',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
