  62,
  'Q62. Which of the following is a purpose of Business Process Management (BPM) in
 corporate activities?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,341.76,533.18,390.13],"text":"Q62.\nWhich of the following is a purpose of Business Process Management (BPM) in\ncorporate activities?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,395.93,360.32,499.21],"text":"a) Analysis and effective use of information resources\nb) Conservation and analysis of customer information\nc) Continuous improvement of business processes\nd) Effective use of management resources"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Analysis and effective use of information resources"},{"label":"b","text":"Conservation and analysis of customer information"},{"label":"c","text":"Continuous improvement of business processes"},{"label":"d","text":"Effective use of management resources"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The purpose of BPM is continuous improvement of business processes, by repeatedly analyzing, designing, executing, monitoring and refining them in a PDCA cycle. Effective use of management resources in general is closer to ERP, and managing customer information belongs to CRM.',
