(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  63,
  'Q63. Which of the following is a scheme where the user establishes a connection to the system
 of a service provider via the Internet and makes online use of only the necessary functions of
 the applications provided by the service provider at the necessary time?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,503.93,533.17,570.13],"text":"Q63.\nWhich of the following is a scheme where the user establishes a connection to the system\nof a service provider via the Internet and makes online use of only the necessary functions of\nthe applications provided by the service provider at the necessary time?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,575.93,490.14,643.21],"text":"a) ERP\nb) SaaS\nc) SCM\nd) XBRL"},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"ERP"},{"label":"b","text":"SaaS"},{"label":"c","text":"SCM"},{"label":"d","text":"XBRL"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'SaaS (Software as a Service) lets users access a provider''s application over the Internet and use only the functions they need, when they need them, usually paying for usage. ERP is integrated enterprise resource management, SCM is supply chain management, and XBRL is a language for financial reporting data.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
