(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  65,
  'Q65. The RFP is presented to each vendor that has responded to an RFI. Which of the
 following should be done beforehand to proceed fairly with the future vendor selection
 processes?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,512.83,388.21],"text":"Q65.\nThe RFP is presented to each vendor that has responded to an RFI. Which of the\nfollowing should be done beforehand to proceed fairly with the future vendor selection\nprocesses?\n\na) Aside from the items of an RFP, giving a high evaluation to a vendor who is familiar"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,510.44,424.21],"text":"with the current system to select that vendor easily\nb) Establishing processes of selection such as setting evaluation standards or weighting"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,516.75,460.21],"text":"rules of conformity to the requested items\nc) Issuing unofficial agreements to all vendors to whom the RFP has been presented and"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,518.76,514.21],"text":"requesting them to prepare a contract and a statement of work to accelerate the\nconclusion of the contract after the vendor selection\nd) Preparing a bailout for a vendor who received a high evaluation on the response to the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,271.78,549.13],"text":"RFI, in case it fails in the selection"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Aside from the items of an RFP, giving a high evaluation to a vendor who is familiar\n with the current system to select that vendor easily"},{"label":"b","text":"Establishing processes of selection such as setting evaluation standards or weighting\n rules of conformity to the requested items"},{"label":"c","text":"Issuing unofficial agreements to all vendors to whom the RFP has been presented and\n requesting them to prepare a contract and a statement of work to accelerate the\n conclusion of the contract after the vendor selection"},{"label":"d","text":"Preparing a bailout for a vendor who received a high evaluation on the response to the\n RFI, in case it fails in the selection"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'To select vendors fairly, the acquirer should decide the selection process in advance, including evaluation criteria and the weighting of requirements, before reviewing proposals. Favoring the incumbent vendor, making informal agreements or preparing a fallback for a preferred vendor would all bias the selection.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q65)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q65. The RFP is presented to each vendor that has responded to an RFI. Which of the
 following should be done beforehand to proceed fairly with the future vendor selection
 processes?

 a) Aside from the items of an RFP, giving a high evaluation to a vendor who is familiar
 with the current system to select that vendor easily
 b) Establishing processes of selection such as setting evaluation standards or weighting
 rules of conformity to the requested items
 c) Issuing unofficial agreements to all vendors to whom the RFP has been presented and
 requesting them to prepare a contract and a statement of work to accelerate the
 conclusion of the contract after the vendor selection
 d) Preparing a bailout for a vendor who received a high evaluation on the response to the
 RFI, in case it fails in the selection',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  66,
  'Q66. A company has products that are at the peak of profitability and sales. As a result, many
 competitors develop similar products to the market. Therefore, a company must develop
 new products to meet new demands and market opportunities. Which of the following is a
 state of such events in the product life cycle?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,532.72,657.13],"text":"Q66.\nA company has products that are at the peak of profitability and sales. As a result, many\ncompetitors develop similar products to the market. Therefore, a company must develop\nnew products to meet new demands and market opportunities. Which of the following is a\nstate of such events in the product life cycle?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,662.93,400.09,747.13],"text":"a) Decline stage\nb) Growth stage\nc) Introduction stage\nd) Maturity stage"},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Decline stage"},{"label":"b","text":"Growth stage"},{"label":"c","text":"Introduction stage"},{"label":"d","text":"Maturity stage"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'This is the maturity stage. Sales and profits are at their peak, many competitors have entered with similar products, and the company must differentiate or develop new products to keep growing. In the growth stage sales are still increasing rapidly, and in the decline stage sales and profits are falling.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q66)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q66. A company has products that are at the peak of profitability and sales. As a result, many
 competitors develop similar products to the market. Therefore, a company must develop
 new products to meet new demands and market opportunities. Which of the following is a
 state of such events in the product life cycle?

 a) Decline stage b) Growth stage
 c) Introduction stage d) Maturity stage',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  67,
  'Q67. Which of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate
 management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,519.75,100.21],"text":"Q67.\n Which of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate\nmanagement?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,510.01,136.21],"text":"a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,528.91,190.21],"text":"services, and operation through comparison with those of competitors or advanced\ncompanies.\nb) It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning its"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,516.52,244.21],"text":"business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of\ninformation technology.\nc) It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,492.18,298.21],"text":"resources in an effective and integrated manner and to achieve an improvement in\nmanagement efficiency.\nd) It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[96.0,302.93,524.46,334.21],"text":"technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other\ncompanies."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,\n services, and operation through comparison with those of competitors or advanced\n companies."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning its\n business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of\n information technology."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management\n resources in an effective and integrated manner and to achieve an improvement in\n management efficiency."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and\n technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other\n companies."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Benchmarking compares a company''s products, services and operations qualitatively and quantitatively with those of competitors or best-practice companies to find gaps and improve. Radical process redesign from a customer viewpoint is BPR, integrated company-wide resource planning relates to ERP, and focusing on unique superior skills is core competence.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q67)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q67. Which of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate
 management?

 a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,
 services, and operation through comparison with those of competitors or advanced
 companies.
 b) It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning its
 business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of
 information technology.
 c) It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management
 resources in an effective and integrated manner and to achieve an improvement in
 management efficiency.
 d) It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and
 technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other
 companies.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  68,
  'Q68. Which of the following is a business management technique that is used to develop
 specific targets and measures to implement a planned strategy, in consideration of the
 appropriate mutual relationships among four perspectives (i.e., financial, customer, business
 process, and learning and growth)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,374.76,531.26,442.21],"text":"Q68.\nWhich of the following is a business management technique that is used to develop\nspecific targets and measures to implement a planned strategy, in consideration of the\nappropriate mutual relationships among four perspectives (i.e., financial, customer, business\nprocess, and learning and growth)?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,412.13,496.21],"text":"a) Balanced scorecard\nb) Growth matrix\nc) Product portfolio management\nd) SWOT analysis"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Balanced scorecard"},{"label":"b","text":"Growth matrix"},{"label":"c","text":"Product portfolio management"},{"label":"d","text":"SWOT analysis"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The balanced scorecard turns strategy into concrete goals and measures from four linked perspectives: financial, customer, internal business process, and learning and growth. PPM classifies products by market growth and share, the growth matrix (Ansoff) chooses growth directions, and SWOT analyzes strengths, weaknesses, opportunities and threats.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q68)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q68. Which of the following is a business management technique that is used to develop
 specific targets and measures to implement a planned strategy, in consideration of the
 appropriate mutual relationships among four perspectives (i.e., financial, customer, business
 process, and learning and growth)?

 a) Balanced scorecard b) Growth matrix
 c) Product portfolio management d) SWOT analysis',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2023-october',
  'A',
  69,
  'Q69. Which of the following is the purpose of SCM?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,517.74,338.85,549.19],"text":"Q69.\nWhich of the following is the purpose of SCM?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,518.03,586.21],"text":"a) To construct favorable customer relationships through unified management, including"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,524.36,640.21],"text":"customer information, purchasing history, and complaints, and also through meticulous\ncustomer response\nb) To improve management efficiency through integrated management of all information"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,531.98,676.21],"text":"concerning core business operations such as production, sales, inventory, and accounting\nc) To improve the efficiency of sales activity through unified management of customer"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,680.93,530.67,730.21],"text":"information, business meeting schedules, and business meeting status including progress\nstatus\nd) To reduce costs and shorten delivery periods through integrated management of"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[102.12,734.93,501.27,748.21],"text":"information across multiple companies or organizations from procurement to sales"},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To construct favorable customer relationships through unified management, including\n customer information, purchasing history, and complaints, and also through meticulous\n customer response"},{"label":"b","text":"To improve management efficiency through integrated management of all information\n concerning core business operations such as production, sales, inventory, and accounting"},{"label":"c","text":"To improve the efficiency of sales activity through unified management of customer\n information, business meeting schedules, and business meeting status including progress\n status"},{"label":"d","text":"To reduce costs and shorten delivery periods through integrated management of\n information across multiple companies or organizations from procurement to sales"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Supply chain management aims to reduce costs and shorten lead times by sharing and managing information across all companies involved, from procurement through production and distribution to sales. Managing customer relationships is CRM, integrating internal core operations is ERP, and managing sales activities is SFA.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q69)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q69. Which of the following is the purpose of SCM?

 a) To construct favorable customer relationships through unified management, including
 customer information, purchasing history, and complaints, and also through meticulous
 customer response
 b) To improve management efficiency through integrated management of all information
 concerning core business operations such as production, sales, inventory, and accounting
 c) To improve the efficiency of sales activity through unified management of customer
 information, business meeting schedules, and business meeting status including progress
 status
 d) To reduce costs and shorten delivery periods through integrated management of
 information across multiple companies or organizations from procurement to sales',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
