  70,
  'Q70. Which of the following is an explanation of the IoT (Internet of Things)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,460.66,81.19],"text":"Q70.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the IoT (Internet of Things)?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,519.01,118.21],"text":"a) It refers to a form of electronic commerce carried out over the Internet, consisting of a"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,529.28,190.21],"text":"typical C to C transaction by which a seller posts a product’s name, photo, minimum\nselling price, and other information on a website, after which the bidder that offers the\nhighest amount within the time limit becomes the successful bidder.\nb) It refers to data centers designed for the connection to the Internet, with server operation"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,532.7,262.21],"text":"failure prevented through the implementation of measures including quality management\nof communication lines, server maintenance, air conditioning, and power source-related\ncountermeasures against power interruptions and outages.\nc) It refers to Internet advertising such as a banner advertisement that displays an image,"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,529.39,316.21],"text":"with a link to an advertiser’s website, or an e-mail advertisement that publicizes an\nadvertiser’s website.\nd) It refers to the installation of communication functionality to various objects, in addition"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[102.12,320.93,524.71,388.21],"text":"to information and communication devices, and enabling automatic recognition or\nremote measurement by connecting these to the Internet, to achieve high-level decision-\nmaking services and automated control through the collection and analysis of large\nvolumes of data."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a form of electronic commerce carried out over the Internet, consisting of a\n typical C to C transaction by which a seller posts a product’s name, photo, minimum\n selling price, and other information on a website, after which the bidder that offers the\n highest amount within the time limit becomes the successful bidder."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to data centers designed for the connection to the Internet, with server operation\n failure prevented through the implementation of measures including quality management\n of communication lines, server maintenance, air conditioning, and power source-related\n countermeasures against power interruptions and outages."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to Internet advertising such as a banner advertisement that displays an image,\n with a link to an advertiser’s website, or an e-mail advertisement that publicizes an\n advertiser’s website."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the installation of communication functionality to various objects, in addition\n to information and communication devices, and enabling automatic recognition or\n remote measurement by connecting these to the Internet, to achieve high-level decision-making services and automated control through the collection and analysis of large\n volumes of data."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'IoT means adding communication functions to all kinds of objects, not only computers, and connecting them to the Internet so they can be recognized, measured and controlled remotely. The collected data is analyzed to support decisions and automated control. The other options describe online auctions, Internet data centers and Internet advertising.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2023A, FE, Subject-A, Q70)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q70. Which of the following is an explanation of the IoT (Internet of Things)?

 a) It refers to a form of electronic commerce carried out over the Internet, consisting of a
 typical C to C transaction by which a seller posts a product’s name, photo, minimum
 selling price, and other information on a website, after which the bidder that offers the
 highest amount within the time limit becomes the successful bidder.
 b) It refers to data centers designed for the connection to the Internet, with server operation
 failure prevented through the implementation of measures including quality management
 of communication lines, server maintenance, air conditioning, and power source-related
 countermeasures against power interruptions and outages.
 c) It refers to Internet advertising such as a banner advertisement that displays an image,
 with a link to an advertiser’s website, or an e-mail advertisement that publicizes an
 advertiser’s website.
 d) It refers to the installation of communication functionality to various objects, in addition
 to information and communication devices, and enabling automatic recognition or
 remote measurement by connecting these to the Internet, to achieve high-level decision-making services and automated control through the collection and analysis of large
 volumes of data.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2023-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
