  77,
  'Q77. When the weather tomorrow is sunny with 30% probability, cloudy with 50% probability, and rainy with 20% probability, which of the following strategies offers the highest expected value?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q77. When the weather tomorrow is sunny with 30% probability, cloudy with 50% probability, and rainy with 20% probability, which of the following strategies offers the highest expected value?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2023-october-a-q77-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"S1"},{"label":"b","text":"S2"},{"label":"c","text":"S3"},{"label":"d","text":"S4"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'S1 has the highest expected value. S1 gives 0.3 × 80 + 0.5 × 20 + 0.2 × (−40) = 24 + 10 − 8 = 26, compared with 21 for S2, 23 for S3 and 19.5 for S4. The expected value weights each outcome by its probability and adds them.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
