  'For blank A, FindWeightClass returns −1 when the weight exceeds 125 kg, so the re-entry loop runs while index == -1. For blank B, malloc must allocate a whole node, so its argument is sizeof(Wrestler_t), not the size of a pointer. For blank C, the first class i with UpperLimits[i] >= weight is the lightest allowed class. In Insert, an empty list gets the node via Entries[i] = wrestler (blank D); otherwise the loop walks to the last node and appends with curr->next = wrestler (blank E). For blank F, Deallocate needs two pointer variables, declared as *curr, *next. For sorted insertion (blank G), the loop continues while curr->next->weight < wrestler->weight. For blank H, line δ (insert at the head) runs for Eric (empty 97 kg list), Faraday (empty 74 kg list) and Issacs (68 is not more than Faraday''s 72), so it runs 3 times.',
