  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The probability is 1/10. Because the two coffees are identical and the three teas are identical, the number of distinct ways to hand out the drinks is 5!/(2!×3!) = 10, and only one of those arrangements gives everyone the drink they ordered. Using 5! = 120 arrangements would overcount, since swapping two identical cups does not change the outcome.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
