  '2024-april',
  'A',
  3,
  'Q3. The expression below is represented in postfix (reverse Polish) notation. What is the
 resulting value of this expression? Here, the numbers are in decimal, and the symbols ‘+’, ‘−’,
 ‘*’, and ‘/’ represent addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division operators, respectively.

 100 5 6 2 + * 12 4 / − − 36 −',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,533.08,297.19],"text":"Q3. The expression below is represented in postfix (reverse Polish) notation. What is the"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[83.28,301.85,533.11,333.13],"text":"resulting value of this expression? Here, the numbers are in decimal, and the symbols ‘+’, ‘−’,\n‘*’, and ‘/’ represent addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division operators, respectively."},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,353.35,299.02,388.15],"text":"100 5 6 2 + * 12 4 / − − 36 −"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,470.1,406.21],"text":"a) 5\nb) 18\nc) 21\nd) 27"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"5"},{"label":"b","text":"18"},{"label":"c","text":"21"},{"label":"d","text":"27"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The result is 27. Evaluating left to right with a stack: 6 2 + gives 8, then 5 8 * gives 40, then 12 4 / gives 3, then 40 3 − gives 37, then 100 37 − gives 63, and finally 63 36 − gives 27. Each operator applies to the two most recent values on the stack, with the earlier one as the left operand.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q3)',
