(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  4,
  'Q4. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of feedback control?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,445.74,451.13,459.19],"text":"Q4.  Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of feedback control?"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,472.36,550.21],"text":"a) It performs control in a predetermined order.\nb) It performs control to keep the output in line with the target value.\nc) It performs control to prevent external disturbances from affecting the output.\nd) It performs control without using the output."},{"type":"code","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 4 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It performs control in a predetermined order."},{"label":"b","text":"It performs control to keep the output in line with the target value."},{"label":"c","text":"It performs control to prevent external disturbances from affecting the output."},{"label":"d","text":"It performs control without using the output."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Feedback control keeps the output in line with the target value: it measures the actual output, compares it with the target, and corrects the input according to the difference. Controlling steps in a predetermined order is sequence control, acting on disturbances before they affect the output is feedforward control, and control that never uses the output is open-loop control.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q4)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q4. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of feedback control?

 a) It performs control in a predetermined order.
