  'Q6. The flowchart below shows an algorithm that determines the sum (i.e. “1 +3+ 5+ … + (2N-1)”) of the first N odd integers from 1 through 2N-1 (where N ≥ 1) and inserts the result into variable x. Which of the following is an expression to be inserted in blank A ?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q6. The flowchart below shows an algorithm that determines the sum (i.e. “1 +3+ 5+ … + (2N-1)”) of the first N odd integers from 1 through 2N-1 (where N ≥ 1) and inserts the result into variable x. Which of the following is an expression to be inserted in blank A ?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-april-a-q06-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"i ≥ 2N – 1"},{"label":"b","text":"i ≥ 2N + 1"},{"label":"c","text":"x ≥ 2N – 1"},{"label":"d","text":"x ≥ 2N + 1"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Blank A should be i ≥ 2N + 1. The loop adds the odd number i to x and then increases i by 2, so it must keep running while i ≤ 2N − 1 and stop once i reaches the next odd number, 2N + 1. Using i ≥ 2N − 1 would exit before the last term 2N − 1 is added, giving the wrong sum.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
