 sorted in reverse order?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,508.99,82.21],"text":"Q7.  How many swaps are required in bubble sort when N elements in the array are already"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[85.74,86.93,201.73,100.21],"text":"sorted in reverse order?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[84.12,127.46,473.58,143.28],"text":"a) N(N-1) ÷ 2\nb) N 2 ÷ 2\nc) N(N-1)\nd) N 2"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"N(N-1) ÷ 2"},{"label":"b","text":"N² ÷ 2"},{"label":"c","text":"N(N-1)"},{"label":"d","text":"N²"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The number of swaps is N(N−1) ÷ 2. When the array is in reverse order, every pair of elements is out of order, and bubble sort performs one swap for each such pair; there are (N−1) + (N−2) + ... + 1 = N(N−1)/2 pairs. This is the worst case for bubble sort.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
