(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  11,
  'Q11. Which of the following is the design for securing safety and reliability known as
 “foolproof”?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,496.43,118.21],"text":"Q11.\nWhich of the following is the design for securing safety and reliability known as\n“foolproof”?"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,524.17,136.21],"text":"a) A redundant configuration, such as duplication, can be used so that even when a device"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,511.2,172.21],"text":"failure occurs, the functions of the overall system are not affected.\nb) Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,525.3,208.21],"text":"system.\nc) When a device failure occurs, damage can be minimized by enabling the system to stop"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,528.96,244.21],"text":"safely.\nd) When a device failure occurs, the system runs even if the usable functions are restricted,"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,300.4,280.15],"text":"and the processing efficiency is reduced."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A redundant configuration, such as duplication, can be used so that even when a device\n failure occurs, the functions of the overall system are not affected."},{"label":"b","text":"Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the\n system."},{"label":"c","text":"When a device failure occurs, damage can be minimized by enabling the system to stop\n safely."},{"label":"d","text":"When a device failure occurs, the system runs even if the usable functions are restricted,\n and the processing efficiency is reduced."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Foolproof design means that even if a user performs an incorrect operation, no problem occurs in the system, for example by disabling invalid inputs or requiring confirmation. Redundant duplication describes fault tolerance, stopping safely on failure is fail-safe, and continuing with reduced functions is fail-soft.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q11)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q11. Which of the following is the design for securing safety and reliability known as
 “foolproof”?

 a) A redundant configuration, such as duplication, can be used so that even when a device
 failure occurs, the functions of the overall system are not affected.
 b) Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the
 system.
 c) When a device failure occurs, damage can be minimized by enabling the system to stop
