 There are five processes A, B, C, D and E arriving at the same time with estimated running
 times of 10, 6, 2, 4, and 8 milliseconds, respectively. Their priorities are 3, 5, 2, 1, and 4,
 where 1 is the highest priority. What is the mean process turnaround time?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,529.2,136.21],"text":"Q13.\nAn operating system adopts the priority scheduling algorithm for scheduling processes.\nThere are five processes A, B, C, D and E arriving at the same time with estimated running\ntimes of 10, 6, 2, 4, and 8 milliseconds, respectively. Their priorities are 3, 5, 2, 1, and 4,\nwhere 1 is the highest priority. What is the mean process turnaround time?"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,470.1,172.21],"text":"a) 14\nb) 16\nc) 20\nd) 22"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"14"},{"label":"b","text":"16"},{"label":"c","text":"20"},{"label":"d","text":"22"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The mean turnaround time is 16 ms. Running in priority order D (4), C (2), A (10), E (8), B (6), the processes finish at 4, 6, 16, 24 and 30 ms, and since all arrived at time 0 these are their turnaround times. Their sum is 80, and 80 ÷ 5 = 16.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
