  14,
  'Q14. Data is continuously sent for T seconds from the sending task to the receiving task in the diagram below. When the volume of data sent in 1 second is S and the volume of data received in 1 second is R, which of the following is the appropriate relational expression indicating the buffer size L to prevent buffer overflow? Here, the sending task has a higher transfer speed than the receiving task, and there is a sufficient time interval until the start of the next transfer.',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q14. Data is continuously sent for T seconds from the sending task to the receiving task in the diagram below. When the volume of data sent in 1 second is S and the volume of data received in 1 second is R, which of the following is the appropriate relational expression indicating the buffer size L to prevent buffer overflow? Here, the sending task has a higher transfer speed than the receiving task, and there is a sufficient time interval until the start of the next transfer."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-april-a-q14-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"L < ( R − S ) × T"},{"label":"b","text":"L < ( S − R ) × T"},{"label":"c","text":"L ≧ ( R − S ) × T"},{"label":"d","text":"L ≧ ( S − R ) × T"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The buffer must satisfy L ≧ (S − R) × T. Because the sender is faster, data piles up in the buffer at a rate of S − R per second, so after T seconds of sending the buffer holds (S − R) × T, and the buffer must be at least that large to avoid overflow. The expressions with R − S have the sign reversed, and the ones with < describe a buffer that is too small.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q14)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q14. Data is continuously sent for T seconds from the sending task to the receiving task in
 the diagram below. When the volume of data sent in 1 second is S and the volume of data
 received in 1 second is R, which of the following is the appropriate relational expression
 indicating the buffer size L to prevent buffer overflow? Here, the sending task has a higher
 transfer speed than the receiving task, and there is a sufficient time interval until the start of
 the next transfer.

 Sending task Buffer size: L Receiving task
 S R

 a) L < ( R − S ) × T b) L < ( S − R ) × T
 c) L ≧ ( R − S ) × T d) L ≧ ( S − R ) × T',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
