  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.16,117.13],"text":"Q21.\nWhich of the following is a clause that is inserted into blank A of the SQL statement\nbelow that calculates the average scores for each class and subject from the “MidtermTest”\ntable and displays them in ascending order of class and subject?"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[96.72,140.93,400.62,172.21],"text":"MidtermTest (Class, Subject, StudentNumber, Name, Score)"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[107.22,176.93,189.42,190.21],"text":"[SQL statement]"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[86.22,197.33,402.83,207.83],"text":"SELECT Class, Subject, AVG(Score) AS AverageScore"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[86.22,215.33,193.85,225.83],"text":"FROM MidtermTest"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[83.1,230.72,536.45,334.21],"text":"A\n\n\na) GROUP BY Class, AverageScore ORDER BY Class, Subject\nb)\nGROUP BY Class, Subject ORDER BY Class, AVG(Score)\nc)\nGROUP BY Class, Subject ORDER BY Class, Subject\nd)\nROUP BY Class, Subject, StudentNumber ORDER BY Class, Subject,"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[104.34,340.69,179.15,351.78],"text":"AverageScore"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"GROUP BY Class, AverageScore ORDER BY Class, Subject"},{"label":"b","text":"GROUP BY Class, Subject ORDER BY Class, AVG(Score)"},{"label":"c","text":"GROUP BY Class, Subject ORDER BY Class, Subject"},{"label":"d","text":"ROUP BY Class, Subject, StudentNumber ORDER BY Class, Subject,\n\n AverageScore"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The clause is GROUP BY Class, Subject ORDER BY Class, Subject. Grouping by both Class and Subject makes AVG(Score) compute one average per class-subject pair, and ordering by the same columns sorts them in ascending order of class and subject. Grouping by StudentNumber would give per-student rows, and the other choices group by an alias or sort by the average instead of by subject.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
