  'Q22. Which of the following can change the deadlock state of the transaction back to the
 normal state?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,391.74,533.11,441.13],"text":"Q22.\nWhich of the following can change the deadlock state of the transaction back to the\nnormal state?"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,522.47,478.15],"text":"a) Commit\nb) Drop\nc) Rollback\nd) Roll Forward"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Commit"},{"label":"b","text":"Drop"},{"label":"c","text":"Rollback"},{"label":"d","text":"Roll Forward"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Rollback resolves a deadlock. The DBMS chooses one of the deadlocked transactions as a victim and rolls it back, which releases its locks so the other transactions can proceed, and the victim can be restarted later. A deadlocked transaction cannot commit because it is waiting, and roll forward is used for recovery after a media failure, not for deadlocks.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q22)',
  ARRAY[11]::int[],
