  23,
  'Q23. Which of the following is the network device that makes a forwarding decision on the
 basis of the destination MAC address in the frame header?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,482.76,533.12,531.13],"text":"Q23.\nWhich of the following is the network device that makes a forwarding decision on the\nbasis of the destination MAC address in the frame header?"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,527.77,586.21],"text":"a) Patch cable\nb) Repeater hub\nc) Router\nd) Switching hub"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Patch cable"},{"label":"b","text":"Repeater hub"},{"label":"c","text":"Router"},{"label":"d","text":"Switching hub"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A switching hub (layer 2 switch) forwards frames based on the destination MAC address, using a MAC address table it learns from incoming frames. A repeater hub simply sends signals out of every port at layer 1, a router forwards packets by IP address at layer 3, and a patch cable is just a passive cable.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
