  27,
  'Q27. Which of the following describes a brute force attack aimed at finding the key of
 symmetric encryption?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,393.72,498.07,443.11],"text":"Q27.\nWhich of the following describes a brute force attack aimed at finding the key of\nsymmetric encryption?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,448.91,513.07,480.19],"text":"a) Finding the key by observing the ciphertext change when the plaintext is altered by a"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,484.91,526.47,516.19],"text":"certain amount\nb) Finding the key by testing all key combinations sequentially when a set of plaintext and"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,520.91,526.0,552.19],"text":"ciphertext is given\nc) Finding the key by using the algebraic expression representing the relationship between"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,556.91,521.66,588.19],"text":"the plaintext, ciphertext, and key as a clue\nd) Finding the key by using the statistical correlation between a part of the information of"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[102.12,592.91,423.06,606.19],"text":"the plaintext and part of the information of the ciphertext as a clue"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Finding the key by observing the ciphertext change when the plaintext is altered by a\n certain amount"},{"label":"b","text":"Finding the key by testing all key combinations sequentially when a set of plaintext and\n ciphertext is given"},{"label":"c","text":"Finding the key by using the algebraic expression representing the relationship between\n the plaintext, ciphertext, and key as a clue"},{"label":"d","text":"Finding the key by using the statistical correlation between a part of the information of\n the plaintext and part of the information of the ciphertext as a clue"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A brute force attack tries every possible key in turn until one transforms the known plaintext into the given ciphertext. Watching how the ciphertext changes when the plaintext is altered describes differential cryptanalysis, the statistical correlation approach is linear cryptanalysis, and the algebraic expression approach is algebraic cryptanalysis.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
