  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is a rootkit, a package of tools an attacker installs after gaining access to keep control of the server, for example by creating a backdoor and hiding the evidence of the intrusion such as processes, files and log entries. RFID is wireless tag technology, TKIP is a Wi-Fi encryption protocol, and a web beacon is a tiny embedded image used to track page views.',
