(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following is an explanation of the timestamp service in information
 security?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,533.16,333.13],"text":"Q31.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the timestamp service in information\nsecurity?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,529.42,370.21],"text":"a) It is a service that authenticates biometric information, such as fingerprints, voice prints,"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,516.74,424.21],"text":"vein patterns, retina, and iris, by using the date and time when the information is\nregistered in the authentication system.\nb) It is a service that certifies that electronic data certainly exists on a particular date and"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,509.43,460.21],"text":"time and that the data has not been modified since that date and time.\nc) It is a service that securely verifies that the date and time information is not falsified"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,513.21,496.21],"text":"midway for setting the clocks of the PCs and servers on the network.\nd) It is a web service that securely displays the global date and time information used in"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,500.93,353.02,532.21],"text":"official records by using encrypted communication."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a service that authenticates biometric information, such as fingerprints, voice prints,\n vein patterns, retina, and iris, by using the date and time when the information is\n registered in the authentication system."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a service that certifies that electronic data certainly exists on a particular date and\n time and that the data has not been modified since that date and time."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a service that securely verifies that the date and time information is not falsified\n midway for setting the clocks of the PCs and servers on the network."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a web service that securely displays the global date and time information used in\n official records by using encrypted communication."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A timestamp service certifies that specific electronic data existed at a particular date and time and has not been modified since. A trusted time-stamping authority signs a hash of the data together with the time, so any later change to the data would no longer match. It is not a biometric service or a clock synchronization service.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[13]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following is an explanation of the timestamp service in information
 security?

 a) It is a service that authenticates biometric information, such as fingerprints, voice prints,
 vein patterns, retina, and iris, by using the date and time when the information is
 registered in the authentication system.
 b) It is a service that certifies that electronic data certainly exists on a particular date and
 time and that the data has not been modified since that date and time.
 c) It is a service that securely verifies that the date and time information is not falsified
 midway for setting the clocks of the PCs and servers on the network.
 d) It is a web service that securely displays the global date and time information used in
 official records by using encrypted communication.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[13]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
