 permissions to determine whether they are allowed or not. When these three bits are
 configured using an octal value from 0 through 7, the trial results below are obtained.
 Which of the following is an appropriate trial result?

 [Trial results]
 (1) When 0 is set, reading, writing, and execution can no longer be performed.
 (2) When 3 is set, reading and writing can be performed, but execution cannot.
 (3) When 7 is set, reading, writing, and execution can be performed.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,506.22,153.13],"text":"Q33.\nIn an OS where permissions for reading, writing, or executing a file can be\nindependently set as attributes of the file, one bit is allocated for each of these three (3)\npermissions to determine whether they are allowed or not. When these three bits are\nconfigured using an octal value from 0 through 7, the trial results below are obtained.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate trial result?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[93.48,176.93,161.72,190.21],"text":"[Trial results]"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,492.93,334.21],"text":"(1) When 0 is set, reading, writing, and execution can no longer be performed.\n(2) When 3 is set, reading and writing can be performed, but execution cannot.\n(3) When 7 is set, reading, writing, and execution can be performed.\n\na) When 2 is set, reading and execution can be performed.\nb) When 4 is set, only execution can be performed.\nc) When 5 is set, only writing can be performed.\nd) When 6 is set, reading and writing can be performed."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"When 2 is set, reading and execution can be performed."},{"label":"b","text":"When 4 is set, only execution can be performed."},{"label":"c","text":"When 5 is set, only writing can be performed."},{"label":"d","text":"When 6 is set, reading and writing can be performed."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'When 4 is set, only execution can be performed. The trial results show that 3 (binary 011) allows reading and writing, so reading is the 1 bit, writing is the 2 bit, and execution must be the 4 bit. With this mapping 2 allows only writing, 5 allows reading and execution, and 6 allows writing and execution, so the other choices are wrong.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'access-control'),
  'medium',
