  36,
  'Q36. Which of the following is the most appropriate description of polymorphism in object-oriented design?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,530.13,99.13],"text":"Q36.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate description of polymorphism in object-\noriented design?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,481.02,136.21],"text":"a) It allows developers to define classes incrementally by reusing classes defined"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,518.45,172.21],"text":"previously as the basis for new classes.\nb) It allows the analyst to focus on the important dimensions while ignoring nonessential"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,176.93,426.04,244.21],"text":"dimensions.\nc) It combines processes and data into a single object.\nd) It is the provision of a single interface to entities of different types."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It allows developers to define classes incrementally by reusing classes defined\n previously as the basis for new classes."},{"label":"b","text":"It allows the analyst to focus on the important dimensions while ignoring nonessential\n dimensions."},{"label":"c","text":"It combines processes and data into a single object."},{"label":"d","text":"It is the provision of a single interface to entities of different types."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Polymorphism is the provision of a single interface to entities of different types, so the same message or method call produces behavior suited to each object''s actual class. Defining new classes by reusing existing ones is inheritance, focusing on essential aspects is abstraction, and combining data and processes into one object is encapsulation.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q36)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q36. Which of the following is the most appropriate description of polymorphism in object-oriented design?

 a) It allows developers to define classes incrementally by reusing classes defined
 previously as the basis for new classes.
 b) It allows the analyst to focus on the important dimensions while ignoring nonessential
 dimensions.
 c) It combines processes and data into a single object.
 d) It is the provision of a single interface to entities of different types.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
