  37,
  'Q37. There is a program module that is executed only when the integer value of integer x is 25 ≤ x < 50. When testing this module using boundary value analysis, which of the following is an appropriate combination of values to be tested?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q37. There is a program module that is executed only when the integer value of integer x is 25 ≤ x < 50. When testing this module using boundary value analysis, which of the following is an appropriate combination of values to be tested?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"24, 25, 49, 50"},{"label":"b","text":"24, 25, 50, 51"},{"label":"c","text":"25, 26, 49, 50"},{"label":"d","text":"25, 26, 50, 51"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The test values are 24, 25, 49 and 50. Boundary value analysis tests each edge of the valid range and the value just outside it: the valid range 25 ≤ x < 50 starts at 25 (invalid neighbour 24) and ends at 49, since x < 50 (invalid neighbour 50). Choosing 50 and 51 is a common mistake that overlooks that 50 itself is already excluded.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
