),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  39,
  'Q39. Which of the following is an explanation of the reverse engineering of software?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,518.76,497.74,549.19],"text":"Q39.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of the reverse engineering of software?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,481.96,586.21],"text":"a) The entire software is reconstructed after the existing software is analyzed and"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,515.32,640.21],"text":"understood.\nb) The existing software is analyzed, and its specification and structure are clarified.\nc) The internal structure of the software is changed without any change to the externally"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,474.03,676.21],"text":"observed behavior.\nd) The source code is automatically generated from the design information by a"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,680.93,230.81,747.13],"text":"development support tool."},{"type":"code","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 15 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The entire software is reconstructed after the existing software is analyzed and\n understood."},{"label":"b","text":"The existing software is analyzed, and its specification and structure are clarified."},{"label":"c","text":"The internal structure of the software is changed without any change to the externally\n observed behavior."},{"label":"d","text":"The source code is automatically generated from the design information by a\n development support tool."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Reverse engineering analyzes existing software to recover and clarify its specifications and structure, often starting from source or object code. Rebuilding the whole software after the analysis is reengineering, changing the internal structure without changing external behavior is refactoring, and generating code from design information is forward engineering.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q39)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q39. Which of the following is an explanation of the reverse engineering of software?

 a) The entire software is reconstructed after the existing software is analyzed and
 understood.
 b) The existing software is analyzed, and its specification and structure are clarified.
 c) The internal structure of the software is changed without any change to the externally
 observed behavior.
 d) The source code is automatically generated from the design information by a
