  'A',
  40,
  'Q40. Which of the following is the appropriate order of the six phases in the SDLC (Software
 Development Life Cycle) model?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.1,82.21],"text":"Q40.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate order of the six phases in the SDLC (Software"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[83.28,86.93,247.31,100.21],"text":"Development Life Cycle) model?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[86.22,122.93,530.94,136.21],"text":"a) Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Deployment → Testing → Maintenance"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[86.22,140.93,531.0,154.21],"text":"b) Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Testing → Deployment → Maintenance"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[86.22,158.93,530.96,172.21],"text":"c) Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Testing → Maintenance → Deployment"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[86.22,176.93,530.96,190.21],"text":"d) Requirements Analysis → Programming → Testing → Design → Maintenance → Deployment"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Deployment → Testing → Maintenance"},{"label":"b","text":"Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Testing → Deployment → Maintenance"},{"label":"c","text":"Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Testing → Maintenance → Deployment"},{"label":"d","text":"Requirements Analysis → Programming → Testing → Design → Maintenance → Deployment"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The order is Requirements Analysis → Design → Programming → Testing → Deployment → Maintenance. Software has to be tested before it is deployed to users, and maintenance follows deployment because it covers the operation and change of the released system. The other choices put deployment before testing, put maintenance before deployment, or put programming before design.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'development-processes'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q40)',
  ARRAY[16]::int[],
