  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q41. The activities and milestones of a project are shown in the arrow diagram below. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the project if the duration of activity B is increased by 5 days?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-april-a-q41-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The earliest start time of activity G is delayed by 5 days."},{"label":"b","text":"The latest start time of activity F is delayed by 5 days."},{"label":"c","text":"The project’s minimum completion time does not change."},{"label":"d","text":"The project’s minimum completion time is increased by 5 days."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The project''s minimum completion time does not change. The critical path is C → D → G → H = 10 + 25 + 15 + 15 = 65 days. Path A → B is 15 days, so the node after B is reached at day 15; with B lengthened to 10 days it is reached at day 20, giving 30 days at the start of G (still earlier than 35 via D) and 40 days before H (still earlier than 50 via G). B has enough float to absorb the 5-day delay, so nothing on the critical path moves.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
