  43,
  'Q43. In ITIL 2011 edition, which of the following is the appropriate order for the service
 lifecycle stages?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,286.85,533.13,318.13],"text":"Q43.\nIn ITIL 2011 edition, which of the following is the appropriate order for the service\nlifecycle stages?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,323.93,490.33,355.21],"text":"a) Service design → Continual service improvement → Service strategy → Service"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,359.84,485.76,391.21],"text":"operation → Service transition\nb) Service design → Service strategy → Service operation → Service transition →"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,395.93,485.76,427.21],"text":"Continual service improvement\nc) Service strategy → Service design → Service operation → Service transition →"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,431.93,488.76,463.21],"text":"Continual service improvement\nd) Service strategy → Service design → Service transition  → Service operation →"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,467.93,262.44,499.15],"text":"Continual service improvement"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Service design → Continual service improvement → Service strategy → Service operation → Service transition"},{"label":"b","text":"Service design → Service strategy → Service operation → Service transition → Continual service improvement"},{"label":"c","text":"Service strategy → Service design → Service operation → Service transition → Continual service improvement"},{"label":"d","text":"Service strategy → Service design → Service transition → Service operation → Continual service improvement"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The ITIL 2011 service lifecycle runs Service strategy → Service design → Service transition → Service operation, with Continual service improvement applied across the whole cycle. A service has to be designed and then transitioned, meaning built, tested and released, before it can be operated, so operation cannot come before transition.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q43)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q43. In ITIL 2011 edition, which of the following is the appropriate order for the service
 lifecycle stages?

 a) Service design  Continual service improvement  Service strategy  Service
 operation  Service transition
 b) Service design  Service strategy  Service operation  Service transition 
 Continual service improvement
 c) Service strategy  Service design  Service operation  Service transition 
 Continual service improvement
 d) Service strategy  Service design  Service transition  Service operation 
 Continual service improvement',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  44,
  'Q44. In IT service management, which of the following is an activity performed for the
 management of incidents and service requests?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,503.76,533.22,589.21],"text":"Q44.\nIn IT service management, which of the following is an activity performed for the\nmanagement of incidents and service requests?\n\na) Evaluating if customer satisfaction with the service desk meets the agreed service targets"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,593.93,520.35,661.21],"text":"and performing a review to identify improvement opportunities\nb) Examining measures wherein the amount of free space on a disk is near its threshold\nc) Investigating the impact of changes made to a program\nd) Receiving a failure report from a user and checking to see if it corresponds to a known"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,665.93,128.43,715.15],"text":"error"},{"type":"code","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 17 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Evaluating if customer satisfaction with the service desk meets the agreed service targets\n and performing a review to identify improvement opportunities"},{"label":"b","text":"Examining measures wherein the amount of free space on a disk is near its threshold"},{"label":"c","text":"Investigating the impact of changes made to a program"},{"label":"d","text":"Receiving a failure report from a user and checking to see if it corresponds to a known\n error"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Receiving a failure report from a user and checking whether it matches a known error is part of incident management, whose goal is to restore normal service quickly, and a known error often comes with a workaround. Reviewing customer satisfaction belongs to service level management, watching disk-space thresholds is capacity management, and analyzing the impact of program changes is change management.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q44)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q44. In IT service management, which of the following is an activity performed for the
 management of incidents and service requests?

 a) Evaluating if customer satisfaction with the service desk meets the agreed service targets
 and performing a review to identify improvement opportunities
 b) Examining measures wherein the amount of free space on a disk is near its threshold
 c) Investigating the impact of changes made to a program
 d) Receiving a failure report from a user and checking to see if it corresponds to a known
 error',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  45,
  'Q45. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning an interview
 conducted by a system auditor?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,513.01,136.21],"text":"Q45.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate description concerning an interview\nconducted by a system auditor?\n\na) The administrator of the audited department, who has experience in auditing tasks, is"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,528.42,172.21],"text":"selected as the interviewee.\nb) The entire interview is conducted by one (1) system auditor, as discrepancies may occur"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,520.77,208.21],"text":"in the record if multiple auditors are involved.\nc) The system auditor instructs the audited department to take improvement measures for"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,511.25,244.21],"text":"deficiencies found during the interview.\nd) The system auditor makes an effort to obtain documents and records that support the"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,448.69,262.21],"text":"information obtained from the audited department during the interview."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The administrator of the audited department, who has experience in auditing tasks, is\n selected as the interviewee."},{"label":"b","text":"The entire interview is conducted by one (1) system auditor, as discrepancies may occur\n in the record if multiple auditors are involved."},{"label":"c","text":"The system auditor instructs the audited department to take improvement measures for\n deficiencies found during the interview."},{"label":"d","text":"The system auditor makes an effort to obtain documents and records that support the\n information obtained from the audited department during the interview."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The auditor should try to obtain documents and records that support what was said in the interview, because audit conclusions must rest on sufficient and reliable evidence, not on oral statements alone. Auditors do not order corrective action themselves; they make recommendations, and the interviewees should be the people who are actually responsible for the work.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q45)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q45. Which of the following is the most appropriate description concerning an interview
 conducted by a system auditor?

 a) The administrator of the audited department, who has experience in auditing tasks, is
 selected as the interviewee.
 b) The entire interview is conducted by one (1) system auditor, as discrepancies may occur
 in the record if multiple auditors are involved.
 c) The system auditor instructs the audited department to take improvement measures for
 deficiencies found during the interview.
 d) The system auditor makes an effort to obtain documents and records that support the
 information obtained from the audited department during the interview.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  46,
  'Q46. Which of the following is a case that enables the customer support operations at a call
 center to improve quality by applying a pattern recognition function or machine learning
 function to the accumulated data?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,301.74,533.14,369.13],"text":"Q46.\nWhich of the following is a case that enables the customer support operations at a call\ncenter to improve quality by applying a pattern recognition function or machine learning\nfunction to the accumulated data?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,514.03,388.21],"text":"a) Deriving the most appropriate response in real time from related materials and all the"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,522.76,424.21],"text":"previous support history according to the content of the inquiry made by a customer\nb) Displaying the digital content of a response manual or basic customer information on a"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,522.04,460.21],"text":"pop-up window of a screen for responding to requests from the operators\nc) Repeatedly providing role play training to new operators from an experienced operator"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,522.85,496.21],"text":"who serves as a lecturer by using the response manual as the teaching material\nd) Transferring a phone call or the relevant support screen to an experienced operator or a"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.12,500.93,509.06,532.21],"text":"dedicated staff when the operator who is responding to a customer over the phone is\nunable to provide an answer"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Deriving the most appropriate response in real time from related materials and all the\n previous support history according to the content of the inquiry made by a customer"},{"label":"b","text":"Displaying the digital content of a response manual or basic customer information on a\n pop-up window of a screen for responding to requests from the operators"},{"label":"c","text":"Repeatedly providing role play training to new operators from an experienced operator\n who serves as a lecturer by using the response manual as the teaching material"},{"label":"d","text":"Transferring a phone call or the relevant support screen to an experienced operator or a\n dedicated staff when the operator who is responding to a customer over the phone is\n unable to provide an answer"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The AI-based case is deriving the best response in real time from related materials and all past support history, based on what the customer asks. That requires pattern recognition or machine learning on accumulated data. Showing a manual in a pop-up, role-play training and escalating calls to an experienced operator are ordinary operational measures that use no learning function.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q46)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q46. Which of the following is a case that enables the customer support operations at a call
 center to improve quality by applying a pattern recognition function or machine learning
 function to the accumulated data?

 a) Deriving the most appropriate response in real time from related materials and all the
 previous support history according to the content of the inquiry made by a customer
 b) Displaying the digital content of a response manual or basic customer information on a
 pop-up window of a screen for responding to requests from the operators
 c) Repeatedly providing role play training to new operators from an experienced operator
 who serves as a lecturer by using the response manual as the teaching material
 d) Transferring a phone call or the relevant support screen to an experienced operator or a
 dedicated staff when the operator who is responding to a customer over the phone is
 unable to provide an answer',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  47,
  'Q47. Which of the following is a description of knowledge management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,436.45,586.21],"text":"Q47.\nWhich of the following is a description of knowledge management?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,525.97,622.21],"text":"a) Conduct business by a flat organizational structure that has as few hierarchical levels as"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,626.93,509.07,658.21],"text":"possible for quick decision making.\nb) Conduct business by utilizing its core strength in know-how and technology that are"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,662.93,499.14,694.21],"text":"unique to the company and cannot be imitated by others.\nc) Conduct business that enhances overall capabilities to solve problems by sharing"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,698.93,496.04,730.21],"text":"knowledge that is scattered throughout the company.\nd) Implement management innovation in the company on the basis of a comparative"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.12,734.93,423.67,748.21],"text":"analysis with companies that have achieved superior performance."},{"type":"code","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 18 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Conduct business by a flat organizational structure that has as few hierarchical levels as\n possible for quick decision making."},{"label":"b","text":"Conduct business by utilizing its core strength in know-how and technology that are\n unique to the company and cannot be imitated by others."},{"label":"c","text":"Conduct business that enhances overall capabilities to solve problems by sharing\n knowledge that is scattered throughout the company."},{"label":"d","text":"Implement management innovation in the company on the basis of a comparative\n analysis with companies that have achieved superior performance."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Knowledge management means improving the whole organization''s ability to solve problems by sharing knowledge and know-how that is scattered among individuals and departments. A flat structure is organizational design, relying on unique strengths that others cannot imitate is core competence management, and comparing against top performers is benchmarking.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q47)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q47. Which of the following is a description of knowledge management?

 a) Conduct business by a flat organizational structure that has as few hierarchical levels as
 possible for quick decision making.
 b) Conduct business by utilizing its core strength in know-how and technology that are
 unique to the company and cannot be imitated by others.
 c) Conduct business that enhances overall capabilities to solve problems by sharing
 knowledge that is scattered throughout the company.
 d) Implement management innovation in the company on the basis of a comparative
 analysis with companies that have achieved superior performance.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  48,
  'Q48. Which of the following is an appropriate description of an RFI?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,428.01,99.13],"text":"Q48.\n Which of the following is an appropriate description of an RFI?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,522.34,118.21],"text":"a) It is a document describing the basic policy for the system, including a summary of the"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,522.98,172.21],"text":"system, purpose, necessary functions, system requirements, and contract matters.\nb) It is a document that is created after an RFP.\nc) It is a document used by companies looking for the implementation of computerization"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,526.93,208.21],"text":"to request specific system proposals from prospective suppliers such as system vendors.\nd) It is a document used to request information concerning computerization from"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,325.09,244.21],"text":"prospective suppliers such as system vendors."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a document describing the basic policy for the system, including a summary of the\n system, purpose, necessary functions, system requirements, and contract matters."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a document that is created after an RFP."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a document used by companies looking for the implementation of computerization\n to request specific system proposals from prospective suppliers such as system vendors."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a document used to request information concerning computerization from\n prospective suppliers such as system vendors."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'An RFI (Request for Information) is a document used to request information about computerization, such as available technologies, products and vendor capabilities, from prospective suppliers. It is usually issued before the RFP, which asks vendors for specific system proposals, so the descriptions of a system policy document and of a request for specific proposals do not fit.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q48)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q48. Which of the following is an appropriate description of an RFI?

 a) It is a document describing the basic policy for the system, including a summary of the
 system, purpose, necessary functions, system requirements, and contract matters.
 b) It is a document that is created after an RFP.
 c) It is a document used by companies looking for the implementation of computerization
 to request specific system proposals from prospective suppliers such as system vendors.
 d) It is a document used to request information concerning computerization from
 prospective suppliers such as system vendors.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  49,
  'Q49. Which of the following is a strategy that concentrates resources in the segment of a
 specific customer or specific product in order to achieve specialization?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,533.16,297.13],"text":"Q49.\nWhich of the following is a strategy that concentrates resources in the segment of a\nspecific customer or specific product in order to achieve specialization?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,414.84,370.21],"text":"a) Challenger strategy\nb) Follower strategy\nc) Leader strategy\nd) Niche strategy"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Challenger strategy"},{"label":"b","text":"Follower strategy"},{"label":"c","text":"Leader strategy"},{"label":"d","text":"Niche strategy"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'This is a niche strategy, in which a firm concentrates its resources on a specific customer segment or product area that larger rivals neglect, in order to specialize and dominate it. Leader, challenger and follower strategies are the positions of firms competing across the broader market by market share.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
