  '3.0',
  'Q49. Which of the following is a strategy that concentrates resources in the segment of a
 specific customer or specific product in order to achieve specialization?

 a) Challenger strategy b) Follower strategy
 c) Leader strategy d) Niche strategy',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  50,
  'Q50. Which of the following is an explanation of core competence that is adopted in business
 administration?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,391.74,533.16,423.13],"text":"Q50.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of core competence that is adopted in business\nadministration?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,507.75,460.21],"text":"a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of its products, services, and"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,521.01,496.21],"text":"operations through comparisons with the strongest competitor or advanced companies.\nb) It refers to dramatical improvements in the costs, quality, service, and speed of a"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,527.65,532.21],"text":"company by fundamentally reviewing and radically redesigning its business processes.\nc) It refers to the company’s unique skills, technologies, and other strenghts that are"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,530.26,568.21],"text":"superior to other companies, which serve as a source of competitive advantage.\nd) It refers to the management of the allocation of company-wide management resources in"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[102.12,572.93,508.3,604.21],"text":"an effective and integrated manner so as to achieve an improvement in management\nefficiency."},{"type":"code","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 19 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of its products, services, and\n operations through comparisons with the strongest competitor or advanced companies."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to dramatical improvements in the costs, quality, service, and speed of a\n company by fundamentally reviewing and radically redesigning its business processes."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to the company’s unique skills, technologies, and other strenghts that are\n superior to other companies, which serve as a source of competitive advantage."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the management of the allocation of company-wide management resources in\n an effective and integrated manner so as to achieve an improvement in management\n efficiency."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Core competence is a company''s unique skills, technologies and other strengths that are superior to competitors'' and hard to imitate, and that serve as the source of its competitive advantage. Comparing against the strongest competitors is benchmarking, radically redesigning business processes is BPR, and integrated management of company-wide resources describes ERP.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q50)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q50. Which of the following is an explanation of core competence that is adopted in business
 administration?

 a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of its products, services, and
 operations through comparisons with the strongest competitor or advanced companies.
 b) It refers to dramatical improvements in the costs, quality, service, and speed of a
 company by fundamentally reviewing and radically redesigning its business processes.
 c) It refers to the company’s unique skills, technologies, and other strenghts that are
 superior to other companies, which serve as a source of competitive advantage.
 d) It refers to the management of the allocation of company-wide management resources in
 an effective and integrated manner so as to achieve an improvement in management
 efficiency.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  51,
  'Q51. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of telemarketing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,451.72,81.19],"text":"Q51.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of telemarketing?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,484.76,118.21],"text":"a) It refers to direct marketing that includes calling people at home and asking for"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,488.42,154.21],"text":"donations, opinions, or purchases.\nb) It refers to direct marketing that sells products and services and builds customer"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,525.99,190.21],"text":"relationships over the Internet.\nc) It refers to direct marketing that sends offers, announcements, reminders, or other items"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,467.06,226.21],"text":"to a person at a particular address.\nd) It refers to direct marketing that sends sales alerts, links to website updates,"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,230.93,405.09,244.21],"text":"appointments, or delivery reminders to large groups of people."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to direct marketing that includes calling people at home and asking for\n donations, opinions, or purchases."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to direct marketing that sells products and services and builds customer\n relationships over the Internet."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to direct marketing that sends offers, announcements, reminders, or other items\n to a person at a particular address."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to direct marketing that sends sales alerts, links to website updates,\n appointments, or delivery reminders to large groups of people."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Telemarketing is direct marketing over the telephone, such as calling people at home to ask for donations, opinions or purchases. Selling and building relationships over the Internet is online marketing, sending offers to a postal address is direct mail marketing, and sending alerts and reminders to large groups describes mass email or mobile messaging.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q51)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q51. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of telemarketing?

 a) It refers to direct marketing that includes calling people at home and asking for
 donations, opinions, or purchases.
 b) It refers to direct marketing that sells products and services and builds customer
 relationships over the Internet.
 c) It refers to direct marketing that sends offers, announcements, reminders, or other items
 to a person at a particular address.
 d) It refers to direct marketing that sends sales alerts, links to website updates,
 appointments, or delivery reminders to large groups of people.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
