(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  52,
  'Q52. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the technology S curve?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,283.74,495.34,297.19],"text":"Q52.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of the technology S curve?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,523.62,334.21],"text":"a) It represents the diffusion process of a new technology. It shows that the growth rate of"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,522.66,388.21],"text":"the penetration rate gradually decreases as products applying the technology penetrate\nthe market, by using a frequency distribution curve.\nb) It represents the maturing process of technology. It shows that during the time until the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,515.72,424.21],"text":"new technology is actually spread, the degree of awareness changes as time passes.\nc) It represents the process of technological progress. It shows that technology advances"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,506.65,460.21],"text":"slowly at the beginning, then advances rapidly, and thereafter, slowly stagnates.\nd) It represents the relationship between production volume and unit cost. It shows the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,464.93,500.66,496.21],"text":"course of reduction in unit cost with an increase in cumulative production volume."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It represents the diffusion process of a new technology. It shows that the growth rate of\n the penetration rate gradually decreases as products applying the technology penetrate\n the market, by using a frequency distribution curve."},{"label":"b","text":"It represents the maturing process of technology. It shows that during the time until the\n new technology is actually spread, the degree of awareness changes as time passes."},{"label":"c","text":"It represents the process of technological progress. It shows that technology advances\n slowly at the beginning, then advances rapidly, and thereafter, slowly stagnates."},{"label":"d","text":"It represents the relationship between production volume and unit cost. It shows the\n course of reduction in unit cost with an increase in cumulative production volume."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The technology S curve describes technological progress: performance improves slowly at first, then rapidly, and finally levels off as the technology approaches its limits, which signals the time to shift to a new technology. The link between unit cost and cumulative production volume is the experience curve, and the awareness change over time describes the hype cycle.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q52)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q52. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of the technology S curve?

 a) It represents the diffusion process of a new technology. It shows that the growth rate of
 the penetration rate gradually decreases as products applying the technology penetrate
 the market, by using a frequency distribution curve.
 b) It represents the maturing process of technology. It shows that during the time until the
 new technology is actually spread, the degree of awareness changes as time passes.
 c) It represents the process of technological progress. It shows that technology advances
 slowly at the beginning, then advances rapidly, and thereafter, slowly stagnates.
 d) It represents the relationship between production volume and unit cost. It shows the
 course of reduction in unit cost with an increase in cumulative production volume.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
