 and are able to identify themselves to other devices?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,500.93,533.16,586.21],"text":"Q53.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate computing concept that describes the idea of\nphysical objects, such as devices, vehicles, and buildings, that are connected to the Internet\nand are able to identify themselves to other devices?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,418.18,658.21],"text":"a) Computer networks\nb) Deep learning\nc) Internet of things\nd) Network topology"},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Computer networks"},{"label":"b","text":"Deep learning"},{"label":"c","text":"Internet of things"},{"label":"d","text":"Network topology"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The Internet of Things (IoT) is the concept of physical objects such as devices, vehicles and buildings being connected to the Internet, identifying themselves and exchanging data with other devices and systems. Computer networks and network topology describe how computers are connected and arranged in general, and deep learning is a machine learning technique.',
