  'A',
  54,
  'Q54. A factory manufactures the three products that are shown in the table below. Which of the following is the maximum possible profit in dollars? Here, there is an upper limit to the monthly demand volume for each product. Also, the factory can only use up to 200 hours per month for the manufacturing process and cannot manufacture more than one products in parallel.',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q54. A factory manufactures the three products that are shown in the table below. Which of the following is the maximum possible profit in dollars? Here, there is an upper limit to the monthly demand volume for each product. Also, the factory can only use up to 200 hours per month for the manufacturing process and cannot manufacture more than one products in parallel."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-april-a-q54-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"26,250"},{"label":"b","text":"30,000"},{"label":"c","text":"31,500"},{"label":"d","text":"33,000"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum profit is 33,000 dollars. Time is the scarce resource (200 hours = 12,000 minutes), so rank products by profit per minute: X earns 18/6 = 3, Y earns 25/10 = 2.5 and Z earns 30/15 = 2. Making all 1,000 units of X uses 6,000 minutes and earns 18,000; the remaining 6,000 minutes make 600 units of Y for 15,000, so the total is 33,000.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q54)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q54. A factory manufactures the three products that are shown in the table below. Which of
 the following is the maximum possible profit in dollars? Here, there is an upper limit to the
 monthly demand volume for each product. Also, the factory can only use up to 200 hours
 per month for the manufacturing process and cannot manufacture more than one products
 in parallel.

 Product X Product Y Product Z
 Profit per unit (dollars) 18 25 30
 Manufacturing time required per unit
 6 10 15
 (minutes)
 Limit to monthly demand (units) 1,000 900 500

 a) 26,250 b) 30,000 c) 31,500 d) 33,000',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
