(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  56,
  'Q56. Which of the following is the maximum value of Z from the constraints that are shown
 below?

 x + y ≤4
 x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0
 Z= 3x + 4y',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,576.48,533.14,607.93],"text":"Q56.\nWhich of the following is the maximum value of Z from the constraints that are shown\nbelow?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,630.65,187.16,696.85],"text":"x + y ≤4\nx ≥ 0, y ≥ 0\nZ= 3x + 4y"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,702.65,470.1,715.93],"text":"a) 12\nb) 14\nc) 16\nd) 18"},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"12"},{"label":"b","text":"14"},{"label":"c","text":"16"},{"label":"d","text":"18"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum value of Z is 16. In linear programming the optimum lies at a vertex of the feasible region, here (0,0), (4,0) and (0,4), where Z = 0, 12 and 16 respectively. Because y has the larger coefficient, putting all of the allowance into y (x = 0, y = 4) gives Z = 3×0 + 4×4 = 16.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q56)',
