(
  '2024-april',
  'A',
  57,
  'Q57. When a company wants to earn a profit of $42,000, which of following is the number
 of units that the company must sell under the conditions shown in the table below?

 Unit: dollar

 Selling price per unit 17

 Fixed costs
 General and administrative expense 130,000
 Interest expense 10,000

 Variable costs
 General and administrative expense 3
 Selling expense 4',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,520.65,100.21],"text":"Q57.\nWhen a company wants to earn a profit of $42,000, which of following is the number\nof units that the company must sell under the conditions shown in the table below?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,122.4,365.33,134.55],"text":"Unit: dollar"},{"type":"table","page":22,"bbox":[100.68,137.46,376.86,264.96],"rows":[["Selling price per unit","17"],["Fixed costs\nGeneral and administrative expense\nInterest expense","130,000\n10,000"],["Variable costs\nGeneral and administrative expense\nSelling expense","3\n4"]]},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,140.88,374.2,153.03],"text":"Selling price per unit\n17"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,159.36,374.21,171.51],"text":"Fixed costs"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,177.36,374.23,189.51],"text":"General and administrative expense\n130,000"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,195.36,374.19,207.51],"text":"Interest expense\n10,000"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,213.9,374.23,226.05],"text":"Variable costs"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,231.9,374.24,244.05],"text":"General and administrative expense\n3"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[106.02,249.9,374.26,262.05],"text":"Selling expense\n4"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,286.91,491.1,300.19],"text":"a) 14,000\nb) 18,200\nc) 26,000\nd) 26,200"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"14,000"},{"label":"b","text":"18,200"},{"label":"c","text":"26,000"},{"label":"d","text":"26,200"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The company must sell 18,200 units. The variable cost per unit is 3 + 4 = 7 dollars, so each unit contributes 17 − 7 = 10 dollars, and total fixed costs are 130,000 + 10,000 = 140,000. The required volume is (fixed costs + target profit) ÷ contribution per unit = (140,000 + 42,000) ÷ 10 = 18,200; 14,000 is only the break-even volume with no profit.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-A, Q57)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q57. When a company wants to earn a profit of $42,000, which of following is the number
