(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  1,
  'Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** through ***C*** in the program.

A school determines the letter grade that a student will receive based on the score, which is
 an integer value between 0 and 100, as follows:

Score Letter grade Description
 80 – 100 D Pass with distinction
 50 – 79 P Pass
 0 – 49 F Fail

The function grade receives a score (non-negative integer value between 0 and 100) and
 returns the letter grade as a character.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** through ***C*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"A school determines the letter grade that a student will receive based on the score, which is\n an integer value between 0 and 100, as follows:\n\nScore Letter grade Description\n 80 – 100 D Pass with distinction\n 50 – 79 P Pass\n 0 – 49 F Fail\n\nThe function grade receives a score (non-negative integer value between 0 and 100) and\n returns the letter grade as a character."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ character: grade(integer: score)\n  character: ret\n  if (score ***A*** 80)\n    ret ← \"D\"\n  elseif (score ***A*** 50)\n    ret ← ***B***\n  else\n    ret ← ***C***\n  endif\n  return ret"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B","C"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"=","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"=","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":">","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":">","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"≥","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"≥","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"= \"P\" \"F\"","values":{"A":"=","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"b","text":"= \"F\" \"P\"","values":{"A":"=","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}},{"label":"c","text":"> \"P\" \"F\"","values":{"A":">","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"d","text":"> \"F\" \"P\"","values":{"A":">","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}},{"label":"e","text":"≥ \"P\" \"F\"","values":{"A":"≥","B":"\"P\"","C":"\"F\""}},{"label":"f","text":"≥ \"F\" \"P\"","values":{"A":"≥","B":"\"F\"","C":"\"P\""}}]'::jsonb,
  'e',
  '{"value":"e"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = ≥, B = "P", C = "F". Score 80 must give D, so the first test is score ≥ 80; the elseif branch is only reached for scores below 80, so score ≥ 50 covers 50 to 79 and returns "P", and everything else (0 to 49) falls to the else branch and returns "F". Using > would wrongly send a score of exactly 80 to P and exactly 50 to F.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-B, Q1)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ___A___ through ___C___ in the program.

 A school determines the letter grade that a student will receive based on the score, which is
 an integer value between 0 and 100, as follows:

 Score Letter grade Description
 80 – 100 D Pass with distinction
 50 – 79 P Pass
 0 – 49 F Fail

 The function grade receives a score (non-negative integer value between 0 and 100) and
 returns the letter grade as a character.

 [Program]
 ○ character: grade(integer: score)
 character: ret
 if (score ___A___ 80)
 ret ← "D"
 elseif (score ___A___ 50)
 ret ← ___B___
 else
 ret ← ___C___
 endif
 return ret

 Answer group
 A B C
 a) = "P" "F"
 b) = "F" "P"
 c) > "P" "F"
 d) > "F" "P"
 e) ≥ "P" "F"
 f) ≥ "F" "P"',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/questions.pdf","pages":[4]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  2,
  'Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the program.

A bus company operates buses between two cities. The standard ticket price is 20 US dollars
 and the discount ticket price for passenger aged 10 and under or aged 60 and over is 10 US
 dollars. Additionally, registered members of all ages always get the ticket at the discount
 price.

The function ticketPrice receives the arguments age (a non-negative integer value) and
 isMember (a boolean indicating that the passenger is a member if the value is true), which
 returns the value ret as the ticket price (in US dollars).',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in\n the program."},{"type":"context","text":"A bus company operates buses between two cities. The standard ticket price is 20 US dollars\n and the discount ticket price for passenger aged 10 and under or aged 60 and over is 10 US\n dollars. Additionally, registered members of all ages always get the ticket at the discount\n price.\n\nThe function ticketPrice receives the arguments age (a non-negative integer value) and\n isMember (a boolean indicating that the passenger is a member if the value is true), which\n returns the value ret as the ticket price (in US dollars)."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ integer: ticketPrice(integer: age, boolean: isMember)\n  integer: ret\n  if (_______)\n    ret ← 10\n  else\n    ret ← 20\n  endif\n  return ret"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"((age ≤ 10) and (age ≥ 60)) and isMember"},{"label":"b","text":"((age ≤ 10) and (age ≥ 60)) or isMember"},{"label":"c","text":"((age ≤ 10) or (age ≥ 60)) and isMember"},{"label":"d","text":"((age ≤ 10) or (age ≥ 60)) or isMember"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is ((age ≤ 10) or (age ≥ 60)) or isMember. A passenger gets the 10-dollar price if they are 10 or under, or 60 or over, or a member, so every condition is joined with or. Using and between the age tests can never be true, since no age is both ≤ 10 and ≥ 60, and using and with isMember would wrongly deny the discount to non-member children and seniors.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-B, Q2)',
  ARRAY[5]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the program.

 A bus company operates buses between two cities. The standard ticket price is 20 US dollars
 and the discount ticket price for passenger aged 10 and under or aged 60 and over is 10 US
 dollars. Additionally, registered members of all ages always get the ticket at the discount
 price.

 The function ticketPrice receives the arguments age (a non-negative integer value) and
 isMember (a boolean indicating that the passenger is a member if the value is true), which
 returns the value ret as the ticket price (in US dollars).

 [Program]
 ○ integer: ticketPrice(integer: age, boolean: isMember)
 integer: ret
 if (_______)
 ret ← 10
 else
 ret ← 20
 endif
 return ret

 Answer group
 a) ((age ≤ 10) and (age ≥ 60)) and isMember
 b) ((age ≤ 10) and (age ≥ 60)) or isMember
 c) ((age ≤ 10) or (age ≥ 60)) and isMember
 d) ((age ≤ 10) or (age ≥ 60)) or isMember',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/questions.pdf","pages":[5]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  3,
  'Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the program.

The program outputs the even numbers between 1 and 100. Subsequently, it prints the sum
 of those even numbers. Note that division is performed for data type integer, that is, a ÷ b is
 the quotient of a divided by b.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in\n the program."},{"type":"context","text":"The program outputs the even numbers between 1 and 100. Subsequently, it prints the sum\n of those even numbers. Note that division is performed for data type integer, that is, a ÷ b is\n the quotient of a divided by b."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"i ÷ 2 = 0"},{"label":"b","text":"i ÷ 2 ≠ 0"},{"label":"c","text":"i mod 2 = 0"},{"label":"d","text":"i mod 2 ≠ 0"},{"label":"e","text":"i = 2"},{"label":"f","text":"i ≠ 2"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is i mod 2 = 0. A number is even exactly when the remainder after dividing by 2 is zero, so this condition outputs and adds 2, 4, ..., 100. The tempting i ÷ 2 = 0 tests the integer quotient instead, which is 0 only for i = 1, so it selects the wrong number.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-B, Q3)',
  ARRAY[6]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the program.

 The program outputs the even numbers between 1 and 100. Subsequently, it prints the sum
 of those even numbers. Note that division is performed for data type integer, that is, a ÷ b is
 the quotient of a divided by b.

 [Program]

 integer: i
 integer: sum ← 0

 for(increase i from 1 to 100 by 1)
 if(_______)
 output i
 sum ← sum + i
 endif
 endfor
 output sum

 Answer group
 a) i ÷ 2 = 0 b) i ÷ 2 ≠ 0
 c) i mod 2 = 0 d) i mod 2 ≠ 0
 e) i = 2 f) i ≠ 2',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/questions.pdf","pages":[6]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  4,
  'Q4. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program.

The function sumDigits receives a non-negative integer value num as argument, and returns
 the sum of the digits of num.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q4. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"The function sumDigits receives a non-negative integer value num as argument, and returns\n the sum of the digits of num."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ integer: sumDigits(integer: num)\n  integer: sum ← 0\n  while (num > 0)\n    sum ← ***A***\n    num ← ***B***\n  endwhile\n  return sum"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"sum + num mod 10","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"sum + num mod 10","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + num mod 10","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + num mod 10","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"sum + num mod 10 num mod 10","values":{"A":"sum + num mod 10","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"b","text":"sum + num mod 10 integer part of (num ÷ 10)","values":{"A":"sum + num mod 10","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"c","text":"sum × 10 + num mod 10 num mod 10","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + num mod 10","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"d","text":"sum × 10 + num mod 10 integer part of (num ÷ 10)","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + num mod 10","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"e","text":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10) num mod 10","values":{"A":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"f","text":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10) integer part of (num ÷ 10)","values":{"A":"sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}},{"label":"g","text":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10) num mod 10","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"num mod 10"}},{"label":"h","text":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10) integer part of (num ÷ 10)","values":{"A":"sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10)","B":"integer part of (num ÷ 10)"}}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = sum + num mod 10 and B = integer part of (num ÷ 10). Each loop adds the last digit (num mod 10) to sum and then removes that digit by integer-dividing num by 10, until num becomes 0; for 345 this adds 5, 4, 3 to give 12. sum × 10 + num mod 10 would instead build the reversed number, and setting num to num mod 10 would never shrink num to 0.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-B, Q4)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q4. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ___A___ and ___B___ in the program.

 The function sumDigits receives a non-negative integer value num as argument, and returns
 the sum of the digits of num.

 [Program]
 ○ integer: sumDigits(integer: num)
 integer: sum ← 0
 while (num > 0)
 sum ← ___A___
 num ← ___B___
 endwhile
 return sum

 Answer group
 A B
 a) sum + num mod 10 num mod 10
 b) sum + num mod 10 integer part of (num ÷ 10)
 c) sum × 10 + num mod 10 num mod 10
 d) sum × 10 + num mod 10 integer part of (num ÷ 10)
 e) sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10) num mod 10
 f) sum + integer part of (num ÷ 10) integer part of (num ÷ 10)
 g) sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10) num mod 10
 h) sum × 10 + integer part of (num ÷ 10) integer part of (num ÷ 10)',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  5,
  'Q5. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program.

The function division receives two integer values a and b and returns the quotient of a
 divided by b. The function modulus receives two integer values a and b and returns the
 remainder of a divided by b. The procedure convert receives the value of seconds as the
 input argument and outputs that value in the form of hours, minutes, and seconds. For
 example, when the procedure convert is called as convert(5450) the output is “1, 30,
 50”. Here, suppose that the range of input values satisfy 0 ≤ input < 86400.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q5. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"The function division receives two integer values a and b and returns the quotient of a\n divided by b. The function modulus receives two integer values a and b and returns the\n remainder of a divided by b. The procedure convert receives the value of seconds as the\n input argument and outputs that value in the form of hours, minutes, and seconds. For\n example, when the procedure convert is called as convert(5450) the output is “1, 30,\n 50”. Here, suppose that the range of input values satisfy 0 ≤ input < 86400."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ convert(integer: input)\n  integer: hour, minute, second\n  second ← modulus(input, 60)\n  minute ← ***A***\n  hour ← ***B***\n  output hour, minute, second\n\n○ integer: division(integer: a, integer: b)\n  integer: u\n  u ← integer part of (a ÷ b)\n  return u\n\n○ integer: modulus(integer: a, integer: b)\n  integer: u\n  u ← a mod b\n  return u"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(input, 3600)"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(input, 3600)"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60) division(input, 3600)","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(input, 3600)"}},{"label":"b","text":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60) division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"c","text":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60) modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","values":{"A":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","B":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"d","text":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60) division(input, 3600)","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(input, 3600)"}},{"label":"e","text":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60) division(modulus(input, 60), 60)","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"division(modulus(input, 60), 60)"}},{"label":"f","text":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60) modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","values":{"A":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)","B":"modulus(division(input, 60), 60)"}}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = modulus(division(input, 60), 60) and B = division(input, 3600). Dividing the seconds by 60 gives the total minutes, and taking that mod 60 leaves only the minutes within the current hour; dividing the seconds by 3600 gives the whole hours. For 5450: 5450 ÷ 60 = 90 and 90 mod 60 = 30 minutes, 5450 ÷ 3600 = 1 hour, and 5450 mod 60 = 50 seconds, matching "1, 30, 50".',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024S, FE, Subject-B, Q5)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q5. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ___A___ and ___B___ in the program.

 The function division receives two integer values a and b and returns the quotient of a
 divided by b. The function modulus receives two integer values a and b and returns the
 remainder of a divided by b. The procedure convert receives the value of seconds as the
 input argument and outputs that value in the form of hours, minutes, and seconds. For
 example, when the procedure convert is called as convert(5450) the output is “1, 30,
 50”. Here, suppose that the range of input values satisfy 0 ≤ input < 86400.

 [Program]
 ○ convert(integer: input)
 integer: hour, minute, second
 second ← modulus(input, 60)
 minute ← ___A___
 hour ← ___B___
 output hour, minute, second

 ○ integer: division(integer: a, integer: b)
 integer: u
 u ← integer part of (a ÷ b)
 return u

 ○ integer: modulus(integer: a, integer: b)
 integer: u
 u ← a mod b
 return u

 Answer group
 A B
 a) division(modulus(input, 60), 60) division(input, 3600)
 b) division(modulus(input, 60), 60) division(modulus(input, 60), 60)
 c) division(modulus(input, 60), 60) modulus(division(input, 60), 60)
 d) modulus(division(input, 60), 60) division(input, 3600)
 e) modulus(division(input, 60), 60) division(modulus(input, 60), 60)
 f) modulus(division(input, 60), 60) modulus(division(input, 60), 60)',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-april/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-april',
  'B',
  6,
  'Q6. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the program.

The function count1 receives the bit8 type (8-bit type) argument byte, and returns the
 number of bits 1 in the argument. For example, when the function count1 is called as
 count1(11001011), the return value is 5.
 Here, operator & represents a bitwise logical product, operator | represents a bitwise logical
 sum; operator >> represents a logical shift to the right, and operator << represents a logical
 shift to the left. For example, v << n performs a logical shift of the value of v by n bits to
 the left.',
