  16,
  'Q16. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program.

The function m_sin calculates and returns the approximate value of sin(x) for the argument
 x using the Maclaurin expansion. The program calculates sin(x) using the approximate
 formula below:
 sin(x) = x/1! - x3/3! + x5/5! - … + (-1)n × ( x(2n+1)/(2n+1)!)
 Here, ! is the factorial symbol, and n is the first integer for which | x(2n+1) / (2n+1)! | ≤ 10-7 is
 satisfied.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q16. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"The function m_sin calculates and returns the approximate value of sin(x) for the argument\n x using the Maclaurin expansion. The program calculates sin(x) using the approximate\n formula below:\n sin(x) = x/1! - x3/3! + x5/5! - … + (-1)n × ( x(2n+1)/(2n+1)!)\n Here, ! is the factorial symbol, and n is the first integer for which | x(2n+1) / (2n+1)! | ≤ 10-7 is\n satisfied."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ real: m_sin(real: x)\n  real: vn ← x\n  real: k ← 1\n  real: sum ← vn\n  real: epsi ← 1×10-7\n  while (abs(vn) ***A***)  // abs(vn) returns the absolute value of vn\n    k ← k + 2\n    vn ← ***B***\n    sum ← sum + vn\n  endwhile\n  return sum\n\nAnswer group"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x ÷ k"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ k2"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ k2"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x ÷ k"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ k2"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"i","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ k2"}},{"label":"j","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"≤ epsi − vn × x ÷ k","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x ÷ k"}},{"label":"b","text":"≤ epsi − vn × x2 ÷ k2","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ k2"}},{"label":"c","text":"≤ epsi − vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"d","text":"≤ epsi − vn × xk ÷ k2","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ k2"}},{"label":"e","text":"≤ epsi − vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)","values":{"A":"≤ epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"f","text":"> epsi − vn × x ÷ k","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x ÷ k"}},{"label":"g","text":"> epsi − vn × x2 ÷ k2","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ k2"}},{"label":"h","text":"> epsi − vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × x2 ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}},{"label":"i","text":"> epsi − vn × xk ÷ k2","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ k2"}},{"label":"j","text":"> epsi − vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)","values":{"A":"> epsi","B":"− vn × xk ÷ ((k − 1) × k)"}}]'::jsonb,
  'h',
  '{"value":"h"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = > epsi and B = − vn × x² ÷ ((k − 1) × k). The loop must keep adding terms while the current term is still larger than 10⁻⁷, so it continues while abs(vn) > epsi. Each new term is obtained from the previous one: after k becomes 3, 5, 7, ..., multiplying by −x² and dividing by (k − 1) × k turns x/1! into −x³/3!, then x⁵/5!, and so on, which reuses vn instead of recomputing powers and factorials.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
