  17,
  'Q17. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description.

An information systems company S has a guideline related to any issue for workers doing
 their daily job. The company has an information security team responsible for related issues
 and updates workers’ knowledge on information security.

One morning, a company worker who had just started his daily job and successfully signed
 into the company’s enterprise system received the following email:

From: Administration Department Staff
 To: To whom it may concern
 Subject: Action Required: Please update your bank account information.

This email has been sent to employees who failed to receive their paychecks because
 their bank account information is incorrect. Please use the link below to update your
 account information ASAP. Please complete the update by noon today to receive
 your next paycheck in time.

Link: https://www.example.com/company-s/paycheck&param=xnt6a5mv9YeKK1

Soon, the worker realized that something wrong. He followed the guideline instead of
 clicking on the link in the email because he suspected this is a ***A*** attack, and it is
 typically conducted through ***B***. He also informed the company’s information
 security team to deal with the issue.

A few days later, the worker received an email from the information security team leader.
 The email was to notify that the issue was resolved, thanking the worker for his
 responsibility in handling the case according to the guideline.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q17. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description."},{"type":"context","text":"An information systems company S has a guideline related to any issue for workers doing\n their daily job. The company has an information security team responsible for related issues\n and updates workers’ knowledge on information security.\n\nOne morning, a company worker who had just started his daily job and successfully signed\n into the company’s enterprise system received the following email:\n\nFrom: Administration Department Staff\n To: To whom it may concern\n Subject: Action Required: Please update your bank account information.\n\nThis email has been sent to employees who failed to receive their paychecks because\n their bank account information is incorrect. Please use the link below to update your\n account information ASAP. Please complete the update by noon today to receive\n your next paycheck in time.\n\nLink: https://www.example.com/company-s/paycheck&param=xnt6a5mv9YeKK1\n\nSoon, the worker realized that something wrong. He followed the guideline instead of\n clicking on the link in the email because he suspected this is a ***A*** attack, and it is\n typically conducted through ***B***. He also informed the company’s information\n security team to deal with the issue.\n\nA few days later, the worker received an email from the information security team leader.\n The email was to notify that the issue was resolved, thanking the worker for his\n responsibility in handling the case according to the guideline."},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"man in the middle","B":"email with incorrect digital signatures"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"man in the middle","B":"links with malicious HTTP request parameters"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"phishing","B":"email directing someone to a spoofed web site"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"phishing","B":"email with incorrect digital signatures"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"SQL injection","B":"email directing someone to a spoofed web site"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"SQL injection","B":"links with malicious HTTP request parameters"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"man in the middle email with incorrect digital signatures","values":{"A":"man in the middle","B":"email with incorrect digital signatures"}},{"label":"b","text":"man in the middle links with malicious HTTP request parameters","values":{"A":"man in the middle","B":"links with malicious HTTP request parameters"}},{"label":"c","text":"phishing email directing someone to a spoofed web site","values":{"A":"phishing","B":"email directing someone to a spoofed web site"}},{"label":"d","text":"phishing email with incorrect digital signatures","values":{"A":"phishing","B":"email with incorrect digital signatures"}},{"label":"e","text":"SQL injection email directing someone to a spoofed web site","values":{"A":"SQL injection","B":"email directing someone to a spoofed web site"}},{"label":"f","text":"SQL injection links with malicious HTTP request parameters","values":{"A":"SQL injection","B":"links with malicious HTTP request parameters"}}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = phishing and B = email directing someone to a spoofed web site. The message impersonates an internal department, creates urgency, and asks the worker to click a link and enter bank details, which is the classic pattern of phishing. Man in the middle intercepts traffic between two parties and SQL injection attacks a database through crafted input, neither of which matches this email.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
