  18,
  'Q18. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be
 inserted into ***A*** through ***C*** in Table 1.

Company X is a small trading company. The company is about to provide a new e-commerce
 web site for customers to make purchases online. The company will also hosts its own email
 service for the employees to conduct business with partners and customers. Company X will
 utilize public key infrastructure (PKI) to provide security for both the web server and email
 service. PKI uses public key cryptography to manage the identity of servers or persons and
 is widely used on the Internet.

Mr. T, the IT support person of company X is assigned to prepare the web server and email
 service in accordance with the following requirements:

● The e-commerce web application will run on the web server that is certified by a third-party certification authority. All connections to the web server will be secured using
 HTTPS.

● The staff directory along with the contact information will be published on the web site
 to enable business partners and customers to use the information to securely
 communicate with employees of company X.

The actions taken by Mr. T are shown in Table 1.

Table 1 Actions taken by Mr. T

No Action
 1 To enable secure and trusted connections to the web server, Mr. T submits the web
 server certificate along with the ***A*** to the third-party certification
 authority. The certification authority signs the certificate with its own private key.
 Then, he installs the signed certificate on company X’s web server.
 2 To allow business partners and customers to send encrypted email messages to
 particular contacts in company X, Mr. T publishes the ***B*** along with the
 employee’s information in the staff directory on company X’s web site.
 3 To send digitally signed email messages to partners and customers, the employees
 of company X are required to install the ***C*** on their email clients.
 Therefore, Mr. T provides support to the employees who require assistance.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q18. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be\n inserted into ***A*** through ***C*** in Table 1."},{"type":"context","text":"Company X is a small trading company. The company is about to provide a new e-commerce\n web site for customers to make purchases online. The company will also hosts its own email\n service for the employees to conduct business with partners and customers. Company X will\n utilize public key infrastructure (PKI) to provide security for both the web server and email\n service. PKI uses public key cryptography to manage the identity of servers or persons and\n is widely used on the Internet.\n\nMr. T, the IT support person of company X is assigned to prepare the web server and email\n service in accordance with the following requirements:\n\n● The e-commerce web application will run on the web server that is certified by a third-party certification authority. All connections to the web server will be secured using\n HTTPS.\n\n● The staff directory along with the contact information will be published on the web site\n to enable business partners and customers to use the information to securely\n communicate with employees of company X.\n\nThe actions taken by Mr. T are shown in Table 1.\n\nTable 1 Actions taken by Mr. T\n\nNo Action\n 1 To enable secure and trusted connections to the web server, Mr. T submits the web\n server certificate along with the ***A*** to the third-party certification\n authority. The certification authority signs the certificate with its own private key.\n Then, he installs the signed certificate on company X’s web server.\n 2 To allow business partners and customers to send encrypted email messages to\n particular contacts in company X, Mr. T publishes the ***B*** along with the\n employee’s information in the staff directory on company X’s web site.\n 3 To send digitally signed email messages to partners and customers, the employees\n of company X are required to install the ***C*** on their email clients.\n Therefore, Mr. T provides support to the employees who require assistance."},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B","C"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"Employees’ private key","C":"customers’ private key"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"Employees’ private key","C":"customers’ public key"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"employees’ private key","C":"employee’s public key"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"customers’ private key"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"customers’ public key"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"employee’s private key"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"web server’s private key Employees’ private key customers’ private key","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"Employees’ private key","C":"customers’ private key"}},{"label":"b","text":"web server’s private key Employees’ private key customers’ public key","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"Employees’ private key","C":"customers’ public key"}},{"label":"c","text":"web server’s private key employees’ private key employee’s public key","values":{"A":"web server’s private key","B":"employees’ private key","C":"employee’s public key"}},{"label":"d","text":"web server’s public key employees’ public key customers’ private key","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"customers’ private key"}},{"label":"e","text":"web server’s public key employees’ public key customers’ public key","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"customers’ public key"}},{"label":"f","text":"web server’s public key employees’ public key employee’s private key","values":{"A":"web server’s public key","B":"employees’ public key","C":"employee’s private key"}}]'::jsonb,
  'f',
  '{"value":"f"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is A = web server''s public key, B = employees'' public key, C = employee''s private key. A certificate binds a public key to an identity, so the server''s public key is submitted for the CA to sign while the private key never leaves the server. Senders encrypt email with the recipient''s public key, so employees'' public keys are published, and a digital signature is created with the signer''s own private key, so each employee installs their private key in their email client.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
