  6,
  'Q6. The function f (n) is recursively defined in terms of the natural number n as below. Which
 of the following is the value of f (5)?

 f (n): if n≦1 then return 1 else return n + f (n−1)',
  '[{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,390.72,531.8,422.17],"text":"Q6.  The function f (n) is recursively defined in terms of the natural number n as below. Which"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,426.89,265.37,458.17],"text":"of the following is the value of f (5)?"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[85.2,462.18,348.9,494.17],"text":"f (n): if n≦1 then return 1 else return n + f (n−1)"},{"type":"text","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,498.89,441.72,548.17],"text":"a)\n6\nb) 9\nc) 15\nd) 25"},{"type":"code","page":6,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 6 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"6"},{"label":"b","text":"9"},{"label":"c","text":"15"},{"label":"d","text":"25"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'f(5) = 15. Unfolding the recursion: f(5) = 5 + f(4) = 5 + 4 + f(3) = 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + f(1), and f(1) = 1, so the total is 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 15. The function simply sums the integers from 1 to n.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
