(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  7,
  'Q7. Which of the following is the appropriate description of the “selection sort” algorithm?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,523.56,81.19],"text":"Q7.  Which of the following is the appropriate description of the “selection sort” algorithm?"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,516.08,118.21],"text":"a) An intermediate reference value is determined, and then the elements are divided into"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,502.71,172.21],"text":"two groups of “larger” values and “smaller” values. This operation is recursively\nrepeated.\nb) Each set of elements extracted at regular intervals is sorted, and then the interval is"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,523.29,208.21],"text":"further decreased. The operation is repeatedly performed until the interval becomes 1.\nc) The element with the largest value is determined and swapped for the last element, and"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,504.37,262.21],"text":"then the largest value of the unsorted elements is determined and swapped for the\nsecond-to-the-last element. This operation is repeated in the same way.\nd) Two adjacent elements are repeatedly compared and swapped if the first element is"},{"type":"text","page":7,"bbox":[102.12,266.93,516.01,298.21],"text":"larger than the second. This operation is repeated until all elements are arranged in an\norderly fashion."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"An intermediate reference value is determined, and then the elements are divided into\n two groups of “larger” values and “smaller” values. This operation is recursively\n repeated."},{"label":"b","text":"Each set of elements extracted at regular intervals is sorted, and then the interval is\n further decreased. The operation is repeatedly performed until the interval becomes 1."},{"label":"c","text":"The element with the largest value is determined and swapped for the last element, and\n then the largest value of the unsorted elements is determined and swapped for the\n second-to-the-last element. This operation is repeated in the same way."},{"label":"d","text":"Two adjacent elements are repeatedly compared and swapped if the first element is\n larger than the second. This operation is repeated until all elements are arranged in an\n orderly fashion."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Selection sort repeatedly finds the largest (or smallest) value among the unsorted elements and swaps it into its final position at the end of the unsorted part, which is description c. Choice a describes quicksort, b describes Shell sort, and d describes bubble sort.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q7)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q7. Which of the following is the appropriate description of the “selection sort” algorithm?

 a) An intermediate reference value is determined, and then the elements are divided into
 two groups of “larger” values and “smaller” values. This operation is recursively
 repeated.
 b) Each set of elements extracted at regular intervals is sorted, and then the interval is
 further decreased. The operation is repeatedly performed until the interval becomes 1.
 c) The element with the largest value is determined and swapped for the last element, and
 then the largest value of the unsorted elements is determined and swapped for the
 second-to-the-last element. This operation is repeated in the same way.
 d) Two adjacent elements are repeatedly compared and swapped if the first element is
 larger than the second. This operation is repeated until all elements are arranged in an
 orderly fashion.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
