  8,
  'Q8. What is the approximate performance of a CPU in MIPS, when the instruction mix of the CPU is shown in the table below? Here, the CPU does not use a pipeline architecture.

Instruction type | Instruction execution time in μs | Appearance ratio
Register to register operation | 0.3 | 30%
Register to memory operation | 0.6 | 50%
Conditional branch operation | 0.1 | 20%',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q8. What is the approximate performance of a CPU in MIPS, when the instruction mix of the CPU is shown in the table below? Here, the CPU does not use a pipeline architecture.\n\nInstruction type | Instruction execution time in μs | Appearance ratio\nRegister to register operation | 0.3 | 30%\nRegister to memory operation | 0.6 | 50%\nConditional branch operation | 0.1 | 20%"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0.03"},{"label":"b","text":"0.41"},{"label":"c","text":"2.44"},{"label":"d","text":"35.00"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The CPU performs about 2.44 MIPS. The average instruction time is 0.3 × 0.3 + 0.6 × 0.5 + 0.1 × 0.2 = 0.09 + 0.30 + 0.02 = 0.41 μs. The number of instructions per microsecond, which equals millions of instructions per second, is 1 ÷ 0.41 ≈ 2.44; 0.41 is the time per instruction, not the MIPS value.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
