  10,
  'Q10. Which of the following is the appropriate purpose of defragmentation of hard disks?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,322.91,514.84,372.19],"text":"Q10.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate purpose of defragmentation of hard disks?"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[91.98,376.91,367.66,444.19],"text":"a) To access disk files faster and more efficiently\nb) To clean up temporary and junk files\nc) To delete IBG (interblock gap) and increase capacity\nd) To protect disk drives from physical failures"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To access disk files faster and more efficiently"},{"label":"b","text":"To clean up temporary and junk files"},{"label":"c","text":"To delete IBG (interblock gap) and increase capacity"},{"label":"d","text":"To protect disk drives from physical failures"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Defragmentation is done to access disk files faster and more efficiently. Over time a file''s blocks become scattered across the disk, forcing extra head movements; defragmentation rearranges each file into contiguous areas to reduce seek time. It does not delete junk files, remove inter-block gaps, or protect against physical failure.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q10)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q10. Which of the following is the appropriate purpose of defragmentation of hard disks?

 a) To access disk files faster and more efficiently
 b) To clean up temporary and junk files
 c) To delete IBG (interblock gap) and increase capacity
 d) To protect disk drives from physical failures',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  11,
  'Q11. Which of the following is a fail-safe concept for improving the security and reliability
 of the information system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,484.74,523.2,498.19],"text":"Q11.\nWhich of the following is a fail-safe concept for improving the security and reliability"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,511.2,552.19],"text":"of the information system?\n\na) Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,556.91,532.49,588.19],"text":"system.\nb) Even when there is a partial system fault, the required functions of the overall system are"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,592.91,521.66,624.19],"text":"maintained.\nc) When a device configuring the system fails, damage can be minimized by enabling the"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,628.91,530.74,713.11],"text":"system to stop safely.\nd) When a system failure occurs, processing is continued by switching to a standby system."},{"type":"code","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 8 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the\n system."},{"label":"b","text":"Even when there is a partial system fault, the required functions of the overall system are\n maintained."},{"label":"c","text":"When a device configuring the system fails, damage can be minimized by enabling the\n system to stop safely."},{"label":"d","text":"When a system failure occurs, processing is continued by switching to a standby system."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Fail-safe means that when a component fails, the system moves to a safe state, such as stopping safely, so that damage is minimized. Choice a describes fool-proofing, b describes fail-soft (graceful degradation), and d describes fault-tolerant switching to a standby system.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q11)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q11. Which of the following is a fail-safe concept for improving the security and reliability
 of the information system?

 a) Even when the user performs an incorrect operation, a problem does not occur in the
 system.
 b) Even when there is a partial system fault, the required functions of the overall system are
 maintained.
 c) When a device configuring the system fails, damage can be minimized by enabling the
 system to stop safely.
 d) When a system failure occurs, processing is continued by switching to a standby system.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
