 having a higher priority than B. Which of the following is the action that the OS takes?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,446.76,521.4,514.21],"text":"Q14.\nA real-time OS that performs preemptive priority scheduling for tasks A and B with A\nhaving a higher priority than B. Which of the following is the action that the OS takes?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,495.41,532.21],"text":"a) When A is launched during the execution of B, B is put into a ready state and A is"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,504.77,568.21],"text":"executed.\nb) When A is launched during the execution of B, B is put into a waiting state and A is"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,495.41,604.21],"text":"executed.\nc) When B is launched during the execution of A, A is put into a ready state and B is"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,504.77,640.21],"text":"executed.\nd) When B is launched during the execution of A, A is put into a waiting state and B is"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[102.12,644.93,150.78,658.21],"text":"executed."},{"type":"code","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 9 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"When A is launched during the execution of B, B is put into a ready state and A is\n executed."},{"label":"b","text":"When A is launched during the execution of B, B is put into a waiting state and A is\n executed."},{"label":"c","text":"When B is launched during the execution of A, A is put into a ready state and B is\n executed."},{"label":"d","text":"When B is launched during the execution of A, A is put into a waiting state and B is\n executed."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'When the higher-priority task A is launched while B is running, the OS preempts B, puts B into the ready state, and runs A. B goes to ready rather than waiting, because B is not waiting for any event; it can run again as soon as the CPU is free. A lower-priority task such as B can never preempt A.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q14)',
  ARRAY[9]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
