  '2024-october',
  'A',
  16,
  'Q16. A graphical symbol for the 2-to-1 MUX (multiplexer) and its truth table are shown in
 the figure below. The MUX has two data inputs (I₀, I₁), one select-line (S) and one output
 (Z). If the select line is S=0, then the output Z is switched to input I₀, whereas if a select line
 is S=1, then the output Z is switched to input I₁.

 Which of the following is a logic gate that is equivalent to the circuit implemented with the
 2-to-1 MUX below?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,520.09,82.21],"text":"Q16.\nA graphical symbol for the 2-to-1 MUX (multiplexer) and its truth table are shown in"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[85.74,86.95,517.7,100.21],"text":"the figure below. The MUX has two data inputs (I₀, I₁), one select-line (S) and one output"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[85.74,104.95,530.06,118.21],"text":"(Z). If the select line is S=0, then the output Z is switched to input I₀, whereas if a select line"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[85.74,122.93,316.5,136.21],"text":"is S=1, then the output Z is switched to input I₁."},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[86.34,247.87,533.16,261.13],"text":"Which of the following is a logic gate that is equivalent to the circuit implemented with the"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[86.34,265.87,187.32,279.13],"text":"2-to-1 MUX below?"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[95.28,401.83,423.3,415.09],"text":"a)\nb)\nc)\nd)"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-october-a-q16-figure1.webp","2024-october-a-q16-figure2.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2024-october-a-q16-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2024-october-a-q16-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2024-october-a-q16-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2024-october-a-q16-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The circuit is equivalent to an XOR gate. X2 feeds input I0 directly and NOT X2 feeds I1, with X1 as the select line. When X1 = 0 the output is X2, and when X1 = 1 the output is NOT X2, so Y = X1''·X2 + X1·X2'', which is X1 XOR X2.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
