  17,
  'Q17. Audio signals are recorded using 8-bit samples at a sampling rate of 11,000 times per
 second. When a flash memory of 512 × 10⁶ bytes is used, what is the maximum recording
 time of such data in minutes?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,477.78,533.17,509.17],"text":"Q17.\nAudio signals are recorded using 8-bit samples at a sampling rate of 11,000 times per\nsecond. When a flash memory of 512 × 10⁶ bytes is used, what is the maximum recording"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[85.08,513.91,229.06,527.17],"text":"time of such data in minutes?"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[84.12,550.99,476.1,564.25],"text":"a) 77\nb) 96\nc) 775\nd) 969"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"77"},{"label":"b","text":"96"},{"label":"c","text":"775"},{"label":"d","text":"969"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum recording time is about 775 minutes. Each 8-bit sample is 1 byte, so the data rate is 11,000 bytes per second. 512 × 10⁶ ÷ 11,000 ≈ 46,545 seconds, and 46,545 ÷ 60 ≈ 775.8, so 775 full minutes fit.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
