  22,
  'Q22. Which of the following is a property on a database that guarantees a result where a
 transaction either fully completes update processing or is revoked as if no processing took
 place at all?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,212.76,520.98,262.21],"text":"Q22.\nWhich of the following is a property on a database that guarantees a result where a\ntransaction either fully completes update processing or is revoked as if no processing took\nplace at all?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,500.18,298.21],"text":"a) Atomicity\nb) Consistency\nc) Durability\nd) Isolation"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Atomicity"},{"label":"b","text":"Consistency"},{"label":"c","text":"Durability"},{"label":"d","text":"Isolation"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'This is atomicity, the A in ACID: a transaction is all or nothing, so it either completes every update or is fully revoked. Consistency keeps the data valid against its rules, isolation stops concurrent transactions from interfering with each other, and durability keeps committed results after a failure.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q22)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q22. Which of the following is a property on a database that guarantees a result where a
 transaction either fully completes update processing or is revoked as if no processing took
 place at all?

 a) Atomicity b) Consistency c) Durability d) Isolation',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  23,
  'Q23. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a device that connects LANs?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,338.76,521.2,352.21],"text":"Q23.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of a device that connects LANs?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,520.02,406.21],"text":"a) A bridge relays frames based on IP addresses.\nb) A gateway converts the protocols of only the first through third levels in the OSI basic"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,529.35,442.21],"text":"reference model.\nc) A repeater extends the transmission distance by amplifying signals between segments of"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,340.37,496.21],"text":"the same type.\nd) A router relays frames based on MAC addresses."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A bridge relays frames based on IP addresses."},{"label":"b","text":"A gateway converts the protocols of only the first through third levels in the OSI basic\n reference model."},{"label":"c","text":"A repeater extends the transmission distance by amplifying signals between segments of\n the same type."},{"label":"d","text":"A router relays frames based on MAC addresses."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct statement is that a repeater extends transmission distance by amplifying (regenerating) signals between segments of the same type; it works at the physical layer. The others are wrong because a bridge relays frames using MAC addresses, a router relays packets using IP addresses, and a gateway handles protocol conversion up to the upper layers, not only layers 1 to 3.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q23)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q23. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a device that connects LANs?

 a) A bridge relays frames based on IP addresses.
 b) A gateway converts the protocols of only the first through third levels in the OSI basic
 reference model.
 c) A repeater extends the transmission distance by amplifying signals between segments of
 the same type.
 d) A router relays frames based on MAC addresses.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  24,
  'Q24. What is the broadcast address of the network 192.168.128.0/22?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,500.93,419.11,531.26],"text":"Q24.\nWhat is the broadcast address of the network 192.168.128.0/22?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,554.93,390.24,604.21],"text":"a) 192.168.128.127\nb) 192.168.128.255\nc) 192.168.131.255\nd) 192.168.255.255"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"192.168.128.127"},{"label":"b","text":"192.168.128.255"},{"label":"c","text":"192.168.131.255"},{"label":"d","text":"192.168.255.255"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The broadcast address is 192.168.131.255. A /22 prefix leaves 10 host bits, so the block covers 4 values in the third octet: 128 to 131. Setting all host bits to 1 gives 192.168.131.255, while 192.168.128.255 would be the broadcast address of a /24 network.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q24)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q24. What is the broadcast address of the network 192.168.128.0/22?

 a) 192.168.128.127 b) 192.168.128.255
 c) 192.168.131.255 d) 192.168.255.255',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  25,
  'Q25. Which of the following is a protocol to gather information on network components to
 manage and troubleshoot the network?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,608.76,520.4,676.21],"text":"Q25.\nWhich of the following is a protocol to gather information on network components to\nmanage and troubleshoot the network?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,680.93,503.44,712.21],"text":"a) NTP\nb) SMTP\nc) SNMP\nd) TELNET"},{"type":"code","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 14 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"NTP"},{"label":"b","text":"SMTP"},{"label":"c","text":"SNMP"},{"label":"d","text":"TELNET"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'SNMP (Simple Network Management Protocol) collects status and statistics from routers, switches and other network devices so administrators can monitor and troubleshoot the network. NTP synchronizes clocks, SMTP transfers email, and TELNET provides remote terminal access.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q25)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q25. Which of the following is a protocol to gather information on network components to
 manage and troubleshoot the network?

 a) NTP b) SMTP c) SNMP d) TELNET',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  26,
  'Q26. Which of the following is the way of using a phone to supply an Internet connection to
 other devices, such as a tablet or laptop computer over either Wi-Fi or Bluetooth?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,526.8,118.21],"text":"Q26.\nWhich of the following is the way of using a phone to supply an Internet connection to\nother devices, such as a tablet or laptop computer over either Wi-Fi or Bluetooth?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,364.46,172.21],"text":"a) Dedicated mobile hotspots\nb) PPPoE\nc) Tethering\nd) UPnP"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Dedicated mobile hotspots"},{"label":"b","text":"PPPoE"},{"label":"c","text":"Tethering"},{"label":"d","text":"UPnP"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Tethering is when a smartphone shares its mobile Internet connection with other devices over Wi-Fi, Bluetooth or USB. A dedicated mobile hotspot is a separate device built only for this purpose, PPPoE is a broadband connection protocol, and UPnP lets devices discover each other on a LAN.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q26)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q26. Which of the following is the way of using a phone to supply an Internet connection to
 other devices, such as a tablet or laptop computer over either Wi-Fi or Bluetooth?

 a) Dedicated mobile hotspots b) PPPoE
 c) Tethering d) UPnP',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  27,
  'Q27. Which of the following is an example of a phishing email?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,175.74,392.44,207.19],"text":"Q27.\nWhich of the following is an example of a phishing email?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,511.75,280.21],"text":"a) An email containing pop-up ads for products unrelated to the email\nb) An email intercepted, altered, and successfully sent\nc) An email with a link that automatically installs an application collecting and sending"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,374.7,334.21],"text":"data to the remote server\nd) An email with a link that redirects to a fake banking site"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"An email containing pop-up ads for products unrelated to the email"},{"label":"b","text":"An email intercepted, altered, and successfully sent"},{"label":"c","text":"An email with a link that automatically installs an application collecting and sending\n data to the remote server"},{"label":"d","text":"An email with a link that redirects to a fake banking site"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Phishing is an email that lures the recipient to a fake site, such as an imitation banking site, to steal credentials or personal data. An email that alters messages in transit is tampering or a man-in-the-middle attack, and a link that silently installs data-stealing software is a malware or spyware attack.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q27)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q27. Which of the following is an example of a phishing email?

 a) An email containing pop-up ads for products unrelated to the email
 b) An email intercepted, altered, and successfully sent
 c) An email with a link that automatically installs an application collecting and sending
 data to the remote server
 d) An email with a link that redirects to a fake banking site',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  28,
  'Q28. Which of the following bitwise logical operation can be applied in stream cipher
 between a plain text and a keystream to produce a cipher text, and between a ciphertext and
 the keystream to recover the plaintext?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,338.93,528.24,423.13],"text":"Q28.\nWhich of the following bitwise logical operation can be applied in stream cipher\nbetween a plain text and a keystream to produce a cipher text, and between a ciphertext and\nthe keystream to recover the plaintext?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,428.93,489.41,477.13],"text":"a) AND\nb) NAND\nc) OR\nd) XOR"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"AND"},{"label":"b","text":"NAND"},{"label":"c","text":"OR"},{"label":"d","text":"XOR"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Stream ciphers use XOR. Because (P XOR K) XOR K = P, XORing the plaintext with the keystream produces the ciphertext, and XORing the ciphertext with the same keystream recovers the plaintext. AND, OR and NAND lose information, so they cannot be reversed this way.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q28)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q28. Which of the following bitwise logical operation can be applied in stream cipher
 between a plain text and a keystream to produce a cipher text, and between a ciphertext and
 the keystream to recover the plaintext?

 a) AND b) NAND c) OR d) XOR',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  29,
  'Q29. Which of the following description is an appropriate use of asymmetric encryption to
 ensure the confidentiality of a message that a sender is going to send to a receiver?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,482.76,519.44,532.15],"text":"Q29.\nWhich of the following description is an appropriate use of asymmetric encryption to\nensure the confidentiality of a message that a sender is going to send to a receiver?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,536.93,394.74,622.15],"text":"a) The message is encrypted using a pre-shared secret key.\nb) The message is encrypted using a private key of the sender.\nc) The message is encrypted using a public key of the receiver.\nd) The message is encrypted using a public key of the sender."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The message is encrypted using a pre-shared secret key."},{"label":"b","text":"The message is encrypted using a private key of the sender."},{"label":"c","text":"The message is encrypted using a public key of the receiver."},{"label":"d","text":"The message is encrypted using a public key of the sender."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'For confidentiality, the sender encrypts the message with the receiver''s public key. Only the receiver holds the matching private key, so only the receiver can decrypt it. Encrypting with the sender''s private key is used for digital signatures (authenticity), not secrecy, and a pre-shared secret key is symmetric encryption.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q29)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q29. Which of the following description is an appropriate use of asymmetric encryption to
 ensure the confidentiality of a message that a sender is going to send to a receiver?

 a) The message is encrypted using a pre-shared secret key.
 b) The message is encrypted using a private key of the sender.
 c) The message is encrypted using a public key of the receiver.
 d) The message is encrypted using a public key of the sender.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. Which type of attack involves intercepting communication between sender and
 receiver?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,626.76,489.81,676.21],"text":"Q30.\nWhich type of attack involves intercepting communication between sender and\nreceiver?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,698.93,458.12,730.21],"text":"a) Brute Force Attack\nb) Man-in-the-Middle Attack\nc) Phishing Attack\nd) Ransomware Attack"},{"type":"code","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 15 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Brute Force Attack"},{"label":"b","text":"Man-in-the-Middle Attack"},{"label":"c","text":"Phishing Attack"},{"label":"d","text":"Ransomware Attack"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A man-in-the-middle attack places the attacker between sender and receiver, letting the attacker intercept, read and possibly alter the communication while both parties believe they are talking directly. Brute force guesses keys or passwords, phishing deceives users, and ransomware encrypts data for ransom.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q30)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q30. Which type of attack involves intercepting communication between sender and
 receiver?

 a) Brute Force Attack b) Man-in-the-Middle Attack
 c) Phishing Attack d) Ransomware Attack',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following refers to a technique that is used in a credential stuffing attack?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,528.21,81.19],"text":"Q31.\nWhich of the following refers to a technique that is used in a credential stuffing attack?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,517.07,118.21],"text":"a) Focusing on the case where there are users that set a word from the dictionary as their"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,519.02,172.21],"text":"password, selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack, and attempting to log in\nusing words in the dictionary and their combinations as the password\nb) Focusing on the case where there are users that use the same user ID and password on"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,520.63,226.21],"text":"multiple websites, and attempting to log in using a list of user IDs and passwords\nfraudulently acquired from other websites\nc) Selecting one (1) frequently used password, and attempting to log in by using user IDs"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,532.98,262.21],"text":"of all possible combinations of characters\nd) Selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack on a website that has a low maximum"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,517.56,316.21],"text":"number of characters for passwords, and attempting to log in by using the user ID and\npasswords of all possible combinations of characters"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Focusing on the case where there are users that set a word from the dictionary as their\n password, selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack, and attempting to log in\n using words in the dictionary and their combinations as the password"},{"label":"b","text":"Focusing on the case where there are users that use the same user ID and password on\n multiple websites, and attempting to log in using a list of user IDs and passwords\n fraudulently acquired from other websites"},{"label":"c","text":"Selecting one (1) frequently used password, and attempting to log in by using user IDs\n of all possible combinations of characters"},{"label":"d","text":"Selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack on a website that has a low maximum\n number of characters for passwords, and attempting to log in by using the user ID and\n passwords of all possible combinations of characters"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Credential stuffing takes user ID and password lists stolen from other websites and tries them on a different site, exploiting users who reuse the same credentials. Choice a describes a dictionary attack, c describes a reverse brute-force (password spraying) attack, and d describes a brute-force attack.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[16]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following refers to a technique that is used in a credential stuffing attack?

 a) Focusing on the case where there are users that set a word from the dictionary as their
 password, selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack, and attempting to log in
 using words in the dictionary and their combinations as the password
 b) Focusing on the case where there are users that use the same user ID and password on
 multiple websites, and attempting to log in using a list of user IDs and passwords
 fraudulently acquired from other websites
 c) Selecting one (1) frequently used password, and attempting to log in by using user IDs
 of all possible combinations of characters
 d) Selecting one (1) user ID as the target of the attack on a website that has a low maximum
 number of characters for passwords, and attempting to log in by using the user ID and
 passwords of all possible combinations of characters',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[16]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  32,
  'Q32. Which of the following is the name of an attack where manipulation is made to display
 a malicious website near the top of the results on a search website?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,320.93,527.78,424.21],"text":"Q32.\nWhich of the following is the name of an attack where manipulation is made to display\na malicious website near the top of the results on a search website?\n\na) Cross-site scripting\nb) DNS cache poisoning\nc) SEO poisoning\nd) Social engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Cross-site scripting"},{"label":"b","text":"DNS cache poisoning"},{"label":"c","text":"SEO poisoning"},{"label":"d","text":"Social engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'SEO poisoning abuses search engine optimization techniques so that a malicious website appears near the top of search results and attracts victims. DNS cache poisoning instead falsifies DNS records to redirect name lookups, and cross-site scripting injects scripts into vulnerable web pages.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
