  '3.0',
  'Q32. Which of the following is the name of an attack where manipulation is made to display
 a malicious website near the top of the results on a search website?

 a) Cross-site scripting b) DNS cache poisoning
 c) SEO poisoning d) Social engineering',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[16]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  33,
  'Q33. Which of the following is a function of security information and event management
 (SIEM)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,463.74,501.32,477.19],"text":"Q33. Which of the following is a function of security information and event management"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[85.08,481.85,130.08,495.13],"text":"(SIEM)?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,501.06,532.21],"text":"a) The centralized control of a range of communication devices in a network, and the"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,489.03,568.21],"text":"changing of network configuration and security settings\nb) The execution of a file in an isolated virtual environment, and the monitoring of"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,520.96,604.21],"text":"communication to a C&C server and other behavior\nc) The general analysis of logs that are collected from a range of devices, and the support"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,492.02,640.21],"text":"of analysis and action by an administrator\nd) The inspection of header information in packets, the identification of application"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[102.12,644.93,455.33,658.21],"text":"programs that receive communication, and the control of communication"},{"type":"code","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 16 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The centralized control of a range of communication devices in a network, and the\n changing of network configuration and security settings"},{"label":"b","text":"The execution of a file in an isolated virtual environment, and the monitoring of\n communication to a C&C server and other behavior"},{"label":"c","text":"The general analysis of logs that are collected from a range of devices, and the support\n of analysis and action by an administrator"},{"label":"d","text":"The inspection of header information in packets, the identification of application\n programs that receive communication, and the control of communication"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'SIEM collects logs from many devices such as servers, firewalls and IDSs, then correlates and analyzes them centrally to detect incidents and support the administrator''s response. Running files in an isolated virtual environment describes a sandbox, and controlling traffic by identifying applications in packets describes a next-generation firewall.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q33)',
  ARRAY[16]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q33. Which of the following is a function of security information and event management
 (SIEM)?

 a) The centralized control of a range of communication devices in a network, and the
 changing of network configuration and security settings
 b) The execution of a file in an isolated virtual environment, and the monitoring of
 communication to a C&C server and other behavior
