  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Concealing implementation details and exposing only a simplified interface for\n interacting with objects"},{"label":"b","text":"Creating a subclass instance inheriting attributes and behaviors from its superclass"},{"label":"c","text":"Defining multiple methods with the same name but different parameters"},{"label":"d","text":"Redefining in the child class a method that is already provided by the superclass with the\n same name and parameters but a different implementation"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Abstraction means hiding the implementation details and exposing only a simplified interface for using an object. Creating a subclass that inherits from a superclass is inheritance, defining methods with the same name but different parameters is overloading, and redefining a superclass method in the child class is overriding.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
