  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A mechanism that creates one (1) new object using multiple objects as its parts"},{"label":"b","text":"A mechanism where a lower-level class inherits the attribute or operation of a higher-level class"},{"label":"c","text":"A mechanism where an application of an operation to a certain object automatically\n causes the application of that operation to related objects"},{"label":"d","text":"A mechanism where an operation to a certain object is internally requested to be\n performed by another object"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Delegation is when an object receives a request for an operation and internally passes it to another object to carry out. Building one object from several part objects is aggregation or composition, a lower class receiving a higher class''s attributes is inheritance, and automatically applying an operation to related objects is propagation.',
