  38,
  'Q38. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of a stub or a driver used in a test?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.08,81.19],"text":"Q38.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate explanation of a stub or a driver used in a test?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,496.35,172.21],"text":"a) A driver is a module that is called from the module to be tested\nb) A driver passes arguments and calls the module to be tested\nc) A stub is a module used to call the module to be tested\nd) A stub is used to display or print the values returned from the module to be tested"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A driver is a module that is called from the module to be tested"},{"label":"b","text":"A driver passes arguments and calls the module to be tested"},{"label":"c","text":"A stub is a module used to call the module to be tested"},{"label":"d","text":"A stub is used to display or print the values returned from the module to be tested"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A driver is a test module that passes arguments to the module under test and calls it, standing in for a higher-level caller in bottom-up testing. A stub is the opposite: a dummy lower-level module that is called by the module under test, used in top-down testing. Choices a and c swap these roles.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
