  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,489.43,117.13],"text":"Q41.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate purpose for using a Work Breakdown\nStructure (WBS) in a software development project?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,525.99,136.21],"text":"a) To clarify the sequence relation of activities and understand the critical path that should"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,525.02,190.21],"text":"be intensively managed\nb) To hierarchically detail activities and segment them into a manageable scale\nc) To optimize the total cost when there is a trade-off between the duration and the cost of"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,520.27,226.21],"text":"development\nd) To represent the schedule of an activity with a horizontal bar, and clarify the start time"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[102.12,230.93,479.02,244.21],"text":"and end time of the activity as well as the progress at the present point in time"}]'::jsonb,
