  'Q43. Which of the following is a requirement for service level management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,482.76,495.08,550.21],"text":"Q43.\nWhich of the following is a requirement for service level management?\n\na) A capacity plan is created, implemented, and maintained while human, technical,"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,498.31,586.21],"text":"informational, and financial resources are considered.\nb) A service catalog and SLA are created for the service to be provided, and they are"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,484.72,622.21],"text":"agreed upon with the customer.\nc) Costs are monitored and reported against the budget; the financial forecasts are"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,626.93,510.94,676.15],"text":"reviewed, and costs are managed.\nd) Risks to service continuity and availability of services are assessed and documented."},{"type":"code","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 19 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A capacity plan is created, implemented, and maintained while human, technical,\n informational, and financial resources are considered."},{"label":"b","text":"A service catalog and SLA are created for the service to be provided, and they are\n agreed upon with the customer."},{"label":"c","text":"Costs are monitored and reported against the budget; the financial forecasts are\n reviewed, and costs are managed."},{"label":"d","text":"Risks to service continuity and availability of services are assessed and documented."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Service level management requires defining a service catalog and SLAs for the services provided and agreeing them with the customer, then monitoring performance against them. Capacity planning is capacity management, monitoring costs against a budget is budgeting and accounting for services, and assessing continuity risks is service continuity and availability management.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
