  45,
  'Q45. Which of the following is the most appropriate description of a system auditor?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,194.76,492.08,262.21],"text":"Q45.\nWhich of the following is the most appropriate description of a system auditor?\n\na) The entire audit interview must be conducted by one (1) system auditor, because"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,471.77,298.21],"text":"discrepancies may occur in the record if multiple auditors are involved.\nb) The system auditor must instruct the department being audited to implement"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,532.96,334.21],"text":"improvement measures for deficiencies identified during the audit interview.\nc) The system auditor must make an effort to obtain documents and records that support the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,531.69,370.21],"text":"information obtained from the department being audited during the audit interview.\nd) The system auditor must select audit interviewees from administrators who have been an"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,374.93,318.43,388.21],"text":"auditor within the department being audited."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The entire audit interview must be conducted by one (1) system auditor, because\n discrepancies may occur in the record if multiple auditors are involved."},{"label":"b","text":"The system auditor must instruct the department being audited to implement\n improvement measures for deficiencies identified during the audit interview."},{"label":"c","text":"The system auditor must make an effort to obtain documents and records that support the\n information obtained from the department being audited during the audit interview."},{"label":"d","text":"The system auditor must select audit interviewees from administrators who have been an\n auditor within the department being audited."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A system auditor should try to obtain documents and records that back up what was heard in the audit interview, because audit conclusions must rest on sufficient evidence. Auditors recommend improvements rather than instructing the audited department, and they must stay independent, so they should not pick interviewees from former auditors inside that department.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q45)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q45. Which of the following is the most appropriate description of a system auditor?

 a) The entire audit interview must be conducted by one (1) system auditor, because
 discrepancies may occur in the record if multiple auditors are involved.
 b) The system auditor must instruct the department being audited to implement
 improvement measures for deficiencies identified during the audit interview.
 c) The system auditor must make an effort to obtain documents and records that support the
 information obtained from the department being audited during the audit interview.
 d) The system auditor must select audit interviewees from administrators who have been an
 auditor within the department being audited.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  46,
  'Q46. Which of the following is an explanation of an application architecture that constitutes
 enterprise architecture?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,428.76,528.7,496.21],"text":"Q46.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of an application architecture that constitutes\nenterprise architecture?\n\na) It systematically describes the business processes or the information flows necessary for"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,530.0,532.21],"text":"the business strategy.\nb) It systematically describes the contents of the data necessary for business operations, the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,522.4,568.21],"text":"relations or structures between the data, etc.\nc) It systematically describes the functions or system configurations that support business"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,530.96,604.21],"text":"processes.\nd) It systematically describes the technical components necessary for the developments and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,608.93,289.42,622.21],"text":"operations of the information systems."},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It systematically describes the business processes or the information flows necessary for\n the business strategy."},{"label":"b","text":"It systematically describes the contents of the data necessary for business operations, the\n relations or structures between the data, etc."},{"label":"c","text":"It systematically describes the functions or system configurations that support business\n processes."},{"label":"d","text":"It systematically describes the technical components necessary for the developments and\n operations of the information systems."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Application architecture describes the functions and system configurations (applications) that support the business processes. In enterprise architecture, business architecture covers business processes and information flows, data architecture covers data content and relationships, and technology architecture covers the technical components.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q46)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q46. Which of the following is an explanation of an application architecture that constitutes
 enterprise architecture?

 a) It systematically describes the business processes or the information flows necessary for
 the business strategy.
 b) It systematically describes the contents of the data necessary for business operations, the
 relations or structures between the data, etc.
 c) It systematically describes the functions or system configurations that support business
 processes.
 d) It systematically describes the technical components necessary for the developments and
 operations of the information systems.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  47,
  'Q47. Which of the following is a description of the SOA?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,361.06,99.13],"text":"Q47.\nWhich of the following is a description of the SOA?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,531.69,118.21],"text":"a) A concept of constructing a system by considering the software functions as components"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,514.36,154.21],"text":"called services and combining them\nb) A concept of improving sales efficiency and quality by using IT for sales activities to"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,501.63,190.21],"text":"increase sales and profits as well as to improve customer satisfaction\nc) A concept of re-designing the business processes to innovatively improve the cost,"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,478.42,226.21],"text":"quality, service, and speed\nd) Outsourcing the in-house operations that are not part of the core businesses to"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[102.12,230.93,406.71,244.21],"text":"concentrate the management resources on the core businesses"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A concept of constructing a system by considering the software functions as components\n called services and combining them"},{"label":"b","text":"A concept of improving sales efficiency and quality by using IT for sales activities to\n increase sales and profits as well as to improve customer satisfaction"},{"label":"c","text":"A concept of re-designing the business processes to innovatively improve the cost,\n quality, service, and speed"},{"label":"d","text":"Outsourcing the in-house operations that are not part of the core businesses to\n concentrate the management resources on the core businesses"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'SOA (Service-Oriented Architecture) builds systems by treating software functions as reusable components called services and combining them, often across the network. Using IT to make sales activities efficient is SFA, redesigning business processes is BPR, and outsourcing non-core operations is BPO.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q47)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q47. Which of the following is a description of the SOA?

 a) A concept of constructing a system by considering the software functions as components
 called services and combining them
 b) A concept of improving sales efficiency and quality by using IT for sales activities to
 increase sales and profits as well as to improve customer satisfaction
 c) A concept of re-designing the business processes to innovatively improve the cost,
 quality, service, and speed
 d) Outsourcing the in-house operations that are not part of the core businesses to
 concentrate the management resources on the core businesses',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
