  'Q48. Which of the following is the work that is performed when non-functional requirements
 are defined?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,265.74,533.19,315.13],"text":"Q48.\nWhich of the following is the work that is performed when non-functional requirements\nare defined?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,533.06,352.21],"text":"a) Clarifying the flow of information (i.e., data) between the functions constituting business"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,531.62,406.21],"text":"operations\nb) Clarifying the interface for exchanging information with other systems\nc) Creating the technical requirements for the development criteria and standards according"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,391.42,460.21],"text":"to the programming language used in system development\nd) Defining the scope to be implemented as system functions"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Clarifying the flow of information (i.e., data) between the functions constituting business\n operations"},{"label":"b","text":"Clarifying the interface for exchanging information with other systems"},{"label":"c","text":"Creating the technical requirements for the development criteria and standards according\n to the programming language used in system development"},{"label":"d","text":"Defining the scope to be implemented as system functions"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Defining non-functional requirements includes setting technical requirements such as development criteria and standards for the programming language used. Non-functional requirements describe quality, performance and technical constraints, while clarifying information flows, defining interfaces with other systems and deciding which functions to implement are all part of functional requirements definition.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
