  '2024-october',
  'A',
  50,
  'Q50. In innovation theory, consumers are classified into five (5) groups innovators, early
 adopters, early majority, late majority, and laggards according to the timing of their
 purchase of a new product. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of the
 early adopters?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,511.22,136.21],"text":"Q50.\nIn innovation theory, consumers are classified into five (5) groups innovators, early\nadopters, early majority, late majority, and laggards according to the timing of their\npurchase of a new product. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of the\nearly adopters?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,530.68,172.21],"text":"a) A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at an early phase, has"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,526.1,226.21],"text":"a large impact on consumers, is sensitive to trends, and makes decisions after collecting\ninformation themselves\nb) A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at the soonest phase"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,511.31,262.21],"text":"without worrying about risks\nc) A group that is skeptical about the adoption of a new product or new technology and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,522.09,298.21],"text":"only adopts it after seeing it being adopted by most people around them\nd) A group that is the most conservative, has limited interest in movements in society and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,515.03,352.21],"text":"tends to adopt new trends only after they become common or, in some cases, remains\nfirm in refusing their adoption"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at an early phase, has\n a large impact on consumers, is sensitive to trends, and makes decisions after collecting\n information themselves"},{"label":"b","text":"A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at the soonest phase\n without worrying about risks"},{"label":"c","text":"A group that is skeptical about the adoption of a new product or new technology and\n only adopts it after seeing it being adopted by most people around them"},{"label":"d","text":"A group that is the most conservative, has limited interest in movements in society and\n tends to adopt new trends only after they become common or, in some cases, remains\n firm in refusing their adoption"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Early adopters adopt a new product at an early phase, are sensitive to trends, gather information themselves, and act as opinion leaders with a large influence on other consumers. The group that adopts first regardless of risk is the innovators, the skeptical group that follows most people is the late majority, and the most conservative group is the laggards.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q50)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q50. In innovation theory, consumers are classified into five (5) groups innovators, early
 adopters, early majority, late majority, and laggards according to the timing of their
 purchase of a new product. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of the
 early adopters?

 a) A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at an early phase, has
 a large impact on consumers, is sensitive to trends, and makes decisions after collecting
 information themselves
 b) A group that accepts a new product, service, or other such offering at the soonest phase
 without worrying about risks
 c) A group that is skeptical about the adoption of a new product or new technology and
 only adopts it after seeing it being adopted by most people around them
 d) A group that is the most conservative, has limited interest in movements in society and
 tends to adopt new trends only after they become common or, in some cases, remains
 firm in refusing their adoption',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  51,
  'Q51. Which of the following is a definition of Customer Relationship Management (CRM)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,373.74,526.4,387.19],"text":"Q51.\nWhich of the following is a definition of Customer Relationship Management (CRM)?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,528.38,424.21],"text":"a) A framework used to support and integrate processes, people, and information across an"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,507.8,478.21],"text":"organization to provide a unified gateway for information and a knowledge base for\nemployees, partners, and customers\nb) A technology for managing all of a company’s relationships and interactions with"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,525.03,514.21],"text":"customers and potential customers in order to improve business relationships\nc) A type of software that organizations use to manage day-to-day business activities such"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,531.27,568.21],"text":"as accounting, procurement, project management, risk management and compliance, and\nsupply chain operations\nd) The broad range of activities required to plan, control, and execute a product''s flow,"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[102.12,572.93,523.81,604.21],"text":"from acquiring raw materials and production through distribution to the final customer,\nin the most streamlined and cost-effective way possible"},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A framework used to support and integrate processes, people, and information across an\n organization to provide a unified gateway for information and a knowledge base for\n employees, partners, and customers"},{"label":"b","text":"A technology for managing all of a company’s relationships and interactions with\n customers and potential customers in order to improve business relationships"},{"label":"c","text":"A type of software that organizations use to manage day-to-day business activities such\n as accounting, procurement, project management, risk management and compliance, and\n supply chain operations"},{"label":"d","text":"The broad range of activities required to plan, control, and execute a product''s flow,\n from acquiring raw materials and production through distribution to the final customer,\n in the most streamlined and cost-effective way possible"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'CRM is the technology and approach for managing all of a company''s relationships and interactions with current and potential customers to improve those relationships and retention. Choice c describes ERP, d describes supply chain management, and a describes an enterprise information portal or knowledge management framework.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q51)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q51. Which of the following is a definition of Customer Relationship Management (CRM)?

 a) A framework used to support and integrate processes, people, and information across an
 organization to provide a unified gateway for information and a knowledge base for
 employees, partners, and customers
 b) A technology for managing all of a company’s relationships and interactions with
 customers and potential customers in order to improve business relationships
 c) A type of software that organizations use to manage day-to-day business activities such
 as accounting, procurement, project management, risk management and compliance, and
 supply chain operations
 d) The broad range of activities required to plan, control, and execute a product''s flow,
 from acquiring raw materials and production through distribution to the final customer,
 in the most streamlined and cost-effective way possible',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
