  52,
  'Q52. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of concurrent engineering?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,496.54,82.21],"text":"Q52.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of concurrent engineering?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,521.64,118.21],"text":"a) A product development technique that sequentially executes processes, such as design,"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,527.69,172.21],"text":"manufacturing, and sales activities\nb) A technique that analyzes a target system and clarifies its specifications\nc) A technique that executes processes, such as design and production planning, in parallel"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,514.4,208.21],"text":"with product development\nd) A technique that grasps the optimal combination of functions and costs and improves"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,286.7,244.21],"text":"value through systematic procedures"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A product development technique that sequentially executes processes, such as design,\n manufacturing, and sales activities"},{"label":"b","text":"A technique that analyzes a target system and clarifies its specifications"},{"label":"c","text":"A technique that executes processes, such as design and production planning, in parallel\n with product development"},{"label":"d","text":"A technique that grasps the optimal combination of functions and costs and improves\n value through systematic procedures"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Concurrent engineering carries out processes such as design and production planning in parallel with product development instead of one after another, shortening development time. Choice a describes the traditional sequential approach, b describes reverse engineering, and d describes value engineering.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q52)',
