(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  58,
  'Q58. Two (2) types of raw materials A and B are required to manufacture products X and Y. The quantity of each raw material required per unit and the procurable quantity are listed in the table below. When the profit per unit is $1 for product X and $1.5 for product Y , which of the following is the maximum profit in dollar?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q58. Two (2) types of raw materials A and B are required to manufacture products X and Y. The quantity of each raw material required per unit and the procurable quantity are listed in the table below. When the profit per unit is $1 for product X and $1.5 for product Y , which of the following is the maximum profit in dollar?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2024-october-a-q58-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"50"},{"label":"b","text":"60"},{"label":"c","text":"70"},{"label":"d","text":"80"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum profit is $70. Maximize x + 1.5y subject to 2x + y ≤ 100 and x + 2y ≤ 80. Solving both constraints as equalities gives x = 40 and y = 20, with profit 40 + 30 = 70, which is higher than the other corners (50, 0) giving $50 and (0, 40) giving $60.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q58)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q58. Two (2) types of raw materials A and B are required to manufacture products X and Y.
 The quantity of each raw material required per unit and the procurable quantity are listed in
 the table below. When the profit per unit is $1 for product X and $1.5 for product Y , which
 of the following is the maximum profit in dollar?

 Raw Required quantity Required quantity Procurable
 material per unit of product X per unit of product Y quantity
 A 2 1 100
 B 1 2 80

 a) 50 b) 60 c) 70 d) 80',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. When the selling price of a product is $50 and the fixed costs for production and sales
 are $100,000, which of the following is the number of units to be sold to achieve the desired
 profit of $50,000? Here, the variable cost ratio is 60%.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,304.74,531.57,354.19],"text":"Q59.\nWhen the selling price of a product is $50 and the fixed costs for production and sales\nare $100,000, which of the following is the number of units to be sold to achieve the desired\nprofit of $50,000? Here, the variable cost ratio is 60%."},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,376.91,491.1,408.19],"text":"a) 5,000\nb) 7,500\nc) 10,000\nd) 12,500"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"5,000"},{"label":"b","text":"7,500"},{"label":"c","text":"10,000"},{"label":"d","text":"12,500"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  '7,500 units must be sold. With a 60% variable cost ratio, each unit contributes $50 × (1 − 0.6) = $20 toward fixed costs and profit. Required units = (fixed costs + target profit) ÷ contribution per unit = (100,000 + 50,000) ÷ 20 = 7,500.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. When the selling price of a product is $50 and the fixed costs for production and sales
 are $100,000, which of the following is the number of units to be sold to achieve the desired
 profit of $50,000? Here, the variable cost ratio is 60%.

 a) 5,000 b) 7,500 c) 10,000 d) 12,500',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2024-october',
  'A',
  60,
  'Q60. Which of the following is an explanation of a volume license agreement?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,412.91,461.82,443.17],"text":"Q60.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of a volume license agreement?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,466.91,484.08,480.19],"text":"a) A contract that establishes standard license conditions and deems that a license"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[102.12,484.91,529.0,498.19],"text":"agreement is automatically established between the rightsholder and the purchaser when"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,502.91,530.95,552.19],"text":"a certain amount of package is unwrapped within the scope of the standard license\nconditions\nb) A contract that predefines the number of installations and permits the use of software for"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,556.91,520.75,588.19],"text":"companies or other such purchasers of large amounts of software\nc) A contract that restricts the location of use and permits the use of an unlimited number"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[84.12,592.91,515.62,624.19],"text":"of units or persons within a specific facility\nd) A contract where use is permitted by selecting to agree to the terms of the contract on"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[102.12,628.91,464.61,642.19],"text":"the screen that is displayed when software is downloaded from the Internet"},{"type":"code","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 25 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A contract that establishes standard license conditions and deems that a license\n agreement is automatically established between the rightsholder and the purchaser when\n a certain amount of package is unwrapped within the scope of the standard license\n conditions"},{"label":"b","text":"A contract that predefines the number of installations and permits the use of software for\n companies or other such purchasers of large amounts of software"},{"label":"c","text":"A contract that restricts the location of use and permits the use of an unlimited number\n of units or persons within a specific facility"},{"label":"d","text":"A contract where use is permitted by selecting to agree to the terms of the contract on\n the screen that is displayed when software is downloaded from the Internet"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A volume license agreement lets organizations that buy software in bulk install it on a predefined number of machines under one contract. Choice a describes a shrink-wrap contract, c describes a site license for unlimited use within a facility, and d describes a click-wrap (click-on) contract.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'intellectual-property'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-A, Q60)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q60. Which of the following is an explanation of a volume license agreement?

 a) A contract that establishes standard license conditions and deems that a license
 agreement is automatically established between the rightsholder and the purchaser when
 a certain amount of package is unwrapped within the scope of the standard license
 conditions
 b) A contract that predefines the number of installations and permits the use of software for
 companies or other such purchasers of large amounts of software
 c) A contract that restricts the location of use and permits the use of an unlimited number
 of units or persons within a specific facility
