  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The matrix P = {{pa, pb}, {pc, pd}} = {{0.7, 0.02}, {0.3, 0.98}}, so row 1 holds the rates of becoming or staying a cyclist and row 2 holds the rates of becoming or staying a non-cyclist. Next year''s cyclists are the 70% of cyclists who keep riding plus the 2% of non-cyclists who start: A = P[1,1] × N[1] + P[1,2] × N[2] = 3,500 + 2,000 = 5,500. Next year''s non-cyclists are B = P[2,1] × N[1] + P[2,2] × N[2] = 1,500 + 98,000 = 99,500, which is a matrix-vector multiplication row by row.',
