  'g',
  '{"value":"g"}'::jsonb,
  'The last decimal digit of a number is its remainder when divided by 10, so condition A is prod_id mod 10 = 3. One coupon is given for every complete group of three products, so B is the integer part of (pur_prod ÷ 3); for example 7 products give 2 coupons. The integer part of (prod_id ÷ 10) tests the tens digit instead, and pur_prod mod 3 gives the leftover products, not the number of groups.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
