  3,
  'Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

The program determines the second-largest element of an integer-type array and outputs its
 value. For instance, the second largest element of the array {2, 6, 9, 1, 7, 5} is 7. Here,
 we assume that the array has two or more elements and that no duplicate elements are present
 in the array.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"The program determines the second-largest element of an integer-type array and outputs its\n value. For instance, the second largest element of the array {2, 6, 9, 1, 7, 5} is 7. Here,\n we assume that the array has two or more elements and that no duplicate elements are present\n in the array."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"integer []: array ← {2, 6, 9, 1, 7, 5}\ninteger: i\ninteger: max1 ← -∞\ninteger: max2 ← -∞\nfor (increase i from 1\n     to the number of elements of array by 1)\n  if (***A***)\n    max2 ← max1\n    max1 ← array[i]\n  elseif (array[i] > max2)\n    ***B***\n  endif\nendfor\noutput max2\n\nAnswer group"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"array[i] < max1","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"array[i] < max1","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"array[i] < max2","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"array[i] < max2","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"array[i] > max1","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"array[i] > max1","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"array[i] > max2","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"array[i] > max2","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"array[i] < max1 max1 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] < max1","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"b","text":"array[i] < max1 max2 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] < max1","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"c","text":"array[i] < max2 max1 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] < max2","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"d","text":"array[i] < max2 max2 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] < max2","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"e","text":"array[i] > max1 max1 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] > max1","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"f","text":"array[i] > max1 max2 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] > max1","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}},{"label":"g","text":"array[i] > max2 max1 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] > max2","B":"←\nmax1 array[i]"}},{"label":"h","text":"array[i] > max2 max2 ← array[i]","values":{"A":"array[i] > max2","B":"←\nmax2 array[i]"}}]'::jsonb,
  'f',
  '{"value":"f"}'::jsonb,
  'The program keeps the largest value in max1 and the second largest in max2. When a new element is larger than max1 (A: array[i] > max1), the old maximum drops to second place (max2 ← max1) and the element becomes the new max1. Otherwise, if the element is only larger than max2, it replaces the second largest (B: max2 ← array[i]). For {2, 6, 9, 1, 7, 5} this ends with max1 = 9 and max2 = 7.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-B, Q3)',
  ARRAY[6]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
