  5,
  'Q5. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

Function calcGeoMean receives the array dataArray (the number of elements ≥ 1) as an
 argument and returns the geometric mean of values in dataArray as the return value. For
 the numbers a₁, a₂, …, aₙ, the geometric mean is √[n](a₁ × a₂ × ⋯ × aₙ). Here, the pow(x,
 y) function returns a real value by raising x to the power of y. In the program, division is
 performed in data type real.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q5. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"Function calcGeoMean receives the array dataArray (the number of elements ≥ 1) as an\n argument and returns the geometric mean of values in dataArray as the return value. For\n the numbers a₁, a₂, …, aₙ, the geometric mean is √[n](a₁ × a₂ × ⋯ × aₙ). Here, the pow(x,\n y) function returns a real value by raising x to the power of y. In the program, division is\n performed in data type real."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ real: calcGeoMean(real []: dataArray)\n  real: product, geomean\n  integer: n ← the number of elements in dataArray\n  integer: i\n\n  product ← 1\n  for (increase i from 1 to n by 1)\n    product ← product × dataArray[i]\n  endfor\n  geomean ← pow(***A***, ***B***)\n  return geomean\n\nAnswer group"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"1 ÷ n","B":"product"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"product","B":"1 ÷ n"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"product","B":"n"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"n","B":"product"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1 ÷ n product","values":{"A":"1 ÷ n","B":"product"}},{"label":"b","text":"product 1 ÷ n","values":{"A":"product","B":"1 ÷ n"}},{"label":"c","text":"product n","values":{"A":"product","B":"n"}},{"label":"d","text":"n product","values":{"A":"n","B":"product"}}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The n-th root of a number is the same as raising it to the power 1/n, so the geometric mean equals product^(1/n). Since pow(x, y) computes x to the power y, A is product and B is 1 ÷ n. Swapping them (pow(1 ÷ n, product)) or using n as the exponent would compute a completely different value.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
