The standard form of a quadratic equation is as follows:

ax² + bx + c = 0, where a, b and c are real numbers and a ≠ 0.

Here, the term b² - 4ac is known as the discriminant of a quadratic equation. It indicates the
 nature of the roots. The formula for solving a quadratic equation is shown in the figure. If
 the discriminant value is positive, there are two solutions; if it is zero, there is one solution.
 Here, we assume that the discriminant value is non-negative.

If the discriminant > 0 | root1 = (−b + √(b² − 4ac))/(2a)
  | root2 = (−b − √(b² − 4ac))/(2a)
If the discriminant = 0 | root1 = root2 = (−b)/(2a)

Figure The formula for solving a quadratic equation

The procedure findRoots receives three real number arguments a, b, and c as coefficients
 and outputs the value of the root(s) of the quadratic equation. Function
 sqrt(discriminant) returns the principal square root value of the parameter
 discriminant.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q6. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** through ***C*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"The standard form of a quadratic equation is as follows:\n\nax² + bx + c = 0, where a, b and c are real numbers and a ≠ 0.\n\nHere, the term b² - 4ac is known as the discriminant of a quadratic equation. It indicates the\n nature of the roots. The formula for solving a quadratic equation is shown in the figure. If\n the discriminant value is positive, there are two solutions; if it is zero, there is one solution.\n Here, we assume that the discriminant value is non-negative.\n\nIf the discriminant > 0 | root1 = (−b + √(b² − 4ac))/(2a)\n  | root2 = (−b − √(b² − 4ac))/(2a)\nIf the discriminant = 0 | root1 = root2 = (−b)/(2a)\n\nFigure The formula for solving a quadratic equation\n\nThe procedure findRoots receives three real number arguments a, b, and c as coefficients\n and outputs the value of the root(s) of the quadratic equation. Function\n sqrt(discriminant) returns the principal square root value of the parameter\n discriminant."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ findRoots(real: a, real: b, real: c)\n  real: discriminant, root1, root2\n  discriminant ← ***A***\n  if (***B***)\n    root1 ← (−b + sqrt(discriminant)) ÷ (2 × a)\n    root2 ← (−b − sqrt(discriminant)) ÷ (2 × a)\n    output \"root1 = \", root1, \" and root2 = \", root2\n  elseif (***C***)\n    root1 ← −b ÷ (2 × a)\n\n    output \"root1 = root2 = \", root1\n  endif"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B","C"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant < 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant < 0"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant > 0"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant > 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant < 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant < 0"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant > 0"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant > 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c discriminant < 0 discriminant = 0","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant < 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"b","text":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c discriminant = 0 discriminant < 0","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant < 0"}},{"label":"c","text":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c discriminant = 0 discriminant > 0","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant > 0"}},{"label":"d","text":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c discriminant > 0 discriminant = 0","values":{"A":"b × 2 − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant > 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"e","text":"b × b − 4 × a × c discriminant < 0 discriminant = 0","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant < 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}},{"label":"f","text":"b × b − 4 × a × c discriminant = 0 discriminant < 0","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant < 0"}},{"label":"g","text":"b × b − 4 × a × c discriminant = 0 discriminant > 0","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant = 0","C":"discriminant > 0"}},{"label":"h","text":"b × b − 4 × a × c discriminant > 0 discriminant = 0","values":{"A":"b × b − 4 × a × c","B":"discriminant > 0","C":"discriminant = 0"}}]'::jsonb,
  'h',
  '{"value":"h"}'::jsonb,
  'The discriminant b² − 4ac must be written as b × b − 4 × a × c; b × 2 doubles b instead of squaring it. The branch that computes two different roots with ±sqrt(discriminant) applies when the discriminant is positive (B: discriminant > 0), and the branch that outputs the single root −b ÷ (2a) applies when it is zero (C: discriminant = 0). A negative case is not needed because the discriminant is assumed non-negative.',
