  8,
  'Q8. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the description.

This program performs operations on a priority queue.
 A priority queue is a queue where the handled elements have a priority assigned to them, and
 the elements are extracted with the order of the highest priority first. The class PrioQueue
 represents a priority queue. The Figure shows an explanation of the class PrioQueue. Here,
 the priority is the integer value 1, 2, or 3, and the smaller the value the higher the priority.
 When the procedure prioSched is called, the order of the output is _______.

Constructor Description
 PrioQueue() Creates an empty priority queue.

Method Type of Description
 return value
 enqueue(string: s, None Adds string s as an element to a priority queue
 integer: prio) with the priority prio.
 dequeue() string Extracts the element with the highest priority in
 a priority queue and returns it. If multiple
 elements with the highest priority exist, it
 extracts the element that was added first and
 returns it.
 size() integer Returns the number of elements that are stored in
 a priority queue.

Figure Explanation of the class PrioQueue',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q8. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in\n the description."},{"type":"context","text":"This program performs operations on a priority queue.\n A priority queue is a queue where the handled elements have a priority assigned to them, and\n the elements are extracted with the order of the highest priority first. The class PrioQueue\n represents a priority queue. The Figure shows an explanation of the class PrioQueue. Here,\n the priority is the integer value 1, 2, or 3, and the smaller the value the higher the priority.\n When the procedure prioSched is called, the order of the output is _______.\n\nConstructor Description\n PrioQueue() Creates an empty priority queue.\n\nMethod Type of Description\n return value\n enqueue(string: s, None Adds string s as an element to a priority queue\n integer: prio) with the priority prio.\n dequeue() string Extracts the element with the highest priority in\n a priority queue and returns it. If multiple\n elements with the highest priority exist, it\n extracts the element that was added first and\n returns it.\n size() integer Returns the number of elements that are stored in\n a priority queue.\n\nFigure Explanation of the class PrioQueue"},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ prioSched()\n  PrioQueue: prioQueue ← PrioQueue()\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"E\", 3)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"F\", 2)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"G\", 1)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"H\", 1)\n  prioQueue.dequeue()  /* The return value is ignored */\n  prioQueue.dequeue()  /* The return value is ignored */\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"I\", 1)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"J\", 1)\n  prioQueue.dequeue()  /* The return value is ignored */\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"K\", 2)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"L\", 3)\n  prioQueue.enqueue(\"M\", 1)"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"\"M\", \"I\", \"K\", \"F\", \"L\", \"E\""},{"label":"b","text":"\"M\", \"L\", \"K\", \"I\", \"F\", \"E\""},{"label":"c","text":"\"J\", \"M\", \"F\", \"K\", \"E\", \"L\""},{"label":"d","text":"\"E\", \"L\", \"F\", \"K\", \"I\", \"M\""}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'After E(3), F(2), G(1), H(1) are added, the two dequeues remove G and H (priority 1, oldest first). Adding I(1) and J(1) and dequeuing once removes I, leaving E(3), F(2), J(1). Adding K(2), L(3), M(1) gives priority 1: J, M; priority 2: F, K; priority 3: E, L, each in insertion order. Emptying the queue therefore outputs "J", "M", "F", "K", "E", "L".',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-B, Q8)',
  ARRAY[13,14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q8. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _______ in
 the description.

 This program performs operations on a priority queue.
 A priority queue is a queue where the handled elements have a priority assigned to them, and
 the elements are extracted with the order of the highest priority first. The class PrioQueue
 represents a priority queue. The Figure shows an explanation of the class PrioQueue. Here,
 the priority is the integer value 1, 2, or 3, and the smaller the value the higher the priority.
 When the procedure prioSched is called, the order of the output is _______.

 Constructor Description
 PrioQueue() Creates an empty priority queue.

 Method Type of Description
 return value
 enqueue(string: s, None Adds string s as an element to a priority queue
 integer: prio) with the priority prio.
 dequeue() string Extracts the element with the highest priority in
 a priority queue and returns it. If multiple
 elements with the highest priority exist, it
 extracts the element that was added first and
 returns it.
 size() integer Returns the number of elements that are stored in
 a priority queue.

 Figure Explanation of the class PrioQueue

 [Program]
 ○ prioSched()
 PrioQueue: prioQueue ← PrioQueue()
 prioQueue.enqueue("E", 3)
 prioQueue.enqueue("F", 2)
 prioQueue.enqueue("G", 1)
 prioQueue.enqueue("H", 1)
 prioQueue.dequeue() /* The return value is ignored */
 prioQueue.dequeue() /* The return value is ignored */
 prioQueue.enqueue("I", 1)
 prioQueue.enqueue("J", 1)
 prioQueue.dequeue() /* The return value is ignored */
 prioQueue.enqueue("K", 2)
 prioQueue.enqueue("L", 3)
 prioQueue.enqueue("M", 1)

while (prioQueue.size() is not equal to 0)
 output prioQueue.dequeue()
 endwhile

Answer group
 a) "M", "I", "K", "F", "L", "E"
 b) "M", "L", "K", "I", "F", "E"
 c) "J", "M", "F", "K", "E", "L"
 d) "E", "L", "F", "K", "I", "M"',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/b/questions.pdf","pages":[13,14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
