(
  '2024-october',
  'B',
  16,
  'Q16. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** through ***C*** in the program.

Function hammingDistance receives two strings as argument and returns Hamming distance
 as the return value. Hamming distance is a metric used to measure the difference between
 two strings of equal length. It counts the number of positions at which the corresponding
 characters are different. For instance, the return value is 2 when the function
 hammingDistance("101010", "111000") is called, because positions 2 and 5 have
 different characters.
 It can also be extended to strings of different lengths by considering the unmatched
 characters as differences. For instance, the return value is 5 when the function
 hammingDistance("101010", "111000111") is called, because of two differences in first
 six characters and addition of three extra unmatched characters.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q16. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** through ***C*** in the program."},{"type":"context","text":"Function hammingDistance receives two strings as argument and returns Hamming distance\n as the return value. Hamming distance is a metric used to measure the difference between\n two strings of equal length. It counts the number of positions at which the corresponding\n characters are different. For instance, the return value is 2 when the function\n hammingDistance(\"101010\", \"111000\") is called, because positions 2 and 5 have\n different characters.\n It can also be extended to strings of different lengths by considering the unmatched\n characters as differences. For instance, the return value is 5 when the function\n hammingDistance(\"101010\", \"111000111\") is called, because of two differences in first\n six characters and addition of three extra unmatched characters."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ integer: hammingDistance(string: s1, string: s2)\n  integer: distance, length1, length2, minLength, remainingLength\n  length1 ← length of s1\n  length2 ← length of s2\n  distance ← 0\n  minLength ← length1\n  if (***A***)\n    minLength ← length2\n  endif\n  for (increase i from 1 to minLength by 1)\n    if (the i-th character of string s1 ***B*** the i-th character of string s2)\n      distance ← distance + 1\n    endif\n  endfor\n  if (length1 > length2)\n    remainingLength = length1 - length2\n  else\n    remainingLength = length2 - length1\n  endif\n  distance ← ***C***\n  return distance"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B","C"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is equal to","C":"remainingLength"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + minLength"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is equal to","C":"remainingLength"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + minLength"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"length2 < length1 is equal to remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is equal to","C":"remainingLength"}},{"label":"b","text":"length2 < length1 is equal to distance + remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"c","text":"length2 < length1 is not equal to distance + minLength","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + minLength"}},{"label":"d","text":"length2 < length1 is not equal to distance + remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 < length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"e","text":"length2 > length1 is equal to remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is equal to","C":"remainingLength"}},{"label":"f","text":"length2 > length1 is equal to distance + remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}},{"label":"g","text":"length2 > length1 is not equal to distance + minLength","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + minLength"}},{"label":"h","text":"length2 > length1 is not equal to distance + remainingLength","values":{"A":"length2 > length1","B":"is not equal to","C":"distance + remainingLength"}}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'minLength starts as length1 and must be replaced by length2 when s2 is shorter, so A is length2 < length1. Inside the loop a position counts as a difference when the characters are not equal (B: is not equal to). Finally, every unmatched extra character also counts, so C is distance + remainingLength; for "101010" and "111000111" this gives 2 + 3 = 5.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2024A, FE, Subject-B, Q16)',
  ARRAY[25,26]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q16. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ___A___ through ___C___ in the program.

 Function hammingDistance receives two strings as argument and returns Hamming distance
 as the return value. Hamming distance is a metric used to measure the difference between
 two strings of equal length. It counts the number of positions at which the corresponding
 characters are different. For instance, the return value is 2 when the function
 hammingDistance("101010", "111000") is called, because positions 2 and 5 have
 different characters.
 It can also be extended to strings of different lengths by considering the unmatched
 characters as differences. For instance, the return value is 5 when the function
 hammingDistance("101010", "111000111") is called, because of two differences in first
 six characters and addition of three extra unmatched characters.

 [Program]
 ○ integer: hammingDistance(string: s1, string: s2)
 integer: distance, length1, length2, minLength, remainingLength
 length1 ← length of s1
 length2 ← length of s2
 distance ← 0
 minLength ← length1
 if (___A___)
 minLength ← length2
 endif
 for (increase i from 1 to minLength by 1)
 if (the i-th character of string s1 ___B___ the i-th character of string s2)
 distance ← distance + 1
 endif
 endfor
 if (length1 > length2)
 remainingLength = length1 - length2
 else
 remainingLength = length2 - length1
 endif
 distance ← ___C___
 return distance

Answer group
 A B C
 a) length2 < length1 is equal to remainingLength
 b) length2 < length1 is equal to distance + remainingLength
 c) length2 < length1 is not equal to distance + minLength
 d) length2 < length1 is not equal to distance + remainingLength
 e) length2 > length1 is equal to remainingLength
 f) length2 > length1 is equal to distance + remainingLength
 g) length2 > length1 is not equal to distance + minLength
 h) length2 > length1 is not equal to distance + remainingLength',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/b/questions.pdf","pages":[25,26]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2024-october/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
