),
(
  '2024-october',
  'B',
  17,
  'Q17. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be
 inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description.

Company A is an e-commerce company specializing in sporting goods. One morning,
 employee X of the company''s accounting department starts up his PC to begin his work.
 When he logged into his PC, he saw an unfamiliar screen with the following message:

*** Attention ***
 Your files have been encrypted.

All of your important files have been encrypted. To restore these files, please follow
 these steps:
 1. transfer $500 worth of cryptcurrency to the currency address provided:
 Address: 1ABCD.... EFGH
 2. As soon as the transfer is confirmed, we will send you the key to decrypt the files.
 3. If the transfer is not confirmed within 48 h, the decryption key will be deleted and
 the files will be lost forever.
 Contact: help@ransomware.example.com

The accounting department immediately requested the security team in company A to help
 resolve the situation. The security team analyzed all the PCs in the accounting department,
 including that of employee X, and noted the following:

1. A total of tow compromised PCs were found. One PC was used by Employee X and
 the other PC was shared by multiple employees.

2. IDS/IPS was not installed in the accounting department LAN, delaying detection of
 ransomware.

3. The shared PC was backed up daily, and important data could be restored from the
 backup at the time when the PC was not compromised by the ransomware.

4. Employee X''s PC was not backed up, and important data could not be restored.

5. The ransomware was saved on Employee X''s PC as an attachment file of an email
 sent by a company pretending to be a business partner. The email envelope and
 content were sophisticatedly disguised and difficult to detect through enhanced spam
 filters.

6. Employee X inadvertently executed the attached file and allowed the ransomware to
 invade his PC.

7. After compromising Employee X''s PC, the ransomware attempted to compromise
 other PCs in the LAN by taking advantage of vulnerabilities in the target OS, but
 succeeded only in compromising the shared PC, which had neglected to apply OS
 security patches.

8. On both PCs, the anti-virus software versions and virus definition files were checked
 for updates on a daily basis and maintained up-to-date.

9. Both PCs had OS storage encryption feature enabled, but it was not effective against
 the ransomware attack in this incident.

The security team and the accounting department decided to take the following approaches
and specific measures as a plan to strengthen the measures against future ransomware attacks.

Table 1. Approaches and Specific Measures (excerpts)
 Approaches Specific Measures
 Prevention User education and training
 ***A***

Detection Network monitoring with IDS/IPS
 Data Protection ***B***',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q17. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be\n inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description."},{"type":"context","text":"Company A is an e-commerce company specializing in sporting goods. One morning,\n employee X of the company''s accounting department starts up his PC to begin his work.\n When he logged into his PC, he saw an unfamiliar screen with the following message:\n\n*** Attention ***\n Your files have been encrypted.\n\nAll of your important files have been encrypted. To restore these files, please follow\n these steps:\n 1. transfer $500 worth of cryptcurrency to the currency address provided:\n Address: 1ABCD.... EFGH\n 2. As soon as the transfer is confirmed, we will send you the key to decrypt the files.\n 3. If the transfer is not confirmed within 48 h, the decryption key will be deleted and\n the files will be lost forever.\n Contact: help@ransomware.example.com\n\nThe accounting department immediately requested the security team in company A to help\n resolve the situation. The security team analyzed all the PCs in the accounting department,\n including that of employee X, and noted the following:\n\n1. A total of tow compromised PCs were found. One PC was used by Employee X and\n the other PC was shared by multiple employees.\n\n2. IDS/IPS was not installed in the accounting department LAN, delaying detection of\n ransomware.\n\n3. The shared PC was backed up daily, and important data could be restored from the\n backup at the time when the PC was not compromised by the ransomware.\n\n4. Employee X''s PC was not backed up, and important data could not be restored.\n\n5. The ransomware was saved on Employee X''s PC as an attachment file of an email\n sent by a company pretending to be a business partner. The email envelope and\n content were sophisticatedly disguised and difficult to detect through enhanced spam\n filters.\n\n6. Employee X inadvertently executed the attached file and allowed the ransomware to\n invade his PC.\n\n7. After compromising Employee X''s PC, the ransomware attempted to compromise\n other PCs in the LAN by taking advantage of vulnerabilities in the target OS, but\n succeeded only in compromising the shared PC, which had neglected to apply OS\n security patches.\n\n8. On both PCs, the anti-virus software versions and virus definition files were checked\n for updates on a daily basis and maintained up-to-date.\n\n9. Both PCs had OS storage encryption feature enabled, but it was not effective against\n the ransomware attack in this incident.\n\nThe security team and the accounting department decided to take the following approaches\nand specific measures as a plan to strengthen the measures against future ransomware attacks.\n\nTable 1. Approaches and Specific Measures (excerpts)\n Approaches Specific Measures\n Prevention User education and training\n ***A***\n\nDetection Network monitoring with IDS/IPS\n Data Protection ***B***"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"SPAM filter enhancement","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"SPAM filter enhancement","B":"Data encryption"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"OS updates","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"OS updates","B":"Data encryption"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"Virus definition updates","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"Virus definition updates","B":"Data encryption"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"SPAM filter enhancement Data backup","values":{"A":"SPAM filter enhancement","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"b","text":"SPAM filter enhancement Data encryption","values":{"A":"SPAM filter enhancement","B":"Data encryption"}},{"label":"c","text":"OS updates Data backup","values":{"A":"OS updates","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"d","text":"OS updates Data encryption","values":{"A":"OS updates","B":"Data encryption"}},{"label":"e","text":"Virus definition updates Data backup","values":{"A":"Virus definition updates","B":"Data backup"}},{"label":"f","text":"Virus definition updates Data encryption","values":{"A":"Virus definition updates","B":"Data encryption"}}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The ransomware spread to the shared PC only because OS security patches had not been applied, so the missing preventive measure A is OS updates; virus definitions were already current, and the email was disguised well enough to pass enhanced spam filters. For data protection, the shared PC could be restored from its daily backup while Employee X''s unbacked-up PC could not, so B is data backup. Storage encryption was already enabled and did nothing against the attack.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
