  20,
  'Q20. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be
 inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description.

Company Y, a trading company, is developing an e-commerce web application for selling
 products to customers directly. The web server hosting the web application is installed on-premise and the web application is to be developed in-house. The communications to the
 web server are allowed only with HTTPS and the server certificate is already signed by the
 third party and installed on the web server. Company Y has an IT department comprising
 three teams—Developer, Security, and Tech Support—and the requirements for the web
 application are specified as follows (excerpt):

• The web application is user-friendly and easy to navigate.
 • The web application is cost-effective to develop and maintain.
 • The web application can prevent malicious inputs into the system.
 • The web application is scalable and can handle a large number of customers.
 • The purchase orders and invoices are digitally signed to confirm integrity and authenticity.

During the initial project meeting, the members from each department discuss their
 respective tasks. The developer team requests the security team to derive specific tasks for
 the above requirements related to security. Ms. B, a member of the security team, suggests
 the following tasks:

• Set up a ***A*** to provide the infrastructure.
 • Install a ***B*** in front of the web server.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q20. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be\n inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description."},{"type":"context","text":"Company Y, a trading company, is developing an e-commerce web application for selling\n products to customers directly. The web server hosting the web application is installed on-premise and the web application is to be developed in-house. The communications to the\n web server are allowed only with HTTPS and the server certificate is already signed by the\n third party and installed on the web server. Company Y has an IT department comprising\n three teams—Developer, Security, and Tech Support—and the requirements for the web\n application are specified as follows (excerpt):\n\n• The web application is user-friendly and easy to navigate.\n • The web application is cost-effective to develop and maintain.\n • The web application can prevent malicious inputs into the system.\n • The web application is scalable and can handle a large number of customers.\n • The purchase orders and invoices are digitally signed to confirm integrity and authenticity.\n\nDuring the initial project meeting, the members from each department discuss their\n respective tasks. The developer team requests the security team to derive specific tasks for\n the above requirements related to security. Ms. B, a member of the security team, suggests\n the following tasks:\n\n• Set up a ***A*** to provide the infrastructure.\n • Install a ***B*** in front of the web server."},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"honeypot"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"VPN gateway"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"web application firewall"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"honeypot"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"VPN gateway"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"web application firewall"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"PKI environment honeypot","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"honeypot"}},{"label":"b","text":"PKI environment VPN gateway","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"VPN gateway"}},{"label":"c","text":"PKI environment web application firewall","values":{"A":"PKI environment","B":"web application firewall"}},{"label":"d","text":"SPF record honeypot","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"honeypot"}},{"label":"e","text":"SPF record VPN gateway","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"VPN gateway"}},{"label":"f","text":"SPF record web application firewall\n\n_ _\nCompany names and product names appearing in the test questions are trademarks or registered\ntrademarks of their respective companies. Note that the ® and ™ symbols are not used within the text.","values":{"A":"SPF record","B":"web application firewall"}}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Digitally signing purchase orders and invoices to prove integrity and authenticity requires keys and certificates, so the infrastructure to set up is a PKI environment. Preventing malicious inputs to the web application calls for a web application firewall (WAF) placed in front of the web server, which inspects HTTP traffic for attacks such as SQL injection and XSS. An SPF record only protects email sender domains, a honeypot only lures attackers, and a VPN gateway does not filter application-level input.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
