(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  1,
  'Q1. For an 8-bit binary integer, which of the following is the operation that extracts the most
 significant 4-bits while making the other bits zero?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,523.79,81.19],"text":"Q1.  For an 8-bit binary integer, which of the following is the operation that extracts the most"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[85.62,85.85,332.87,99.13],"text":"significant 4-bits while making the other bits zero?"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,306.13,208.21],"text":"a) Bitwise AND operation with 11110000.\nb) Bitwise NAND operation with 11110000.\nc) Bitwise OR operation with 00001111.\nd) Bitwise XOR operation with 00001111."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Bitwise AND operation with 11110000."},{"label":"b","text":"Bitwise NAND operation with 11110000."},{"label":"c","text":"Bitwise OR operation with 00001111."},{"label":"d","text":"Bitwise XOR operation with 00001111."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct choice is a bitwise AND with the mask 11110000. ANDing a bit with 1 keeps its value and ANDing with 0 forces it to 0, so the upper four bits pass through unchanged and the lower four become zero. OR with 00001111 would instead force the lower bits to 1, and XOR would flip them.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q1)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
