 fraction 23.375?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,525.19,243.19],"text":"Q2.  Which of the following is the binary fraction that is the nearest equivalent to the decimal"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[85.62,247.85,167.29,261.13],"text":"fraction 23.375?"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,284.93,501.96,316.21],"text":"a) 10111.011\nb) 10111.110\nc) 11101.011\nd) 11101.110"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"10111.011"},{"label":"b","text":"10111.110"},{"label":"c","text":"11101.011"},{"label":"d","text":"11101.110"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct binary value is 10111.011. Convert the parts separately: 23 = 16 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 10111, and 0.375 = 0.25 + 0.125 = 2⁻² + 2⁻³ = .011. Choices with 11101 have the integer bits reversed (that is 29), and .110 would be 0.75.',
