 nodes visited are the same in the tree shown below, when the left child is explored first?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q5. Among the four tree traversal techniques—breadth-first, in-order, post-order, and pre-order—which of the following is the appropriate combination to ensure that the last two\n nodes visited are the same in the tree shown below, when the left child is explored first?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-april-a-q05-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Breadth-First Post-order"},{"label":"b","text":"Breadth-First Pre-order"},{"label":"c","text":"In-order Post-order"},{"label":"d","text":"In-order Pre-order"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct pair is in-order and pre-order, because both end with 20 then 22. In-order (left, node, right) gives 3, 5, 18, 20, 22 and pre-order (node, left, right) gives 18, 5, 3, 20, 22. Breadth-first ends with 3, 22 and post-order ends with 20, 18, so any pair containing those two does not match.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
