  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The hit ratio is about 0.83. Effective access time = h × cache time + (1 − h) × main memory time, so for A it is 14h + 80(1 − h) = 80 − 66h and for B it is 12h + 90(1 − h) = 90 − 78h. Setting them equal gives 12h = 10, so h = 10/12 ≈ 0.83; 0.17 is the miss ratio, not the hit ratio.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q10)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q10. The table below shows the access times for the cache memory and main memory in
 systems A and B. Which of the following is the approximate hit ratio of the cache memory,
 when the effective access time and the cache memory hit ratio are the same for systems A
 and B?

 System A System B

 Cache memory 14 ns 12 ns

 Main memory 80 ns 90 ns

 a) 0.17 b) 0.20 c) 0.83 d) 1.00',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  11,
  'Q11. Which of the following is a merit of migrating an internal business system to a cloud
 service?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,291.6,517.18,322.99],"text":"Q11.\nWhich of the following is a merit of migrating an internal business system to a cloud\nservice?"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,328.79,500.74,360.07],"text":"a) If an internal business system that requires a very high level of availability is to be"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,364.79,513.65,414.07],"text":"migrated to IaaS, all service providers guarantee high availability, so the migration is\neasy.\nb) If an internal on-premises business system with company-specific functions is to be"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,418.79,533.03,468.07],"text":"migrated to a system provided by SaaS, the migration of the company-specific functions\nalso becomes easier.\nc) If PaaS is to be used, platform management and OS updates are performed by the service"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,472.79,494.37,504.07],"text":"provider, so the burden of installation and operation can be reduced.\nd) If SaaS is to be used temporarily for the development or evaluation of an internal"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,508.79,478.03,540.01],"text":"business system, a highly flexible development environment can be provided."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"If an internal business system that requires a very high level of availability is to be\n migrated to IaaS, all service providers guarantee high availability, so the migration is\n easy."},{"label":"b","text":"If an internal on-premises business system with company-specific functions is to be\n migrated to a system provided by SaaS, the migration of the company-specific functions\n also becomes easier."},{"label":"c","text":"If PaaS is to be used, platform management and OS updates are performed by the service\n provider, so the burden of installation and operation can be reduced."},{"label":"d","text":"If SaaS is to be used temporarily for the development or evaluation of an internal\n business system, a highly flexible development environment can be provided."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The merit is that with PaaS the provider manages the platform, including OS updates, which reduces the user''s installation and operation burden. Not every IaaS provider guarantees high availability, SaaS makes company-specific functions harder rather than easier to migrate, and a flexible development environment is what PaaS or IaaS offers, not SaaS.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q11)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q11. Which of the following is a merit of migrating an internal business system to a cloud
 service?

 a) If an internal business system that requires a very high level of availability is to be
 migrated to IaaS, all service providers guarantee high availability, so the migration is
 easy.
 b) If an internal on-premises business system with company-specific functions is to be
 migrated to a system provided by SaaS, the migration of the company-specific functions
 also becomes easier.
 c) If PaaS is to be used, platform management and OS updates are performed by the service
 provider, so the burden of installation and operation can be reduced.
 d) If SaaS is to be used temporarily for the development or evaluation of an internal
 business system, a highly flexible development environment can be provided.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
