  16,
  'Q16. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of an actuator?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,176.93,438.76,207.19],"text":"Q16.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of an actuator?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,232.91,528.27,264.19],"text":"a) It amplifies weak electrical signals sent from microphones, sensors, and similar devices.\nb) It compares a given target value with a controlled value obtained from a sensor, and"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,268.91,507.82,300.19],"text":"outputs an operation amount to match the controlled value with the target value.\nc) It converts power from an energy source into rotation, translational motion, or other"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,304.91,484.66,336.19],"text":"movements based on control signals.\nd) It detects position, angle, velocity, acceleration, force, temperature, and similar"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[102.12,340.91,382.99,354.19],"text":"parameters, and converts them into electrical information."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It amplifies weak electrical signals sent from microphones, sensors, and similar devices."},{"label":"b","text":"It compares a given target value with a controlled value obtained from a sensor, and\n outputs an operation amount to match the controlled value with the target value."},{"label":"c","text":"It converts power from an energy source into rotation, translational motion, or other\n movements based on control signals."},{"label":"d","text":"It detects position, angle, velocity, acceleration, force, temperature, and similar\n parameters, and converts them into electrical information."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'An actuator converts energy from a power source into physical motion such as rotation or linear movement according to a control signal, for example a motor or solenoid. Detecting position or temperature and converting it to an electrical signal is what a sensor does, comparing target and measured values is a controller, and amplifying weak signals is an amplifier.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q16)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
