  18,
  'Q18. Of the functions provided by a DBMS, which of the following is a means for achieving
 protection for data confidentiality?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,601.74,533.12,632.17],"text":"Q18. Of the functions provided by a DBMS, which of the following is a means for achieving"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[85.74,636.66,256.0,650.11],"text":"protection for data confidentiality?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,675.89,480.34,743.17],"text":"a) Checking referential constraints when the data is updated\nb) Managing a transaction that combines a series of processes as a logical unit\nc) Managing the data access rights of users\nd) Placing an exclusive lock to data before updates"},{"type":"code","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 10 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Checking referential constraints when the data is updated"},{"label":"b","text":"Managing a transaction that combines a series of processes as a logical unit"},{"label":"c","text":"Managing the data access rights of users"},{"label":"d","text":"Placing an exclusive lock to data before updates"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Confidentiality is protected by managing users'' data access rights, so only authorized users can read or change the data. Referential constraint checks protect integrity, transaction management protects consistency and atomicity, and exclusive locks control concurrent updates rather than who can see the data.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
