  '[{"label":"a","text":"To create a physical data model of the database"},{"label":"b","text":"To define the logical structure of the database"},{"label":"c","text":"To determine the exact data types for every database attribute"},{"label":"d","text":"To implement database security measures"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The primary goal of conceptual database design is to define the logical structure of the data, such as the entities, attributes and relationships the business needs, independently of any specific DBMS. Deciding exact data types, storage and security measures belongs to the later logical/physical design and implementation stages.',
