  24,
  'Q24. In the OSI model, which of the following is the layer that is responsible for routing
 datagrams between hosts utilizing IP addresses across one or more networks?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,508.82,99.13],"text":"Q24.\nIn the OSI model, which of the following is the layer that is responsible for routing\ndatagrams between hosts utilizing IP addresses across one or more networks?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,122.93,497.58,154.21],"text":"a) Data link\nb) Network\nc) Physical\nd) Transport"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Data link"},{"label":"b","text":"Network"},{"label":"c","text":"Physical"},{"label":"d","text":"Transport"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The network layer (layer 3) routes datagrams between hosts across one or more networks using logical addresses such as IP addresses. The data link layer delivers frames within one link using MAC addresses, and the transport layer provides end-to-end delivery between processes using ports.',
