  25,
  'Q25. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation regarding Address Resolution
 Protocol (ARP)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,158.76,510.17,207.13],"text":"Q25.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation regarding Address Resolution\nProtocol (ARP)?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,230.93,410.71,316.21],"text":"a) It converts MAC addresses into IP addresses.\nb) It resolves domain names into its IP addresses.\nc) It resolves IP addresses into the corresponding MAC addresses.\nd) It translates IPv4 addresses into IPv6 addresses."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It converts MAC addresses into IP addresses."},{"label":"b","text":"It resolves domain names into its IP addresses."},{"label":"c","text":"It resolves IP addresses into the corresponding MAC addresses."},{"label":"d","text":"It translates IPv4 addresses into IPv6 addresses."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'ARP resolves a known IP address into the corresponding MAC address on the local network, by broadcasting a request and receiving the owner''s reply. Resolving domain names to IP addresses is DNS, and converting a MAC address to an IP address is the reverse function (RARP).',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
