),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  27,
  'Q27. Which of the following is the attack that is classified as DNS cache poisoning?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,577.68,489.09,609.13],"text":"Q27.\nWhich of the following is the attack that is classified as DNS cache poisoning?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,632.87,529.67,646.15],"text":"a) False domain information is injected into the DNS server that is referenced by a PC, and"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,650.87,468.74,682.15],"text":"it leads the user to a fake server.\nb) In order to interrupt the target service, the attacker uses the DNS server as a"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,686.87,526.68,718.15],"text":"steppingstone to send a large number of recursive queries.\nc) In order to obtain internal information, the zone information stored in the DNS server is"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,722.87,513.36,754.15],"text":"compiled and transferred.\nd) The version information of the DNS server software is obtained to identify a security"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[102.12,758.87,128.77,772.15],"text":"hole."},{"type":"code","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 13 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"False domain information is injected into the DNS server that is referenced by a PC, and\n it leads the user to a fake server."},{"label":"b","text":"In order to interrupt the target service, the attacker uses the DNS server as a\n steppingstone to send a large number of recursive queries."},{"label":"c","text":"In order to obtain internal information, the zone information stored in the DNS server is\n compiled and transferred."},{"label":"d","text":"The version information of the DNS server software is obtained to identify a security\n hole."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'DNS cache poisoning injects false domain-to-IP information into the cache of the DNS server the PC uses, so users are sent to a fake server. Using DNS servers as a steppingstone for many queries is a DNS reflection/amplification DoS attack, and copying zone information is a zone transfer abuse, not poisoning.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q27)',
  ARRAY[13]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q27. Which of the following is the attack that is classified as DNS cache poisoning?

 a) False domain information is injected into the DNS server that is referenced by a PC, and
 it leads the user to a fake server.
 b) In order to interrupt the target service, the attacker uses the DNS server as a
 steppingstone to send a large number of recursive queries.
 c) In order to obtain internal information, the zone information stored in the DNS server is
 compiled and transferred.
 d) The version information of the DNS server software is obtained to identify a security
 hole.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[13]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  28,
  'Q28. A given application only has the functions of retrieving and displaying user information
 from a database that stores such information. When considering information security, which
 of the following is the appropriate database access right assigned to an account that the
 application uses to access the database? The names and scopes of rights are listed below.

 [The names and scopes of rights]
 Reference right: Allows the application to select a record
 Update right: Allows the application to insert, update, and drop a record
 Administrator right: Allows the application to display, create, alter, and drop a
 table',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,531.47,171.13],"text":"Q28.\nA given application only has the functions of retrieving and displaying user information\nfrom a database that stores such information. When considering information security, which\nof the following is the appropriate database access right assigned to an account that the\napplication uses to access the database? The names and scopes of rights are listed below.\n\n[The names and scopes of rights]"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[85.2,175.85,510.2,261.13],"text":"Reference right:\nAllows the application to select a record\nUpdate right:\nAllows the application to insert, update, and drop a record\nAdministrator right:\nAllows the application to display, create, alter, and drop a\ntable"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,484.34,315.13],"text":"a) Administrator right\nb) Reference right\nc) Update right\nd) Update right and reference right"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Administrator right"},{"label":"b","text":"Reference right"},{"label":"c","text":"Update right"},{"label":"d","text":"Update right and reference right"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The account should get only the reference right, because the application just selects and displays records. This follows the principle of least privilege: granting update or administrator rights would let an attacker who hijacks the application modify or drop data.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'access-control'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q28)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q28. A given application only has the functions of retrieving and displaying user information
 from a database that stores such information. When considering information security, which
 of the following is the appropriate database access right assigned to an account that the
 application uses to access the database? The names and scopes of rights are listed below.

 [The names and scopes of rights]
 Reference right: Allows the application to select a record
 Update right: Allows the application to insert, update, and drop a record
 Administrator right: Allows the application to display, create, alter, and drop a
 table

 a) Administrator right b) Reference right
 c) Update right d) Update right and reference right',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
