(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  29,
  'Q29. Which of the following is a merit in using SaaS?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,319.74,343.82,351.19],"text":"Q29.\nWhich of the following is a merit in using SaaS?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,526.29,388.21],"text":"a) No system access management needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,522.08,442.21],"text":"the procedure for password initialization or a password policy that satisfies complexity\nrequirements is required.\nb) No system construction needs to be performed, and neither the definition of security"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,528.06,496.21],"text":"requirements for application software development nor the design of storage volume for\nsystem logs is required.\nc) No system operation needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning work"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,503.42,532.21],"text":"procedures at the time of a failure or backup is required.\nd) No system security management needs to be performed, and neither the creation of"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,536.93,492.43,604.15],"text":"information security management rules nor the assignment of an administrator is\nrequired."},{"type":"code","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 14 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"No system access management needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning\n the procedure for password initialization or a password policy that satisfies complexity\n requirements is required."},{"label":"b","text":"No system construction needs to be performed, and neither the definition of security\n requirements for application software development nor the design of storage volume for\n system logs is required."},{"label":"c","text":"No system operation needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning work\n procedures at the time of a failure or backup is required."},{"label":"d","text":"No system security management needs to be performed, and neither the creation of\n information security management rules nor the assignment of an administrator is\n required."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The merit of SaaS is that the provider builds and runs the system, so the user does not have to construct it, define security requirements for application development, or design log storage. The user still has to manage access and passwords, plan for failures and backups, and keep security rules and an administrator, so the other choices overstate what SaaS removes.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q29)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q29. Which of the following is a merit in using SaaS?

 a) No system access management needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning
 the procedure for password initialization or a password policy that satisfies complexity
 requirements is required.
 b) No system construction needs to be performed, and neither the definition of security
 requirements for application software development nor the design of storage volume for
 system logs is required.
 c) No system operation needs to be performed, and no consideration concerning work
 procedures at the time of a failure or backup is required.
 d) No system security management needs to be performed, and neither the creation of
 information security management rules nor the assignment of an administrator is
 required.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. Which of the following is an appropriate operation for user authentication that uses an
 IC card and a PIN?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.13,99.13],"text":"Q30.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate operation for user authentication that uses an\nIC card and a PIN?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,532.31,136.21],"text":"a) Given that each user can be identified by an IC card, a common PIN is set for all users in"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,530.03,172.21],"text":"order to reduce the management workload.\nb) If an IC card is lost, a new IC card is issued, and after the PIN is reset, the lost IC card is"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,527.96,208.21],"text":"deactivated.\nc) The PIN is set by combining the numeric information imprinted on the surface of the IC"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,528.57,244.21],"text":"card.\nd) When an IC card is delivered, the PIN is not enclosed, but is notified to the user through"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,184.42,262.21],"text":"another channel."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Given that each user can be identified by an IC card, a common PIN is set for all users in\n order to reduce the management workload."},{"label":"b","text":"If an IC card is lost, a new IC card is issued, and after the PIN is reset, the lost IC card is\n deactivated."},{"label":"c","text":"The PIN is set by combining the numeric information imprinted on the surface of the IC\n card."},{"label":"d","text":"When an IC card is delivered, the PIN is not enclosed, but is notified to the user through\n another channel."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The appropriate practice is to deliver the IC card without the PIN and tell the user the PIN through a separate channel, so a person who intercepts one item cannot use both factors. A shared PIN or a PIN derived from numbers printed on the card is easy to guess, and a lost card should be deactivated immediately, before reissuing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'access-control'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q30)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q30. Which of the following is an appropriate operation for user authentication that uses an
 IC card and a PIN?

 a) Given that each user can be identified by an IC card, a common PIN is set for all users in
 order to reduce the management workload.
 b) If an IC card is lost, a new IC card is issued, and after the PIN is reset, the lost IC card is
 deactivated.
 c) The PIN is set by combining the numeric information imprinted on the surface of the IC
 card.
 d) When an IC card is delivered, the PIN is not enclosed, but is notified to the user through
 another channel.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following is the most effective method of detecting unauthorized changes
 of the contents of a web server?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,284.76,528.53,333.13],"text":"Q31.\nWhich of the following is the most effective method of detecting unauthorized changes\nof the contents of a web server?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,463.04,370.21],"text":"a) Communications to the web server are monitored to ensure that there is no"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,518.25,406.21],"text":"communication other than HTTP and HTTPS.\nb) The hash value of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and periodically"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,410.93,505.14,442.21],"text":"compared with the hash value generated from each file.\nc) The memory usage of the web server is checked periodically to ensure that a buffer"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,446.93,518.3,478.21],"text":"overflow has not occurred.\nd) The updated date of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and compared"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,482.93,328.39,514.21],"text":"periodically with the updated date of each file."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Communications to the web server are monitored to ensure that there is no\n communication other than HTTP and HTTPS."},{"label":"b","text":"The hash value of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and periodically\n compared with the hash value generated from each file."},{"label":"c","text":"The memory usage of the web server is checked periodically to ensure that a buffer\n overflow has not occurred."},{"label":"d","text":"The updated date of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and compared\n periodically with the updated date of each file."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The most effective method is to store a hash value of each content file and periodically compare it with a newly calculated hash, because any change to a file changes its hash. File update dates can be forged easily by an attacker, and monitoring traffic or memory usage does not show whether file contents were altered.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following is the most effective method of detecting unauthorized changes
 of the contents of a web server?

 a) Communications to the web server are monitored to ensure that there is no
 communication other than HTTP and HTTPS.
 b) The hash value of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and periodically
 compared with the hash value generated from each file.
 c) The memory usage of the web server is checked periodically to ensure that a buffer
 overflow has not occurred.
 d) The updated date of each file of the contents of the web server is stored and compared
 periodically with the updated date of each file.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  32,
  'Q32. Which of the following is the function of a WAF?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,350.54,566.65],"text":"Q32.\nWhich of the following is the function of a WAF?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,573.89,361.41,641.17],"text":"a) Encrypting data and controlling access on web server\nb) Inspecting and filtering HTTP requests\nc) Managing user authentication and authorization\nd) Scanning malware on a web server"},{"type":"code","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 15 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Encrypting data and controlling access on web server"},{"label":"b","text":"Inspecting and filtering HTTP requests"},{"label":"c","text":"Managing user authentication and authorization"},{"label":"d","text":"Scanning malware on a web server"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A web application firewall inspects HTTP requests and responses and filters ones that look like attacks, such as SQL injection or cross-site scripting. It does not encrypt data, perform user authentication, or scan files for malware.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q32)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q32. Which of the following is the function of a WAF?

 a) Encrypting data and controlling access on web server
 b) Inspecting and filtering HTTP requests
 c) Managing user authentication and authorization
 d) Scanning malware on a web server',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
