  34,
  'Q34. Which of the following is the software architecture that decomposes applications into
 small, loosely coupled services that communicate over APIs?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,283.74,520.48,315.13],"text":"Q34.\nWhich of the following is the software architecture that decomposes applications into\nsmall, loosely coupled services that communicate over APIs?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,516.39,370.21],"text":"a) Event-Driven Architecture\nb) Microservices Architecture\nc) Serverless Architecture\nd) Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA)"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Event-Driven Architecture"},{"label":"b","text":"Microservices Architecture"},{"label":"c","text":"Serverless Architecture"},{"label":"d","text":"Service-Oriented Architecture (SOA)"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'This is microservices architecture, which splits an application into small, independently deployable, loosely coupled services that communicate through APIs. SOA also uses services but typically larger ones connected through shared middleware such as an enterprise service bus, and serverless and event-driven describe execution and communication styles rather than this decomposition.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
