(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  36,
  'Q36. Which of the following is an explanation of a software testing tool corresponding to a
 static analysis tool that supports static testing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,521.48,99.13],"text":"Q36.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of a software testing tool corresponding to a\nstatic analysis tool that supports static testing?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,507.97,136.21],"text":"a) Data concerning the operating characteristics during program execution, such as the"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,523.6,190.21],"text":"module calling frequency and execution time, or the execution frequency of executable\nstatement is measured.\nb) The instruction coverage rate and the branch coverage rate are automatically measured"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,523.59,226.21],"text":"and analyzed on the basis of the test execution results.\nc) The source code is analyzed to find out if grammatical errors or logical errors exist in a"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,496.7,262.21],"text":"program.\nd) The test data of the specified conditions and the program input files are generated"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,173.46,298.21],"text":"automatically."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Data concerning the operating characteristics during program execution, such as the\n module calling frequency and execution time, or the execution frequency of executable\n statement is measured."},{"label":"b","text":"The instruction coverage rate and the branch coverage rate are automatically measured\n and analyzed on the basis of the test execution results."},{"label":"c","text":"The source code is analyzed to find out if grammatical errors or logical errors exist in a\n program."},{"label":"d","text":"The test data of the specified conditions and the program input files are generated\n automatically."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A static analysis tool examines source code without running it, looking for grammatical errors, rule violations and logical errors. Measuring calling frequency or execution time and measuring instruction or branch coverage require executing the program, so those are dynamic tools, and generating test data is a test data generator.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q36)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q36. Which of the following is an explanation of a software testing tool corresponding to a
 static analysis tool that supports static testing?

 a) Data concerning the operating characteristics during program execution, such as the
 module calling frequency and execution time, or the execution frequency of executable
 statement is measured.
 b) The instruction coverage rate and the branch coverage rate are automatically measured
 and analyzed on the basis of the test execution results.
 c) The source code is analyzed to find out if grammatical errors or logical errors exist in a
 program.
 d) The test data of the specified conditions and the program input files are generated
 automatically.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  37,
  'Q37. Test cases for the part of a program shown in the flowchart below are created to achieve
 decision condition coverage (branch coverage). In order to make the test cases achieve
 multiple-condition coverage, which of the following is the appropriate set of test cases to be
 added? Here, the part enclosed by parentheses () represents a test case.

• Test cases to achieve decision condition coverage (branch coverage)
 (A = 4, B = 1), (A = 5, B = 0)',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q37. Test cases for the part of a program shown in the flowchart below are created to achieve\n decision condition coverage (branch coverage). In order to make the test cases achieve\n multiple-condition coverage, which of the following is the appropriate set of test cases to be\n added? Here, the part enclosed by parentheses () represents a test case.\n\n• Test cases to achieve decision condition coverage (branch coverage)\n (A = 4, B = 1), (A = 5, B = 0)"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-april-a-q37-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"(A = 3, B = 0), (A = 7, B = 2)"},{"label":"b","text":"(A = 3, B = 2), (A = 8, B = 0)"},{"label":"c","text":"(A = 4, B = 0), (A = 8, B = 0)"},{"label":"d","text":"(A = 7, B = 0), (A = 8, B = 2)"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The cases to add are (A = 7, B = 0) and (A = 8, B = 2). Multiple-condition coverage needs every true/false combination of the conditions A > 6 and B = 0. The existing cases give (false, false) and (false, true), so the missing combinations are (true, true), supplied by A = 7, B = 0, and (true, false), supplied by A = 8, B = 2.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q37)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q37. Test cases for the part of a program shown in the flowchart below are created to achieve
 decision condition coverage (branch coverage). In order to make the test cases achieve
 multiple-condition coverage, which of the following is the appropriate set of test cases to be
 added? Here, the part enclosed by parentheses () represents a test case.

 Process 1

 No
 A > 6 or B = 0

 Yes
