),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  39,
  'Q39. Which of the following is the term that represents the process of generating a UML
 class diagram from a program?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,178.12,509.67,225.13],"text":"Q39.\nWhich of the following is the term that represents the process of generating a UML\nclass diagram from a program?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,230.93,430.77,298.21],"text":"a) Backtracking\nb) Forward engineering\nc) Re-engineering\nd) Reverse engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Backtracking"},{"label":"b","text":"Forward engineering"},{"label":"c","text":"Re-engineering"},{"label":"d","text":"Reverse engineering"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Generating a design model such as a UML class diagram from existing program code is reverse engineering, which recovers specifications from an implementation. Forward engineering goes the other way, from design to code, and re-engineering uses reverse engineering and then rebuilds the system.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
