  40,
  'Q40. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of a Sprint in the Scrum
 methodology?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,482.47,351.13],"text":"Q40.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of a Sprint in the Scrum\nmethodology?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,374.93,483.76,460.15],"text":"a) A daily meeting where team members review progress and plan the day''s work\nb) A fixed-length period dedicated to developing a product increment\nc) A self-organizing team responsible for product development\nd) List of tasks and features the Scrum team has yet to complete"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A daily meeting where team members review progress and plan the day''s work"},{"label":"b","text":"A fixed-length period dedicated to developing a product increment"},{"label":"c","text":"A self-organizing team responsible for product development"},{"label":"d","text":"List of tasks and features the Scrum team has yet to complete"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A Sprint is a fixed-length time box, usually one to four weeks, in which the Scrum team builds a usable product increment. The daily meeting is the Daily Scrum, the list of remaining work is the Product Backlog, and the self-organizing group is the Scrum Team.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'development-processes'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q40)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
