(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  41,
  'Q41. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of earned value in project
 management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,464.76,490.22,513.13],"text":"Q41.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate explanation of earned value in project\nmanagement?"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,503.37,604.21],"text":"a) A measure of work completed in terms of budget authorized for that work.\nb) A time-phased budget that estimates the total cost of a project\nc) An authorized budget for the planned work\nd) Realized cost incurred for the work performed on an activity during a specific time"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.12,608.93,135.79,622.21],"text":"period"},{"type":"code","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 18 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A measure of work completed in terms of budget authorized for that work."},{"label":"b","text":"A time-phased budget that estimates the total cost of a project"},{"label":"c","text":"An authorized budget for the planned work"},{"label":"d","text":"Realized cost incurred for the work performed on an activity during a specific time\n period"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Earned value (EV) measures the work actually completed, expressed as the budget that was authorized for that work. An authorized budget for planned work is planned value (PV), the actual cost incurred is actual cost (AC), and a time-phased total budget is the performance measurement baseline.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q41)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q41. Which of the following is an appropriate explanation of earned value in project
 management?

 a) A measure of work completed in terms of budget authorized for that work.
 b) A time-phased budget that estimates the total cost of a project
 c) An authorized budget for the planned work
 d) Realized cost incurred for the work performed on an activity during a specific time
 period',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[18]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  42,
  'Q42. Which of the following is the method of estimation in the COCOMO model in software
 estimation?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,531.58,99.13],"text":"Q42.\nWhich of the following is the method of estimation in the COCOMO model in software\nestimation?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,522.99,172.21],"text":"a) The effort and duration of the project are estimated based on the size of the software.\nb) The effort of the project is estimated based on the duration of the project.\nc) The size of the software and duration of the project are estimated based on the effort of"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,522.97,208.21],"text":"the project.\nd) The size of the software and effort of the project are estimated based on the duration of"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,159.13,244.21],"text":"the project."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The effort and duration of the project are estimated based on the size of the software."},{"label":"b","text":"The effort of the project is estimated based on the duration of the project."},{"label":"c","text":"The size of the software and duration of the project are estimated based on the effort of\n the project."},{"label":"d","text":"The size of the software and effort of the project are estimated based on the duration of\n the project."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'COCOMO estimates the effort (person-months) and the development duration from the size of the software, usually in thousands of lines of code, adjusted by cost drivers. The other choices reverse the direction: size is the input, not something derived from effort or duration.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
