  'Q42. Which of the following is the method of estimation in the COCOMO model in software
 estimation?

 a) The effort and duration of the project are estimated based on the size of the software.
 b) The effort of the project is estimated based on the duration of the project.
 c) The size of the software and duration of the project are estimated based on the effort of
 the project.
 d) The size of the software and effort of the project are estimated based on the duration of
 the project.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  43,
  'Q43. An IT service is provided under the conditions below. What is the maximum downtime in
 hours that satisfies the SLA during a service period of one (1) month? Here, the number of
 business days in one (1) month is 30, and no maintenance or other scheduled downtime of the
 service is performed during the service period.

 [Conditions of the SLA]
 - The service period is from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM on business days.
 - The availability should be 99.5% or more.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,533.07,279.19],"text":"Q43. An IT service is provided under the conditions below. What is the maximum downtime in"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.62,283.85,533.16,333.13],"text":"hours that satisfies the SLA during a service period of one (1) month? Here, the number of\nbusiness days in one (1) month is 30, and no maintenance or other scheduled downtime of the\nservice is performed during the service period."},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[86.22,360.53,206.14,373.81],"text":"[Conditions of the SLA]"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[93.6,377.81,432.98,409.09],"text":"- The service period is from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM on business days.\n- The availability should be 99.5% or more."},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,432.89,465.96,464.11],"text":"a) 0.3\nb) 2.1\nc) 3.0\nd) 3.6"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0.3"},{"label":"b","text":"2.1"},{"label":"c","text":"3.0"},{"label":"d","text":"3.6"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum downtime is 2.1 hours. The service runs 14 hours a day (8:00 AM to 10:00 PM) for 30 days, giving 420 service hours, and 99.5% availability allows 0.5% of that to be down: 420 × 0.005 = 2.1 hours. Using 24 hours a day would give 3.6, which is wrong because downtime outside service hours does not count.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q43)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q43. An IT service is provided under the conditions below. What is the maximum downtime in
 hours that satisfies the SLA during a service period of one (1) month? Here, the number of
 business days in one (1) month is 30, and no maintenance or other scheduled downtime of the
 service is performed during the service period.

 [Conditions of the SLA]
 - The service period is from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM on business days.
 - The availability should be 99.5% or more.

 a) 0.3 b) 2.1 c) 3.0 d) 3.6',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  44,
  'Q44. Which of the following should be accomplished in service management concerning
 Maximum Tolerable Downtime (MTD), Recovery Point Objective (RPO), and Recovery
 Time Objective (RTO)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,468.72,514.43,535.09],"text":"Q44.\nWhich of the following should be accomplished in service management concerning\nMaximum Tolerable Downtime (MTD), Recovery Point Objective (RPO), and Recovery\nTime Objective (RTO)?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,558.89,514.32,590.11],"text":"a) MTD < RPO\nb) MTD < RTO\nc) RPO < MTD\nd) RTO < MTD"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"MTD < RPO"},{"label":"b","text":"MTD < RTO"},{"label":"c","text":"RPO < MTD"},{"label":"d","text":"RTO < MTD"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The requirement is RTO < MTD: the target time to restore the service must be shorter than the maximum downtime the business can tolerate, or the recovery plan would fail the business. RPO measures acceptable data loss as a point in time, so it is not directly compared with MTD, and MTD below RTO would mean recovery always comes too late.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q44)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q44. Which of the following should be accomplished in service management concerning
 Maximum Tolerable Downtime (MTD), Recovery Point Objective (RPO), and Recovery
 Time Objective (RTO)?

 a) MTD < RPO b) MTD < RTO c) RPO < MTD d) RTO < MTD',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  45,
  'Q45. Which of the following is a checkpoint for auditing the control of risks related to
 information leakage and unauthorized use of documents concerning a system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,594.72,498.15,643.09],"text":"Q45.\nWhich of the following is a checkpoint for auditing the control of risks related to\ninformation leakage and unauthorized use of documents concerning a system?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[84.12,648.89,446.92,734.17],"text":"a) Creating the necessary documents even in prototype development\nb) Standardizing documents\nc) Taking measures to ensure the confidentiality of documents\nd) Updating documents without delay as changes are made in the system"},{"type":"code","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 19 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Creating the necessary documents even in prototype development"},{"label":"b","text":"Standardizing documents"},{"label":"c","text":"Taking measures to ensure the confidentiality of documents"},{"label":"d","text":"Updating documents without delay as changes are made in the system"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'For risks of information leakage and unauthorized use of system documents, the audit checkpoint is whether measures are in place to keep those documents confidential, such as access restrictions and handling rules. Creating documents, standardizing them and updating them promptly relate to completeness and accuracy of documentation, not to leakage control.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q45)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q45. Which of the following is a checkpoint for auditing the control of risks related to
 information leakage and unauthorized use of documents concerning a system?

 a) Creating the necessary documents even in prototype development
 b) Standardizing documents
 c) Taking measures to ensure the confidentiality of documents
 d) Updating documents without delay as changes are made in the system',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
