 similarities in risks and investment value?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,518.18,117.13],"text":"Q46.\nWhich of the following is a technique that is used to perform the optimal resource\nallocation for a computerization investment in each category classified on the basis of the\nsimilarities in risks and investment value?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,407.12,172.21],"text":"a) 3C analysis\nb) Benchmarking\nc) Enterprise architecture\nd) IT portfolio"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"3C analysis"},{"label":"b","text":"Benchmarking"},{"label":"c","text":"Enterprise architecture"},{"label":"d","text":"IT portfolio"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'IT portfolio management classifies IT investments into categories with similar risk and value characteristics and then allocates resources across them optimally, like an investment portfolio. 3C analysis studies customer, competitor and company, benchmarking compares with best practice, and enterprise architecture models the organization''s business and systems.',
