),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  47,
  'Q47. Which of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for
 visualizing business processes?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,211.74,533.17,243.13],"text":"Q47.\nWhich of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for\nvisualizing business processes?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,510.41,280.21],"text":"a) Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,517.38,316.21],"text":"entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities.\nb) To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,501.5,352.21],"text":"data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow.\nc) To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,529.67,406.21],"text":"methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for\nobject modeling.\nd) To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,410.93,430.29,424.21],"text":"single request are described by using the conditional branch format."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as\n entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities."},{"label":"b","text":"To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and\n data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow."},{"label":"c","text":"To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling\n methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for\n object modeling."},{"label":"d","text":"To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a\n single request are described by using the conditional branch format."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'UML represents a process from several viewpoints by using purpose-specific diagrams (such as activity, use case and sequence diagrams), each drawn with standardized object-modeling notation. The data-oriented entity/attribute/relationship approach describes an E-R diagram, and data flows, sources, sinks and stores describe a DFD.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q47)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q47. Which of the following is a usage scenario for the adoption of UML as a technique for
 visualizing business processes?

 a) Diagrams are shown by using a data-oriented approach where objects are handled as
 entities, their attributes, and the relationships among the entities.
 b) To represent processes by using data flows, sources and sinks of data, data stores, and
 data processes are connected with arrows that indicate data flow.
 c) To represent processes from multiple viewpoints, some purpose-specific modeling
 methods are used, and each model is depicted by using standardized notation rules for
 object modeling.
 d) To thoroughly represent the functions of a process, the events that occur in response to a
 single request are described by using the conditional branch format.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  48,
  'Q48. Which of the following is an explanation of a hybrid cloud?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,463.74,397.41,477.19],"text":"Q48.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of a hybrid cloud?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,482.93,524.24,514.21],"text":"a) To configure and provide the service content of a cloud service for both consumers and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,485.84,550.21],"text":"companies\nb) To customize some of the functions that are provided by a cloud service for the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,483.23,586.21],"text":"company’s own use\nc) To provide an environment where data and application software are linked and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,590.93,527.66,640.21],"text":"interoperable between a cloud service for the exclusive use of a company and a general-\npurpose cloud service\nd) To separately provide the service content of a cloud service as paid services and free"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[102.12,644.93,143.76,658.21],"text":"services"},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"To configure and provide the service content of a cloud service for both consumers and\n companies"},{"label":"b","text":"To customize some of the functions that are provided by a cloud service for the\n company’s own use"},{"label":"c","text":"To provide an environment where data and application software are linked and\n interoperable between a cloud service for the exclusive use of a company and a general-purpose cloud service"},{"label":"d","text":"To separately provide the service content of a cloud service as paid services and free\n services"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A hybrid cloud links a private cloud dedicated to one company with a general-purpose public cloud so that data and applications can interoperate between them. The other choices describe serving both consumer and business markets, customizing a service, or freemium pricing, none of which is a hybrid deployment model.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q48)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q48. Which of the following is an explanation of a hybrid cloud?

 a) To configure and provide the service content of a cloud service for both consumers and
 companies
 b) To customize some of the functions that are provided by a cloud service for the
 company’s own use
 c) To provide an environment where data and application software are linked and
 interoperable between a cloud service for the exclusive use of a company and a general-purpose cloud service
 d) To separately provide the service content of a cloud service as paid services and free
 services',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  49,
  'Q49. Which of the following is an explanation of green procurement?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,418.4,81.19],"text":"Q49.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of green procurement?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,86.93,510.93,118.21],"text":"a) It refers not only to the fulfillment of the requirements of quality and price but to the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,523.45,172.21],"text":"preferential purchase of products and services with a lower environmental burden from\ncompanies that work toward a reduction in their environmental impact.\nb) It refers to a certificate that enables commercial trading of the green power that is"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,531.54,226.21],"text":"generated from natural energy sources such as solar, biomass, wind power, and\ngeothermal heat.\nc) It refers to international standards concerning environmental labels that are certified by a"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,503.76,262.21],"text":"third party on the basis of certain criteria.\nd) It refers to mass promotion of the details of environmental protection activities and"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,384.13,298.21],"text":"raising funds for environmental protection from investors."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers not only to the fulfillment of the requirements of quality and price but to the\n preferential purchase of products and services with a lower environmental burden from\n companies that work toward a reduction in their environmental impact."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to a certificate that enables commercial trading of the green power that is\n generated from natural energy sources such as solar, biomass, wind power, and\n geothermal heat."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to international standards concerning environmental labels that are certified by a\n third party on the basis of certain criteria."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to mass promotion of the details of environmental protection activities and\n raising funds for environmental protection from investors."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Green procurement means buying, in addition to meeting quality and price requirements, products and services with a lower environmental burden from suppliers that work to reduce their environmental impact. A tradable certificate for renewable power is a green power certificate, and third-party certified environmental labels are a labelling standard, not a purchasing policy.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q49)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q49. Which of the following is an explanation of green procurement?

 a) It refers not only to the fulfillment of the requirements of quality and price but to the
 preferential purchase of products and services with a lower environmental burden from
 companies that work toward a reduction in their environmental impact.
 b) It refers to a certificate that enables commercial trading of the green power that is
 generated from natural energy sources such as solar, biomass, wind power, and
 geothermal heat.
 c) It refers to international standards concerning environmental labels that are certified by a
 third party on the basis of certain criteria.
 d) It refers to mass promotion of the details of environmental protection activities and
 raising funds for environmental protection from investors.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  50,
  'Q50. Which of the following is a characteristic of the growth stage in a product life cycle?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,517.07,350.89],"text":"Q50.\nWhich of the following is a characteristic of the growth stage in a product life cycle?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,503.28,370.21],"text":"a) Demand decreases, and the withdrawal of some companies is observed. A decision"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,525.43,424.21],"text":"needs to be made regarding whether it is possible to gain a strong foothold at this stage.\nMigration into an alternative market is also considered.\nb) Demand is occasional, and exploiting new demand is key to success. Conviction for"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,519.78,460.21],"text":"succeeding in a specific target market is necessary.\nc) Demand reaches a peak, and the differentiation of the product and segmentation of the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,501.46,514.21],"text":"market become clear. The competition between competitors also intensifies, and it\nbecomes important to add new product types and reduce costs.\nd) The market starts to understand the value of the product. Both the product line and"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,518.93,522.71,568.21],"text":"distribution channels need to be expanded. This stage sees an increase in sales and also\nrequires investment."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Demand decreases, and the withdrawal of some companies is observed. A decision\n needs to be made regarding whether it is possible to gain a strong foothold at this stage.\n Migration into an alternative market is also considered."},{"label":"b","text":"Demand is occasional, and exploiting new demand is key to success. Conviction for\n succeeding in a specific target market is necessary."},{"label":"c","text":"Demand reaches a peak, and the differentiation of the product and segmentation of the\n market become clear. The competition between competitors also intensifies, and it\n becomes important to add new product types and reduce costs."},{"label":"d","text":"The market starts to understand the value of the product. Both the product line and\n distribution channels need to be expanded. This stage sees an increase in sales and also\n requires investment."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'In the growth stage the market recognizes the product''s value, sales increase rapidly, and the company must expand product lines and distribution channels, which requires investment. Occasional demand describes the introduction stage, peak demand with intense competition describes maturity, and falling demand with companies withdrawing describes decline.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q50)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q50. Which of the following is a characteristic of the growth stage in a product life cycle?

 a) Demand decreases, and the withdrawal of some companies is observed. A decision
 needs to be made regarding whether it is possible to gain a strong foothold at this stage.
 Migration into an alternative market is also considered.
 b) Demand is occasional, and exploiting new demand is key to success. Conviction for
 succeeding in a specific target market is necessary.
 c) Demand reaches a peak, and the differentiation of the product and segmentation of the
 market become clear. The competition between competitors also intensifies, and it
 becomes important to add new product types and reduce costs.
 d) The market starts to understand the value of the product. Both the product line and
 distribution channels need to be expanded. This stage sees an increase in sales and also
 requires investment.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  51,
  'Q51. Which of the following is a description of cost-plus pricing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,589.74,399.81,603.19],"text":"Q51.\nWhich of the following is a description of cost-plus pricing?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,523.65,640.21],"text":"a) It determines a competitive price by referring to the industry average and the pricing of"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,498.39,676.21],"text":"competitors.\nb) It determines a price by adding a certain margin to the manufacturing cost and the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,680.93,532.34,712.21],"text":"purchasing cost.\nc) It determines a price that ensures a certain profit margin after all costs are covered on the"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,716.93,506.42,748.21],"text":"basis of a target volume of sales.\nd) It determines an appealing price by researching the quality and price that customers"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[102.12,752.93,138.8,766.21],"text":"accept."},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It determines a competitive price by referring to the industry average and the pricing of\n competitors."},{"label":"b","text":"It determines a price by adding a certain margin to the manufacturing cost and the\n purchasing cost."},{"label":"c","text":"It determines a price that ensures a certain profit margin after all costs are covered on the\n basis of a target volume of sales."},{"label":"d","text":"It determines an appealing price by researching the quality and price that customers\n accept."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Cost-plus pricing sets the price by adding a fixed margin to the manufacturing or purchasing cost. Pricing by reference to competitors is going-rate pricing, pricing to secure a target profit at a planned sales volume is target-return pricing, and pricing by what customers will accept is perceived-value pricing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q51)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q51. Which of the following is a description of cost-plus pricing?

 a) It determines a competitive price by referring to the industry average and the pricing of
 competitors.
 b) It determines a price by adding a certain margin to the manufacturing cost and the
 purchasing cost.
 c) It determines a price that ensures a certain profit margin after all costs are covered on the
 basis of a target volume of sales.
 d) It determines an appealing price by researching the quality and price that customers
 accept.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  52,
  'Q52. Which of the following is an explanation of Supply Chain Management (SCM)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,495.8,81.19],"text":"Q52.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of Supply Chain Management (SCM)?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,514.87,118.21],"text":"a) Customer information that are collected through various channels is consolidated and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,511.4,154.21],"text":"utilized to establish closer relationships with customers.\nb) Employees’ skills and behavior characteristics are grasped, and management such as"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,517.99,208.21],"text":"appropriate personnel assignment and evaluation from the perspective of human\nresources strategy is performed.\nc) Intellectual assets of individuals, such as know-how and experience, are shared across"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,212.93,513.45,244.21],"text":"the organization to be used for creative work.\nd) The entire series of business operations, from purchasing and production to sales and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,518.09,298.21],"text":"distribution, is reexamined both within the company and among companies in view of\ntotal optimization in order to shorten delivery times and minimize inventory."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Customer information that are collected through various channels is consolidated and\n utilized to establish closer relationships with customers."},{"label":"b","text":"Employees’ skills and behavior characteristics are grasped, and management such as\n appropriate personnel assignment and evaluation from the perspective of human\n resources strategy is performed."},{"label":"c","text":"Intellectual assets of individuals, such as know-how and experience, are shared across\n the organization to be used for creative work."},{"label":"d","text":"The entire series of business operations, from purchasing and production to sales and\n distribution, is reexamined both within the company and among companies in view of\n total optimization in order to shorten delivery times and minimize inventory."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'SCM re-examines the whole chain from purchasing and production through sales and distribution, across the company and its partners, aiming for total optimization that shortens delivery times and reduces inventory. Consolidating customer information is CRM, managing employee skills is talent management, and sharing know-how is knowledge management.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q52)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q52. Which of the following is an explanation of Supply Chain Management (SCM)?

 a) Customer information that are collected through various channels is consolidated and
 utilized to establish closer relationships with customers.
 b) Employees’ skills and behavior characteristics are grasped, and management such as
 appropriate personnel assignment and evaluation from the perspective of human
 resources strategy is performed.
 c) Intellectual assets of individuals, such as know-how and experience, are shared across
 the organization to be used for creative work.
 d) The entire series of business operations, from purchasing and production to sales and
 distribution, is reexamined both within the company and among companies in view of
 total optimization in order to shorten delivery times and minimize inventory.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  53,
  'Q53. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation for product innovation in the
 management of technology?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,508.85,351.13],"text":"Q53.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate explanation for product innovation in the\nmanagement of technology?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,521.03,460.21],"text":"a) Acquiring business profits through the achievements of technology development\nb) Developing new products or products that enable differentiation from other companies\nc) Making innovative reforms in business processes\nd) Strategically managing business with technology as the core"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Acquiring business profits through the achievements of technology development"},{"label":"b","text":"Developing new products or products that enable differentiation from other companies"},{"label":"c","text":"Making innovative reforms in business processes"},{"label":"d","text":"Strategically managing business with technology as the core"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Product innovation means developing new products, or products that differentiate the company from competitors. Innovating business processes is process innovation, and the other choices describe gaining profit from technology or the general idea of management of technology.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q53)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q53. Which of the following is the appropriate explanation for product innovation in the
 management of technology?

 a) Acquiring business profits through the achievements of technology development
 b) Developing new products or products that enable differentiation from other companies
 c) Making innovative reforms in business processes
 d) Strategically managing business with technology as the core',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  54,
  'Q54. Which of the following is a characteristic of MRP?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,481.74,355.47,495.19],"text":"Q54.\nWhich of the following is a characteristic of MRP?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,518.93,509.09,532.21],"text":"a) The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,532.0,568.21],"text":"simultaneously in parallel.\nb) The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,572.93,499.76,640.21],"text":"plan of a product.\nc) The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received.\nd) Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet."},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed\n simultaneously in parallel."},{"label":"b","text":"The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production\n plan of a product."},{"label":"c","text":"The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received."},{"label":"d","text":"Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'MRP (Material Requirements Planning) calculates the quantity and timing of required components from the production plan of the end products, using the bill of materials and inventory data. Doing development and production preparation in parallel is concurrent engineering, starting production after receiving an order is build-to-order, and giving instructions with a worksheet card is the kanban method.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q54)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q54. Which of the following is a characteristic of MRP?

 a) The development, designing, and production preparation of a product are performed
 simultaneously in parallel.
 b) The number of required components is calculated on the basis of the standard production
 plan of a product.
 c) The production of a product is initiated after an order from a customer is received.
 d) Work instructions and transport instructions are provided by using a worksheet.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
