  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q55. Which of the following corresponds to (5) in the example of a model of an affiliate\n program that is shown in the Internet advertising? Here, (1) to (5) indicate the order of\n operations in the model, and (1), (2), (4), and (5) each correspond to one of the options a) to\n d)."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-april-a-q55-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Agree to and participate in the affiliate program"},{"label":"b","text":"Click the advertisement on the website"},{"label":"c","text":"Pay a success fee on the basis of the sales of the product"},{"label":"d","text":"Purchase the desired product"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Step (5), the arrow from the EC site back to the web site operator, is paying a success fee based on product sales. The flow is: (1) the operator joins the affiliate program, (2) the viewer clicks the ad, (3) the viewer is sent to the link, (4) the viewer buys the product, and (5) the advertiser pays the operator a commission.',
