  '3.0',
  'Q58. The figure below shows part of a cause and effect diagram (also known as a fishbone
 diagram). Which of the following is the relationship between A and B?

 A

 B

 a) B is an attribute of A. b) B is the cause of A.
 c) B is the means of A. d) B is the purpose of A.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  59,
  'Q59. Both Data mining and Process mining are methods for improving business operations.
 While Data mining aims to discover knowledge by analyzing large amounts of data by using
 statistical and AI analysis methods, which of the following is an appropriate explanation of
 Process mining?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,517.74,532.91,603.13],"text":"Q59.\nBoth Data mining and Process mining are methods for improving business operations.\nWhile Data mining aims to discover knowledge by analyzing large amounts of data by using\nstatistical and AI analysis methods, which of the following is an appropriate explanation of\nProcess mining?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,506.64,640.21],"text":"a) It is a management strategy focused on changing workflows and business processes"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,503.34,676.21],"text":"within an organization by emphasizing new ideas and new ways of doing business.\nb) It is a method aimed at analyzing data sets, finding unsuspected relationships, and"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,680.93,528.97,712.21],"text":"summarizing the data in novel ways.\nc) It is a methodology for improving performance by systematically removing unnecessary"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,716.93,513.75,748.21],"text":"data.\nd) It is a technique for analyzing and improving business processes by using knowledge"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,752.93,262.47,766.21],"text":"that is extracted from event logs."},{"type":"code","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 24 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a management strategy focused on changing workflows and business processes\n within an organization by emphasizing new ideas and new ways of doing business."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a method aimed at analyzing data sets, finding unsuspected relationships, and\n summarizing the data in novel ways."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a methodology for improving performance by systematically removing unnecessary\n data."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a technique for analyzing and improving business processes by using knowledge\n that is extracted from event logs."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Process mining analyzes and improves business processes using knowledge extracted from event logs recorded by information systems, reconstructing how processes actually run and where bottlenecks occur. Finding unexpected relationships in data sets describes data mining, and radically changing workflows with new ideas describes BPR.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q59)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q59. Both Data mining and Process mining are methods for improving business operations.
 While Data mining aims to discover knowledge by analyzing large amounts of data by using
 statistical and AI analysis methods, which of the following is an appropriate explanation of
 Process mining?

 a) It is a management strategy focused on changing workflows and business processes
 within an organization by emphasizing new ideas and new ways of doing business.
 b) It is a method aimed at analyzing data sets, finding unsuspected relationships, and
 summarizing the data in novel ways.
 c) It is a methodology for improving performance by systematically removing unnecessary
 data.
 d) It is a technique for analyzing and improving business processes by using knowledge
 that is extracted from event logs.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-april',
  'A',
  60,
  'Q60. Company A purchased a machine for an original cost of $126,000. The salvage value
 after 6 years is $6,000. What is the annual depreciation expense (in dollars) by using the
 straight-line method?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.1,117.13],"text":"Q60.\nCompany A purchased a machine for an original cost of $126,000. The salvage value\nafter 6 years is $6,000. What is the annual depreciation expense (in dollars) by using the\nstraight-line method?"},{"type":"text","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,140.93,483.96,172.21],"text":"a) 12,000\nb) 20,000\nc) 21,000\nd) 36,000"},{"type":"code","page":25,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 25 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"12,000"},{"label":"b","text":"20,000"},{"label":"c","text":"21,000"},{"label":"d","text":"36,000"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The annual depreciation is $20,000. Straight-line depreciation spreads the depreciable amount evenly: (cost − salvage value) ÷ useful life = (126,000 − 6,000) ÷ 6 = 120,000 ÷ 6 = 20,000. Forgetting to subtract the salvage value gives 21,000.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'finance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025S, FE, Subject-A, Q60)',
  ARRAY[25]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q60. Company A purchased a machine for an original cost of $126,000. The salvage value
 after 6 years is $6,000. What is the annual depreciation expense (in dollars) by using the
 straight-line method?

 a) 12,000 b) 20,000 c) 21,000 d) 36,000',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/questions.pdf","pages":[25]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-april/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
)
