  'h',
  '{"value":"h"}'::jsonb,
  'Converting Gray code to binary means XOR-ing each bit with all higher Gray bits, which the loop achieves by repeatedly shifting z right one bit (A is >>) and XOR-ing it into y (B is y ^ z) until z becomes 0. Trace for 00001100: y becomes 00001010, then 00001001, then 00001000, matching the expected result. A left shift would push bits toward higher positions, which is the wrong direction, and AND or OR would not produce the parity of the higher bits.',
