  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q8. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"The function reverse takes a string inputStr as a parameter and returns the reversed string.\n Here, the length of the string given to inputStr is 100 or less. In the program, areas outside\n of the arrays must not be referenced and the undefined value must not be appended to a string."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"global: character []: stack ← {100 undefined}\nglobal: integer: sp ← 0\n\n○ string: reverse(string: inputStr)\n  integer: n ← length of inputStr\n  integer: i\n  character: x, v\n  string: outputStr ← \"\"\n  for (increase i from 1 to n by 1)\n    x ← the i-th character of string inputStr\n    push(x)\n  endfor\n  while (sp ≠ ***A***)\n    v ← pop()\n    append v to outputStr\n  endwhile\n  return outputStr\n\n○ push(character: x)\n   sp ← sp + 1\n   stack[sp] ← x\n\n○ character: pop()\n  character: retvar\n  ***B***\n  return retvar"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp + 1"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp − 1"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nsp sp + 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nsp sp − 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp + 1"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp − 1"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nsp sp + 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nsp sp − 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}}]}]'::jsonb,
