  '[{"label":"a","text":"−1\n sp ← sp + 1\n retvar ← stack[sp]","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp + 1"}},{"label":"b","text":"−1\n sp ← sp − 1\n sp ← sp + 1","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp − 1"}},{"label":"c","text":"−1\n retvar ← stack[sp]\n sp ← sp − 1","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nsp sp + 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"d","text":"−1\n retvar ← stack[sp]\n retvar ← stack[sp]","values":{"A":"−1","B":"←\nsp sp − 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"e","text":"0\n sp ← sp + 1\n retvar ← stack[sp]","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp + 1"}},{"label":"f","text":"0\n sp ← sp − 1\n sp ← sp + 1","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nretvar stack[sp]\n←\nsp sp − 1"}},{"label":"g","text":"0\n retvar ← stack[sp]\n sp ← sp − 1","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nsp sp + 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}},{"label":"h","text":"0\n retvar ← stack[sp]","values":{"A":"0","B":"←\nsp sp − 1\n←\nretvar stack[sp]"}}]'::jsonb,
  'f',
  '{"value":"f"}'::jsonb,
  'push increments sp before storing, so sp always points to the top element and sp = 0 means the stack is empty; the while loop must therefore run until sp equals 0 (A). pop must read the top element first and then move the pointer down: retvar ← stack[sp] followed by sp ← sp − 1 (B). Decrementing first would skip the top character and eventually read stack[0], outside the array, and using −1 for A would pop once too often.',
