  '[{"label":"a","text":"current.prev current.prev.next","values":{"A":"current.prev","B":"current.prev.next"}},{"label":"b","text":"current.prev current.next","values":{"A":"current.prev","B":"current.next"}},{"label":"c","text":"current current.prev.next","values":{"A":"current","B":"current.prev.next"}},{"label":"d","text":"current current.next","values":{"A":"current","B":"current.next"}},{"label":"e","text":"current.next current.prev.next","values":{"A":"current.next","B":"current.prev.next"}},{"label":"f","text":"current.next current.next","values":{"A":"current.next","B":"current.next"}}]'::jsonb,
  'e',
  '{"value":"e"}'::jsonb,
  'To find the last element, the loop must keep moving while there is a next element, so A is current.next (is not undefined); the loop stops with current at the last node. To remove it when there are several elements, the previous node''s forward link must be cut, so B is current.prev.next ← undefined. Setting current.next to undefined would change nothing, because it is already undefined at the last node.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
