  '{"value":"i"}'::jsonb,
  'The root cause was an internal file, marked with the "For Internal Use" watermark, being uploaded to the public directory and missed by the manual check, so A is an automated tool that blocks uploading watermarked files to the public directory. To detect such mistakes quickly, B is periodic checks of the files in the public directory to find anything exposed by mistake. A credential scanner would not help because the files contained no credentials, and monitoring unauthorized access misses files that are legitimately public but should not be.',
