whelmed network traffic in\nCompany A''s system"}},{"label":"i","text":"employee accounts system\n\n_ _\nCompany names and product names appearing in the test questions are trademarks or registered\ntrademarks of their respective companies. Note that the ® and ™ symbols are not used within the text.","values":{"A":"Multi-Factor Authentication to all\nemployee accounts","B":"unpatched servers in Company A''s\nsystem"}}]'::jsonb,
  'g',
  '{"value":"g"}'::jsonb,
  'The pattern is credential stuffing: the employee reused a password from other services, and many ID and password pairs were tried from abroad, so a more complex password would not help; A is multi-factor authentication for all employee accounts, which blocks login even with a stolen password. For quick detection, B is alerting on login attempts from locations where the account does not usually log in, since the attack came from a country with no office or travelling staff.',
