(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  1,
  'Q1. In the single precision format of the “IEEE Standard for Binary Floating-Point Arithmetic” (IEEE 754), a 32-bit floating point number is represented as below:

S: Sign (1 bit) | E: Exponent (8 bits) | F: Fraction (23 bits)

If 0 < E < 255, then the value of the number is (−1)^S × 2^(E−127) × (1+F)
where F represents the fractional part of the number, stored as a 23-bit binary sequence. This F is the sum of its weighted binary components: F = b₁×2⁻¹ + b₂×2⁻² + ⋯ + b₂₃×2⁻²³, where b₁, b₂, …, b₂₃ are the binary digits of F.

According to the IEEE-754 standard, which of the following is the decimal equivalent of the 32-bit floating point number given below?

01000001011000000000000000000000',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q1. In the single precision format of the “IEEE Standard for Binary Floating-Point Arithmetic” (IEEE 754), a 32-bit floating point number is represented as below:\n\nS: Sign (1 bit) | E: Exponent (8 bits) | F: Fraction (23 bits)\n\nIf 0 < E < 255, then the value of the number is (−1)^S × 2^(E−127) × (1+F)\nwhere F represents the fractional part of the number, stored as a 23-bit binary sequence. This F is the sum of its weighted binary components: F = b₁×2⁻¹ + b₂×2⁻² + ⋯ + b₂₃×2⁻²³, where b₁, b₂, …, b₂₃ are the binary digits of F.\n\nAccording to the IEEE-754 standard, which of the following is the decimal equivalent of the 32-bit floating point number given below?\n\n01000001011000000000000000000000"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0.1875"},{"label":"b","text":"0.4375"},{"label":"c","text":"6.0"},{"label":"d","text":"14.0"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is 14.0. Split the bits: sign 0 (positive), exponent 10000010 = 130, and fraction 1100...0, so F = 0.5 + 0.25 = 0.75. The value is 2^(130−127) × (1 + 0.75) = 8 × 1.75 = 14.0. Forgetting the hidden leading 1 would give 8 × 0.75 = 6.0, which is the tempting wrong choice.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q1)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q1. In the single precision format of the “IEEE Standard for Binary Floating-Point Arithmetic”
 (IEEE 754), a 32-bit floating point number is represented as below:

 S: Sign (1 bit) E: Exponent (8 bits) F: Fraction (23 bits)

 If 0 < E < 255, then the value of the number is (–1)S × 2 (E–127) × (1+F)
 where F represents the fractional part of the number, stored as a 23-bit binary sequence. This
 F is the sum of its weighted binary components: F=b1×2−1+b2×2−2+⋯+b23×2−23 , where b₁,
 b₂, …, b₂₃ are the binary digits of F.

 According to the IEEE-754 standard, which of the following is the decimal equivalent of the
 32-bit floating point number given below?

 01000001011000000000000000000000

 a) 0.1875 b) 0.4375 c) 6.0 d) 14.0',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[4]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  2,
  'Q2. Let n be a binary integer represented in two’s complement. Which of the following is the
 operation that results in the value 9 × n using only bit shifting and an addition or subtraction?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,355.91,533.17,387.19],"text":"Q2.  Let n be a binary integer represented in two’s complement. Which of the following is the"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,391.91,533.14,423.19],"text":"operation that results in the value 9 × n using only bit shifting and an addition or subtraction?"},{"type":"text","page":4,"bbox":[65.22,427.91,369.09,513.19],"text":"a) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then add n to the result.\nb) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result.\nc) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then add n to the result.\nd) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Shift n 2 bits to the left, then add n to the result."},{"label":"b","text":"Shift n 2 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."},{"label":"c","text":"Shift n 3 bits to the left, then add n to the result."},{"label":"d","text":"Shift n 3 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The answer is to shift n 3 bits to the left and then add n. A left shift by 3 bits multiplies by 2³ = 8, and 8n + n = 9n. Shifting by 2 bits gives 4n, so 4n + n = 5n and 4n − n = 3n, while 8n − n = 7n.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q2)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q2. Let n be a binary integer represented in two’s complement. Which of the following is the
 operation that results in the value 9 × n using only bit shifting and an addition or subtraction?

 a) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then add n to the result.
 b) Shift n 2 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result.
 c) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then add n to the result.
 d) Shift n 3 bits to the left, then subtract n from the result.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[4]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  3,
  'Q3. Three friends and 4 other people are randomly seated in 7 seats arranged in a row. What is the probability that the 3 friends sit next to one another?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q3. Three friends and 4 other people are randomly seated in 7 seats arranged in a row. What is the probability that the 3 friends sit next to one another?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1/168"},{"label":"b","text":"1/42"},{"label":"c","text":"1/35"},{"label":"d","text":"1/7"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The probability is 1/7. Treat the 3 friends as one block: the block and the 4 other people make 5 units, arranged in 5! ways, and the friends can be ordered inside the block in 3! ways, giving 120 × 6 = 720 favourable arrangements. The total number of arrangements is 7! = 5,040, and 720 / 5,040 = 1/7.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q3)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'manual_review',
