  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q4. For an automaton with input and output symbols {0, 1} and a state transition diagram shown below, which of the following is the output string for the input string 0011001110? Here, S₁ represents the initial state, and the label x/y on each arc indicates that if x is an input, then y is the corresponding output at the state transition."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q04-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"0001000110"},{"label":"b","text":"0001001110"},{"label":"c","text":"0010001000"},{"label":"d","text":"0011111110"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The output is 0001000110. Tracing from S1: 0 stays in S1 (out 0), 0 stays (0), 1 goes to S2 (0), 1 goes to S3 (1), 0 returns to S1 (0), 0 stays (0), 1 goes to S2 (0), 1 goes to S3 (1), 1 stays in S3 (1), and 0 returns to S1 (0). The machine outputs 1 only when a 1 is read in S2 or S3, i.e. on the second and later 1s of a run of consecutive 1s.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
