(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  5,
  'Q5. The table below shows the data in a list structure that has bidirectional pointers. In this table, a new Employee G is to be inserted between Employee A and Employee K. Which of the following contains only the pointers (among a through f) whose values change after the insertion?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q5. The table below shows the data in a list structure that has bidirectional pointers. In this table, a new Employee G is to be inserted between Employee A and Employee K. Which of the following contains only the pointers (among a through f) whose values change after the insertion?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q05-figure1.webp","2025-october-a-q05-figure2.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"a, b, e, f"},{"label":"b","text":"a, e, f"},{"label":"c","text":"a, f"},{"label":"d","text":"b, e"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The pointers that change are a and f. G (address 400) goes between A (100) and K (300), so A''s NextPointer must change from 300 to 400 (a), and K''s PreviousPointer must change from 100 to 400 (f). A''s PreviousPointer, T''s pointers and K''s NextPointer to T are unaffected; G''s own pointers x and y are new values, not changes.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'data-structures'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q5)',
