  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The average access time is 25.725 ms. At 6,000 RPM one rotation takes 10 ms, so the average rotational latency is half a rotation, 5 ms. The transfer time is 16 kB ÷ 1,024 kB/s = 0.015625 s = 15.625 ms. Adding seek 5 + overhead 0.1 + latency 5 + transfer 15.625 gives 25.725 ms.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q9)',
  ARRAY[7]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q9. When an HDD has the specifications shown in the table below, what is the average access
 time for the HDD to transfer 16 kB of data in milliseconds (ms)? The average access time is
 calculated as the sum of the average seek time, controller overhead, rotational latency, and
 transfer time. Other overheads can be ignored. Here, 1 MB = 1,024 kB.

 Average seek time 5 ms

 Rotation Speed 6,000 RPM

 Transfer rate 1 MB/s

 Controller overhead 0.1 ms

 a) 20.1 b) 25.725 c 30.725 d) 74.1',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[7]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
