  'A',
  10,
  'Q10. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a 3D printer’s function?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,523.72,136.21],"text":"Q10.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of a 3D printer’s function?\n\na) It detects the shape of three-dimensional objects and produces output of 3D data.\nb) It functions by pushing the pins of a high-temperature printing head onto heat-sensitive"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,519.71,190.21],"text":"paper.\nc) It makes three-dimensional objects using methods such as fused filament fabrication.\nd) It projects computer graphics onto uneven three-dimensional objects such as buildings"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[102.12,194.93,170.47,208.21],"text":"and furniture."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It detects the shape of three-dimensional objects and produces output of 3D data."},{"label":"b","text":"It functions by pushing the pins of a high-temperature printing head onto heat-sensitive\n paper."},{"label":"c","text":"It makes three-dimensional objects using methods such as fused filament fabrication."},{"label":"d","text":"It projects computer graphics onto uneven three-dimensional objects such as buildings\n and furniture."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A 3D printer builds physical three-dimensional objects layer by layer, for example by fused filament fabrication, where melted plastic filament is deposited in layers. Detecting an object''s shape and outputting 3D data describes a 3D scanner, pressing hot pins on heat-sensitive paper is a thermal printer, and projecting graphics onto buildings is projection mapping.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q10)',
