),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  11,
  'Q11. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of edge computing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,247.74,497.73,261.19],"text":"Q11.\n Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of edge computing?"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,266.93,530.93,298.21],"text":"a) Increasing the operability and expressiveness of web application software by performing"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,302.93,522.73,334.21],"text":"screen creation and data processing on the client side\nb) Increasing the real-time nature of processing by performing primary processing of data"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,514.07,388.21],"text":"on a server or other such computer in a location close to the origin of data, such as a\nsensor that is attached to a user or a device\nc) Increasing throughput with parallel processing by virtualizing and integrating several"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,511.93,424.21],"text":"servers and PCs and creating a single high-performance computer\nd) Starting up the required server only when data comes in, and freeing up resources by"},{"type":"text","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,428.93,372.81,496.15],"text":"stopping the server as soon as the processing is finished"},{"type":"code","page":8,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 8 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Increasing the operability and expressiveness of web application software by performing\n screen creation and data processing on the client side"},{"label":"b","text":"Increasing the real-time nature of processing by performing primary processing of data\n on a server or other such computer in a location close to the origin of data, such as a\n sensor that is attached to a user or a device"},{"label":"c","text":"Increasing throughput with parallel processing by virtualizing and integrating several\n servers and PCs and creating a single high-performance computer"},{"label":"d","text":"Starting up the required server only when data comes in, and freeing up resources by\n stopping the server as soon as the processing is finished"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Edge computing performs primary processing of data on servers or devices located close to where the data is generated, such as sensors, to improve real-time responsiveness. This reduces the latency and network load of sending everything to a distant cloud. Client-side screen processing describes rich clients, combining many machines into one virtual computer describes grid computing, and starting servers only on demand describes serverless computing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q11)',
  ARRAY[8]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q11. Which of the following is the most appropriate explanation of edge computing?

 a) Increasing the operability and expressiveness of web application software by performing
 screen creation and data processing on the client side
 b) Increasing the real-time nature of processing by performing primary processing of data
 on a server or other such computer in a location close to the origin of data, such as a
 sensor that is attached to a user or a device
 c) Increasing throughput with parallel processing by virtualizing and integrating several
 servers and PCs and creating a single high-performance computer
 d) Starting up the required server only when data comes in, and freeing up resources by
 stopping the server as soon as the processing is finished',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[8]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
