  'A',
  12,
  'Q12. One (1) server, three (3) clients, and two (2) printers are connected via a LAN as shown in the figure below. This system prints data that is located on the server in response to instructions from the clients. When the availability of each device is as shown in the table below, which of the following is the expression that represents the availability for the system? Here, the system is considered available if one (1) of the three (3) clients and one (1) of the two (2) printers are running.

Device | Availability
Server | a
Client | b
Printer | c
LAN | 1',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q12. One (1) server, three (3) clients, and two (2) printers are connected via a LAN as shown in the figure below. This system prints data that is located on the server in response to instructions from the clients. When the availability of each device is as shown in the table below, which of the following is the expression that represents the availability for the system? Here, the system is considered available if one (1) of the three (3) clients and one (1) of the two (2) printers are running.\n\nDevice | Availability\nServer | a\nClient | b\nPrinter | c\nLAN | 1"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q12-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"ab³c²"},{"label":"b","text":"a (1−b³) (1−c²)"},{"label":"c","text":"a (1−b)³ (1−c)²"},{"label":"d","text":"a (1−(1−b)³) (1−(1−c)²)"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The availability is a(1 − (1 − b)³)(1 − (1 − c)²). The server (a) is needed in series with the client group and the printer group. The three clients are in parallel, so the group fails only if all fail: 1 − (1 − b)³; likewise the two printers give 1 − (1 − c)². The LAN has availability 1, so it does not change the product.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q12)',
  ARRAY[9]::int[],
