(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  13,
  'Q13. Five processes A, B, C, D and E arrive at almost the same time in the order of A, B, C, D
 and E. The processes have estimated running times of 10, 6, 2, 8, and 4 milliseconds,
 respectively. Which of the following is the average process turnaround time with the First-Come-First-Served (FCFS) scheduling algorithm?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,520.0,533.1,604.93],"text":"Q13.\nFive processes A, B, C, D and E arrive at almost the same time in the order of A, B, C, D\nand E. The processes have estimated running times of 10, 6, 2, 8, and 4 milliseconds,\nrespectively. Which of the following is the average process turnaround time with the First-\nCome-First-Served (FCFS) scheduling algorithm?"},{"type":"text","page":9,"bbox":[84.12,627.65,470.1,640.93],"text":"a) 14\nb) 19.2\nc) 20\nd) 22"},{"type":"code","page":9,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,311.58,807.97],"text":"– 9 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"14"},{"label":"b","text":"19.2"},{"label":"c","text":"20"},{"label":"d","text":"22"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The average turnaround time is 20 ms. Under FCFS the processes run in arrival order, so they finish at A = 10, B = 16, C = 18, D = 26 and E = 30 ms. Since all arrive at about time 0, these are the turnaround times, and (10 + 16 + 18 + 26 + 30) ÷ 5 = 100 ÷ 5 = 20.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
