(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  14,
  'Q14. In indirect addressing of direct file organization, which of the following is an appropriate
 method for calculating the record address from a record key in the superposition addressing
 method, or folding and adding method? Here, the record key is 123456 in decimal. The total
 number of records is 1,000, and the closest prime number to 1,000 is 997. The decimal number
 123456 is equivalent to 361100 in octal.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.29,154.21],"text":"Q14.\nIn indirect addressing of direct file organization, which of the following is an appropriate\nmethod for calculating the record address from a record key in the superposition addressing\nmethod, or folding and adding method? Here, the record key is 123456 in decimal. The total\nnumber of records is 1,000, and the closest prime number to 1,000 is 997. The decimal number\n123456 is equivalent to 361100 in octal."},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,176.93,495.97,244.21],"text":"a) Converting the record key into 361100 and using it as the address\nb) Dividing the record key by 997 and using the remainder of 825 as the address\nc) Splitting the record key into 123 and 456 and using their sum, 579, as the address\nd) Using the record key 123456 as the address"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Converting the record key into 361100 and using it as the address"},{"label":"b","text":"Dividing the record key by 997 and using the remainder of 825 as the address"},{"label":"c","text":"Splitting the record key into 123 and 456 and using their sum, 579, as the address"},{"label":"d","text":"Using the record key 123456 as the address"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The folding (superposition) method splits the key into parts and adds them, so 123456 becomes 123 + 456 = 579, which is used as the record address. Dividing by the prime 997 and using the remainder is the division-remainder method, and converting the key to another radix is the radix conversion method. Using the key itself as the address is direct addressing, not a calculated one.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q14)',
  ARRAY[10]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q14. In indirect addressing of direct file organization, which of the following is an appropriate
 method for calculating the record address from a record key in the superposition addressing
 method, or folding and adding method? Here, the record key is 123456 in decimal. The total
 number of records is 1,000, and the closest prime number to 1,000 is 997. The decimal number
 123456 is equivalent to 361100 in octal.

 a) Converting the record key into 361100 and using it as the address
 b) Dividing the record key by 997 and using the remainder of 825 as the address
 c) Splitting the record key into 123 and 456 and using their sum, 579, as the address
 d) Using the record key 123456 as the address',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[10]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
