  15,
  'Q15. The page capacity of main memory is three pages, and the pages are referenced in the
 order {1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5}. Which of the following is the page that will be replaced from main
 memory for the last page reference if LRU is used as the page replacement technique?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,533.16,334.21],"text":"Q15.\nThe page capacity of main memory is three pages, and the pages are referenced in the\norder {1, 2, 3, 2, 1, 4, 5}. Which of the following is the page that will be replaced from main\nmemory for the last page reference if LRU is used as the page replacement technique?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,464.1,388.21],"text":"a) 1\nb) 2\nc) 3\nd) 4"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1"},{"label":"b","text":"2"},{"label":"c","text":"3"},{"label":"d","text":"4"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Page 2 is replaced at the last reference. After 1, 2, 3, 2, 1 the frames hold {1, 2, 3}; referencing 4 evicts page 3, the least recently used, giving {1, 2, 4}. When 5 is referenced, page 2 (last used at the fourth reference) is now older than page 1 (fifth) and page 4 (sixth), so LRU removes page 2.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'operating-systems'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
