  16,
  'Q16. Which of the following is equivalent to the logical circuit shown below?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.34,392.93,461.88,424.21],"text":"Q16.\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the logical circuit shown below?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,533.94,482.76,550.28],"text":"a) A ∙ B\nb) A̅ ∙ B\nc) A ∙ B̅\nd) A̅ ∙ B̅"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q16-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A ∙ B"},{"label":"b","text":"A̅ ∙ B"},{"label":"c","text":"A ∙ B̅"},{"label":"d","text":"A̅ ∙ B̅"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The circuit is equivalent to A̅ ∙ B. The upper gate is a NAND of A̅ and B, giving NOT(A̅B), and the lower gate is a NOR of A and B, giving NOT(A + B). The final NOR outputs NOT(NOT(A̅B) + NOT(A + B)) = A̅B ∙ (A + B) = A̅B, because A̅B is already contained in A + B.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'computer-architecture'),
  'medium',
