  17,
  'Q17. Which of the following is a method used to improve the appearance of a jagged edge of
 a slanted line so that it appears smooth on a screen, such as that of an LCD?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,590.76,533.17,622.21],"text":"Q17.\nWhich of the following is a method used to improve the appearance of a jagged edge of\na slanted line so that it appears smooth on a screen, such as that of an LCD?"},{"type":"text","page":10,"bbox":[84.12,646.91,412.84,678.19],"text":"a) Anti-aliasing\nb) Bump mapping\nc) Shading\nd) Texture mapping"},{"type":"code","page":10,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 10 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Anti-aliasing"},{"label":"b","text":"Bump mapping"},{"label":"c","text":"Shading"},{"label":"d","text":"Texture mapping"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Anti-aliasing smooths the jagged, staircase-like edges of slanted lines by blending the colours of edge pixels with the background colour. Bump mapping simulates surface roughness, shading sets brightness according to light, and texture mapping pastes an image onto a surface; none of these specifically removes jaggies.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
