 SupplierCode → {SupplierName, SupplierAddress, SupplierManagerCode}
 CustomerCode → {CustomerName, CustomerAddress}',
  '[{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,231.28,533.14,316.21],"text":"Q19.\nWhen the functional dependencies shown below are satisfied, which of the following is\nthe transitive functional dependency that holds? Here, “A→B” indicates that B is functionally\ndependent on A, and “A→{B, C}” indicates that “A→B” and “A→C ” both hold."},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[75.24,320.93,205.18,334.21],"text":"[Functional dependencies]"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[100.68,339.95,455.97,353.23],"text":"{OrderCode, ProductCode} → {CustomerOrderQuantity, OrderAmount}"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[100.68,358.91,417.16,372.19],"text":"OrderCode → {OrderDate, CustomerCode, OrderManagerCode}"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[100.68,377.93,422.54,391.21],"text":"ProductCode → {ProductName, SupplierCode, ProductSalePrice}"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[100.68,396.89,469.09,410.17],"text":"SupplierCode → {SupplierName, SupplierAddress, SupplierManagerCode}"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[100.68,415.91,372.42,429.19],"text":"CustomerCode → {CustomerName, CustomerAddress}"},{"type":"text","page":11,"bbox":[65.22,434.93,401.77,538.15],"text":"a) OrderCode → CustomerCode → CustomerAddress\nb) OrderCode → ProductCode → CustomerOrderQuantity\nc) ProductCode → SupplierCode → ProductSalePrice\nd) SupplierCode → SupplierManagerCode → SupplierAddress"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"OrderCode → CustomerCode → CustomerAddress"},{"label":"b","text":"OrderCode → ProductCode → CustomerOrderQuantity"},{"label":"c","text":"ProductCode → SupplierCode → ProductSalePrice"},{"label":"d","text":"SupplierCode → SupplierManagerCode → SupplierAddress"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The transitive dependency is OrderCode → CustomerCode → CustomerAddress. OrderCode determines CustomerCode, and CustomerCode determines CustomerAddress, so CustomerAddress depends on OrderCode only indirectly through a non-key attribute. The other choices use dependencies that are not given, for example ProductCode does not determine CustomerOrderQuantity on its own.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
