  22,
  'Q22. In the context of transaction management, which of the following is a condition that the
 Isolation property ensures?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,420.72,533.21,452.17],"text":"Q22.\nIn the context of transaction management, which of the following is a condition that the\nIsolation property ensures?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[84.12,474.89,370.71,542.17],"text":"a) Data is written permanently after a transaction.\nb) Only valid data is written to the database.\nc) Transactions are either fully completed or revoked.\nd) Transactions are executed without affecting each other."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Data is written permanently after a transaction."},{"label":"b","text":"Only valid data is written to the database."},{"label":"c","text":"Transactions are either fully completed or revoked."},{"label":"d","text":"Transactions are executed without affecting each other."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Isolation ensures that concurrently executed transactions do not affect each other, so the result is the same as if they had run one at a time. Permanent recording after commit is Durability, writing only valid data is Consistency, and all-or-nothing completion is Atomicity.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'databases'),
  'medium',
