  '[{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,582.72,533.09,650.17],"text":"Q23.\nWhich of the following is a mechanism used to prioritize traffic based on its importance\nand minimize network latency for network applications?"},{"type":"text","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,654.89,480.1,686.17],"text":"a) AAA\nb) PoE\nc) QoS\nd) RTP"},{"type":"code","page":12,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 12 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"AAA"},{"label":"b","text":"PoE"},{"label":"c","text":"QoS"},{"label":"d","text":"RTP"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'QoS (Quality of Service) classifies traffic and gives priority and bandwidth to important flows such as voice or video, reducing their latency and jitter. AAA is authentication, authorization and accounting, PoE supplies power over Ethernet cables, and RTP is a protocol that carries real-time media but does not itself prioritize traffic.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
