  24,
  'Q24. PC5 has been newly added to the network. It wants to send data to PC4 using SSH protocol. It must resolve the MAC address of PC4 from its IP address before sending the data. Which of the following is the destination MAC address that PC5 will use in ARP request?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q24. PC5 has been newly added to the network. It wants to send data to PC4 using SSH protocol. It must resolve the MAC address of PC4 from its IP address before sending the data. Which of the following is the destination MAC address that PC5 will use in ARP request?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q24-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"00:00:00:00:00:00"},{"label":"b","text":"78:E1:00:3C:A1:8B"},{"label":"c","text":"78:E1:00:3C:A1:9F"},{"label":"d","text":"FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The destination MAC address is FF:FF:FF:FF:FF:FF, the broadcast address. PC5 does not yet know PC4''s MAC address, so the ARP request is broadcast to every host on the LAN, and only PC4 (192.168.1.10) replies with its MAC address 78:E1:00:3C:A1:8B. That address appears in the reply, not as the destination of the request.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'networking'),
