  27,
  'Q27. An attacker left a USB stick labeled “Next ITPEC exam questions and answers” that
 contains malware in front of an office, expecting someone to plug it into a PC. Once plugged
 in, the attacker gains control of the PC. Which of the following types of attack is this?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,598.74,533.11,612.19],"text":"Q27.\nAn attacker left a USB stick labeled “Next ITPEC exam questions and answers” that"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[85.74,616.91,533.1,630.19],"text":"contains malware in front of an office, expecting someone to plug it into a PC. Once plugged"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[85.74,634.91,501.32,648.19],"text":"in, the attacker gains control of the PC. Which of the following types of attack is this?"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,670.91,392.86,684.19],"text":"a) Baiting\nb) Identity theft"},{"type":"text","page":13,"bbox":[84.12,688.91,379.75,702.19],"text":"c) Phishing\nd) Pretexting"},{"type":"code","page":13,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 13 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Baiting"},{"label":"b","text":"Identity theft"},{"label":"c","text":"Phishing"},{"label":"d","text":"Pretexting"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'This is baiting, a social engineering attack that leaves a tempting item, such as an infected USB stick with an attractive label, for a victim to pick up and use. Phishing uses fraudulent messages, pretexting uses an invented story to obtain information, and identity theft is the misuse of someone''s personal data.',
