  28,
  'Q28. When X receives a message with a digital signature that uses public key cryptography
 from Y, which of the following is the key that X uses to verify that the message truly came
 from Y?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.13,118.21],"text":"Q28.\nWhen X receives a message with a digital signature that uses public key cryptography\nfrom Y, which of the following is the key that X uses to verify that the message truly came\nfrom Y?"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,140.93,405.79,207.13],"text":"a) X’s private key\nb) X’s public key\nc) Y’s private key\nd) Y’s public key"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"X’s private key"},{"label":"b","text":"X’s public key"},{"label":"c","text":"Y’s private key"},{"label":"d","text":"Y’s public key"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'X verifies the signature with Y''s public key. Y signs the message digest with Y''s private key, and only Y''s public key can verify that signature, which proves the message came from Y and was not altered. X''s own keys play no part in checking Y''s signature.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
