 server for name resolution.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,212.76,533.1,406.15],"text":"Q29.\nThe IP address of server X that is owned by an attacker, is recorded on Company B’s\nDNS cache server as the IP address corresponding to the FQDN of Company A’s web server.\nAs a result, which of the following are the users that unintentionally connect to server X?\nHere, the employees of Company A and Company B use their own company’s DNS cache\nserver for name resolution.\n\na) Company A employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server\nb) Company A employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server\nc) Company B employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server\nd) Company B employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Company A employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server"},{"label":"b","text":"Company A employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server"},{"label":"c","text":"Company B employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server"},{"label":"d","text":"Company B employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'Company B employees who try to connect to Company A''s web server are redirected to server X. This is DNS cache poisoning: the false record sits in Company B''s DNS cache server and concerns Company A''s FQDN. Company A employees use their own DNS server, which is not poisoned, and lookups for Company B''s own server are unaffected.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q29)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q29. The IP address of server X that is owned by an attacker, is recorded on Company B’s
 DNS cache server as the IP address corresponding to the FQDN of Company A’s web server.
 As a result, which of the following are the users that unintentionally connect to server X?
 Here, the employees of Company A and Company B use their own company’s DNS cache
 server for name resolution.

 a) Company A employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server
 b) Company A employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server
 c) Company B employees who try to connect to Company A’s web server
 d) Company B employees who try to connect to Company B’s web server',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  30,
  'Q30. When a fraud occurs, all three (3) elements of the “fraud triangle” are believed to exist.
 Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of an element of the “fraud triangle”?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,410.76,533.16,496.21],"text":"Q30.\nWhen a fraud occurs, all three (3) elements of the “fraud triangle” are believed to exist.\nWhich of the following is the appropriate explanation of an element of the “fraud triangle”?\n\na) “Information and communication” refers to the identification, understanding, and"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,517.64,550.21],"text":"processing of the required information, and its proper communication both within and\noutside the organization, and among the concerned persons.\nb) “Opportunity” refers to the existence of an environment, such as technologies like the"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,517.69,604.21],"text":"information system, physical environment, organizational rules, etc., that makes fraud\npossible or easy to commit.\nc) “Pressure,” also known as incentive or motivation, refers to the selfish reasoning to"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,529.3,658.21],"text":"justify committing fraud, such as interpreting things in a way that overcomes guilt or\nshifts blame.\nd) “Rationalization” refers to the feeling of being forced caused by unrealistic performance"},{"type":"text","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,662.93,140.15,694.15],"text":"targets."},{"type":"code","page":14,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 14 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"“Information and communication” refers to the identification, understanding, and\n processing of the required information, and its proper communication both within and\n outside the organization, and among the concerned persons."},{"label":"b","text":"“Opportunity” refers to the existence of an environment, such as technologies like the\n information system, physical environment, organizational rules, etc., that makes fraud\n possible or easy to commit."},{"label":"c","text":"“Pressure,” also known as incentive or motivation, refers to the selfish reasoning to\n justify committing fraud, such as interpreting things in a way that overcomes guilt or\n shifts blame."},{"label":"d","text":"“Rationalization” refers to the feeling of being forced caused by unrealistic performance\n targets."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct description is of Opportunity: an environment, such as weak systems, physical conditions or rules, that makes fraud possible or easy. The fraud triangle consists of opportunity, pressure (motivation) and rationalization. The descriptions of pressure and rationalization in the other choices are swapped, and information and communication is a component of internal control, not of the fraud triangle.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q30)',
  ARRAY[14]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q30. When a fraud occurs, all three (3) elements of the “fraud triangle” are believed to exist.
 Which of the following is the appropriate explanation of an element of the “fraud triangle”?

 a) “Information and communication” refers to the identification, understanding, and
 processing of the required information, and its proper communication both within and
 outside the organization, and among the concerned persons.
 b) “Opportunity” refers to the existence of an environment, such as technologies like the
 information system, physical environment, organizational rules, etc., that makes fraud
 possible or easy to commit.
 c) “Pressure,” also known as incentive or motivation, refers to the selfish reasoning to
 justify committing fraud, such as interpreting things in a way that overcomes guilt or
 shifts blame.
 d) “Rationalization” refers to the feeling of being forced caused by unrealistic performance
 targets.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[14]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  31,
  'Q31. Which of the following is a function of an IDS?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,68.93,328.99,99.19],"text":"Q31. Which of the following is a function of an IDS?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,516.33,154.21],"text":"a) It checks whether software products that are installed on a PC are the latest version.\nb) It collects the status of information security measures, such as the status of operations"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,521.36,226.21],"text":"management for an information system, and also obtains company information, then\nperforms a self-diagnosis on the status of activities for information security in an\norganization.\nc) It monitors a server or a network and notifies the administrator when it has detected an"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,230.93,509.38,262.21],"text":"intrusion or infringement.\nd) It sends test data to a product that it examines and detects any vulnerability from the"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,266.93,278.39,298.21],"text":"response or behavior of the product."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It checks whether software products that are installed on a PC are the latest version."},{"label":"b","text":"It collects the status of information security measures, such as the status of operations\n management for an information system, and also obtains company information, then\n performs a self-diagnosis on the status of activities for information security in an\n organization."},{"label":"c","text":"It monitors a server or a network and notifies the administrator when it has detected an\n intrusion or infringement."},{"label":"d","text":"It sends test data to a product that it examines and detects any vulnerability from the\n response or behavior of the product."}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'An IDS (intrusion detection system) monitors a server or network and alerts the administrator when it detects an intrusion or other unauthorized activity. Checking software versions is patch or asset management, self-diagnosis of security activities is a security self-assessment, and sending test data to find vulnerabilities is fuzzing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q31)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q31. Which of the following is a function of an IDS?

 a) It checks whether software products that are installed on a PC are the latest version.
 b) It collects the status of information security measures, such as the status of operations
 management for an information system, and also obtains company information, then
 performs a self-diagnosis on the status of activities for information security in an
 organization.
 c) It monitors a server or a network and notifies the administrator when it has detected an
 intrusion or infringement.
 d) It sends test data to a product that it examines and detects any vulnerability from the
 response or behavior of the product.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  32,
  'Q32. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the timing and purpose
 of port scanning when an attacker intrudes into a system?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,533.16,333.19],"text":"Q32. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the timing and purpose"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[85.74,337.68,364.66,351.13],"text":"of port scanning when an attacker intrudes into a system?"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,376.91,516.1,390.19],"text":"a) It is conducted at the post-processing stage in order to look for any evidence of attack"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,394.91,529.41,426.19],"text":"that may remain in the system log.\nb) It is conducted at the preliminary investigation stage in order to look for any service that"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,430.91,517.96,462.19],"text":"can be attacked.\nc) It is conducted at the privilege escalation stage in order to look for any account whose"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[84.12,466.91,528.1,498.19],"text":"privileges can be obtained.\nd) It is conducted at the unauthorized action stage in order to look for any user information"},{"type":"text","page":15,"bbox":[102.12,502.91,285.42,516.19],"text":"that may be beneficial to the attacker."},{"type":"code","page":15,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 15 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is conducted at the post-processing stage in order to look for any evidence of attack\n that may remain in the system log."},{"label":"b","text":"It is conducted at the preliminary investigation stage in order to look for any service that\n can be attacked."},{"label":"c","text":"It is conducted at the privilege escalation stage in order to look for any account whose\n privileges can be obtained."},{"label":"d","text":"It is conducted at the unauthorized action stage in order to look for any user information\n that may be beneficial to the attacker."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'Port scanning is done at the preliminary investigation (reconnaissance) stage to find open ports and the services behind them that can be attacked. It happens before the intrusion itself, not during privilege escalation, unauthorized actions, or the clean-up of logs afterwards.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'security-threats'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q32)',
  ARRAY[15]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q32. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning the timing and purpose
 of port scanning when an attacker intrudes into a system?

 a) It is conducted at the post-processing stage in order to look for any evidence of attack
 that may remain in the system log.
 b) It is conducted at the preliminary investigation stage in order to look for any service that
 can be attacked.
 c) It is conducted at the privilege escalation stage in order to look for any account whose
 privileges can be obtained.
 d) It is conducted at the unauthorized action stage in order to look for any user information
 that may be beneficial to the attacker.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[15]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  33,
  'Q33. In a system with the configuration and communication services shown in the figure below, which of the following is the most appropriate location for the installation of a WAF as a countermeasure for a vulnerability in a web application? Here, the WAF has no function to encrypt or decrypt communications.',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q33. In a system with the configuration and communication services shown in the figure below, which of the following is the most appropriate location for the installation of a WAF as a countermeasure for a vulnerability in a web application? Here, the WAF has no function to encrypt or decrypt communications."}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q33-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A"},{"label":"b","text":"B"},{"label":"c","text":"C"},{"label":"d","text":"D"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The WAF should be installed at C, between the SSL accelerator and the web server. A WAF must inspect HTTP request content to block attacks such as SQL injection or XSS, and since it cannot decrypt traffic, it must sit where the traffic is already decrypted plain HTTP. At A and B the traffic is still HTTPS, and D carries database access rather than web requests.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'network-security'),
  'medium',
