  'A',
  34,
  'Q34. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a UML use case diagram?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,517.74,502.69,531.19],"text":"Q34.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of a UML use case diagram?"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,532.67,622.21],"text":"a) It shows the behavior during the object’s life cycle using finite state transitions.\nb) It shows the exchange of messages among objects and objects’ lifelines in a time series.\nc) It shows the flow from one activity to another activity in a system or business process.\nd) It shows the scenarios for how actors, i.e., external users or machines, interact with a"},{"type":"text","page":16,"bbox":[102.12,626.93,141.48,640.21],"text":"system."},{"type":"code","page":16,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 16 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It shows the behavior during the object’s life cycle using finite state transitions."},{"label":"b","text":"It shows the exchange of messages among objects and objects’ lifelines in a time series."},{"label":"c","text":"It shows the flow from one activity to another activity in a system or business process."},{"label":"d","text":"It shows the scenarios for how actors, i.e., external users or machines, interact with a\n system."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A use case diagram shows how actors, i.e. external users or systems, interact with the system through use cases, capturing functional requirements from the outside. Life cycle state transitions are shown in a state machine diagram, time-ordered message exchange in a sequence diagram, and the flow between activities in an activity diagram.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q34)',
  ARRAY[16]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q34. Which of the following is an appropriate description of a UML use case diagram?

 a) It shows the behavior during the object’s life cycle using finite state transitions.
 b) It shows the exchange of messages among objects and objects’ lifelines in a time series.
 c) It shows the flow from one activity to another activity in a system or business process.
 d) It shows the scenarios for how actors, i.e., external users or machines, interact with a
 system.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[16]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  35,
  'Q35. In the development process, which of the following is an activity that should be
 performed in software architecture design?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,539.02,190.21],"text":"Q35.\nIn the development process, which of the following is an activity that should be\nperformed in software architecture design?\n\na) Analyzing the requirements in incremental steps by arranging them in the form of a chart\nb) Describing the specifications so that the program is clarified on a line-by-line basis\nc) Obtaining the opinion of the customer and deciding on the specifications\nd) Transforming the requirements for the software items into a design that describes its top-"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,194.93,370.47,226.15],"text":"level structure and identifies the software components"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Analyzing the requirements in incremental steps by arranging them in the form of a chart"},{"label":"b","text":"Describing the specifications so that the program is clarified on a line-by-line basis"},{"label":"c","text":"Obtaining the opinion of the customer and deciding on the specifications"},{"label":"d","text":"Transforming the requirements for the software items into a design that describes its top-level structure and identifies the software components"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Software architecture design transforms the requirements for the software item into a top-level structure and identifies its software components. Line-by-line program specifications belong to detailed design, and analyzing requirements or agreeing specifications with the customer belong to requirements definition, which comes earlier.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q35)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q35. In the development process, which of the following is an activity that should be
 performed in software architecture design?

 a) Analyzing the requirements in incremental steps by arranging them in the form of a chart
 b) Describing the specifications so that the program is clarified on a line-by-line basis
 c) Obtaining the opinion of the customer and deciding on the specifications
 d) Transforming the requirements for the software items into a design that describes its top-level structure and identifies the software components',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  36,
  'Q36. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning a state transition test in
 a system integration test?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,230.76,533.24,280.21],"text":"Q36.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description concerning a state transition test in\na system integration test?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,531.06,334.21],"text":"a) A method for black box tests that does not focus on a system’s internal state.\nb) A method that checks whether a system behaves according to the designed combinations"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,338.93,528.74,370.21],"text":"of events and internal states.\nc) A method that is suitable for tests of calculations and processing systems whose internal"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,528.37,406.21],"text":"state does not change depending on the occurrence of an event.\nd) A method that uses a data flow diagram and a decision table to analyze the internal state"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,410.93,162.78,442.21],"text":"of a system."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A method for black box tests that does not focus on a system’s internal state."},{"label":"b","text":"A method that checks whether a system behaves according to the designed combinations\n of events and internal states."},{"label":"c","text":"A method that is suitable for tests of calculations and processing systems whose internal\n state does not change depending on the occurrence of an event."},{"label":"d","text":"A method that uses a data flow diagram and a decision table to analyze the internal state\n of a system."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A state transition test checks whether the system behaves as designed for each combination of event and internal state, for example by covering the transitions in a state transition diagram or table. It is a black-box technique that explicitly focuses on internal states, so it suits systems whose behaviour changes with state, not stateless calculations.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q36)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q36. Which of the following is an appropriate description concerning a state transition test in
 a system integration test?

 a) A method for black box tests that does not focus on a system’s internal state.
 b) A method that checks whether a system behaves according to the designed combinations
 of events and internal states.
 c) A method that is suitable for tests of calculations and processing systems whose internal
 state does not change depending on the occurrence of an event.
 d) A method that uses a data flow diagram and a decision table to analyze the internal state
 of a system.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  37,
  'Q37. Which of the following is an appropriate description of an acceptance test?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,447.28,475.7,478.21],"text":"Q37.\n Which of the following is an appropriate description of an acceptance test?"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,510.08,532.21],"text":"a) It is conducted by developers to verify response time and other performance items.\nb) It is conducted by testers to ensure that the interfaces and linkages between different"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,523.73,568.21],"text":"software parts work properly.\nc) It is conducted by the project manager to verify whether users’ functional requirements"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,525.3,604.21],"text":"are met or not.\nd) It is conducted by users to confirm that the software is complete and meets the business"},{"type":"text","page":17,"bbox":[102.12,608.93,346.33,622.21],"text":"needs that prompted the software to be developed."},{"type":"code","page":17,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 17 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is conducted by developers to verify response time and other performance items."},{"label":"b","text":"It is conducted by testers to ensure that the interfaces and linkages between different\n software parts work properly."},{"label":"c","text":"It is conducted by the project manager to verify whether users’ functional requirements\n are met or not."},{"label":"d","text":"It is conducted by users to confirm that the software is complete and meets the business\n needs that prompted the software to be developed."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'An acceptance test is performed by the users (or the customer) to confirm that the completed software meets the business needs it was developed for, before accepting it. Performance checks by developers belong to system testing, and interface checks between parts are integration testing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q37)',
  ARRAY[17]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q37. Which of the following is an appropriate description of an acceptance test?

 a) It is conducted by developers to verify response time and other performance items.
 b) It is conducted by testers to ensure that the interfaces and linkages between different
 software parts work properly.
 c) It is conducted by the project manager to verify whether users’ functional requirements
 are met or not.
 d) It is conducted by users to confirm that the software is complete and meets the business
 needs that prompted the software to be developed.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[17]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  38,
  'Q38. What is the expected value in dollars for the correction cost of an application program in
 the first year under the conditions shown below?

 [Conditions]
 (1) Program size: 2,000 k steps
 (2) Potential defective rate of program: 0.04 defects / k steps
 (3) Annual discovery rate of potential defects: 20% / year
 (4) Classification of discovered defects:
 –Major impact: 20%
 –Minor impact: 80%
 (5) Correction cost per defect
 Defects with major impact: 20,000 dollars
 Defects with minor impact: 5,000 dollars
 (6) In the first year, only defects with major impact are corrected',
  '[{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.14,136.21],"text":"Q38.\nWhat is the expected value in dollars for the correction cost of an application program in\nthe first year under the conditions shown below?\n\n[Conditions]"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.36,140.93,399.8,208.21],"text":"(1) Program size: 2,000 k steps\n(2) Potential defective rate of program: 0.04 defects / k steps\n(3) Annual discovery rate of potential defects: 20% / year\n(4) Classification of discovered defects:"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[102.36,212.93,250.94,262.21],"text":"–Major impact: 20%\n–Minor impact: 80%\n(5) Correction cost per defect"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[85.2,266.93,420.43,334.21],"text":"Defects with major impact: 20,000 dollars\nDefects with minor impact: 5,000 dollars\n(6) In the first year, only defects with major impact are corrected"},{"type":"text","page":18,"bbox":[86.22,338.93,468.72,352.21],"text":"a)\n64,000\nb) 128,000\nc) 160,000\nd) 640,000"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"64,000"},{"label":"b","text":"128,000"},{"label":"c","text":"160,000"},{"label":"d","text":"640,000"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The expected cost is 64,000 dollars. The program has 2,000 × 0.04 = 80 latent defects, 20% of which (16) are found in the first year. Only the 20% with major impact are corrected, i.e. 3.2 defects, and 3.2 × 20,000 = 64,000 dollars. Including the minor defects would wrongly add 12.8 × 5,000 = 64,000 more.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'quality-assurance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q38)',
  ARRAY[18]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q38. What is the expected value in dollars for the correction cost of an application program in
 the first year under the conditions shown below?

 [Conditions]
 (1) Program size: 2,000 k steps
 (2) Potential defective rate of program: 0.04 defects / k steps
 (3) Annual discovery rate of potential defects: 20% / year
 (4) Classification of discovered defects:
 –Major impact: 20%
