  'A',
  41,
  'Q41. Eight (8) activities and milestones of a project are shown in the arrow diagram below. Which of the following is the critical path of this project?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q41. Eight (8) activities and milestones of a project are shown in the arrow diagram below. Which of the following is the critical path of this project?"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-a-q41-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A, C, E, H"},{"label":"b","text":"A, C, F, G"},{"label":"c","text":"B, E, H"},{"label":"d","text":"B, F, G"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'The critical path is A, C, E, H, taking 55 days. A and C finish at day 30, and the dummy arrow means E cannot start until then (D alone would finish at only 25). E then ends at 45 and H at 55, while the path through F and G ends at 30 + 15 + 5 = 50, and B (10 days) is shorter than A plus C.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q41)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q41. Eight (8) activities and milestones of a project are shown in the arrow diagram below.
 Which of the following is the critical path of this project?

 A D E
 15 10 15 H
 B C 15
 F G 10 10
 15 5

 Legend:

 Activity name
 Number of days
 required
 Dummy

 a) A, C, E, H b) A, C, F, G c) B, E, H d) B, F, G',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  42,
  'Q42. Based on the requirements gathered, the cost of a software project under normal
 conditions is estimated at $70,000. In case of smooth project implementation, some activities
 are not required and the estimated cost is reduced to $50,000; however, in the worst-case
 scenario, additional tasks are required and the cost increases to $120,000. What is the
 expected cost of the project (in dollars) that is calculated by using the three-point estimate in
 the beta distribution, also known as PERT?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,608.76,533.17,622.21],"text":"Q42.\nBased on the requirements gathered, the cost of a software project under normal"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.74,626.93,533.12,640.21],"text":"conditions is estimated at $70,000. In case of smooth project implementation, some activities"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.74,644.93,533.12,658.21],"text":"are not required and the estimated cost is reduced to $50,000; however, in the worst-case"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.74,662.93,533.04,676.21],"text":"scenario, additional tasks are required and the cost increases to $120,000. What is the"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.74,680.93,533.17,694.21],"text":"expected cost of the project (in dollars) that is calculated by using the three-point estimate in"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[85.74,698.93,296.4,712.21],"text":"the beta distribution, also known as PERT?"},{"type":"text","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,734.93,491.1,765.13],"text":"a) 70,000\nb) 75,000\nc) 80,000\nd) 85,000"},{"type":"code","page":19,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 19 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"70,000"},{"label":"b","text":"75,000"},{"label":"c","text":"80,000"},{"label":"d","text":"85,000"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The PERT expected cost is 75,000 dollars. The three-point estimate weights the most likely value four times: (optimistic + 4 × most likely + pessimistic) ÷ 6 = (50,000 + 4 × 70,000 + 120,000) ÷ 6 = 450,000 ÷ 6 = 75,000. A simple average of the three values would give 80,000.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'project-management'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q42)',
  ARRAY[19]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q42. Based on the requirements gathered, the cost of a software project under normal
 conditions is estimated at $70,000. In case of smooth project implementation, some activities
 are not required and the estimated cost is reduced to $50,000; however, in the worst-case
 scenario, additional tasks are required and the cost increases to $120,000. What is the
 expected cost of the project (in dollars) that is calculated by using the three-point estimate in
 the beta distribution, also known as PERT?

 a) 70,000 b) 75,000 c) 80,000 d) 85,000',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[19]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  43,
  'Q43. IT services are provided under the conditions in the SLA shown below. What is the
 maximum number of hours of downtime in a month that can satisfy the SLA?

 [Conditions in the SLA]
 ‐Number of business days per month: 30
 ‐Service hours: 7 AM to 11 PM on business days
 ‐Agreed availability: 99% or more
 ‐Maintenance time can be ignored.',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.05,118.21],"text":"Q43.\nIT services are provided under the conditions in the SLA shown below. What is the\nmaximum number of hours of downtime in a month that can satisfy the SLA?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[110.7,122.93,357.39,208.21],"text":"[Conditions in the SLA]\n‐Number of business days per month: 30\n‐Service hours: 7 AM to 11 PM on business days\n‐Agreed availability: 99% or more\n‐Maintenance time can be ignored."},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,230.93,473.1,262.15],"text":"a) 1.2\nb) 3.0\nc) 4.8\nd) 7.2"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"1.2"},{"label":"b","text":"3.0"},{"label":"c","text":"4.8"},{"label":"d","text":"7.2"}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'The maximum downtime is 4.8 hours. Service runs from 7 AM to 11 PM, which is 16 hours a day, so a month has 16 × 30 = 480 service hours. With 99% availability, up to 1% of that may be downtime: 480 × 0.01 = 4.8 hours. Using 24 hours a day would wrongly give 7.2.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q43)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q43. IT services are provided under the conditions in the SLA shown below. What is the
 maximum number of hours of downtime in a month that can satisfy the SLA?

 [Conditions in the SLA]
 ‐Number of business days per month: 30
 ‐Service hours: 7 AM to 11 PM on business days
 ‐Agreed availability: 99% or more
 ‐Maintenance time can be ignored.

 a) 1.2 b) 3.0 c) 4.8 d) 7.2',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  44,
  'Q44. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record
 of an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,266.76,533.14,352.21],"text":"Q44.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record\nof an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?\n\na) A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the problem is included in the record of"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,356.93,527.93,388.21],"text":"the problem.\nb) If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,516.35,442.21],"text":"record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted.\nc) One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record.\nd) Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,446.93,151.45,478.21],"text":"incidents."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the problem is included in the record of\n the problem."},{"label":"b","text":"If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the\n record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted."},{"label":"c","text":"One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record."},{"label":"d","text":"Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of\n incidents."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A problem record includes a cross-reference to the incident or incidents that triggered it, so the two can be traced to each other. Incident records are kept rather than deleted when a known error is identified, one problem can be linked to many incidents, and problems are normally classified with the same criteria as incidents to make matching easier.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q44)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q44. Which of the following is an appropriate description of the relationship between a record
 of an incident and a record of a problem in IT service management?

 a) A cross-reference to the incident that triggered the problem is included in the record of
 the problem.
 b) If known errors have been identified at the time of ending the record of the problem, the
 record of the incident that triggered the record of the problem is deleted.
 c) One (1) problem record is always associated with one (1) incident record.
 d) Problems are classified and recorded by a different criterion from the classification of
 incidents.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  45,
  'Q45. In the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk
 of user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,482.76,533.3,550.21],"text":"Q45.\nIn the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk\nof user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,554.93,517.58,568.21],"text":"a) Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,572.93,493.01,604.21],"text":"standards\nb) Whether the program specifications are created on the basis of the system design"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,608.93,509.08,640.21],"text":"documents\nc) Whether the test plan is created on the basis of the system test requirements, and the"},{"type":"text","page":20,"bbox":[84.12,644.93,524.36,676.21],"text":"manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained\nd) Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents"},{"type":"code","page":20,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 20 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and\n standards"},{"label":"b","text":"Whether the program specifications are created on the basis of the system design\n documents"},{"label":"c","text":"Whether the test plan is created on the basis of the system test requirements, and the\n manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained"},{"label":"d","text":"Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The auditor should check whether the user department participates in reviewing the system design documents. User participation in the design review is the control that ensures user requirements are correctly reflected, reducing the risk that they are not met. Coding standards, program specifications and test plans are controls for later phases and other risks.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'it-governance'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q45)',
  ARRAY[20]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q45. In the system design phase, when an audit is performed on the control to reduce the risk
 of user requirements not being met, which of the following is a point to be checked?

 a) Whether programming is performed in accordance with the specified conventions and
 standards
 b) Whether the program specifications are created on the basis of the system design
 documents
 c) Whether the test plan is created on the basis of the system test requirements, and the
 manager’s approval of the system operations department is obtained
 d) Whether the user department participates in the review of the system design documents',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[20]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  46,
  'Q46. Which of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether
 the lifetime benefits of the proposed information system are greater than its lifetime costs?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,67.74,533.1,99.13],"text":"Q46.\nWhich of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether\nthe lifetime benefits of the proposed information system are greater than its lifetime costs?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[84.12,122.86,438.19,157.48],"text":"a) Economic feasibility\nb) Operational feasibility\nc) Scheduling feasibility\nd) Technical feasibility"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Economic feasibility"},{"label":"b","text":"Operational feasibility"},{"label":"c","text":"Scheduling feasibility"},{"label":"d","text":"Technical feasibility"}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Economic feasibility, often done as cost-benefit analysis, checks whether the lifetime benefits of the proposed system exceed its lifetime costs. Operational feasibility asks whether the system will be used and fit the organization, scheduling feasibility asks whether it can be delivered on time, and technical feasibility asks whether the technology is available.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q46)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q46. Which of the following is an appropriate feasibility evaluation when checking whether
 the lifetime benefits of the proposed information system are greater than its lifetime costs?

 a) Economic feasibility b) Operational feasibility
 c) Scheduling feasibility d) Technical feasibility',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  47,
  'Q47. Which of the following is a measure for the risk of a decline in the system maintenance
 and operation quality during the outsourcing of an IT service?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,194.76,533.16,406.21],"text":"Q47.\nWhich of the following is a measure for the risk of a decline in the system maintenance\nand operation quality during the outsourcing of an IT service?\n\na)\nClearly stating the detailed fee structure by service in the contract or other documents,\nin order to validate the service costs\nb)\nRequesting a proposal for the human resource development plan of the company after\noutsourcing during the stage of subcontractor selection, and clearly stating it in the\ncontract or other documents\nc)\nSecuring human resources with capabilities to evaluate the appropriateness of service\ncosts for system maintenance and operation within the company\nd)\nUsing indexes that demonstrate the service quality in order to promote improvement\nactivities after agreeing on the desired level of quality with the subcontractor"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Clearly stating the detailed fee structure by service in the contract or other documents,\n in order to validate the service costs"},{"label":"b","text":"Requesting a proposal for the human resource development plan of the company after\n outsourcing during the stage of subcontractor selection, and clearly stating it in the\n contract or other documents"},{"label":"c","text":"Securing human resources with capabilities to evaluate the appropriateness of service\n costs for system maintenance and operation within the company"},{"label":"d","text":"Using indexes that demonstrate the service quality in order to promote improvement\n activities after agreeing on the desired level of quality with the subcontractor"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The measure that addresses declining maintenance and operation quality is to agree the desired service level with the subcontractor and use quality indicators to drive improvement, typically through an SLA. Detailed fee structures and in-house staff who can judge cost appropriateness address cost risks, and a human resource development plan addresses the subcontractor''s staffing rather than service quality directly.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'procurement'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q47)',
  ARRAY[21]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q47. Which of the following is a measure for the risk of a decline in the system maintenance
 and operation quality during the outsourcing of an IT service?

 a) Clearly stating the detailed fee structure by service in the contract or other documents,
 in order to validate the service costs
 b) Requesting a proposal for the human resource development plan of the company after
 outsourcing during the stage of subcontractor selection, and clearly stating it in the
 contract or other documents
 c) Securing human resources with capabilities to evaluate the appropriateness of service
 costs for system maintenance and operation within the company
 d) Using indexes that demonstrate the service quality in order to promote improvement
 activities after agreeing on the desired level of quality with the subcontractor',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[21]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
