  48,
  'Q48. In a business scenario where marketing managers analyze customer interests and sales
 patterns, design promotional campaigns, and then send targeted emails to customers, which
 of the following is a modeling technique used to represent how information flows between
 internal processes, data stores, and external entities?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,446.76,533.2,532.21],"text":"Q48.\nIn a business scenario where marketing managers analyze customer interests and sales\npatterns, design promotional campaigns, and then send targeted emails to customers, which\nof the following is a modeling technique used to represent how information flows between\ninternal processes, data stores, and external entities?"},{"type":"text","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,536.93,460.83,586.21],"text":"a) Class Diagram\nb) Data Flow Diagram (DFD)\nc) Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD)\nd) Use Case Diagram"},{"type":"code","page":21,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 21 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"Class Diagram"},{"label":"b","text":"Data Flow Diagram (DFD)"},{"label":"c","text":"Entity-Relationship Diagram (ERD)"},{"label":"d","text":"Use Case Diagram"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'A data flow diagram (DFD) models how data flows between processes, data stores and external entities, which matches the marketing scenario described. A class diagram shows classes and their relationships, an ER diagram shows entities and relationships of stored data, and a use case diagram shows actor interactions, none of which focus on data flow.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'software-development'),
