(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  49,
  'Q49. Which of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate
 management?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,533.12,100.21],"text":"Q49.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate\nmanagement?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,516.13,136.21],"text":"a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,140.93,520.63,190.21],"text":"services, and operations through comparison with those of competitors or advanced\ncompanies.\nb) It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,522.64,244.21],"text":"its business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of\ninformation technology.\nc) It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,248.93,492.62,298.21],"text":"resources in an effective and integrated manner in order to improve management\nefficiency.\nd) It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,302.93,530.58,352.21],"text":"technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other\ncompanies."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,\n services, and operations through comparison with those of competitors or advanced\n companies."},{"label":"b","text":"It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning\n its business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of\n information technology."},{"label":"c","text":"It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management\n resources in an effective and integrated manner in order to improve management\n efficiency."},{"label":"d","text":"It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and\n technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other\n companies."}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'Benchmarking means understanding a company''s own products, services and operations qualitatively and quantitatively by comparing them with those of competitors or best-practice companies, then using the gap to improve. Redesigning processes with IT is BPR, integrated planning of company-wide resources is ERP, and concentrating on unique superior skills is core competence.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q49)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q49. Which of the following is an explanation of benchmarking that is used for corporate
 management?

 a) It refers to a qualitative and quantitative understanding of a company’s own products,
 services, and operations through comparison with those of competitors or advanced
 companies.
 b) It refers to drastically reforming the quality and structure of a company by redesigning
 its business processes from a customer viewpoint and by taking full advantage of
 information technology.
 c) It refers to the ability to plan and manage the allocation of company-wide management
 resources in an effective and integrated manner in order to improve management
 efficiency.
 d) It refers to the concentration of management resources on the unique skills and
 technologies of a company that can generate profit and that are superior to those of other
 companies.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  50,
  'Q50. Which of the following is an explanation of relationship marketing?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,356.93,436.45,387.19],"text":"Q50.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of relationship marketing?"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,392.93,523.73,424.21],"text":"a) It is a marketing technique of setting a time limit for a short period, ranging from a few"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,490.43,460.21],"text":"hours to a few days, and selling products on the Internet only during that period.\nb) It is a marketing technique of using the GPS function of a smartphone to send"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,464.93,511.71,496.21],"text":"advertisements from stores near the current location.\nc) It is a marketing technique that aims at a diversified approach to consumers by using"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,500.93,515.74,532.21],"text":"several media such as television, newspapers, and magazines.\nd) It is a marketing technique that aims to acquire stable sales over a long period of time"},{"type":"text","page":22,"bbox":[84.12,536.93,458.68,568.21],"text":"from each customer by maintaining a good connection with the customer.\n."},{"type":"code","page":22,"bbox":[65.22,794.63,314.58,807.97],"text":"– 22 –"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a marketing technique of setting a time limit for a short period, ranging from a few hours to a few days, and selling products on the Internet only during that period."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a marketing technique of using the GPS function of a smartphone to send advertisements from stores near the current location."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a marketing technique that aims at a diversified approach to consumers by using several media such as television, newspapers, and magazines."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a marketing technique that aims to acquire stable sales over a long period of time from each customer by maintaining a good connection with the customer."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'Relationship marketing aims to secure stable sales from each customer over a long period by building and maintaining a good relationship with that customer, focusing on retention and lifetime value. Time-limited online sales are flash sales, GPS-based advertising is location-based marketing, and using several media together is media mix.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q50)',
  ARRAY[22]::int[],
  'manual_review',
  '3.0',
  'Q50. Which of the following is an explanation of relationship marketing?

 a) It is a marketing technique of setting a time limit for a short period, ranging from a few
 hours to a few days, and selling products on the Internet only during that period.
 b) It is a marketing technique of using the GPS function of a smartphone to send
 advertisements from stores near the current location.
 c) It is a marketing technique that aims at a diversified approach to consumers by using
 several media such as television, newspapers, and magazines.
 d) It is a marketing technique that aims to acquire stable sales over a long period of time
 from each customer by maintaining a good connection with the customer.
 .',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[22]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  51,
  'Q51. Which of the following is an explanation of ERP?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,343.69,100.21],"text":"Q51. Which of the following is an explanation of ERP?"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,529.33,118.21],"text":"a) It is a method or concept by which wholesalers and manufacturers expand their business"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,497.08,154.21],"text":"transactions with retail stores by supporting the business activities of retail stores.\nb) It is a method or concept for performing business transactions with consumers or"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,507.72,190.21],"text":"between companies through the use of electronic networks such as the Internet.\nc) It is a method or concept that aims to drastically increase sales, profit, and customer"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[84.12,194.93,521.68,244.21],"text":"satisfaction by improving the efficiency and quality of sales through the use of IT in\nsales activities.\nd) It is a method or concept that aims to improve management efficiency by planning and"},{"type":"text","page":23,"bbox":[102.12,248.93,484.69,280.21],"text":"controlling the management resources of an entire company in an effective and\ncomprehensive manner."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a method or concept by which wholesalers and manufacturers expand their business\n transactions with retail stores by supporting the business activities of retail stores."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a method or concept for performing business transactions with consumers or\n between companies through the use of electronic networks such as the Internet."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a method or concept that aims to drastically increase sales, profit, and customer\n satisfaction by improving the efficiency and quality of sales through the use of IT in\n sales activities."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a method or concept that aims to improve management efficiency by planning and\n controlling the management resources of an entire company in an effective and\n comprehensive manner."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'ERP (Enterprise Resource Planning) aims to improve management efficiency by planning and controlling the management resources of the whole company, such as people, goods, money and information, in an integrated way. Supporting retailers'' activities is retail support, electronic transactions over networks is e-commerce, and using IT to improve sales activities is SFA.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q51)',
  ARRAY[23]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q51. Which of the following is an explanation of ERP?

 a) It is a method or concept by which wholesalers and manufacturers expand their business
 transactions with retail stores by supporting the business activities of retail stores.
 b) It is a method or concept for performing business transactions with consumers or
 between companies through the use of electronic networks such as the Internet.
 c) It is a method or concept that aims to drastically increase sales, profit, and customer
 satisfaction by improving the efficiency and quality of sales through the use of IT in
 sales activities.
 d) It is a method or concept that aims to improve management efficiency by planning and
 controlling the management resources of an entire company in an effective and
 comprehensive manner.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[23]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
