  'A',
  54,
  'Q54. Which of the following is a characteristic of an IC tag (RFID)?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,68.76,412.42,100.21],"text":"Q54.\nWhich of the following is a characteristic of an IC tag (RFID)?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,104.93,530.39,118.21],"text":"a) It handles a large amount of information, so it uses an external storage device for storing"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,122.93,490.93,154.21],"text":"information.\nb) It is stain-resistant, and recorded information can be read from the outside of the"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,158.93,512.32,208.21],"text":"package.\nc) It is used by inserting the tag into a dedicated magnetic reader.\nd) It uses GPS to display location information or attribute information about the current"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,212.93,146.77,244.21],"text":"location."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It handles a large amount of information, so it uses an external storage device for storing\n information."},{"label":"b","text":"It is stain-resistant, and recorded information can be read from the outside of the\n package."},{"label":"c","text":"It is used by inserting the tag into a dedicated magnetic reader."},{"label":"d","text":"It uses GPS to display location information or attribute information about the current\n location."}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'An IC tag (RFID) is resistant to dirt and its data can be read wirelessly, even from outside the packaging, without direct contact or line of sight. It stores its information in its own small IC chip rather than external storage, it does not need to be inserted into a magnetic reader, and it does not use GPS.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-operations'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q54)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q54. Which of the following is a characteristic of an IC tag (RFID)?

 a) It handles a large amount of information, so it uses an external storage device for storing
 information.
 b) It is stain-resistant, and recorded information can be read from the outside of the
 package.
 c) It is used by inserting the tag into a dedicated magnetic reader.
 d) It uses GPS to display location information or attribute information about the current
 location.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'A',
  55,
  'Q55. Which of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?',
  '[{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[65.22,248.93,418.75,279.19],"text":"Q55.\nWhich of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,284.93,516.58,316.21],"text":"a) It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,320.93,527.34,370.21],"text":"urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which improves the quality of people’s\nlives and achieves sustainable economic growth.\nb) It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases through the use"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,374.93,532.01,424.21],"text":"of IT, eliminating the supply and demand gap via SCM progress, which leads to\nsustainable inflation-free growth.\nc) It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are integrated to combine"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[84.12,428.93,507.05,460.21],"text":"the benefits of both and expand overall sales.\nd) It is a mechanism, mainly between individuals, that uses the community function or"},{"type":"text","page":24,"bbox":[102.12,464.93,492.61,496.21],"text":"other functions of social media to share, lend, or borrow unused assets owned by\nindividuals."}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and\n urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which improves the quality of people’s\n lives and achieves sustainable economic growth."},{"label":"b","text":"It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases through the use\n of IT, eliminating the supply and demand gap via SCM progress, which leads to\n sustainable inflation-free growth."},{"label":"c","text":"It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are integrated to combine\n the benefits of both and expand overall sales."},{"label":"d","text":"It is a mechanism, mainly between individuals, that uses the community function or\n other functions of social media to share, lend, or borrow unused assets owned by\n individuals."}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'A sharing economy is a mechanism, mainly between individuals, that uses social media and online platforms to share, lend or borrow unused assets such as rooms, cars or skills. Using IT to run energy and urban infrastructure describes a smart city, and integrating store and Internet sales describes omni-channel retailing.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'business-strategy'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-A, Q55)',
  ARRAY[24]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q55. Which of the following is an explanation of a sharing economy?

 a) It is a concept by which efficient management and operation of renewable energy and
 urban infrastructure are performed by using IT, which improves the quality of people’s
 lives and achieves sustainable economic growth.
 b) It is a concept by which the productivity of an entire economy increases through the use
 of IT, eliminating the supply and demand gap via SCM progress, which leads to
 sustainable inflation-free growth.
 c) It is a mechanism by which over-the-counter and Internet sales are integrated to combine
 the benefits of both and expand overall sales.
 d) It is a mechanism, mainly between individuals, that uses the community function or
 other functions of social media to share, lend, or borrow unused assets owned by
 individuals.',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/questions.pdf","pages":[24]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/a/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
