  58,
  'Q58. The horizontal and vertical axes of an Operating Characteristic (OC) curve in quality management generally represent the percent defective of a lot and the success rate of a lot, respectively. Samples of size n are extracted from a lot of size N. When the number of defective samples is less than or equal to the pass quantity C, the lot is considered to have passed; otherwise, it is considered to have failed.
Which of the following is a diagram that shows the trend of change in the OC curve when N and n are fixed and C takes the values 0, 1, and 2?',
  '[{"type":"text","text":"Q58. The horizontal and vertical axes of an Operating Characteristic (OC) curve in quality management generally represent the percent defective of a lot and the success rate of a lot, respectively. Samples of size n are extracted from a lot of size N. When the number of defective samples is less than or equal to the pass quantity C, the lot is considered to have passed; otherwise, it is considered to have failed.\nWhich of the following is a diagram that shows the trend of change in the OC curve when N and n are fixed and C takes the values 0, 1, and 2?"}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"","image":"2025-october-a-q58-choice-a.webp"},{"label":"b","text":"","image":"2025-october-a-q58-choice-b.webp"},{"label":"c","text":"","image":"2025-october-a-q58-choice-c.webp"},{"label":"d","text":"","image":"2025-october-a-q58-choice-d.webp"}]'::jsonb,
  'b',
  '{"value":"b"}'::jsonb,
  'The correct diagram is the one where the C = 0 curve is lowest and drops fastest, with C = 1 and then C = 2 lying progressively further to the upper right. Raising the acceptance number C makes it easier for a lot to pass, so for any percent defective the probability of acceptance is higher. All curves start at 100% acceptance when the defective rate is 0 and fall as it rises.',
