(
  '2025-october',
  'B',
  1,
  'Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

The function sum receives an integer array array with at least two elements and two positive
 integers k and m (k < m ≤ number of elements in array). It calculates the sum of even
 elements of the array array whose indices are from k to m.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"The function sum receives an integer array array with at least two elements and two positive\n integers k and m (k < m ≤ number of elements in array). It calculates the sum of even\n elements of the array array whose indices are from k to m."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ integer: sum(integer []: array, integer: k, integer: m)\n  integer: s ← 0\n  integer: i ← k\n  while (i ≤ m)\nif (***A***)\n      s ← s + array[i]\n    endif"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 = 0","B":"←\ni i + 1"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 = 0","B":"←\ni i - 1"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0","B":"←\ni i + 1"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0","B":"←\ni i - 1"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"array[i] mod 2 = 0 i ← i + 1","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 = 0","B":"←\ni i + 1"}},{"label":"b","text":"array[i] mod 2 = 0 i ← i - 1","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 = 0","B":"←\ni i - 1"}},{"label":"c","text":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0 i ← i + 1","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0","B":"←\ni i + 1"}},{"label":"d","text":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0 i ← i - 1","values":{"A":"array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0","B":"←\ni i - 1"}}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A is array[i] mod 2 = 0 and B is i ← i + 1. Only even elements may be added to s, and an element is even exactly when its remainder on division by 2 is 0. Because i starts at k and the loop runs while i ≤ m, i must increase by 1 each pass; decrementing it would move away from m and never end the loop.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-B, Q1)',
  ARRAY[4]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q1. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ____A____ and ____B____ in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

 The function sum receives an integer array array with at least two elements and two positive
 integers k and m (k < m ≤ number of elements in array). It calculates the sum of even
 elements of the array array whose indices are from k to m.

 [Program]
 ○ integer: sum(integer []: array, integer: k, integer: m)
 integer: s ← 0
 integer: i ← k
 while (i ≤ m)
 if (____A____)
 s ← s + array[i]
 endif
 ____B____

 endwhile
 return s

 Answer group
 A B
 a) array[i] mod 2 = 0 i ← i + 1
 b) array[i] mod 2 = 0 i ← i - 1
 c) array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0 i ← i + 1
 d) array[i] mod 2 ≠ 0 i ← i - 1',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/b/questions.pdf","pages":[4]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'B',
  2,
  'Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

In statistics, the mode is the value that occurs most frequently in a dataset. For example, the
 mode of the integer array {2, 1, 1, 9, 6, 6, 2, 5, 6} is 6, as it occurs most often. The function
 findMode receives an integer array arr as a dataset and returns the mode for it.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"In statistics, the mode is the value that occurs most frequently in a dataset. For example, the\n mode of the integer array {2, 1, 1, 9, 6, 6, 2, 5, 6} is 6, as it occurs most often. The function\n findMode receives an integer array arr as a dataset and returns the mode for it."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ integer: findMode(integer []: arr)\n  integer: n ← the number of elements in arr\n  integer: m ← arr[1]  /* Current mode value */\n  integer: m_c ← 1     /* Frequency count of mode */\n  integer: c, i, j\n  for (increase i from 1 to n - 1 by 1)\n    c ← 1\n    for (increase j from i + 1 to n by 1)\n      if (***A***)\n        c ← c + 1\n      endif\n    endfor\n    if (***B***)\n      m_c ← c\n      m ← arr[i]\n    endif\n  endfor\n  return m"},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m < arr[i]"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m ≠ arr[i]"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m_c < c"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m_c > c"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m < arr[i]"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m ≠ arr[i]"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m_c < c"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m_c > c"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"arr[i] = arr[j] m < arr[i]","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m < arr[i]"}},{"label":"b","text":"arr[i] = arr[j] m ≠ arr[i]","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m ≠ arr[i]"}},{"label":"c","text":"arr[i] = arr[j] m_c < c","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m_c < c"}},{"label":"d","text":"arr[i] = arr[j] m_c > c","values":{"A":"arr[i] = arr[j]","B":"m_c > c"}},{"label":"e","text":"m = arr[j] m < arr[i]","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m < arr[i]"}},{"label":"f","text":"m = arr[j] m ≠ arr[i]","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m ≠ arr[i]"}},{"label":"g","text":"m = arr[j] m_c < c","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m_c < c"}},{"label":"h","text":"m = arr[j] m_c > c","values":{"A":"m = arr[j]","B":"m_c > c"}}]'::jsonb,
  'c',
  '{"value":"c"}'::jsonb,
  'A is arr[i] = arr[j] and B is m_c < c. For each position i, the inner loop counts in c how many elements from i onward equal arr[i], so A must compare arr[i] with each later arr[j]. The current mode m and its count m_c should be replaced only when this new count c is larger than the best so far, which is the condition m_c < c; using m_c > c would update on a smaller count instead.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
  0.5,
  'questions.pdf',
  '(2025A, FE, Subject-B, Q2)',
  ARRAY[5]::int[],
  'native_text',
  '3.0',
  'Q2. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ___A___ and ___B___ in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

 In statistics, the mode is the value that occurs most frequently in a dataset. For example, the
 mode of the integer array {2, 1, 1, 9, 6, 6, 2, 5, 6} is 6, as it occurs most often. The function
 findMode receives an integer array arr as a dataset and returns the mode for it.

 [Program]
 ○ integer: findMode(integer []: arr)
 integer: n ← the number of elements in arr
 integer: m ← arr[1] /* Current mode value */
 integer: m_c ← 1 /* Frequency count of mode */
 integer: c, i, j
 for (increase i from 1 to n - 1 by 1)
 c ← 1
 for (increase j from i + 1 to n by 1)
 if (___A___)
 c ← c + 1
 endif
 endfor
 if (___B___)
 m_c ← c
 m ← arr[i]
 endif
 endfor
 return m

 Answer group
 A B
 a) arr[i] = arr[j] m < arr[i]
 b) arr[i] = arr[j] m ≠ arr[i]
 c) arr[i] = arr[j] m_c < c
 d) arr[i] = arr[j] m_c > c
 e) m = arr[j] m < arr[i]
 f) m = arr[j] m ≠ arr[i]
 g) m = arr[j] m_c < c
 h) m = arr[j] m_c > c',
  '{"question_pdf":{"filename":"questions.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/b/questions.pdf","pages":[5]},"answer_pdf":{"filename":"answers.pdf","storage_path":"2025-october/b/answers.pdf","pages":[1]}}'::jsonb,
  true
),
(
  '2025-october',
  'B',
  3,
  'Q3. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the program. Here, the array index starts at 1.

Given an array of positive integers and a target sum, the problem is to find the subarray
 whose sum is equal to the target sum. A subarray is a part of the given array composed of
 contiguous elements. For example, when the target sum is 14, the shaded subarray in the
 figure satisfies the given condition.

6 3 2 5 1 1 7 3

