  'A is temp > 0, B is rev × 10 + rm, and C is integer part of (temp ÷ 10). Each pass takes the ones digit rm = temp mod 10, shifts the reversed number left one place and appends rm (456 gives rev = 6, 65, 654), then drops the ones digit from temp by integer division by 10. The loop must test temp, not num, because num never changes and num > 0 would loop forever; temp − rm would only zero the last digit rather than remove it.',
