 (a) Reverse the order of the elements in the list starting from head, and set the next element
 of the last element in the reversed list—that is, the next element of head—to elm.
 To “reverse the order of the elements in the list starting from head,” reverse the list starting
 from the next element of head, and then connect head to the end of the reversed list. In other
 words, execute (a) by setting head as elm, and the next element of head as head.

