The function checkMagicSquare receives a two-dimensional 3 × 3 integer array (matrix) m
 containing the numbers 1 to 9, and returns whether the given matrix is a magic square or not.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q14. From the answer group below, select the correct answer to be inserted into _________ in\n the program. Here, the array index starts at 1."},{"type":"context","text":"A 3 × 3 normal magic square is a 3 × 3 matrix where the sum of the elements for each row,\n each column, and each diagonal is the same. The square contains the numbers 1 to 9, exactly\n as shown in the figure.\n\n4 9 2 15\n 3 5 7 15\n 8 1 6 15\n\n15 15 15 15 15\n Figure 3 × 3 normal magic square\n\nThe function checkMagicSquare receives a two-dimensional 3 × 3 integer array (matrix) m\n containing the numbers 1 to 9, and returns whether the given matrix is a magic square or not."},{"type":"code","language":"itpec-pseudocode","text":"○ boolean: checkMagicSquare(integer [,]: m)\n  integer: i, j, k\n  integer: dia1Sum ← 0\n  integer: dia2Sum ← 0\n  integer []: rowSum ← {0, 0, 0}\n  integer []: colSum ← {0, 0, 0}\n  for (increase i from 1 to 3 by 1)\n    for (increase j from 1 to 3 by 1)\n      rowSum[i] ← rowSum[i] + m[i,j]\n      colSum[i] ← colSum[i] + m[j,i]\n    endfor\n    dia1Sum ← dia1Sum + m[i,i]\n    dia2Sum ← dia2Sum + m[i,3 - i + 1]\n  endfor\n  if (dia1Sum ≠ dia2Sum)\n    return false\n  endif\n  for (increase k from 1 to 3 by 1)"}]'::jsonb,
  '["2025-october-b-q14-figure1.webp"]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"(rowSum[k] = colSum[k]) and (rowSum[k] = dia1Sum)"},{"label":"b","text":"(rowSum[k] = colSum[k]) or (rowSum[k] = dia1Sum)"},{"label":"c","text":"(rowSum[k] ≠ colSum[k]) and (rowSum[k] ≠ dia1Sum)"},{"label":"d","text":"(rowSum[k] ≠ colSum[k]) or (rowSum[k] ≠ dia1Sum)"}]'::jsonb,
  'd',
  '{"value":"d"}'::jsonb,
  'The condition is (rowSum[k] ≠ colSum[k]) or (rowSum[k] ≠ dia1Sum). The function must return false as soon as any row or column sum differs from the common value, and the two diagonals have already been checked equal. A failure in either comparison is enough to reject the square, so the two ≠ tests are joined with or; using and would reject only when both comparisons fail at once.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'algorithms'),
  'medium',
