  '2025-october',
  'B',
  17,
  'Q17. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be
 inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description.

Company P is a small business that recently formed a data analytics team to perform business
 data analytics using internal business data. This data is stored on a database system
 configured with a synchronous (real-time) mirror. The database is backed up regularly. The
 database servers and IT infrastructure are maintained by a third-party IT support provider.

A junior data analyst was mistakenly granted database superuser privileges to the production
 database. This decision was made due to a lack of security understanding in the company.
 The data analyst, unfamiliar with the sensitivity of their access level, was tasked with
 executing a series of routine database queries and migrations. However, due to an error in a
 script, the data analyst accidentally ran a command that dropped critical tables, resulting in
 a significant loss of data. This caused the company’s internal applications to stop working.

The company engaged their IT support provider, and the database system was quickly put
 back in service by ***A***. To prevent this incident from happening again, their IT
 support provider recommended that the company implement ***B***.',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q17. From the answer group below, select the most appropriate combination of answers to be\n inserted into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description."},{"type":"context","text":"Company P is a small business that recently formed a data analytics team to perform business\n data analytics using internal business data. This data is stored on a database system\n configured with a synchronous (real-time) mirror. The database is backed up regularly. The\n database servers and IT infrastructure are maintained by a third-party IT support provider.\n\nA junior data analyst was mistakenly granted database superuser privileges to the production\n database. This decision was made due to a lack of security understanding in the company.\n The data analyst, unfamiliar with the sensitivity of their access level, was tasked with\n executing a series of routine database queries and migrations. However, due to an error in a\n script, the data analyst accidentally ran a command that dropped critical tables, resulting in\n a significant loss of data. This caused the company’s internal applications to stop working.\n\nThe company engaged their IT support provider, and the database system was quickly put\n back in service by ***A***. To prevent this incident from happening again, their IT\n support provider recommended that the company implement ***B***."},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"principle of least privilege"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"principle of least privilege"}},{"label":"g","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"h","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"i","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"principle of least privilege"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"restarting the database server database encryption","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"b","text":"restarting the database server multi-factor authentication","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"c","text":"restarting the database server principle of least privilege","values":{"A":"restarting the database server","B":"principle of least privilege"}},{"label":"d","text":"restoring from backups database encryption","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"e","text":"restoring from backups multi-factor authentication","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"f","text":"restoring from backups principle of least privilege","values":{"A":"restoring from backups","B":"principle of least privilege"}},{"label":"g","text":"switching to the database mirror database encryption","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"database encryption"}},{"label":"h","text":"switching to the database mirror multi-factor authentication","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"multi-factor authentication"}},{"label":"i","text":"switching to the database mirror principle of least privilege","values":{"A":"switching to the database mirror","B":"principle of least privilege"}}]'::jsonb,
  'f',
  '{"value":"f"}'::jsonb,
  'A is restoring from backups and B is principle of least privilege. Because the mirror is synchronous, the table drop was replicated to it immediately, so switching to the mirror would not recover the data, and restarting the server cannot bring back dropped tables; only the regular backups still contain them. The root cause was a junior analyst holding superuser rights, so the fix is to grant each user only the privileges their work needs; encryption or MFA would not stop an authorised user''s mistaken command.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'access-control'),
  'medium',
