(
  '2025-october',
  'B',
  19,
  'Q19. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted
 into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description.

Company R is a software company that sells video editing software for consumers. The
 company has branch offices in multiple countries, all managed by its head office. In
 Company R’s customer support department, customer satisfaction surveys are sent to
 selected customer who have received support. The survey results are aggregated at each
 branch, and must be sent to the customer survey analysis team at the head office every day.
 Ms. T at the customer survey analysis team at the head office is responsible for managing
 and securing the survey data. The considerations for collecting survey data from each branch
 office are as follows:
 - The employees responsible for sending the survey data at each branch office changes
 daily.
 - At the head office, Ms. T in the customer survey analysis team is responsible for
 receiving and analyzing the survey data from the branch offices. After receiving the
 survey data from the branch offices, she saves the data to a shared folder that only the
 customer survey analysis team can access.
 - The file size of survey data is large, so using inefficient encryption methods would take
 too much time and is therefore not suitable.
 - Since the survey data contains confidential information, it must be ensured that no one
 other than the sender and the intended recipients can view the contents during
 transmission between the head office and branch offices.
 - The key used to encrypt the files must be transmitted in a way that prevents it from
 being stolen by a man-in-the-middle attacker.
 - There are many branch offices and it is not practical to visit each office in person to
 distribute keys.

Ms. T decided to adopt a new method in which the branch offices upload the survey data,
 encrypted using file encryption, to a shared folder. She set up this shared folder with access
 permissions granted to both the head office and branch office staff, and instructed the branch
 office staff to upload the encrypted survey data to it. Taking into account the considerations
 related to collecting information from the branches, Ms. T decided to use ***A*** as the
 encryption method. In this method, the key used for encrypting the survey data is encrypted
 using the public key of ***B*** .',
  '[{"type":"prompt","text":"Q19. From the answer group below, select the correct combination of answers to be inserted\n into ***A*** and ***B*** in the description."},{"type":"context","text":"Company R is a software company that sells video editing software for consumers. The\n company has branch offices in multiple countries, all managed by its head office. In\n Company R’s customer support department, customer satisfaction surveys are sent to\n selected customer who have received support. The survey results are aggregated at each\n branch, and must be sent to the customer survey analysis team at the head office every day.\n Ms. T at the customer survey analysis team at the head office is responsible for managing\n and securing the survey data. The considerations for collecting survey data from each branch\n office are as follows:\n - The employees responsible for sending the survey data at each branch office changes\n daily.\n - At the head office, Ms. T in the customer survey analysis team is responsible for\n receiving and analyzing the survey data from the branch offices. After receiving the\n survey data from the branch offices, she saves the data to a shared folder that only the\n customer survey analysis team can access.\n - The file size of survey data is large, so using inefficient encryption methods would take\n too much time and is therefore not suitable.\n - Since the survey data contains confidential information, it must be ensured that no one\n other than the sender and the intended recipients can view the contents during\n transmission between the head office and branch offices.\n - The key used to encrypt the files must be transmitted in a way that prevents it from\n being stolen by a man-in-the-middle attacker.\n - There are many branch offices and it is not practical to visit each office in person to\n distribute keys.\n\nMs. T decided to adopt a new method in which the branch offices upload the survey data,\n encrypted using file encryption, to a shared folder. She set up this shared folder with access\n permissions granted to both the head office and branch office staff, and instructed the branch\n office staff to upload the encrypted survey data to it. Taking into account the considerations\n related to collecting information from the branches, Ms. T decided to use ***A*** as the\n encryption method. In this method, the key used for encrypting the survey data is encrypted\n using the public key of ***B*** ."},{"type":"answer_table","columns":["A","B"],"rows":[{"label":"a","values":{"A":"hybrid encryption","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"b","values":{"A":"hybrid encryption","B":"the branch office staff"}},{"label":"c","values":{"A":"public key encryption only","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"d","values":{"A":"public key encryption only","B":"the branch office staff"}},{"label":"e","values":{"A":"symmetric key encryption only","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"f","values":{"A":"symmetric key encryption only","B":"the branch office staff"}}]}]'::jsonb,
  '[]'::jsonb,
  '[{"label":"a","text":"hybrid encryption Ms. T","values":{"A":"hybrid encryption","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"b","text":"hybrid encryption the branch office staff","values":{"A":"hybrid encryption","B":"the branch office staff"}},{"label":"c","text":"public key encryption only Ms. T","values":{"A":"public key encryption only","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"d","text":"public key encryption only the branch office staff","values":{"A":"public key encryption only","B":"the branch office staff"}},{"label":"e","text":"symmetric key encryption only Ms. T","values":{"A":"symmetric key encryption only","B":"Ms. T"}},{"label":"f","text":"symmetric key encryption only the branch office staff","values":{"A":"symmetric key encryption only","B":"the branch office staff"}}]'::jsonb,
  'a',
  '{"value":"a"}'::jsonb,
  'A is hybrid encryption and B is Ms. T. The large files are encrypted with a fast symmetric (common) key, and that key is then encrypted with the recipient''s public key, so no in-person key distribution is needed and a man-in-the-middle cannot read the key. The recipient is Ms. T, so her public key is used and only her private key can recover the file key; public-key-only encryption would be too slow for large files, and symmetric-only would leave the key distribution problem unsolved.',
  (SELECT id FROM subtopics WHERE slug = 'cryptography'),
