  'A is integrating automated secret scanning tools and B is adding a rule that mandates regular rotation of secrets. Secret scanning tools examine code for API keys and other credentials before it is committed or published, which is exactly the detection step described; API log checks and antivirus scans do not find secrets in source code. Regular rotation limits how long any leaked secret remains valid, which minimises damage if one still escapes, whereas MFA on the repository does not protect a key that is already public.',
